Abaeus,m,Ἀβαῖος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Ἀβαῖος (Abaios) meaning ""of Abai"", an epithet of the Greek god Apollo, given because the ancient town of Ἄβαι (Abai) (see Abae) in Phocis was the site of an oracle of the god and of a temple dedicated to him."
