Aban,,آبان(Persian),Persian Mythology|Persian|Indian (Parsi)|Medieval Arabic (Moorish)|Arabic,,,,,,,,"From Middle Persian ābān meaning ""waters"" (plural of āb), from Avestan āpas. In modern Persian it refers to ""the eighth solar month of the Persian calendar (October-November)"". In Persian mythology, this is also the name of the Angel of October."
