Abandokht,f,"آباندخت, آبان‌دخت(Persian)",Old Persian|Persian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Means ""daughter of the waters"" (or possibly ""daughter of Aban"", the name of a yazata or angel in Zoroastrianism), from Middle Persian ābān meaning ""waters"" (plural of āb) combined with دخت (doxt) meaning ""daughter"". By some accounts, this was the name of a wife of Darius III, the last Achaemenid emperor."
