Abatur,m,,Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend|Near Eastern Mythology|Arabic (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Means literally, ""father of the Uthre"" in Mandaean, which translates roughly to ""father of the angels,"" derived from aba ""father"" combined with uthra ('utria) ""angel"". In the Mandaean Gnostic cosmology, Abatur is ""the third of four emanations from the supreme, unknowable deity"", and the father of Ptahil, the Mandaean demiurge."
