Abdalmassih,m,عبد المسح(Arabic),Arabic,/ʕab.dul.ma.siːħ/,,,,,,,"Means ""servant of the Messiah"", from Arabic عبد ال (ʿabd al) and المسح (masih) ""messiah, Christ"". It was borne by a ninth-century martyr who was executed for reverting to Christianity after having converted to Islam. It is typically used by Christian Arabs."
