Aberforth,m,,Literature,AB-ər-forth,,,,,,,"Variant of Aberford, a village in West Yorkshire, meaning ""Eadburg's ford"" in Old English. This was the name of schoolmaster Albus Dumbledore's more eccentric brother in J. K. Rowling's 'Harry Potter' books, released between 1997 and 2007."
