Abhinandananatha,m,अभिनन्दननाथ(Sanskrit),Jainism,/ɐ.bʱi.n̪ɐn̪.d̪ɐ.n̪ɐ.ˈn̪ɑː.t̪ʰɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit अभिनन्दन (abhinandana) meaning ""greeting, welcoming, praising, applauding"" and नाथ (nātha) meaning ""master, lord"". In Jain tradition this is the name of the fourth of the 24 tirthankaras (enlightened spiritual teachers)."
Abhinavagupta,m,अभिनवगुप्त(Sanskrit),Sanskrit,,,,,,,,"From Sanskrit अभिनव (abhinava) ""young, fresh"" and गुप्त (gupta) ""protected"". This was the name of a Kashmirian philosopher, mystic and aesthetician who lived during 950 to 1016 CE."
