Abiasaph,m,אֲבִיאָסָף(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""my father has gathered"" in Hebrew, derived from אָב (ʾav) meaning ""father"" and the verb אסף (asap) meaning ""to gather, to collect"" (compare Asaph). This name is mentioned in the Old Testament as belonging to a son of Korah son of Izhar (the cousin of Moses and Aaron)."
