Abinoam,m,אֲבִינֹּעַם(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""my father is pleasantness"" or ""father of delight"", derived from the Hebrew roots אָב (ʾav) meaning ""father"" and נָעַם (naʿam) meaning ""to be pleasant"". In the Old Testament this name belonged to the father of the famous general Barak."
