Abrotonon,f,Ἀβρότονον(Ancient Greek),Thracian (Hellenized)|Ancient Greek (?),,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown, traditionally connected to the Greek word ἁβρός (habros) meaning ""delicate"" but more likely a loanword, possibly borrowed from Akkadian. Abrotonon was the name of the Thracian mother of Themistocles, of a Thracian hetaera in the writings of Plutarch, and a plant mentioned by Pliny the Elder."
