Abul,m,أبو ال(Arabic)|ابو ال(Urdu),Arabic|Afghan|Pakistani|Urdu,,,,,,,,"Means ""father of the"" in Arabic, derived from Arabic أبو (abu) meaning ""father of"" (see Abu) combined with Arabic ال (al) meaning ""the"". Also compare names like Abul-Fazl.Notable bearers of this name include the Indian scholar Abul Kalam Azad (1888-1958) and the Pakistani philosopher Abul A'la Maududi (1903-1979)."
