Achaius,m,,Scottish,aKYus,,,,,,,Scottish given name meaning 'Friend of a horse'.
Achaje,m,,Chewa,,,,,,,,"Means ""stranger"" in Chichewa."
Achak,m,,Siksika|Algonquin,,,,,,,,Variant of Achachak.
Achala,f,"अचल(Hindi, Sanskrit)",Indian|Sanskrit,a-CHU-la(Indian),,,,,,,"Derived from Sanskrit achala ""constant; unceasing"" and ""the earth""."
Achali,,אַחְלָֽי(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Variant transcription of Ahlai.This transcription is used in The Compete Jewish Bible, Hebrew Names Version, and Orthodox Jewish Bible."
Achall,f,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Achall, daughter of Cairbre Nia Fer, king of Tara, and his wife Fedelm Noíchrothach, is a minor character from the Ulster Cycle of Irish mythology. After her brother Erc was killed by Conall Cernach, she died of grief on a hill near Tara, which was named Achall after her."
