Acheflour,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"Arthur's sister and Perceval's mother in the Middle English Sir Perceval of Galles.Her husband, also named Perceval, was slain by the Red Knight, leading Acheflour to raise Perceval ignorant of war and knighthood so that he might avoid the same fate. Eventually, Perceval left for Arthur's court. Acheflour went insane when she mistakenly thought Perceval had been killed. At the end of the romance, however-and in contrast to other Perceval romances in which his mother dies-Perceval and Acheflour are joyously reunited and Acheflour regains her sanity.Her name is probably a corruption of Blancheflour."
Acheflow,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"Variant of Acheflour, which is probably a corruption of Blancheflour (see Blanchefleur) meaning ""white flower"" in Old French. In the Middle English romance 'Sir Perceval of Galles', Acheflour was the sister of King Arthur and mother of Perceval."
