Acidusa,f,Ἀκίδουσα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀκίς (akis) meaning ""pointed object; barb, arrow"". This was the name of the wife of Scamander, whom he named the well of Boeotia after."
