Adabell,f,,English,,,,,,,,Variant of Adabel.
Adabella,f,,"English (Modern, Rare)",/æd.ə.ˈbɛl.ə/,,,,,,,Combination of Ada 1 and Bella.
Adabelle,f,,English (American),,,,,,,,Variant of Adabel.
Adacia,f,,"English (American, Rare)",ə-DAY-shə(American English),,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. This name may possibly be a combination of the name Ada 1 with any feminine name ending in -cia, such as Acacia, Alicia, Felicia and Patricia."
Adad-guppi,f,,Babylonian,,,,,,,,"Means ""Adad has saved"", possibly deriving from the Old Akkadian element gamalum (""to save""). Name borne by a prominent priestess of the moon god Sin."
Adaego,f,,Igbo,Ed-a-go,,,,,,,"Means ""daughter of money"" in Igbo."
Adael,,"אַדָאֵל, עֲדָאֵל(Hebrew)",Hebrew (Rare),/a.da.ˈʔel/,,,,,,,"Means ""adornment of god, god is eternal, god's ornament"", from עָדָה (ʿaḏa) ""to adorn, to pass by"" combined with אֵל (ʾel) ""god"".According to the Social Security Administration, at least 325 boys had this name between 2002 and 2021.A famous bearer of this name is Adael Alexander Amador (2003-)."
Adaela,f,,"American (Rare, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Variant of Adela.
Adaelia,f,,Spanish (Mexican),,,,,,,,Not available.
Adaem,m,,Medieval Dutch,/a.ˈdaːm/|/ɑ.ˈdaːm/,,,,,,,"Medieval Dutch form of Adam via its latinized form Adamus, as is indicated by the pronunciation of both names."
Adaer,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,Possibly a variant of Adair.
Adaezennaya,f,,Igbo,,,,,,,,Means “princess” in Igbo.
Adagio,m,,"English (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From the Italian adagio meaning ""slowly, at ease"", a word to indicate a musical composition should be played slowly."
Adagonda,f,,Dutch,ah-dah-KHAWN-dah,,,,,,,Variant of Adelgonda.
Adaheli,,,New World Mythology,,,,,,,,The Venezuelan Carib personification of the Sun.
Adahlia,f,,"English (Modern, Rare)",ə-DAH-lee-ə,,,,,,,"Either a variant of Adalia, or a combination of the prefix a with Dahlia."
Adai,m,阿台(Chinese)|Адай(Mongolian Cyrillic),History,,,,,,,,"This is the name of Adai Khan, a khagan of the Northern Yuan dynasty who ruled from 1425 to 1438."
Adaia,f,,Hebrew|Spanish,,,,,,,,Hebrew variant and Spanish form of Adaiah.
Adaiha,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,Not available.
Adailson,m,,Portuguese (Brazilian),,,,,,,,Probably a variant of Adeilson.
Adailton,m,,Portuguese (Brazilian),,,,,,,,Not available.
