Adamanteia,f,,Greek Mythology (?),,,,,,,,"Apparently derived from Greek ἀδάμαντος (adamantos) meaning ""unbreakable, inflexible"" (compare Adamantia). The 1st-century BC Roman writer Hyginus called the nymph Amaltheia by this name in his Fabulae (139)."
