Adekagagwaa,m,,Iroquois,ah-deh-kah-GAH-gwah(Iroquoian),,,,,,,"Adekagagwaa is the name of the Iroquois Spirit of Summer. According to myth, Adekagagwaa oversees other weather gods, including Gǎ-oh (wind), Hé-no (thunder), and Gohone (winter), and departs for southern skies during winter, leaving behind a ""sleep spirit."""
