Adinda,f,,Indonesian|Dutch,/a.ˈdin.da/(Indonesian),,,,,,,"From an honorific term of address for a younger sibling, derived from Indonesian adik meaning ""younger sibling"" combined with the respectful suffix -anda. As a Dutch name its use is likely influenced by the story ""Saïdjah and Adinda"" in the 1860 novel Max Havelaar by Dutch author Eduard Douwes Dekker (1820-1887), also known as Multatuli."
