Agasias,m,Ἀγασίας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/a.ɡa.sí.aːs/(Attic Greek)|/a.ɣa.ˈsi.as/(Koine Greek)|/a.ˈɡa.si.aːs/(Classical Latin),,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαστός (agastos) meaning ""admirable""."
Agasidamos,m,"Ἀγασίδαμος, Ἀγασίδημος(Doric Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαστός (agastos) meaning ""admirable"" and δᾶμος (damos) meaning ""the people"", a Doric Greek variant of δῆμος (demos)."
Agasigratis,f,Ἀγασιγράτις(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαστός (agastos) meaning ""admirable"" and an uncertain second element, possibly γράτις (gratis) meaning ""grass, green fodder""."
