Agathanor,m,Ἀγαθάνωρ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""good man"", derived from the Greek adjective ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" combined with the Greek noun ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man""."
Agatharche,f,Ἀγαθάρχη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Agatharchos.
Agatharchides,m,Ἀγαθαρχίδης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Agatharchos"" in Greek, derived from the name Agatharchos combined with the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).A notable bearer of this name was the Greek historian and geographer Agatharchides of Cnidus (2nd century BC)."
Agatharchos,m,Ἀγάθαρχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"". The second element is either derived from Greek ἀρχός (archos) ""master"" or from Greek ἀρχή (arche) ""origin, source""."
Agatharchus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agatharchos.
Agatharkhos,m,Ἀγάθαρχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Greek Ἀγάθαρχος (see Agatharchos).
Agathemeris,f,Ἀγαθημερίς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Probably means ""of good days, one who brings lucky days"", derived from Ancient Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good, noble, fortunate"" combined with ἡμέρα (hemera) meaning ""day"". Compare the word ἀγαθήμερος (agathemeros) meaning ""of good days, of lucky days"". Alternatively, the second element could derive from ἥμερος (hemeros) meaning ""civilized, gentle""."
Agathemeros,m,Ἀγαθήμερος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""good day"" in Ancient Greek, a masculine form of Agathemeris."
Agathenor,m,Ἀγαθήνωρ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Variant of Agathanor.
Agathestrate,f,Ἀγαθεστράτη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and στρατός (stratos) meaning ""army""."
Agathetyche,f,Ἀγαθητύχη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""good fortune"", from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and τύχη (tyche) meaning ""fortune, chance, fate""."
Agathetychos,m,Ἀγαθήτυχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Masculine form of Agathetyche.
Agathia,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,Variant of Agatha.
Agathias,m,Ἀγαθίας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" (see Agathon). It was borne by a 6th-century Greek historian and poet, who chronicled the reign of Byzantine emperor Justinian I."
Agathie,f,Αγαθή(Greek),"Greek (Rare)|Greek (Cypriot, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant transliteration of Αγαθή (see Agathi and Agathy).
