Agathios,m,Ἀγάθιος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good""."
Agathippe,f,Ἀγαθίππη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and ἵππος (hippos) meaning ""horse"". This was the name of a lover of Apollo."
Agathippos,m,Ἀγάθιππος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Masculine form of Agathippe.
Agathius,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agathios.
Agatho,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History,,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agathon. This name was borne by a 7th-century pope.
Agathoboule,f,Ἀγαθοβούλη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Agathoboulos.
Agathoboulos,m,Ἀγαθόβουλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" combined with the Greek verb βούλομαι (boulomai) meaning ""to will, to wish, to prefer"". Also compare the Greek noun βουλή (boule) meaning ""will, determination"" as well as ""counsel, advice"" and the Greek verb βουλεύω (bouleuo) meaning ""to take counsel, to deliberate""."
Agathobulus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agathoboulos. This was the name of a Cynic philosopher from the 2nd century AD.
Agathoclea,f,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agathokleia. This was the name of the favourite mistress of the Egyptian Greek pharaoh Ptolemy IV Philopator (3rd century BC).
Agathocleia,f,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Variant latinization of Agathokleia, because its proper (and most common) latinized form is Agathoclea."
Agathoclia,f,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Variant latinization of Agathokleia, because its proper (and most common) latinized form is Agathoclea.This was the name of a Roman saint from Hispania, who died around 230 AD."
Agathoclie,f,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,French form of Agathokleia.
Agathodaemon,m,Ἀγαθοδαίμων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Ἀγαθοδαίμων (Agathodaimon) meaning ""noble spirit"", from ἀγαθὸς (agathos) ""good, noble"" and δαίμων (daimon) ""spirit"".In Greek mythology he was the daemon, or presiding spirit, of the vineyards and grain fields, and a personal companion spirit, ensuring good luck, health, and wisdom. In Ptolemaic Egypt he was associated with the Egyptian god of fate Shai. He was depicted as a serpent or as a young man holding a cornucopia and a bowl in one hand and a poppy and an ear of grain in the other. The agathodaemon was later adapted into a general daemon of Fortuna, particularly of the continued abundance of a family's good food and drink. Pausanias conjectured that the name was a mere epithet of Zeus."
Agathodika,f,Ἀγαθοδίκα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and δίκη (dike) meaning ""justice, custom, order""."
Agathodoros,m,Ἀγαθόδωρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Ancient Greek name meaning ""good gift"" with the elements ἀγαθὸς (agathos) ""good"" and δῶρον (doron) ""gift"". In turn, the name means “gifted person, good gift, donor of goods.”"
Agathodorus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Agathodoros. Agathodorus was an early Christian martyr in Pergamon, Asia Minor."
Agathokleia,f,Αγαθόκλεια(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|History,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Agathokles. This name was borne by an Indo-Greek queen from the 2nd century BC.
Agathoklis,m,Αγαθοκλής(Greek),Greek,a-gah-to-KLEES,,,,,,,Modern Greek spelling of Agathokles.
Agathomenes,m,Ἀγαθομένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and an uncertain second element; possibly μένος (menos) meaning ""mind, strength, courage"" or μένω (meno) meaning ""to stay, wait, remain""."
Agathomoros,m,Ἀγαθόμορος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθὸς (agathos) meaning ""good"" and μόρος (moros) meaning ""fate, destiny; doom""."
Agathonica,f,,Late Greek (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latin variant of Agathonice, which is the latinized form of the Greek given name Agathonike. This name was borne by Agathonica of Pergamus, a martyr and saint from the 3rd century AD."
Agathonice,f,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Agathonike. This name was borne by an early Christian saint from Thyatira, who was either martyred with her brother Papylus and a companion named Carpus, or committed suicide after Carpus and Papylus were tortured and sacrificed by pagans."
Agathonicus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Agathonikos. This name was borne by saint Agathonicus of Nicomedia (3rd century AD).
Agathonike,f,Ἀγαθονίκη(Ancient Greek),Late Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Agathonikos. This name was borne by an early Christian saint from Thyatira, who was either martyred with her brother Papylus and a companion named Carpus, or committed suicide after Carpus and Papylus were tortured and sacrificed by pagans."
Agathoniki,f,Αγαθονίκη(Greek),Greek,,,,,,,,Modern Greek form of Agathonike.
Agathonikos,m,Ἀγαθόνικος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" combined with the Greek noun νίκη (nike) meaning ""victory""."
Agathonique,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,French form of Agathonikos (see Agathonicus).
Agathonymos,m,Ἀγαθώνυμος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""of good name, of honourable name"", derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and ὄνυμα (onyma) meaning ""name""."
Agathophanes,m,Ἀγαθοφάνης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and φανής (phanes) meaning ""appearing, seeming""."
Agathopheron,m,Ἀγαθοφέρων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and φέρω (phero) meaning ""to bring, to carry, to bear""."
Agathopherousa,f,Ἀγαθοφέρουσα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Agathopheron.
Agathophon,m,Ἀγαθοφῶν(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and φωνή (phone) meaning ""voice""."
Agathophoros,m,Ἀγαθοφόρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""bearing good tidings, bringing good news"" in Greek, derived from ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and φέρω (phero) meaning ""to bring, to carry, to bear""."
Agathopoleia,f,Ἀγαθοπόλεια(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Agathopolis.
Agathopolis,m,Ἀγαθόπολις(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and πόλις (polis) meaning ""city""."
Agathopus,m,Ἀγαθόπους(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and πούς (pous) meaning ""foot""."
Agathos,m,,Greek (?),AHG-UH-THOS,,,,,,,"Masculine form of ""Agatha""."
Agathostratos,m,Ἀγαθόστρατος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀγαθός (agathos) meaning ""good"" and στρατός (stratos) meaning ""army""."
