Agesilaos,m,Ἀγησίλαος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is either derived from Greek ἆγειν (agein) meaning ""to carry, to fetch"" or from Greek ἄγω (ago) ""to guide, to lead"" (also see Agis). The second element is derived from Greek λαός (laos) meaning ""(the) people""."
