Agnellus,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin agnus ""lamb"" and the diminutive suffix -ellus. Agnellus of Naples (535 - 596) was a Basilian monk and later Augustinian friar. He is venerated as a saint by the Catholic Church, with a feast day on 14 December, the date of his death."
