Agoes,m,,Indonesian,/ˈa.ɡʊs/,,,,,,,Older spelling of Agus influenced by Dutch orthography.
Agofredus,m,,Frankish (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of a Frankish name derived from the elements aggju meaning ""blade"" and friþu meaning ""peace"". This was the name of an 8th-century French saint, also known as Aifroy, who served as a Benedictine monk and abbot. He was the brother of Saint Leutfridus."
Agofroy,m,,Medieval French|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,French form of Agofredus.
