Ahijah,m,אֲחִיָּה(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""brother of Yahweh"" in Hebrew, derived from אָח (ʾaḥ) meaning ""brother"" and יָהּ (yah) referring to the Hebrew God. In the Old Testament, this was the name of several characters, including a Levite prophet in Shiloh who foretold Jeroboam that he would be king."
