Ahinadab,m,אחינדב(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical Hebrew,,,,,,,,"Meaning, ""My Brother Is Noble."" Son of Iddo, is one of the twelve commissariat officers appointed by Solomon in so many districts of his kingdom to raise supplies by monthly rotation for his household. He was appointed to the district of Mahanaim (1 Kings 4:14), east of Jordan."
