Ahoeitu,m,,Polynesian Mythology|Tongan,ah-ho-ay-too,,,,,,,"Means ""day god; day has dawned; feast day"" in Tongan. Ahoeitu was the first king of the Tu'i Tonga dynasty in Tongan mythology. The god Eitumatupua climbed down from the sky on a great tree, and took a worm descendant, Ilaheva, as his wife. Returning to the sky, the god left the woman and her child, Ahoeitu, on the Earth."
