Aitu,,,Polynesian Mythology|Samoan,IE-too,,,,,,,"Means ""ghost"" and ""spirit"" in Māori, Samoan, Tongan and Tahitian. In Polynesian mythology Aitu are lesser gods of Atua ""gods"". In Māori aitu also refers to ""sickness, calamity"" and ""malevolent spirit"". Aitu is a cognate of Filipino anito and Indonesian antu."
