Akasha,f,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Used by author Anne Rice for a character in her 'Vampire Chronicles' series - introduced in the second novel, 'The Vampire Lestat' (1985) - where it belongs to a pre-Egyptian queen who becomes the first vampire and 'mother' of all vampires. Akasha was portrayed by Aaliyah in the 2002 movie 'Queen of the Damned'. Rice possibly intended the name to appear derived from the identical Sanskrit word आकाश (ākāśa) meaning ""open space, sky, ether, quintessence""."
