Akatamachetos,m,Ἀκαταμάχητος(Ancient Greek),Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἀκαταμάχητος (akatamachetos) meaning ""unconquerable"", which consists of the Greek negative prefix ἀ (a) and the Greek verb καταμάχομαι (katamachomai) meaning ""to conquer, to subdue by fighting"".Since medieval times (as early as the 11th century), Akatamachetos is also used as an epithet for the Virgin Mary."
Akatauira,m,,Cook Islands Māori,,,,,,,,"Means ""to observe and mark"". This is the name of a star important for its use in navigation."
Akatendeka,,,Shona,A-ka-te-nde-ka,,,,,,,"Meaning ""one who is faithful"", deriving from the verb kutendeka."
Akates,m,,Finnish (Rare),AH-kah-tehs,,,,,,,Variant of Achates.
Akatius,m,,Finnish (Rare),AH-ka-tyus,,,,,,,Finnish form of Achatius.
Akatosh,m,,Popular Culture,,,,,,,,"In the popular video game series 'The Elder Scrolls', Akatosh is the chief deity of the Nine Divines (the pantheon of gods in the game). He is generally considered to be the first of the Gods to form in the Beginning Place; after his establishment, other spirits found the process of being easier and the various pantheons of the world emerged. He embodies the qualities of endurance, invincibility, and everlasting legitimacy while promoting the virtues of duty, service, and obedience. His avatar is a dragon, and he is often called the Dragon God of Time, with Alduin sometimes being mistaken as an aspect of him. Akatosh is thought to be the father of all dragons, and the dragons' leader Alduin was titled ""First-Born of Akatosh""."
Ákãtsiaĸ,m,,Greenlandic,,,,,,,,"Means ""beautiful, precious uncle (father's brother)"" from Greenlandic Áka and -tsiaq ""beautiful, precious""."
Akatsuki,,"暁, 暁月, 緋月, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あかつき(Japanese Hiragana)|アカツキ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare)|Popular Culture,[à.ká.t͡sɨ̥̀ᵝ.kʲì](Japanese),,,,,,,"From 暁 (akatsuki) meaning ""dawn, daybreak,"" shifted from earlier akatoki, made up of 明 (aka) meaning ""bright"" and 時 (toki) meaning ""time.""It can also be combined with 月 (tsuki) meaning ""moon."" Alternatively, the first kanji can be substituted with one that can be read as aka, e.g. 緋 meaning ""scarlet.""One bearer of this name was I-Novel author Akatsuki Kambayashi (上林 暁), born Iwaki Tokuhiro (徳廣 巌城) (1902-1980).This name is rarely used."
Akau,m,,Tongan,,,,,,,,"Means ""tree, plant, timber"" in Tongan."
Akawel,m,,Berber,,,,,,,,"Means ""the black"" in Amazigh."
