Akerbeltz,m,,Basque Mythology,a-ker-behlts,,,,,,,"Literally meaning “Black goat” in Basque, this name belongs to a spirit/deity in Basque mythology. Usually depicted as a billy goat, the spirit was earlier seen as pagan deity of the protection of animals and houses. Later on, Akerbeltz was demonized by Christianity as a living image of the devil."
