Albania,f,,English,al-BAY-nee-ə,,,,,,,"From the name of the country in the Balkans, as well as various other places, perhaps ultimately from a pre-Indo-European word *alb meaning ""hill"" or from the Indo-European root *alb ""white"" (see Albus).It can also be used as an elaboration of Alba (the Scottish Gaelic name for Scotland) or a feminine form of Alban."
