Alectryon,m,Ἀλεκτρυών(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/a.lek.try.ɔ̌ːn/(Attic Greek)|/a.lek.try.ˈon/(Koine Greek)|/a.lek.tri.ˈon/(Constantinopolitan Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""rooster, cock, chicken"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, this was the name of a soldier who failed to alert Ares of Helios’s approach while guarding his door, causing the god’s affair with Aphrodite to be discovered. In anger, Ares transformed the youth into a rooster, which thereafter always announced the rising sun."
