Alemonia,f,,Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Perhaps related to Greek ἀλήμων (ălēmon) ""a wanderer, rover"". In Roman mythology, Alemona or Alemonia was a minor, tutelary goddess of the fetus, the entity responsible for feeding the unborn child (i.e., nourishing growth in utero)."
