Alexianna,f,Αλεξιάννα(Greek),English (Rare)|Greek (Rare),,,,,,,,"Variant of Alexiana. As a modern Greek name, it is a combination of Alexia and Anna."
Alexiano,m,,"Spanish (Latin American, Rare)|Portuguese (Brazilian, Rare)|Italian (Rare)",,,,,,,,Spanish and Portuguese form of Alexian.
Alexianus,m,,Late Roman,,,,,,,,Extended form of Alexius.
Alexiares,m,Ἀλεξιάρης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἀλεξιάρης (alexiares), the masculine form of ἀλεξιάρη (alexiare) meaning ""she that guards from death and ruin"". It consists of ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend, to help"" combined with ἀρή (are) meaning ""bane, ruin"". Also compare the name of the Greek war god Ares, which is thought to be etymologically related.In Greek mythology, this was the name of one of the divine sons of the Greek hero Herakles and the goddess Hebe, to whom he was wed following his apotheosis. Alexiares and his brother Anicetus may have been considered gatekeepers of Olympus, alongside their father."
Alexibia,f,Ἀλεξιβία(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Alexibios.
Alexibios,m,Ἀλεξίβιος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek verb ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend"" as well as ""to help"" combined with either the Greek noun βία (bia) meaning ""bodily strength, force"" or the Greek noun βίος (bios) meaning ""life"".This name was borne by an Olympic victor from 312 BC."
Alexibius,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Alexibios. This name was borne by an Olympic victor from 312 BC.
Alexiboulos,m,Ἀλεξίβουλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend, to help"" and βουλή (boule) meaning ""counsel, advice"" as well as ""will, determination"".Also compare the Greek verbs βουλεύω (bouleuo) meaning ""to take counsel, to deliberate"" and βούλομαι (boulomai) meaning ""to will, to wish, to prefer""."
Alexicacus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Alexikakos.This was an epithet of the Greek hero Herakles. It was also applied to several Greek gods, such as Zeus, Hermes and Apollo. The latter was worshipped in Athens as Apollo Alexicacus, because as the god of (among others) disease and medicine, he had been credited with stopping the disastrous Plague of Athens (5th century BC)."
Alexicles,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Alexikles. This was the name of an Athenian general from the 5th century BC.
Alexicrates,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Alexikrates. This was the name of a Pythagorean philosopher, who lived around the turn of the 1st century AD."
Alexidamos,m,Ἀλεξίδαμος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend, to help"" and δᾶμος (damos), the Doric Greek form of (demos) ""the people"".Also compare the name Alexidemos, which is closely related."
Alexidamus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Alexidamos.
Alexideios,m,"Ἀλεξιδήϊος, Ἀλεξιδήιος(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend, to help"" and δήϊος (deios) meaning ""hostile, destructive"" as well as ""unhappy, wretched"", which is related to δηϊόω (deioo) meaning ""to slay, to cut down"" (see Deianeira)."
Alexidemos,m,Ἀλεξίδημος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek verb ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend"" as well as ""to help"" combined with the Greek noun δῆμος (demos) meaning ""the people""."
Alexidemus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Alexidemos.
Alexidike,f,Ἀλεξιδίκη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Alexidikos.
Alexidikos,m,Ἀλεξίδικος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἀλέξω (alexo) meaning ""to defend, to help"" and δίκη (dike) meaning ""justice, judgement"" as well as ""custom, usage""."
Alexie,f,,"English|Romanian|Louisiana Creole|History (Ecclesiastical)|French (Modern)|French (Belgian, Modern)",/a.lɛk.si/(French),,,,,,,Diminutive of Alexandra.
Alexiea,f,,Obscure,,,,,,,,Not available.
