Alkhaabaatar,m,Алхаабаатар(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Probably from Mongolian алхаа (alkhaa) meaning ""step"" and баатар (baatar) meaning ""hero""."
Alkhansa,f,الخنساء(Arabic),Arabic (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Arabic الخنساء (al-Khansā), which is said to mean ""the snub-nosed"" or ""the gazelle"". This was the nickname of a 7th-century Arab poet who was a companion of the Prophet Muhammad. Her birth name was Tumāḍir bint ‛Amr.This name appears to be very rare; as an Arabic feminine name, the form Khansa (without the definite article al-) is given more frequently."
