Altaira,f,,"English (Modern, Rare)|Spanish (Latin American, Modern, Rare)|Popular Culture",,,,,,,,"The name of a character in the classic 1956 science fiction film, Forbidden Planet. Altaira Morbius was the daughter of the scientist and space voyager Dr. Edward Morbius. The name Altaira is derived from Altair, the brightest star in the constellation of the Eagle (Aquila)."
Altaluna,f,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Italian alta, the feminine form of the adjective alto, meaning ""high; deep; big; towering; elevated"" and, when used in a poetic context, ""grand; sublime; noble"" and luna ""moon"".A known bearer of this name was Altaluna della Scala, daughter of Mastino II della Scala, a 14th-cenutry lord of Verona, sister of Viridis and wife of Louis V, Duke of Bavaria.Whether Altalune, the name Uma Thurman gave her daughter born in 2012, is a medieval variant of this name, is still debated."
