Alvan,m,עַלְוָן(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical|English (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Hebrew verb עָלָה ('alah) meaning ""to ascend, to rise"". Also compare the related name Alvah. In the Old Testament (Genesis 36:23), Alvan is the eldest son of Shobal and a descendant of Seir the Horite; in 1 Chronicles 1:40, he is called Alian."
