Amat al-Razzak,f,أمة الرزاق(Arabic),Arabic,,,,,,,,"Means ""maidservant of the all-provider"" from Arabic أمة ال (amat al) meaning ""maidservant of the"" and رزاق (razzāq) ""provider, sustainer""."
Amatasana,f,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"Medieval Italian name composed of Latin amata ""loved"" (compare Amata) and sana ""healthy""."
