Amaymon,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly from Aramaic מָמוֹנָא (māmōnā) meaning ""money, wealth, riches"" or from a Greek root meaning ""terrible violence and vehemence"". This is the name of a demon who appears in numerous works on demonology, including the 17th-century grimoire The Lesser Key of Solomon (author unknown) and the Pseudomonarchia Daemonum (1563) by Dutch physician Johann Weyer. He is said to be the only being with power over the demon Asmodeus."
