Amba,f,अम्बा(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈɐm.bɑː/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""mother"" in Sanskrit. This is the name of a princess of the Kashi kingdom in the Hindu epic the Mahabharata. After being rejected by her beloved, Shalva, as well by as Bhishma, she is reborn as Shikhandi in her next life."
