Ambiorix,m,,Old Celtic|History,,,,,,,,"Continental Celtic name, derived from Celtic ambio ""enclosure"" (or ambi ""around, about"" or ambitio ""rich"") combined with Celtic rix ""king."" This was the name of one of the two kings of a Gaulish tribe called the Eburones, who was famous for revolting against Julius Caesar in 54 BC (which eventually led to the extermination of the Eburones)."
