Amelius,m,,Medieval Dutch|Dutch (Rare),/aː.ˈmeː.li.jʏs/(Dutch),,,,,,,"Medieval Dutch variant of Aemilius (see Emil).However, since other medieval variants (Amilius and Emilius) are more faithful to the original, it seems more likely that this name was originally a latinized short form of masculine Germanic names that contain the element amal meaning ""unceasing, vigorous, brave"" (in battle). Such names often became Amel- in Dutch, e.g. Amelryck. As such, it is certainly feasible that the latinized Germanic name Amelius became increasingly conflated with Aemilius and its variant Amilius over time, to the point that its Germanic origin was eventually forced into the background.Also compare Amelia, which has regularly been confused with Aemilia and Emilia."
