Amemar,m,אַמֵּימָר(Ancient Hebrew),Ancient Aramaic,,,,,,,,"Formed from the personal name Ammi (which means ""my people"" from Hebrew עַם (ʿam) ""people, nation, kinsman"" and the suffix י (i) ""my"") and the title מַר (mar) meaning ""master"". This was the name of a Babylonian rabbi of the 5th and 6th centuries."
