Amoghasiddhi,m,अमोघसिद्धि(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/ɐ.ˈmoː.ɡʱɐ.s̪id̪.d̪ʱi/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""unfailing success"" from Sanskrit अमोघ (amogha) meaning ""unfailing, infallible"" and सिद्धि (siddhi) meaning ""accomplishment, success, attainment"". In the Mahayana and Vajrayana Buddhist traditions this is the name of a buddha associated with wisdom, the promotion of the Buddhist path and the destruction of envy and evil."
