Amon,m,"亜門, 阿門(Japanese Kanji)|あもん(Japanese Hiragana)|アモン(Japanese Katakana)|อมร(Thai)|אָמוֹן, אָמֹן(Ancient Hebrew)|Ἀμών(Ancient Greek)","Japanese|Thai|Biblical Hebrew|Biblical Greek|Biblical|Biblical Italian|Dutch|English (African)|English (American, Archaic)|French (Modern)|Franco-Provençal|German (Rare)",AH-MON|/ʔa˨˩.ˈmɔːn˧/|/ˈa.mɔn/(German),,,,,,,"This name combines 亜 (a, tsu.gu) meaning ""Asia, come after, rank next"" or 阿 (a, o, omone.ru, kuma) meaning ""corner, flatter, nook"" with 門 (mon, kado, to) meaning ""gate.""As a word, Amon (亜門) refers to a sub-phylum or a biological subdivision.One bearer of this name is stage director and choreographer Amon Miyamoto (宮本 亜門) (1958-)."
