Amrapali,f,"आम्रपाली(Sanskrit, Hindi, Marathi)",Sanskrit|Indian|Marathi,,,,,,,,"Means ""mango leaves"", from Sanskrit आम्र (āmra) meaning ""mango"" and पल्लव (pallava) meaning ""bud, young leaf, sprout"". This was the name of a famous courtesan in ancient India, known for becoming a devotee of the Buddha and gifting him her mango groves to host sermons in."
