Amurelle,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"The wife of Blandukors, a nobleman who hosted Gawain during one of his adventures in Heinrich von dem Türlin’s Diu Crône.She had a daughter named Sgaipegaz."
Amurfina,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"Daughter of Lord Laniure of Serre and Ansgien, sister of Sgoidamur, and eventual wife of Gawain in Heinrich's Diu Crone. When her father died, Amurfina took possession of a magic bridle that controlled the family fortune, thus disinheriting her sister. In the dispute, both of them solicited Gawain as their champion. While Gawain was visiting her castle, her servant Aclamet served him a love potion which caused him to fall madly in love with Amurfina. They married and Gawain became the lord of Serre. Amurfina's uncle, Gansguoter, was Arthur's step- father. A character of similar nature appears unnamed in La Mule sans Frein."
Amurfine,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"Daughter of Lord Laniure of Serre and Ansgien, sister of Sgoidamur, and eventual wife of Gawain in Heinrich’s Diu Crône.When her father died, she took possession of a magic bridle that controlled the family fortune, thus disinheriting her sister. In the dispute, both of them solicited Gawain as their champion.While Gawain was visiting her castle, her servant Aclamet served him a love potion which caused him to fall madly in love with Amurfine. They married and Gawain became the lord of Serre. Amurfine’s uncle, Gansguoter, was Arthur’s step-father.A character of similar nature appears unnamed in La Mule sans Frein."
Amurkhan,m,Амурхан(Ossetian),Ossetian|Ingush,,,,,,,,Ossetian and Ingush form of Amirkhan.
Amuro,m,,Japanese (?)|Popular Culture,,,,,,,,Not available.
Amusa,f,,Southern African,,,,,,,,It is a Silozi or Lozi Name. Silozi or Lozi is a Zambian language.
Amusan,m,,Yoruba,,,,,,,,"Means ""one who holds the whip"" in Yoruba, from mú ""to hold, grasp"" and ìṣán, a kind of whip or cane used in Egúngún (or Masquerade) festivals. Usually given to children born holding the umbilical cord, with a membrane ""mask"" covering their head, or the third-born of triplets."
Amusko,m,,Medieval Basque,ah-MUS-koh,,,,,,,"Common Basque name in the middle ages. It possibly originates from the Basque toponyms Muskitz or Muskiz. It has been documented mainly in Navarre, as early as the 10th century."
Amustan,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"a variant of Amustans, the chaplain of King Leodegan of Carmelide (Leodegrance) (Guinevere’s father) in the Vulgate romances."
Amustans,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"The chaplain of King Leodegan of Carmelide (Leodegrance) (Guinevere’s father) in the Vulgate romances. He married Arthur and Guinevere and accompanied them to Arthur’s court, where he continued his service as chaplain. He later became a hermit, but he helped Arthur during the False Guinevere episode by identifying the real Guinevere.Since he knew Guinevere in her childhood and was instrumental, by scolding Arthur and helping get deathbed confessions from Genievre and Bertholai, in reconciling Arthur with Guenevere after Genievre’s last attempt to supplant her half-sister.In Lancelot of the Laik he is called Amytans."
Amustant,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"a variant of Amustans, the chaplain of King Leodegan of Carmelide (Leodegrance) (Guinevere’s father) in the Vulgate romances."
Amutenya,m,,Ovambo,,,,,,,,"Means ""midday"" in Ovambo. This name is traditionally given to children born during the afternoon."
