Anabia,f,انابیہ(Urdu),"Urdu (Modern)|Indian (Muslim, Modern)",,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly an invented name, popularly associated with Arabic أناب (ʾanāba) meaning ""to return"" (a word found in the Quran, which is also the source of Muniba and Munib). Furthermore, many websites falsely claim that this name means ""door of heaven"", though none of the doors of Paradise in Islam have a name similar to this.This was used for the title character of the 2016 Pakistani television series Anabia or Anabiya, played by actress Neelam Muneer."
