Anactoria,f,Ἀνακτορία(Ancient Greek),"Literature|Greek Mythology (Latinized, ?)|Ancient Greek (Latinized, ?)",,,,,,,,"Latinized form of the Greek Ἀνακτορία (Anaktoria), derived from ἀνακτόρῐος (anaktorios) ""royal"", literally ""belonging to a king, a lord"" from ἀνάκτωρ (anaktor) ""lord"", from ἄναξ (anax) ""lord"". This name was mentioned in a poem by the 7th-century BC lyric poet Sappho as a female lover of hers."
