Anaideia,f,Ἀναίδεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"From Greek ἀναίδεια (anaideia) meaning ""shamelessness"", derived from ἀν- (an-) ""without"" (alternative form of the negative prefix ἀ- (a-) used before a vowel) combined with αἰδώς (aidos) ""shame, decency, regard for others, respect, reverence"". In Greek mythology, Anaideia was the personification of shamelessness, ruthlessness and unforgiveness. She was a companion of Hybris. Her opposite was Eleos, the personification of mercy."
