Andromedes,m,"Ἀνδρομέδης, Ἀνδρομήδης(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"In ancient Greek, there are two possible ways to write this name, and with each way the meaning is different.When written as Ἀνδρομέδης, this name is the masculine form of Andromeda. But when written as Ἀνδρομήδης, the name basically means ""a man's plan"" or even ""to think like a man"", derived from Greek ἀνδρός (andros) meaning ""of a man"" combined with the Greek verb μήδομαι (medomai) meaning ""to think, to plan, to plot"".In Greek mythology, Andromedes is one of the suitors of Penelope."
