Angosto,f,,"Spanish (European, Rare)",/ãŋ.ˈɡos.t̪o/(Spanish),,,,,,,"Taken from the title of the Virgin Mary Nuestra Señora de Angosto ""Our Lady of Angosto"". Angosto is a former place name meaning ""narrow"" in Spanish, possibly referring to the width of a river. According to folk legend, in 1089, a local shepherd rescued a carving of the Virgin from the Tumecillo River (located in the Spanish province of Álava)."
