Ankayarkanni,f,அங்கயற்கண்ணி(Tamil),Tamil,ANG-AYAR-KANN-NI,,,,,,,"Alternate transcription of Tamil அங்கயற்கண்ணி (see Angayarkanni).-------------------------------------Name which means ""a girl/woman who has fish-like eyes"" in Tamil. Derived from Tamil words அம் (am) ""like"", கயல் (kayal) ""fish"", கண்ணி (kanni) ""eye of a girl/woman"". அம் + கயல் + கண்ணி - அங்கயற்கண்ணி. This is the native name of the famous goddess in Madurai in Tamil Nadu, South India, which is now known as Minakshi Temple."
