Antão,m,,Portuguese|Portuguese (Brazilian),"/ɐ̃.ˈtɐ̃w̃/(Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese)",,,,,,,"Portuguese form of Antonius.In Portuguese, Santo Antão is the common name of Saint Anthony the Great, or Saint Anthony of Egypt. In turn, the medieval Saint Anthony of Padua (born in Portugal, and who took his religious name after that Saint) is known as Santo António. The popularity of the latter saint in Portugal and in other countries means that this form of the name has been eclipsed by António."
