Anysia,f,Άνυσία(Greek),History (Ecclesiastical),/a.ny.ˈsi.a/(Koine Greek)|/ə.ˈni.ʃi.ə/(English),,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek ἄνυσις (anusis) ""fulfillment, accomplishment"", ultimately from άνύω (anúō) (""to accomplish, to cause""). Saint Anysia of Salonika was a Christian virgin and martyr of the 4th century."
