Anyte,f,Ἀνύτη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Anytos. Anyte of Tegea was a 3rd-century BC Arcadian poet, admired by her contemporaries and later generations for her charming epigrams and epitaphs."
Anytos,m,Ἄνυτος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἁνύτω (anyto), the Attic form of ἀνύω (anyo), meaning ""to effect, achieve, accomplish, complete"". This was the name of a titan in Greek mythology, said to have raised the goddess Despoine."
