Aozora,,"青空, 蒼空, 碧空, 葵空, 蒼天, 碧天, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あおぞら(Japanese Hiragana)|アオゾラ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Modern),[ä.o̞.zo̞.ɾä],,,,,,,"From 青空 (aozora) meaning ""blue sky.""It can also be written as 蒼空 or 碧空. The first kanji can be changed to 葵, normally read as aoi, which refers to a mallow plant. The second kanji can be substituted with one that has the same or similar meaning(s) to 空, like 天.Nowadays, excluding 葵空, the kanji combinations used for this name are most commonly read as Sora."
