Apollogenes,m,Ἀπολλογένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""born of Apollo"" from the name of the god Apollo combined with Ancient Greek γενής (genes) meaning ""born"". This name was borne by an eponymous archon of Athens, who lived in the 1st century BC."
