Apseudes,,Ἀψευδής(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""truthful, without deceit, sincere"" in Ancient Greek, composed of the negative prefix ἀ (a) combined with ψευδής (pseudes) meaning ""lying, false, untrue"". In Greek mythology, Apseudes was one of the fifty Nereids, sea-nymph daughters of Nereus and the Oceanid Doris. As an Ancient Greek given name, this name was exclusively masculine."
