Araci,f,,Tupi|Brazilian,/a.ɾa.ˈsi/(Brazilian),,,,,,,"Derived from either Tupi arasy ""mother of day"", itself derived from ara ""day"" and sy ""mother; origin, source"", and thus referring to the sun, or from Tupi aracê ""sunrise, daybreak, morning"". In some instances, however, it may also be a contracted form of Araceli."
