Arakiel,m,,Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Means ""earth of God"" or ""land of God"", derived from Aramaic אֲרַק (ʿăraq) meaning ""earth, ground, land"" and Hebrew אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"". The Book of Enoch names him as a fallen angel, one of the 200 Watchers who copulated with human women. Other sources hold him as a holy angel who guides human souls to judgment."
