A-ran,f,"아란(Korean Hangul)|雅蘭, 娥蘭, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/ä.ɾän/,,,,,,,"Combination of an a hanja, like 雅 meaning ""clean, pure"" or 娥 meaning ""pretty, lovely, beautiful,"" and a ran hanja, e.g. 蘭 meaning ""orchid."""
Arán,,,Spanish,/a.ˈɾan/,,,,,,,Spanish form of Aran 3.
Aran,,"アラン(Japanese Katakana)|あらん(Japanese Hiragana)|阿蘭, 安卵, 和蘭, 愛覧, 亜嵐, 愛藍, 愛欄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|อรัญ(Thai)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)|Kurdish|Thai|Basque",A-RAN|/ʔa˨˩.ˈran˧/|[a.ɾãn],,,,,,,"Japanese form of Alan. It can be spelled with Japanese 亜 or 亞 (a) meaning ""second, Asia, sub-"" or 阿 (a) meaning ""nook, corner"" combined with 蘭 (ran) meaning ""orchid"", 藍 (ran) meaning ""indigo"" or 卵 (ran) meaning ""egg, ovum"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Arana,f,"新夏, 新菜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Basque (Rare)|Japanese|Māori|Tagalog,AH-ṘA-NAH|ah-rah-na,,,,,,,Strictly feminine form of Aran.
Arənauuāčī,f,,Persian Mythology|Avestan,,,,,,,,"Avestan name that probably meant ""she who speaks the injustice (to denounce it)"", from arəna- ""injustice"" and ouuāč-ī ""she who speaks"". In Persian mythology this name belonged to a sister or daughter of King Jamshid. According to the 11th-century Shahnameh, she became a wife of Fereydoun and the mother of his youngest but wisest and noblest son: Iraj."
