Aretaeus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Aretaios. A known bearer of this name of Aretaeus of Cappadocia, a Greek physician who lived in the 1st century AD."
Aretaios,m,Ἀρεταῖος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from either Greek ἀρετάω (aretao) ""to thrive, to prosper"" or from Greek ἀρετή (arete) meaning ""goodness, excellence"" as well as ""virtue, skill""."
