Areum,,"아름(Korean Hangul)|雅凛, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean (Modern),/ä.ɾɯm/,,,,,,,"From the first part of adjective 아름답다 (areumdapda) meaning ""beautiful.""On rare occasions, it can also be written with hanja, e.g. combining 雅 (a) meaning ""clean, pure"" with 凛 (reum) meaning ""cold."""
Areum-byeol,f,아름별(Korean Hangul),"Korean (Modern, Rare)",/ä.ɾɯm.bjʌɭ/,,,,,,,Combination of Areum and Byeol.
