Argjend,m,,Albanian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Albanian argjend ""silver; silver thread""."
Argo,m,,Estonian|Javanese,/ˈar.ɡɔ/,,,,,,,"Of uncertain origin and meaning. Theories include a variant of Ardo and a derivation from Argo, the name of the ship used by Jason and the Argonauts (whose name is said to be derived from Greek άργυρος (argyros) ""silver""). The name was first recorded in the early 1960s."
