Arilda,f,,"History (Ecclesiastical)|French (Quebec, Rare)|French (Acadian, Archaic)|Norwegian (Archaic)|Portuguese (Brazilian)|Albanian|American (South, Archaic)|English (American, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Saint Arilda is an obscure female saint from Oldbury-on-Severn in the English county of Gloucestershire who probably lived in the 5th or 6th century. She may have been of either Anglo-Saxon or Welsh origin.
