Arina,f,"アリナ(Japanese Katakana)|ありな(Japanese Hiragana)|亜莉菜, 亜璃菜, 安里奈 愛李奈, 阿理菜, 有菜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|아리나(Korean Hangul)",Japanese|Hungarian|Dutch|Afrikaans|Korean (Rare),A-REE-NA|/a.ɾi.na/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 亜 (a) meaning ""sub-, second, Asia"", 莉 (ri) meaning ""white jasmine"" or 璃 (ri) meaning ""glassy, lapis lazuli"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"". Other combinations of kanji are also possible.Usage of this name is, most likely, influenced by the name Alina."
