Arioldus,m,,Germanic (Latinized)|Theatre,,,,,,,,Probably a variant of Arialdus. This is the name of a character from the 17th-century stage play The Swisser.
Arion,m,"Ἀρίων, Ἀρείων(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology|Albanian,/a.ˈri.on/(Koine Greek)|/ə.ˈraɪ.ən/(English),,,,,,,"Possibly related to Ancient Greek ἀρείων (areion) meaning ""better, worthier, stronger"" (see aristos), or perhaps a patronymic form of the name of the god Ares (compare Areios). This was the name of a semi-legendary Ancient Greek poet and musician from Lesbos, who was supposedly rescued from pirates by a pod of dolphins. It was also the name of an immortal horse of divine origin and incredible speed in Greek mythology, in some accounts gifted with human speech and the power of prophecy."
