Arishia,f,"ありしあ(Japanese Hiragana)|アリシア(Japanese Katakana)|愛梨志亜, 有詩愛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)",A-REESH-EE-A,,,,,,,"From Japanese 亜 (a) meaning ""second, Asia"", 梨 (ri) meaning ""pear"", 志 (shi) meaning ""purpose, will, determination, aspiration, ambition"" combined with 愛 (a) meaning ""love, affection"". Other kanji combination are possible.Usage of this name is, most likely, influenced by the name Alishia or Alicia."
