Aristobia,f,Ἀριστοβία(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""the best life"" from the Greek elements ἄριστος (aristos) ""best"" and βίος (bios) ""life"" (compare Aristobios); alternatively, the second element may be Greek βία (bia) meaning ""bodily strength, force; act of violence""."
Aristobios,m,Ἀριστόβιος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""the best life"", derived from Greek ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" and βίος (bios) meaning ""life""."
