Aristocrates,m,Ἀριστοκράτης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of the Greek name Ἀριστοκράτης (Aristokrates) meaning ""the best power"", from ἄριστος (aristos) ""best"" and κράτος (kratos) meaning ""power, strength"" (whence modern English aristocrat). This was the name of two Ancient Greek rulers of Orchomenus in Arcadia."
