Aristocritus,m,Ἀριστόκριτος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Ἀριστόκριτος (Aristokritos), a Greek name meaning ""the best judge"" from the elements ἄριστος (aristos) meaning ""best"" and κριτής (krites) meaning ""judge, critic"". This was the name of several Ancient Greek people, including the father of Spartan general Lysander."
Aristodama,f,Ἀριστοδάμα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from ἄριστος (aristos) ""best"". The second element is uncertain, but may be derived δᾶμος (damos) which is a Doric Greek variant of δῆμος (demos) meaning ""the people""."
