Aristonike,f,Αριστονικη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Aristonikos. According to the 5th-century BC historian Herodotus, this was the name of the oracle of Delphi in the time of Xerxes' invasion."
