Arito,m,"現人, 彩斗, 在史, 在人, 有人, 有登, 可人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-ṘEE-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 現 (ari) meaning ""present, existing, actual"", 彩 (ari) meaning ""colour"", 在 (ari) meaning ""exist, outskirts, suburbs, located in"", 有 (ari) meaning ""exist"" or 可 (ari) meaning ""can, passable, mustn't, should not, do not"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"", 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation, 史 (to) meaning ""history, chronicle"" or 登 (to) meaning ""ascend, climb up"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Arito Tsukahara, a Japanese kickboxer."
Aritomo,m,"有朋, 存知, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ありとも(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/ä.ɾi.to̞.mo̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 有 (ari) meaning ""have, possess"" or 存 (ari) meaning ""exist"" combined with 朋 (tomo) meaning ""friend"" or 知 (tomo) meaning ""know, perceive, comprehend"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
