Arixen,f,,Medieval Basque,,,,,,,,Medieval Basque feminine name of unknown origin and meaning. It was first recorded in Pamplona in the 1200s.
Ariya,,"อารียา, อริยา, อริยะ(Thai)",Thai,/ʔaː˧.riː˧.ˈjaː˧/|/ʔa˨˩.ri˦˥.ˈjaː˧/|/ʔa˨˩.ri˦˥.ˈja˦˥/,,,,,,,"From Thai อริย (ariya) meaning ""noble, honourable, respectable, eminent"", ultimately derived from Sanskrit आर्य (ārya). This transcription represents both the feminine forms อารียา (with a long second vowel) and อริยา (with a short second vowel), as well as the masculine form อริยะ."
