Arjo,m,,Dutch (Rare)|Flemish (Rare),AHR-yo,,,,,,,"At least one source lists this name as being a combination of the names Adrianus and Johannes, but it could also easily be a combination of a name starting with Ar- (such as Arend) with a name starting with Jo- (such as Jozef). It should also be noted that it is also possible that in at least some cases, Arjo is a short form of the names Arjan 1 and/or Arjen.In the Netherlands, a well-known bearer of this name is Arjo Klamer (b. 1953), a Dutch economist, professor and author."
