Artorias,m,,Popular Culture,Ar-tor-ee-as,,,,,,,"Variant of Artorius used for a character in the 2012 video game Dark Souls: Artorias of the Abyss.Name of one of Gwyn, the lord of Cinder's knights, fought the abyss with his beloved Dog Sif, whom he trapped to save her/him from the abyss."
Artoriis,m,,Ancient Oscan,,,,,,,,"From the Etruscan praenomen Arnthur, of uncertain etymology. It may have been borrowed from the Messapic name Artas/Artorres. This name eventually became the Roman gens Artoria, of which multiple members have been found in inscriptions. It has been speculated that Artorius was the origin of the Welsh name Arthur."
Artorius,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Of debated origin and meaning. While some scholars propose a derivation from the Etruscan praenomen Arnthur, perhaps Latinized as Artor, others have proposed a Messapic origin, identifying a nomen Artorres, said to mean ""descendant of Artas"". Lucius Artorius Castus (fl. 2nd century AD), a Roman military commander, has been suggested as a potential historical basis for King Arthur."
