Arvirargus,m,,Old Celtic|Literature,ahr-veer-AHR-gus|ahr-veer-AHR-guws,,,,,,,"Possibly a Latinized form of an old Celtic name, composed of the elements ard ""high, paramount"" and rhaig ""king"". This was the name of a legendary, possibly historical, British king of the 1st century AD. References to him appear in a poem by Juvenal; Geoffrey of Monmouth's Historia Regum Britanniae; William Shakespeare's Cymbeline; and Geoffrey Chaucer's Canterbury Tales."
