Ashutosha,m,आशुतोष(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ɑː.ɕu.ˈt̪oː.ʂɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""easily content, quick to please"" from Sanskrit आशु (āśu) meaning ""fast, quick, rapid"" and तोष (toṣa) meaning ""satisfaction, contentment, pleasure"". This is an epithet of the Hindu god Shiva."
