Ašratum,f,𒀭𒀸𒊏𒌈(Sumerian Cuneiform),Near Eastern Mythology,,,,,,,,"A cognate of the Ugaritic Asherah. Name borne by an Amorite goddess who was likely derived from the same source as Asherah, however she came to occupy her own distinct position in the Amorite pantheon. She was regarded as the wife of the god Amurru (the representative god of the Amorite people)."
Asri,,عصري(Malay Jawi),Indonesian|Malay,,,,,,,,"Means ""my age, my time"" from Arabic عصر ('asr) meaning ""time, age, era"". This also coincides with the Indonesian word asri meaning ""beautiful, fair"". It is a unisex name in Indonesia while it is only masculine in Malaysia."
