Ástrós,f,,Icelandic,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Norse elements áss ""god"" (which becomes ást when preceding a liquid r, compare Ástríður) or ást ""affection, love, devotion"" and rós ""rose""."
Astruc,m,,Judeo-Spanish|Judeo-Provençal|Medieval Jewish|Judeo-Catalan,"ah-strook(Judeo-Spanish, Judeo-Provençal)",,,,,,,"Derived from Provençal astruc ""lucky"", ultimately from Greek aster ""star"" and thus having the extended meaning of ""born under a good star"".It was generally given as an amuletic name and sometimes used as a translation of Hebrew Mazel Tov and/or Gad."
