Asuma,m,"あすま(Japanese Hiragana)|愛洲馬, 明日真, 明日磨, 明日茉, 明日馬, 明日麻, 明馬, 未来磨, 遊馬, 飛海, 飛馬, 飛麻, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-SUU-MAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 愛 (a) meaning ""love, affection"", 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"", 明 (asu) meaning ""bright, light"", 未来 (asu) meaning ""future"", 遊 (asu) meaning ""play"" or 飛 (asu) meaning ""fly"", 洲 (su) meaning ""continent, sandbar, island, country"" combined with 馬 (ma) meaning ""horse"", 真 (ma) meaning ""true, reality"", 磨 (ma) meaning ""grind, polish, scour, improve, brush (teeth)"", 茉 (ma) meaning ""jasmine"", 麻 (ma) meaning ""flax, linen, hemp"" or 海 (ma) meaning ""sea, ocean"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Asumi,f,"あすみ(Japanese Hiragana)|アスミ(Japanese Katakana)|安純, 阿澄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-SOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 安 (a) meaning ""peace, low, cheap, relax, inexpensive"" combined with 純 (sumi) meaning ""innocent"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Asumiko,f,明日美子(Japanese Kanji),"Japanese (Rare, ?)",AH-SOO-MEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 明日 (asu) meaning ""tomorrow"", 美 (mi) meaning ""beauty"", and 子 (ko, shi) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A notable bearer is Asumiko Nakamura, a manga artist."
