Atsu,m,"纂, 敦, 厚, 暖, 淳, 阿鶴, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese|Ewe,AH-TSOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 纂 (atsu) meaning ""gather, compile"", 敦 (atsu) meaning ""affinity, kindness"", or 篤 (atsu) meaning ""cordial, faithful, sincere"". Other kanji or kanji combinations can be used."
Atsuaki,m,"あつあき(Japanese Hiragana)|アツアキ(Japanese Katakana)|熱顕, 暖旺, 醇亮, 敦晟, 厚昭, 纂旭, 豊堯, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-TSOO-A-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 晃 (aki) meaning ""clear"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsue,f,"あつえ(Japanese Hiragana)|アツエ(Japanese Katakana)|熱映, 温栄, 豊慧, 淳重, 厚慧, 篤枝, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-TSOO-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 熱 (atsu) meaning ""passion, temperature"" combined with 永 (e) meaning ""eternity, long, lengthy"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuharu,m,"暖理, 溌春, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),AH-TSOO-HAH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 暖 (atsu) meaning ""warm"" and 理 (haru) meaning ""logic, reason"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsuhi,f,"渥火, 渥日, 厚妃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-HEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""moisten, make moist"" combined with 火 (hi) meaning ""fire"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuhiko,m,"温彦, 宏彦, 純彦, 敦彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-HEE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 温 (atsu) meaning ""warm"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy, prince"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous bearer is Atsuhiko Ejiri, a retired Japanese footballer. He played in a midfield position for JEF United Ichihara."
Atsuhiro,m,"貴裕, 逸裕, 厚博(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"Japanese masculine name derived from either 貴裕, meaning ""precious; plentiful"", 逸裕 meaning ""escape, break free; plentiful"" or 厚博 ""thick and broad, rich, plentiful""."
Atsuhito,m,"厚人, 厚仁, 篤仁, 敦仁, 充仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あつひと(Japanese Hiragana)|アツヒト(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,[à.t͡sɨ́ᵝ.çì̥.tò̞],,,,,,,"From the stem of adjective 厚/篤い (atsui) meaning ""kind, cordial, hospitable, warm"" (also used as 敦 or 充, the last one meaning ""full"") combined with 人 (hito) meaning ""person,"" also used as 仁 meaning ""benevolence, compassion, humanity."""
Atsuichi,m,"渥一, 厚市, 淳一, 敦一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-EE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""moist"" combined with 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuichiro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Atsuichirou.
Atsuichirou,m,"淳一郎, 充一郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-EE-CHEE-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 淳 (atsu) meaning ""honest, simple, unsophisticated"", 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuŝio,m,,Esperanto,,,,,,,,Esperanto form of Atsushi.
Atsuji,m,"淳二, 淳弐, 篤司, 篤時, 篤二, 敦, 敦時, 敦冶, 諄二, 温久, 温二, 厚, 厚至, 厚治, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-JEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 淳 (atsu) meaning ""pure"" combined with 二 (ji) meaning ""two"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Atsuji Miyahara​, a Japanese wrestler and Olympic champion in Greco-Roman wrestling."
Atsujiro,m,,Japanese,AH-TSOO-ZHEE-RO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Atsujirou.
Atsujirou,m,"篤二郎, 篤次郎, 厚二郎, 敦次郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-JEE-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"", 二 (ji) meaning ""two"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsujo,m,,Esperanto,,,,,,,,Esperanto form of Atsuya.
Atsuka,f,"篤花, 惇佳, 醇香, 敦歌, 敦香, 諄耶, 淳夏, 厚香, 京佳, 温香, 貴香, 扱, 亜津香, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 花 (ka) meaning ""flower"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuki,m,"渥幹, 渥樹, 杏槻, 温輝, 温己, 貴規, 貴樹, 厚基, 彩月季, 充己, 淳希, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-TSOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""moist"" combined with 幹 (ki) meaning ""tree trunk"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuma,m,"あつま(Japanese Hiragana)|渥真, 敦真, 厚馬, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),A-TSOO-MA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""moist"" or 敦 (atsu) meaning ""kindness, affinity"" combined with 真 (ma) meaning ""real, genuine"". Other combinations of kanji can form this name as well."
Atsumasa,m,"厚正, 京昌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-MAH-SAH,,,,,,,"From 厚 (atsu) meaning ""thick, heavy, kind"" or 京 (atsu) meaning ""capital city, Tokyo, Kyoto, ten quadrillion, ten thousand billion"" combined with 雅 (masa) meaning ""elegant, graceful"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsume,f,"純瞳, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 純 (atsu) meaning ""pure, innocent"" combined with 瞳 (me) meaning ""pupil"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsumi,f,"アツミ(Japanese Katakana)|渥美, 敦美, 暖己, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""glossy, moisten, moist, cordial, kind"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are possible as well."
Atsumichi,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Atsumiko,f,"温美子, 敦美子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),A-TSOO-MEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 温 (atsu) meaning ""warm"" or 篤 (atsu) meaning ""deep, true, sincere"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beauty"", and 子 (ko, shi) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsumori,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Atsumu,m,"アツム(Japanese Katakana)|纂, 集, 侑, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-MOO,,,,,,,"From 侑 (atsumu) meaning ""to help, to assist, urge to eat"", 集 (atsumu) meaning ""to gather, congregate"" or 纂 (atsumu) meaning ""editing, compiling, gather"". Other spellings are possible."
Atsuna,f,"あつな(Japanese Hiragana)|アツナ(Japanese Katakana)|亜津奈, 渥奈, 温奈, 淳名, 篤菜, 惇菜, 敦奈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),A-TSOO-NA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 亜 (a) meaning ""second, Asia"", 津 (tsu), a place name, such as Tsu city in Mie prefecture combined with 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsunao,m,,Japanese,AH-TSOO-NAH-OH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""deep, true, sincere"" or 敦 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 直 (nao) meaning ""straight, direct"" or 尚 (shou, nao) meaning ""esteem, furthermore, still, yet"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsundo,m,"篤人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あつんど(Japanese Hiragana)|アツンド(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[à.t͡sɨ̃́ᵝǹ.dò̞],,,,,,,Shift from Atsuhito.This name is very rarely used.
Atsuno,f,"あつ乃(Kanji/Hiragana)|あつの(Japanese Hiragana)|篤乃, 惇乃, 淳野, 厚野, 渥野, 渥乃, 諄乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Atsunobu,m,"厚信, 篤信, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|あつのぶ(Japanese Hiragana)|アツノブ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ä.t͡sɨᵝ.no̞.bɯᵝ/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 厚 (atsu) meaning ""thick, heavy"" or 篤 (atsu) meaning ""deep, true, sincere"" combined with 信 (nobu) meaning ""trust"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Atsunori,m,"渥訓, 温規, 温教, 温法, 厚紀, 厚, 厚範, 充文, 淳永, 淳慎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-NO-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 渥 (atsu) meaning ""moist"" combined with 訓 (nori) meaning ""teach, instruct"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous bearer is Atsunori Inaba, a Japanese former professional baseball player. He was the Most Valuable Player of the 2006 Japan Series."
Atsuo,m,"温男, 教生, 渥郎, 渥男, 厚於, 厚男, 厚郎, 淳央, 醇郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 温 (atsu) meaning ""warm"" combined with 男 (o) meaning ""male"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Atsurou.
Atsurou,m,"篤郎, 篤朗, 敦良, 敦郎, 淳朗, 重郎, 郭郎, 諄郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Atsuro Watabe, a Japanese actor."
Atsushige,m,"京茂, 厚重, 慎茂, 篤重, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-SHEE-GEH,,,,,,,"From 京 (atsu) meaning ""capital city, Tokyo, Kyoto, ten quadrillion, ten thousand billion"" or 厚 (atsu) meaning ""thick, heavy, kind"" combined with 重 (shige) meaning ""layers, folds"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsusuke,m,"温助, 温祐, 温輔, 厚佑, 淳祐, 敦助, 敦祐, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-SUU-KE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 温 (atsu) meaning ""warm"" combined with 助 (suke) meaning ""help, assistance"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsutaka,m,"あつたか(Japanese Hiragana)|アツタカ(Japanese Katakana)|京崇, 敦堯, 渥天, 惇剛, 重敬, 淳琢, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-TSOO-TA-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" or 熱 (atsu) meaning ""passion, temperature"" combined with 孝 (taka) meaning ""filial piety"" or 堯 (taka) meaning ""high, far"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsutake,m,"篤威, 篤毅, 惇岳, 敦剛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-TAH-KE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 威 (take) meaning ""intimidate"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsutane,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Atsutaro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Atsurou.
Atsutarou,m,"宏太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSUU-TAH-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 宏 (atsu) meaning ""wide, spacious, great, vast"", 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuto,m,"敦斗, 敦人, 敦翔, 厚斗, 厚人, 厚翔, 篤斗, 篤人, 篤翔(Japanese Kanji)|あつと(Japanese Hiragana)|アツト(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),AHTS-TO|AH-TSUU-TO,,,,,,,"This name combines 敦 (ton, tai, dai, chou, atsu.i) meaning ""industry, kindliness"", 厚 (kou, atsu.i, aka) meaning ""thick, heavy, rich, kind, cordial, brazen, shameless"" or 篤 (toku, atsu.i) meaning ""fervent, kind, cordial, serious, deliberate"" with 斗 (to, tou) meaning ""Big Dipper, sake dipper"", 人 (jin, nin, -to, hito, -ri) meaning ""person"" or 翔 (shou, kage.ru, to.bu) meaning ""fly, soar.""This name is rarely given to boys, if given at all."
Atsuya,m,"アツヤ(Japanese Katakana)|敦也, 篤也, 纂哉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-YAH,,,,,,,"Derived from 纂 (atsu) meaning ""compile, gather"" or 敦 (atsu) meaning ""candid, sincere, honest"" and 也 (ya) meaning ""also"". Other kanji combinations can spell this name."
Atsuyasu,m,"温安, 篤康, 敦坦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-YAH-SOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 温 (atsu) meaning ""warm"", 篤 (atsu) meaning ""deep, true, sincere"" or 敦 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 安 (yasu) meaning ""peace, quiet"", 康 (yasu) meaning ""peaceful"" or 坦 (yasu) meaning ""flat, smooth, level""."
Atsuyo,f,"あつよ(Japanese Hiragana)|篤世, 惇代, 春代, 修代, 惇葉, 敦代, 農代, 厚代, 安都代, 渥世, 阿都世, 亜都代, 亜津世, 諄代, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,A-TSOO-YO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 篤 (atsu) meaning ""honest"" combined with 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" or 世 (yo) meaning ""world"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Atsuyoshi,m,"敦成, 敦義, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 敦 (atsu.shi) meaning ""kindness, honesty"" and 成 (yoshi) meaning ""become"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsuyuki,m,"京行, 京千, 京征, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,AH-TSOO-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From 京 (atsu) meaning ""capital city, Tokyo, Kyoto, ten quadrillion, ten thousand billion"" and 行 (yuki) meaning ""line, row"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Atsy,f,,Spanish,,,,,,,,Not available.
Atsyrukhs,f,Ацырухс(Ossetian),Ossetian Mythology|Ossetian (Rare),/ɐ.ˈt͡sɨ.rʊxs/(Russian),,,,,,,"From Ossetian ацы (atsy) meaning ""present, real, true"" and рухс (rukhs) meaning ""light"". This is the name of a character in the Nart sagas, the daughter of the god Khur."
Ätta,f,,Swedish (Archaic),,,,,,,,Variant of Etta.
Atta,m,,Akan|Arabic|Popular Culture,,,,,,,,"Means ""twin"" in Fante, an Akan language."
Attaces,m,,History,,,,,,,,"Attaces (died 418 A.D.) was king of the western Alans in Hispania (the Iberian Peninsula, modern Spain and Portugal).The Alans were an ancient and medieval Iranian nomadic pastoral people of the North Caucasus."
Attachai,m,อรรถชัย(Thai),Thai,/ʔat̚˨˩.tʰaː˩˩˦.ˈt͡ɕʰaj˧/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Thai อรรถชัย (see Atthachai).
Attagares,f,,Guanche,a-ta-GAH-res,,,,,,,"From Guanche *hata-tagarest, meaning ""here is the frost"". This was recorded as the name of a 5-year-old Guanche girl from Tenerife who was sold at the slave market in Valencia in 1494."
Attagora,f,,Guanche,,,,,,,,"Name borne by three Guanche women, aged 26, 28 and 30, who were sold at the slave market in Valencia in 1494."
Attai,m,עַתַּי(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,AT-ie(Biblical English),,,,,,,"The name comes from the verb ענה ('ana), which can mean one of four things: ""to answer"", ""to be occupied with"", ""to afflict"", or ""to sing"".In the Bible, there are three people named Attai. The first, in 1 Chronicles 2:35, is one of the descendants of Jerahmeel. He is the son of Jarha, grandson of Sheshan, father of Nathan, and grandfather of Zabad. The second, in 1 Chronicles 12:11, is the sixth of Gad's captains. The third, in 2 Chronicles 11:20, is the son of King Rehoboam and his second wife, Maakah; as well as the brother of Abijah, Ziza, and Shelomith."
Attakullakulla,m,ᎠᏔᎫᎧᎷ(Cherokee),Cherokee,,,,,,,,"Means ""leaning wood"" in Cherokee, from *ada meaning ""wood"", and *gulkalu, a verb that implies something long, leaning against some other object."
Attala,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Derived from an Ancient Germanic word meaning ""fatherly, paternal""."
Attale,m,,French,,,,,,,,French form of Attalus.
Attallah,,,Arabic|African American (Rare),,,,,,,,"Variant of Atallah, a masculine Arabic name, which is borne by Attallah Shabazz (1958-), the eldest daughter of American activist Malcolm X."
Attalos,m,Ἄτταλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek (Rare),,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Greek ἀταλός (atalos) meaning ""delicate, tender"" or the related ἀτάλλω (atallo) meaning ""to bring up a child, to foster"", ""to grow"" or ""to skip, gambol, frolic""."
Attalus,m,Ἄτταλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Gaulish,,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Attalos. This was borne by numerous ancient Greek historical figures, including a general of Alexander the Great and three kings of Pergamon in Asia Minor.The famous marble statue The Dying Gaul is a Roman copy of a lost bronze sculpture which was commissioned by the 3rd-century BC king Attalus I to celebrate his defeat of the Galatians, a Celtic tribe."
Áttán,m,,Sami,,,,,,,,Sami form of Adam.
Attanasiu,m,,Corsican,,,,,,,,Corsican form of Athanasios.
Attanatda,f,,Guanche,a-ta-NAHT-da,,,,,,,"From Guanche *hata-tanaṭda, meaning ""here is the (personified) authority"". This was recorded as the name of a 35-year-old Guanche woman from Tenerife who was sold at the slave market in Valencia in 1494."
Attaphol,m,อรรถพล(Thai),Thai,/ʔat̚˨˩.tʰaː˩˩˦.ˈpʰon˧/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Thai อรรถพล (see Atthaphon).
