Âu Cơ,f,嫗姬(Vietnamese Chữ Nôm),Vietnamese Mythology,/ʔəw˧˧ kəː˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 嫗姬 (Âu Cơ) meaning ""lady of the Âu Việt"", the name of a group of ancient tribes that inhabited northern Vietnam and southern China in the 3rd century BC. In Vietnamese mythology, Âu Cơ is a fairy deity, the daughter of Thần Nông (or sometimes the daughter of Đế Lai) and the wife of Lạc Long Quân. She is honoured as the mother of the modern Vietnamese people."
