Aulis,f,Αὐλίς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek αὖλις (aulis) meaning ""place to spend the night, resting place; encampment, tent, roosting-place"", or perhaps the related αὐλή (aule) meaning ""courtyard, quadrangle, hall, house, dwelling place"". This was the name of the eponym of an ancient port town in Boeotia in Greek mythology, one of the three Praxidicae, goddesses who oversaw the swearing of oaths in Boeotia."
