Aureus,m,,Late Roman,AWR-ee-əs(English)|OW:-re-oos(Latin),,,,,,,"Means ""golden, gilded"" in Latin, from aurum ""gold"" (see Aurea). An aureus was also a gold coin of ancient Rome, equivalent to 25 denarii. This was the name of a Christian saint who was martyred in the 5th century with his sister Saint Justina at the cathedral of Mainz in Germany; they were killed by invading Huns while celebrating Mass."
