Aurisma,f,,Medieval French|Medieval Latin (?),,,,,,,,"Derived from Proto-Indo-European aues meaning ""brilliant, shining"" (related to Proto-Italic *auzōs, from the Proto-Indo-European root *h₂éwsōs meaning ""dawn"" - the source also of Aurora and Auster) combined with -isma, a variant of the Latin superlative suffix -issima."
