Auristela,f,,Portuguese (Brazilian)|Spanish (Latin American)|Literature (Rare),,,,,,,,"From the Latin words auris (""of gold"") and stella (""star""), thus intended to mean ""golden star"". This name was invented by Spanish writer Miguel de Cervantes (1547-1616) as a byname for Sigismunda, one of the main characters in his novel Los trabajos de Persiles y Sigismunda. This name became popular in Venezuela and Brazil in the mid 20th century."
