Aurvandill,m,,Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""beam; morning; morning star"", or possibly derived from aur (""water"") and vandill (""sword""). In Norse mythology one of Aurvandill's toes broke off. Thor threw it into the sky, where it became a star."
Aurvangr,m,,Old Norse|Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""one from Aurvangar"". Aurvangar ""the gravelly wetlands"", also called Jǫruvellir ""sandy plain"", is the home of the dwarfs. In Norse mythology Aurvangr is the name of a dwarf."
