Auðlín,f,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Norse elements auðr ""fortune, riches"" and lín ""flax, linen"". Alternatively the second element could be derived from Hlín (which occurs in many Old Norse poetic compounds meaning ""woman"") or Lína."
