Authrounios,m,,Gnosticism,,,,,,,,"Authrounios is a divine or semi-divine revelatory figure in the Sethian Gnostic text Zostrianos, where he is described as a “great ruler” or high-ranking spiritual authority who instructs the protagonist during his ascent through the cosmic realms. In the narrative, Authrounios functions as a teacher of esoteric cosmology, explaining the structure of the lower worlds, the origin of the material cosmos, and the deceptive nature of creation as a reflection of higher divine realities. He appears as part of the complex hierarchy of aeons and intelligences characteristic of Sethian Gnosticism, serving a role similar to an initiatory guide who imparts salvific knowledge (gnosis) necessary for spiritual ascent. Not widely attested outside this text."
Auðrún,f,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Norse elements auðr meaning ""wealth, fortune"" (or possibly the poetic word auðr which meant ""fate, destiny"") and rún meaning ""secret lore, rune""."
