Avo,m,,Germanic|Estonian,,,,,,,,"Of disputed origin and meaning.The general consensus is that Avo (as well as its feminine counterpart Ava 3) was originally a short form of Germanic names beginning with the element avi. The meaning of this name element, however, is still disputed. Current theories include a derivation from a word meaning ""desired"", a derivation from Old Saxon aval ""strength; power"", or else a derivation from Old High German alfi ""elf""."
