Aydeniz,f,,Medieval Turkic,[AHY-deh-neez],,,,,,,"Composed of Ay (""moon"") and Deniz (""sea""). It creates the imagery of the ""lunar sea,"" signifying a vast, reflective, and serene presence that mirrors the cosmic depth of the ocean."
Aydenk,f,,Turkish,[AHY-denk],,,,,,,"A combination of Ay (""moon"") and Denk (""equal,"" ""balanced,"" ""equivalent""). It denotes ""equal to the moon"" or ""lunar equilibrium,"" characterizing the bearer as someone of balanced temperament and peerless beauty."
