Azaes,m,Ἀζάης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Possibly related to the toponym Ἀζανία (Azania), which could mean ""land of Zeus"". Alternatively, it could derive from ἄζα (aza) ""heat, dryness"". Azaes was one of the ten sons of Poseidon and Cleito in Plato's myth of Atlantis, his twin brother being Diaprepes."
