Azeus,m,Ἀζεύς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly related to ἄζα (aza) meaning ""heat, dryness, drought"". This was the name of a Minyan prince in Greek mythology, the youngest son of King Clymenus of Orchomenus (located in modern-day Greece)."
