Azjargal,,Азжаргал(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Means ""happiness, bliss"" in Mongolian, from аз (az) meaning ""fortune, luck"" and жаргал (jargal) meaning ""happiness, blessing""."
Azka,,أزكى(Arabic)|ازکی(Urdu),Arabic|Indonesian|Urdu,/ˈʔaz.qaː/(Arabic)|/ˈaz.ka/(Indonesian),,,,,,,"Means ""purer, more befitting, better"" in Arabic, ultimately from the root زكا (zakā) meaning ""to be good or just, to be suitable"". It is sometimes used as a masculine name in Indonesia, while it is solely feminine elsewhere."
