Babylos,m,Βαβύλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Semitic (Hellenized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. It is often confused or conflated with Babylas, but the two names are not necessarily related to each other. For example, Babylas is confirmed to ultimately be of Akkadian origin, whilst for Babylos, there is at least one source that states that the name is of Syrian (or rather Assyrian) origin and means ""rebel"" or ""rebellion, uprising"".A notable bearer of this name is saint Matrona of Perge (6th century AD), who spent some time in a monastery, disguised as a eunuch named Babylos."
