Bądzimir,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Polish bądź, which is the second-person singular imperative form of the verb być ""to be"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". As such, one could say that this name is a later (or more elaborate) form of Bytomir."
