Báine,,,Irish|Scottish Gaelic|Irish Mythology,bayn(Scottish Gaelic),,,,,,,"An Irish name meaning ""whiteness, pallor"". In Irish Mythology, Báine was a princess, daughter of Tuathal Techtmar, ancestor of the kings of Ireland. ""Cailín na Gruaige Báine"" and ""Bruach na Carraige Báine"" are the names of two traditional Irish songs.-------------------------------------Coming from a nick-name for a blonde person from the Gaelic word 'bàn' meaning white or fair. It may also be from Old and Middle English words meaning 'bone' and 'welcoming' respectively."
