Balagangadharanatha,m,बलगङ्गाधरनाथ(Hindi),"Obscure|Indian (Rare, ?)",,,,,,,,"Means ""finding refuge in the might of the Ganges-supporter (i.e. Shiva)"" in Sanskrit, from a combination of Sanskrit बल (bala) ""might, strength"" with Gangadhara, a name of the god Shiva meaning ""Ganga-supporter, Ganges-receiver, the ocean"", and नाथ (nātha) ""patron, protector, lord"" or ""refuge"". This name was borne by Balagangadharanatha Swamiji (1945-2013), an Indian religious leader."
