Bathycles,m,Βαθυκλῆς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized),/ba.tʰy.klɛ̂ːs/(Classical Greek),,,,,,,"From the Greek name Βαθυκλῆς (Bathykles), which was derived from the Greek elements βαθύς (bathus, bathys) meaning ""deep, profound"" and κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory, fame"". This was the name of a warrior mentioned in Homer's Iliad, one of the Myrmidons who took part in the Trojan War."
