Batia,f,Βάτεια(Ancient Greek)|בתיה(Hebrew),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Jewish,Bat-ya,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Ancient Greek βάτος (batos) meaning ""bramble bush, wild blackberry"". This was the name of a naiad of the town of Sparta in Greek mythology, who married an early Spartan king, Oibalos. It was also the name of a daughter (or possibly aunt) of King Teucer."
