Bec,f,,Irish Mythology (?),BECK,,,,,,,"Allegedly an older form of Irish beag ""small"".In Irish mythology, Bec is one of the Tuatha Dé Danann. ""She was known for having a magic well, guarded by her three daughters. When Fionn mac Cumhaill approached the well to ask for a drink, her daughters tried to prevent him from getting the water; 'one of them threw water over him to scare him away and some of it went into his mouth. From the water he gained wisdom.'"""
