Bela,m,בֶּלַע(Ancient Hebrew)|ბელა(Georgian),Biblical|Yiddish|Judeo-French|Georgian|Spanish|Portuguese|Banat Swabian|Danish|Finnish|Norwegian|Swedish|Judeo-Anglo-Norman,,,,,,,,"Means ""to swallow"" in Hebrew. This is the name of several characters in the Bible. One of them, Bela ben Beor (Bela, son of Beor) was the first king of Edom.Bela is also mentioned as another name for the city Zoar in Genesis 14:2."
Belacane,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"The mother of Feirefiz, Parsifal's half-brother, in Wolfram von Eschenbach's 'Parsifal'."
