Belatucadros,m,,Celtic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Often translated as ""fair shining one"" or ""fair slayer"", derived in part from Celtic *bel(l)- ""strong, powerful"" or *belo- ""bright"" (cf. Belenus). This was the name of a Celtic deity often identified with Mars, sometimes referred to as Mars Belatucadrus."
Belatz,m,,Medieval Basque,,,,,,,,"Derived from Basque belatz ""sparrowhawk""."
Belay,f,,Filipino,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Isabel.
Belaya Noch,f,Белая Ночь(Russian),Soviet,,,,,,,,"Means ""white night"" in Russian."
Belaye,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,A princess and wife of Lohengrin. She died of grief when Lohengrin was murdered by men sent by her parents.
Belayneh,m,"በላይነህ, በላይ ነህ(Amharic)",Eastern African|Amharic,,,,,,,,"It is an Amharic expression, which means ""the new child is above all others"". From the Amharic elements በላይ (belay) meaning ""above"" and ነህ (Neh) means ""you"".It also means ""You Are On Top, you are up there"" in Amharic."
Belaynesh,f,"በላይነሽ, በላይ ነሽ(Amharic)",Eastern African|Amharic,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Belayneh.
Belbiche,f,,African,,,,,,,,Not available.
Bēl-bullissu,m,,Babylonian,,,,,,,,"Means ""Bel, keep him alive"", deriving from the Akkadian element balāṭu (""to revive ; to keep alive, healthy"")."
Belcalis,f,,"Obscure|Spanish (Caribbean, Rare)",/ˈbɛl.kə.liːz/(English),,,,,,,"Possibly an elaboration of Belkis using the popular Caribbean Spanish name suffix lis (from Elizabeth or a related name). This is the real name of American rapper, songwriter and television personality Cardi B (1992-), who was born Belcalis Marlenis Almánzar to Caribbean immigrants - a Dominican father and a Trinidadian mother."
Belcebú,m,,Biblical Spanish,/bel.se.ˈβu/(Latin American Spanish)|/bel.θe.ˈβu/(European Spanish),,,,,,,Spanish form of Beelzebub.
