Belena,f,,Old Celtic|German|Danish|Celtic Mythology,"be-LEN-ə(Old Celtic, German, Danish)",,,,,,,Latinized feminine form of Belenus. Belena was the wife of the Gaulish solar god Belenus and the goddess of the sun and the beginning summer.
Belend,m,بلند(Kurdish Sorani),Kurdish,Blynd,,,,,,,"Originated from a Turkish name meaning: High in rank, or tall in general"
