Bellaria,f,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Perhaps derived from Latin bellare meaning ""to fight"". This name was used by Robert Greene for a character in his prose romance 'Pandosto: The Triumph of Time' (1588). It was also used by Henry Fielding in his play 'The Temple Beau' (1730), and by Aaron Hill (1685-1750) in his poem 'Bellaria, at her Spinnet'."
