Benjirō,m,"弁次郎, 弁治郎, 弁二郎, 勉次郎, 勉治郎, 勉二郎, 辨次郎, 辨治郎, 辨二郎(Japanese Kanji)|べんじろう(Japanese Hiragana)|ベンジロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/bẽ̞ɲ̟.d͡ʑi.ɾo̞ː/,,,,,,,"This name combines 弁/辨 (hen, ben, araso.u, hanabira, wakima.eru, wa.keru) meaning ""dialect, speech, petal"" or 勉 (ben, tsuto.meru) meaning ""exertion"" with 次 (shi, ji, tsugi, tsu.gu) meaning ""next, second,"" 治 (ji, chi, osa.ma/eru, nao.su/ru) meaning ""cure, heal, rule"" or 二 (ji, ni, futa(.tsu), futata.bi) meaning ""two"" and 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son.""This name was occasionally used from the late Edo Period (1603-1868) to the first half of the 20th century but nowadays, it is very rarely given to boys, if given at all."
