Beornwulf,m,,Anglo-Saxon,/ˈbe͜orn.wulf/(Old English),,,,,,,"Derived from Old English beorn ""warrior, man"" and wulf ""wolf"". This was the name of a King of Mercia who reigned in the 9th century. Cognate to Germanic Bernulf."
