Bhadra,,"भद्र, भद्रा(Sanskrit, Hindi)",Hinduism|Hindi,,,,,,,,"Means ""good, excellent, fortunate"" or ""prosperity, happiness, health"" in Sanskrit. This is the name of several figures in Hinduism, including an aspect of the goddess Devi, and one of the eight queen-consorts of Krishna. It is also the name of an obscure goddess of the hunt."
