Bhagyashri,f,भाग्यश्री(Marathi),Marathi,,,,,,,,"From Sanskrit भाग्य (bhāgya) meaning ""luck, destiny, fate, fortune"" and श्री (śrī) meaning ""diffusing light, radiance, splendour, beauty, holy, sacred""."
Bhairava,m,भैरव(Sanskrit),Hinduism|Buddhism,/ˈbʱɑj.ɾɐ.ʋɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""fearsome, terrible"" in Sanskrit. This is the name of a fierce form of the Hindu god Shiva, often depicted wearing a garland of decapitated heads and accompanied by a dog. He is revered in both Hindu and Buddhist traditions, particularly in the Shaivite Hindu denomination."
Bhairavi,f,"भैरवी(Sanskrit, Marathi)|ભૈરવી(Gujarati)",Hinduism|Marathi|Gujarati,/ˈbʱɑj.ɾɐ.ʋiː/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Feminine form of Bhairava. In Hindu tradition she is the consort of Bhairava, the fierce form of Shiva, and the fifth of the ten Mahavidyas, the Tantric manifestations of the mother goddess Mahadevi."
Bhaishajyaguru,m,भैषज्यगुरु(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/bʱɑj.ˈʂɐd͡ʑ.jɐ.ɡu.ɾu/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""master of medicine"" from Sanskrit भैषज्य (bhaiṣajya) meaning ""curativeness, healing, remedy, medicine"" and गुरु (guru) meaning ""teacher, sage, master"". In the Mahayana and Vajrayana Buddhist traditions this is the name of a buddha associated with medicine and healing."
Bhaishajyaraja,m,भैषज्यराज(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/bʱɑj.ʂɐd͡ʑ.jɐ.ˈɾɑː.d͡ʑɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""king of healing"" from Sanskrit भैषज्य (bhaiṣajya) meaning ""curativeness, healing, remedy, medicine"" and राज (rāja) meaning ""king"". In Buddhist tradition this is the name of a bodhisattva associated with medicine and healing."
Bhaishajyasamudgata,m,भैषज्यसमुद्गत(Sanskrit),Buddhism,,,,,,,,"From Sanskrit भैषज्य (bhaiṣajya) meaning ""curativeness, healing, remedy, medicine"" and समुद्गत (samudgata) meaning ""risen, come forth, appeared, begun"". In Buddhist tradition this is the name of a bodhisattva associated with healing and medicine."
Bhajan,,भजन(Hindi)|ਭਜਨ(Gurmukhi)|ভজন(Bengali),Hindi|Punjabi|Bengali,/ˈbʱə.d͡ʒən/(Hindi)|/ˈbʱɔ.d͡ʒon/(Bengali)|/ˈbʱɔ.dʑon/(Bengali),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit भजन (bhajana) meaning ""reverence, worship, adoration"", also referring to a type of devotional song or hymn. As a Punjabi name it is sometimes feminine."
