Bifrons,m,,Literature|Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin bifrons meaning ""having two faces, two-faced"". This is an epithet of the Roman god Janus, who is often depicted with two faces looking in opposite directions. It is also the name of a demon who appears in several works on demonology, including the 17th-century grimoire The Lesser Key of Solomon (author unknown) and the Pseudomonarchia Daemonum (1563) by Dutch physician Johann Weyer."
