Bloodgood,m,,American (Rare),BLUD-guwd,,,,,,,Name of New York farmer Bloodgood Haviland Cutter (1817–1906). He was known as a 'farmer poet'. Well known author Mark Twain humorously dubbed Cutter the 'Poet Lariat' in Twain's non-fiction travelogue 'Innocents Abroad'. Cutter's first name was his paternal grandmother's maiden name.
