Bochia,m,ბოჩია(Georgian),Mingrelian|Georgian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Mingrelian ბოში (boši) or (boshi) meaning ""boy"". As such, this name is the Mingrelian equivalent of Bichia.Also compare dialectal Georgian ბოვში (bovshi) and standard Georgian ბავშვი (bavshvi), which both mean ""baby, child"".It is possible that there is also an etymological connection to Bochi, the name of an ancient Georgian (or rather Kartvelian) deity."
