Bodhidharma,m,बोधिधर्म(Sanskrit),Sanskrit|History|Buddhism,,,,,,,,"Means ""dharma of enlightenment"" in Sanskrit, from Sanskrit बोधि (bodhi) ""state of enlightenment"" and धर्म (dharma) ""that which is established, law, duty, virtue"". This was the name of a semi-legendary Buddhist monk who lived during the 5th or 6th century CE."
