Bodhisattva,,,"Buddhism|English (American, Modern, Rare)",/ˌboʊ̯.diː.ˈsɑt.və/(English)|/ˌboʊ̯.diː.ˈsʌt.və/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""enlightened being"" from Sanskrit, literally ""one whose essence is perfect knowledge"", composed of बोधि (bodhi) ""perfect knowledge, perfect wisdom"" (see Bodhi; also related to Buddha) and सत्त्व (sattva) ""essence, reality, being"". In Buddhism, a bodhisattva is a person who is on the path towards the attainment of bodhi (perfect knowledge) or Buddhahood."
