Boeotus,m,Βοιωτός(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek (Latinized),/biː.ˈoʊ.təs/(English)|/boe̯.ˈoː.tus/(Classical Latin)|/be.ˈo.tus/(modern Ecclesiastical Latin)|/boi̯.ɔː.tós/(Attic Greek)|/βy.o.ˈtos/(Koine Greek)|/vy.o.ˈtos/(Byzantine Greek)|/vi.o.ˈtos/(Constantinopolitan Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from Greek βοώτης (bootes) meaning ""herdsman"", itself from βοῦς (bous) meaning ""ox, cow""."
