Borvonia,f,,Celtic Mythology,,,,,,,,"""Borvonia"" (or Bormana) is a Gallo-Celtic goddess of healing, thermal waters, and fertility. Her name shares a Proto-Celtic root meaning ""to boil"". She was revered by ancient tribes, particularly in Gaul (modern-day France), as the divine feminine consort to the hot-spring god Borvo (also known as Bormanus)."
