Boy,m,,North Frisian|West Frisian|East Frisian|Dutch|Danish|German|English (Rare),BOI(English),,,,,,,"Variant form of Boye. In English-speaking countries, the name is usually derived from the English word boy meaning ""boy"" (in a manner comparable to the name Sonny) or a short form of the given names Boyce and Boyd.A known bearer of this name was the German sculptor and writer of children's books Boy Lornsen (1922-1995)."
