Boye,m,,West Frisian|East Frisian|North Frisian,,,,,,,,"There are many etymologies possible for this Frisian name. One is that it is a pet form of Germanic given names that contained the element bodo meaning ""lord, ruler"" or baug meaning ""bow"". Another is that it was derived from Proto-Germanic bojo meaning ""boy"". One source even mentioned that it could possibly be derived from Boii (known in German as Boier and Bojer), which was the latinized name of a Gallic tribe from ancient times."
