Brandon,m,,Medieval French,,,,,,,,"Medieval French form of Brando. At the same time, it was also a diminutive of Germanic names that contain the element brant meaning ""sword"", as -on is a French diminutive suffix.This name has fallen out of use in the francophone world; it now only survives there as a patronymic surname."
