Bregowine,m,,Anglo-Saxon|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from Old English bregu ""ruler"" (compare Breguswið) and wine ""friend"". This was the name of a medieval Archbishop of Canterbury, the successor of Cuthbert. After his death in 764, Bregowine was considered a saint and a vita (or hagiographical life) about him was written in the 12th century."
