Briac,m,,French|Breton,BREE-AHK(French)|BREE-ahk(Breton),,,,,,,"From a Brythonic name derived from the Celtic element *brigo ""high, noble, mighty"". As such this name can be viewed as a Breton cognate of Brian. In the case of Saint Briac, who arrived in Brittany with Saint Tugdual circa 548, this was a short form of the old Welsh name Briafael."
