Brindabella,f,,Indigenous Australian,brin-duh-BEL-uh,,,,,,,"Locational name, from the Brindabella mountain range on the border of New South Wales and the Australian Capital Territory. Usually said to be from a local language, meaning ""two hopping mice"" - hopping mice are native Australian mice. Another theory is that it is from brindy brindy, meaning ""water running over rocks"", with a European -bella added to suggest ""beautiful""."
Brindin,,,English (Rare),brin-din,,,,,,,The name Brindin is a rare variant on the names Brandon and Brendan. It is more closely related to the name Brindon.
