Bringfriede,f,,"German (Modern, Rare)",bring-FREE-də,,,,,,,"Coined from the German phrase Bring Friede ""bring peace!"". The name was given to girls in Germany during and after the two world wars to express the desire for peace.A notable bearer of the name is the German politician Bringfiede Kahrs who served as Senator in Bremen."
