Briog,m,,Breton|Welsh|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from Breton and Middle Welsh bri, ultimately from Proto-Celtic *brigo ""high, noble"" or *brīgos ""importance"". Briog (died c. 502) was a 5th-century Welsh holy man who became the first abbot of Saint-Brieuc in Brittany. He is one of the seven founder saints of Brittany."
