Briseus,m,Βρισεύς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Probably derived from Βρῖσα (Brisa) (also Βρήση), the name of a location in Lesbos, Greece. A connection to the Ancient Greek word βρίθω (britho) meaning ""to be heavy, weighed down; to bear down"" or ""to prevail"" has also been suggested, but this is likely folk etymology. This was an epithet of the god Dionysos in Smyrna. It was also the name of the father of Briseis."
