Brisley,f,,English (British),briss-lee(British English),,,,,,,"the name brisley is of Anglo-Saxon origin and typically functions as a locational name referring to someone from a specific place. It is most prominently tied to a small village in Norfolk, England and has historical roots dating back in medieval times. the meaning of the name brisley is the Gadfly Meadow the most common etymological breakdown suggests it comes from the Old English words brīosa (meaning Gadfly) and lēah (meaning a ""woodland clearing"" or ""meadow"")."
