Bryaxis,m,"Βρύαξις, Βρυαξις(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, sometimes also found spelled as Βρύασσις (Bryassis). Possibly derived from – or otherwise, related to – Greek βρυασμός (bryasmos), which can mean ""delight, lust"" as well as ""voluptuousness"". Also compare Greek βρυάζω (bryazo) ""to swell, to teem"". Last but not least, Greek βρυάκτης (bruaktes) or (bryaktes) also seems related, as it basically means ""the jolly god, the joyous god"" and is used in reference to the god Pan. A known bearer of this name was Bryaxis, an ancient Greek sculptor from the 4th century BC."
