Buckbeak,m,,Literature|Pet,/bʌk.biːk/(Literature),,,,,,,From the name of a fictional creature (hippogriff) that is featured on the movie Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban.
Buckie,m,,English,,,,,,,,Variant of Bucky.
Buckingham,m,,English (Archaic),,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Buckingham. A known bearer of this name was the American writer and politician Buckingham Smith (1810-1871).
Buckland,m,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Buckland.
Bucklee,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Buckley.
