Buddug,f,,Welsh,[ˈbiˑ.ðɪg],,,,,,,"Derived from Welsh budd ""profit, advantage"". It is a cognate of Boudicca, the name of a 1st-century queen of the Iceni (a Celtic people) who is known as Buddug in Welsh, and is sometimes considered a Welsh equivalent of Victoria."
Budeia,f,Βούδεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),/bjuː.ˈdiː.ə/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""oxen-yoker"", derived from Ancient Greek βοῦς (bous) meaning ""ox, cow"" and δέω (deo) meaning ""to bind, tie, fasten"". Budeia, also called Βουζύγη (Bouzyge), is the name of a daughter of Lycus in Greek mythology. It is also an epithet of the goddess Athena."
Budha,m,बुध(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈbu.d̪ʱɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""Mercury (planet)"" or ""wise, intelligent, learned"" in Sanskrit. In Hindu mythology this is the name of the god of the planet Mercury who also represents intellect and wisdom. According to legend he was born out of an affair between the moon god Chandra and the astral goddess Tara, with his birth ultimately leading to a great war."
Budhi,m,,Indonesian,/ˈbu.di/,,,,,,,Variant of Budi.
Budhy,m,,Indonesian,,,,,,,,Variant of Budi.
Budianto,m,ꦧꦸꦢꦶꦪꦤ꧀ꦠꦺꦴ(Javanese),Javanese,/bu.di.ˈan.to/(Indonesian),,,,,,,"Means ""virtuous"" from Indonesian budi meaning ""sense, mind, character""."
Budiarto,m,,Javanese|Indonesian,/bu.di.ˈar.tɔ/(Javanese)|/bu.di.ˈar.to/(Indonesian),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit बुद्धि (buddhi) meaning ""intellect, reason, mind"" and अर्थ (artha) meaning ""wealth, property""."
Budiasa,m,,Indonesian,,,,,,,,"Connected to the name Budi, which is ultimately derived from Sanskrit बुद्धि (buddhi) meaning ""intellect."""
Budig,m,,Medieval Breton,,,,,,,,Not available.
Budiharto,m,,Javanese|Indonesian,/bu.di.ˈhar.tɔ/(Javanese)|/bu.di.ˈhar.to/(Indonesian),,,,,,,Variant of Budiarto.
Budiman,m,,Indonesian,/bu.ˈdi.man/,,,,,,,"Means ""intelligent, wise"" in Indonesian, ultimately from Sanskrit बुद्धिमान (buddhimāna)."
Budimansyah,m,,Indonesian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Combination of Budiman and Persian شاه (shāh) meaning ""king""."
Budimil,m,,Croatian (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Budimir.
Budimir,m,Будимир(Serbian),Croatian|Serbian,BOO-dee-mir,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from (Serbo-)Croatian buditi ""to awaken, to (a)rouse"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"" or ""world"". In other words, this name is the Croatian and Serbian cognate of the Polish name Budzimir."
Budimira,f,,Croatian (Rare),,,,,,,,Feminine form of Budimir.
Budimirka,f,,Croatian (Rare),,,,,,,,Feminine form of Budimir.
Budiono,m,,Javanese,/bu.di.ˈɔ.nɔ/,,,,,,,"From Javanese budi meaning ""sense, mind, character"" combined with either the masculine suffix -na or the word ana meaning ""being, having, holding""."
Budisatrio,m,,Indonesian (Rare),/bu.di.sa.ˈtri.o/,,,,,,,Combination of Budi and Satrio.
Budislav,m,Будислав(Serbian),Czech|Croatian|Serbian,BOO-dis-lahv,,,,,,,"Deroved from buditi, ""to wake up"", and slava, ""fame, glory""."
Budislava,f,,Serbian (Rare)|Croatian (Rare),,,,,,,,Feminine form of Budislav.
Budivoj,m,Будивој(Serbian),Czech|Croatian|Serbian,BOO-dee-voy,,,,,,,"Derived from buditi, ""to wake up"", and voi, ""army""."
