Buga,f,,Croatian (Rare)|Slavic Mythology,BOO-gah(Croatian),,,,,,,"From the verb bugariti meaning ‘'to sing'’.According to a legend, this is a name of one of two sisters who, together with their five brothers, came to Croatian area in the 7th century."
Buğçe,f,,Turkish,boo-CHEH,,,,,,,"A multi-layered Turkish feminine name consisting of the ancient root buğ- combined with the traditional Turkic feminine diminutive/endearment suffix +çe. Depending on the historical dialect, the root carries diverse symbolic meanings, mirroring a shifting cloud that holds great power within:1. Steam/Vapor: buğ or buğu represents moist heat rising into the air, symbolizing ethereal beauty or a transformative spirit.2. Majestic Animals: Related to ancient animal roots like buğra (male camel) or buğaç/boğaç (bull), denoting innate strength.3. Nourishment: Tied to buğday (wheat), symbolizing fertility, harvest, and life-giving abundance.4. Passionate Intensity: In Old Turkic and certain Altaic dialects, buğ signifies inner heat, deep distress, or a sudden outburst of fiery emotion.5. Authority: Connected to leadership titles like başbuğ (chief, commander) or buğruk/buyruk (command), derived from the root of ultimate authority."
