Burgo,f,,Spanish (Rare),/ˈbuɾ.ɣo/,,,,,,,"From the Marian titles Virgen del Burgo and Nuestra Señora del Burgo, venerated in Alfaro (La Rioja). The original church was erected outside the walls, and later reconstructed within them. The name probably derives from burgo ""hamlet""."
Burgold,m,,"Medieval German|German (Silesian, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Composed from the Germanic name elements burg ""protection; protected place"" and walt ""to rule""."
