Byeong-eun,m,"병은(Korean Hangul)|丙垠, 炳彥, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/pjʌŋ.ɯn/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 丙 (byeong) referring to the third of the ten Heavenly Stems or 炳 (byeong) meaning ""bright, luminous, glorious"" combined with 垠 (eun) meaning ""boundary, limit, riverbank"" or 彥 (eun) meaning ""elegant, handsome, learned"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
