Caelus,m,,Roman Mythology,[ˈkäe̯.ɫ̪ʊs̠](Classical Latin),,,,,,,"Means ""sky"" or ""the heavens"" in Latin (related to the word caelum). Caelus is the Roman god of the sky, the equivalent of the Greek god Uranus."
