Caesius,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Latin adjective caesius, denoting a light blue or blue-grey colour, typically used to refer to the colour of a person's eyes. The same root may have given rise to the praenomen Caeso and perhaps also to the cognomen Caesar."
