Caireall,m,,Irish,KA-ral,,,,,,,"The meaning of this name is unknown.One bearer of this name was Caireall mac Curnain (alive in mid to late 5th century), aka Saint Kerrill, who was a Christian missionary in the kingdom called Tír Sogháin (now eastern County Galway)."
Caireallán,m,,Irish,,,,,,,,From the name Caireall combined with the diminutive suffix án.
Cairenn,f,,Irish Mythology,Care-in,,,,,,,"In medieval Irish legends, this name was borne by the mother of Niall of the Nine Hostages, a concubine of King Eochu (or Eochaid). She was treated harshly by his jealous wife Queen Mongfind, but later rescued by her son."
