Caiseal,,,Irish (Modern)|English (Modern),KUSH-el(Irish)|KASH-el(English),,,,,,,"From Irish caiseal meaning ""great stone fort"" or ""castle"". A notable bearer of the name is the Australian Sci-Fi and fantasy novelist, artist and musician Caiseal Mór. This is a modern Irish word name and not commonly used in Ireland or Northern Ireland."
