Caislín,f,,Irish (Modern)|English (Modern),KUSH-leen,,,,,,,"Supposed to mean ""little castle"" from Irish caiseal meaning ""castle"" combined with the Irish diminutive of ín. It also coincides with the rare Irish word caislín meaning ""chat"" (a type of bird). This is a modern name, most likely invented by English speakers, with no (or hardly any) usage in Ireland or Northern Ireland."
