Caliandra,f,,Portuguese,kah-lee-aun-drah,,,,,,,"Caliandra is the name of a flower, whose scientific name is Calliandra harrisii, and its denomination derives from the combination of the Greek elements Kallio (beautiful) and Andros (man), probably meaning ""beautiful and masculine"" or ""beautiful and manlike""."
