Calliopius,m,Καλλιόπιος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Related to (or derived from) Calliope, meaning ""beautiful voice"". This was the name of a Greek rhetor and official of the Roman Empire."
Calliphaea,f,Καλλιφάεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek καλός (kalos) meaning ""beautiful, good"" and possibly φάος (phaos) meaning ""light"". This was the name of one of the Ionides naiad nymphs in Greek mythology, whose spring waters were believed to cure diseases."
