Calliste,,Καλλίστη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Greek Mythology (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical)|French,/ka.list/(French),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Kalliste. In Greek mythology, this was the name of a sea nymph, who was one of the daughters of the sea-god Triton. It was also a descriptive epithet of the goddess Artemis.In French, this name is unisex: it is the French form of both Callista and Callistus, the Latinate forms of respectively Kallista (sometimes also Kalliste) and Kallistos."
