Całomierz,m,,Polish,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Polish cały ""whole, entire, complete"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic cělъ ""whole, entire"". Also compare Czech celý and Croatian cijel, both of which mean ""whole, entire"". The second element of this name is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". As such, this name roughly means ""complete peace"" or ""peace is complete""."
