Cangoşa,f,Джангоша(Karachay-Balkar),Karachay-Balkar,,,,,,,,"From the Persian جان (jan) meaning ""soul"" and Karachay-Balkar гоша (goşa) meaning ""lady""."
Cangqiong,f,苍穹(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"Cāng (苍) means ""blue"" or ""green"" while qióng (穹) means ""arch"", ""dome"", or ""elevated"". Together, it means ""heavens"", ""sky"", or ""the blue dome of heaven"". Cangqiong is the mascot for a voicebank of the same name for the Synthesizer V software."
Cangrande,m,,Medieval Italian|Literature,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Italian noun can meaning ""khan"" as well as ""dog"" combined with the Italian adjective grande meaning ""big, great"".A notable bearer of this name was the Italian nobleman Cangrande I della Scala (1291-1329). In his case, the meaning of the name might be more like ""Can the Great"", since his full name was Can Francesco della Scala. He is featured prominently in Giovanni Boccaccio's Decameron (14th century)."
