Canidia,f,,Ancient Roman,KA-nee-dee-ah(Latin),,,,,,,"From the latin adjective canus, meaning ""white"" or ""grey"", to describe an older woman with white hair. Canidia is the name of a witch in Ancient Rome, appearing several times in Horace's writing."
