Canon,m,,English,,,,,,,,"From the English word ""canon"" meaning ""a generally accepted rule or principle; works considered to be authentic; religious law; or catalog of saints"". From the Old French canon, from Latin canōn, from Ancient Greek kanón (κανών) 'measuring rod, standard'. May also be considered a variant of Cannon."
