Carabí,m,,Charrúa,KA-RA-BEE,,,,,,,Carabí was a tribe leader from Argentina whom put up resistance against the Spaniards for 15 years both in Santa Fé and Buenos Aires. He was the most respected tribe leader of his time.
Carabosse,f,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin cara, meaning ""face"", and Old French bosse meaning ""inflammation"". This describes a bubo gotten through pox. This name was first used on the wicked fairy godmother in Madame d'Aulnoy's fairy tale The Princess Mayblossom (1697), though nowadays it is more famous as the name given to the wicked fairy godmother in Tchaikovsky's ballet The Sleeping Beauty (1890)."
