Caress,f,,"English (American, Rare)|African American (Rare)",/kə.ˈɹɛs/(English),,,,,,,"Directly from the English word caress meaning ""an act or expression of kindness or affection"", ultimately from Latin carus ""beloved"". A fictional bearer was Cassandra 'Caress' Morell, a prominent character on the American soap opera Dynasty, who appeared on the show in 1986. That year 69 girls born in the United States were named Caress."
