Carpo,f,Καρπώ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Astronomy|Italian|Spanish|Portuguese,,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Καρπώ (Karpô), which is derived from Greek καρπόω (karpoô) ""to bear fruit; to reap or enjoy fruit"". In Greek mythology this was the name of one of the Horae or Seasons; Carpo was the goddess of autumn and of the harvest, that is, the fruits of summer. A moon of Jupiter also bears this name."
Carpocrates,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Karpokrates. A known bearer of this name was Carpocrates of Alexandria, the founder of an early Gnostic sect from the 2nd century AD."
