Casmilla,f,,Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"In Roman mythology, Casmilla is the mother of the legendary Volscian warrior queen, Camilla. Featured in Virgil’s Aeneid, Casmilla is a minor but pivotal figure whose name serves as the namesake for her famous daughter, the swift-footed huntress and devotee of Diana.Casmilla was the queen of the Volscian city of Privernum and married to King Metabus. While her specific fate is largely unmentioned in the epic, she is assumed to have died during the political upheaval that resulted in her husband being exiled by his own citizens. Before fleeing the city with their infant daughter, King Metabus adapted his wife's name (Casmilla) to create the name Camilla."
