Cassiphone,f,Κασσιφόνη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""fratricide, brother-killer"", derived from Ancient Greek κάσις (kasis) meaning ""sibling, brother, sister"" and φόνος (phonos) meaning ""murder, slaughter"". This was the name of the daughter of Circe and Odysseus in a later account of Greek mythology, where she killed her half-brother Telegonus for murdering her own mother. She likely originally had a different name, with Cassiphone being a later descriptive nickname."
