Cataldo,m,,Italian,cah-TAHL-doh,,,,,,,"Of debated origin and meaning. Some scholars argue that Cataldo might be an Italian adoption and adaption of Irish Cathal and Cathlarm via a corruption into Cathald by way of association with the Germanic element -ald ""old"". Others theorize a derivation from the Germanic elements hadu/hatu ""battle, combat"" and wald ""power"", while a last group of academics assume a corruption of Gaidoaldo."
