Catin,f,,French (Archaic)|Afro-American (Slavery-era)|Walloon (Archaic),"/ka.tɛ̃/(French, Afro-American (Slavery-era))",,,,,,,"Originally a (now archaic) French diminutive of Catherine. While in Louisiana French catin also means ""doll; mannequin, dummy"", in European French catin means ""harlot, slattern"" (which is no doubt the reason this form of the name fell out of usage in France)."
