Catullus,m,,Ancient Roman,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Ancient Roman cognomen Catullus with uncertain meaning. Possibly it comes from the Gaulish catu meaning ""battle"" with the diminutive suffix -ullus. In alternative it comes from Latin catulus meaning ""cub, whelp""."
