Cèilidh,f,,"Scottish Gaelic (Modern, Rare)",KAY-lee,,,,,,,"Directly taken from Scottish Gaelic cèilidh, a traditional folk music and storytelling party.Its modern usage as a name was certainly influenced by the popularity of the homophonous Kaylee and its variants. This spelling is hardly ever used in Scotland itself, where Kayleigh is the most common spelling."
