Celadon,m,Κελάδων(Ancient Greek),"Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Late Greek (Latinized, Rare)",/ˈsɛl.ə.dɒn/(English),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κελάδων (Keladôn), derived from κέλαδος (kelados) which meant ""a noise as of rushing waters; loud noise, din, clamour"". This was the name of several figures in Greek mythology, including an Ethiopian chief in the court of Cepheus, and a Lapith who fought against the centaurs. It was also the name of a stream in Elis."
