Celidonius,m,,Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Variant form of Chelidonius, which is the proper latinized form of the Greek name Chelidonios. In Christian tradition this name is sometimes given to the unnamed 'man born blind' whose sight Jesus miraculously healed, according to the Gospel of John 9:1-12. The form Celedonius belonged to an early saint, martyred ca. 300."
