Chaitanya,m,చైతన్య(Telugu)|ଚୈତନ୍ୟ(Odia)|চৈতন্য(Bengali),Telugu|Odia|Bengali,/ˈtʃai.ta.ɲa/(Telugu)|/t͡ʃɔi̯.ˈt̪ɔ.n̪jɔ/(Odia)|/ˈt͡ʃoi̯.t̪ɔnː.o/(Bengali)|/ˈtɕoi̯.t̪ɔnː.o/(Bengali),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit चैतन्य (caitanya) meaning ""consciousness, intellect, soul, spirit"". It was borne by 16th-century Bengali Hindu saint Chaitanya Mahaprabhu, who founded the Gaudiya Vaishnavi tradition."
