Chalvano,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"A variant form of Gawaine. The eldest son of King Lot of Orkney and Queen Morgawse (or Anna), Arthur’s sister or half-sister. Brother of Gareth, Gaheris and Agravaine, chief of the Orkney clan (which included his brothers and half brother Mordred), Arthur’s favorite nephew, and one of the most strongest and famous knights of the Round Table.In the medieval Italian poetry (like certain cantari) where the name ""Chalvano' is used, he is often specifically celebrated as a ""paragon of courtesy"" for his interactions with mysterious hosts."
