Charitina,f,,Late Greek (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Charitine. Saint Charitina of Amisus (also known as Charitina of Rome) was a virgin martyr from Asia Minor, distinguished by strict chastity and piety, while Charitina of Lithuania (died 1281) is a saint in the Eastern Orthodox Church."
Charitine,f,Χαριτίνη(Ancient Greek),Late Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek χαρις (charis) meaning ""grace, kindness"". This name can be viewed as a feminine equivalent of Chariton. This was the name of an early Christian martyr from Amisus, a city in Pontus in modern-day Turkey, also known as Saint Charitina."
