Chariulf,m,,Frankish,,,,,,,,"Frankish form of Hariulf. Also compare the similar-looking names Garulf and Gerulf, which can easily get confused with this name and vice versa.This name was borne by a 6th-century Frankish nobleman as well as by an obscure saint, who was one of the disciples of the Frankish missionary and saint Marculf (c. 490-558). The disciple in question is better known under the French names Cariulphe and Criou."
Chariveus,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Chariveus was a Merovingian-era nobleman who served as Count of Laon in the late 7th century, living from approximately 660 to 692 AD. He is recognized in genealogy as the husband of Saint Irmina of Oeren and the maternal grandfather of Charlemagne's mother, Bertrada of Laon."
