Ch'aska,f,,Incan Mythology|Quechua,,,,,,,,"In Incan mythology, Ch'aska (""Venus"") or Ch'aska Quyllur (""Venus star"") was the goddess of dawn and twilight, the planet Venus, flowers, maidens, and sex. She protected virgin girls. This name is of a separate etmology, with the Quechua ch'aska referring to what they thought was the brightest star but was the planet Venus. The Quechue quyllur means 'star'."
