Cherita,f,,English|American (Hispanic),che-REE-ta(English),,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. It is most likely based on the the French word chérie meaning ""darling"" combined with the Spanish suffix ita. Cherita Chen is a character in the 2001 cult movie Donnie Darko.In the case of the hispanic variant, may be a diminutive of Cher or names that begin with Cher-."
Cherith,f,,English|Northern Irish,,,,,,,,"This is a common English spelling of the Hebrew place name כְּרִית (Kərīṯ), which comes from the Hebrew root כרת (kh*r*t) meaning ""to cut off; cut down"". Cherith was a brook or wadi mentioned in the Old Testament. The prophet Elijah hid himself on the banks of the Cherith and was fed by ravens during the early part of the three years' drought which he announced to King Ahab."
