Chimera,f,Χίμαιρα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Anglicized),/kaɪ.ˈmɪɹ.ə/|/kaɪ.ˈmɛɹ.ə/|/kə.ˈmɪɹ.ə/,,,,,,,"From Latin Chimaera, which is derived from the Ancient Greek word χίμαιρα (chimaira) meaning ""(young) she-goat"" (literally ""one winter old"", cognate with χεῖμα (cheima), χειμών (cheimon) ""winter""). In Greek mythology this was the name of a monstrous fire-breathing beast which consisted of three animals merged into one, usually depicted as a lion with a goat's head on its back and a tail capped with a snake's head, and was the enemy of the hero Bellerophon."
Chimere,f,,African American|Igbo,shi-MEER|CHI-MEH-RAY,,,,,,,"From the brand of perfume called Chimère, which was introduced by Prince Matchabelli in 1979. The French word chimère means ""chimera"", a hybrid creature in Greek mythology (see Chimera), in this case referring to the new dual role experienced by the 'modern woman' of the 1970s (when high inflation and economic recession made a single-income household unsustainable for many families, pushing more wives and mothers into the workforce out of necessity).Though it has typically been used as a feminine name, this is the middle name of American (male) R&B singer Ne-Yo (1979-), real name Shaffer Chimere Smith."
