Chisaki,f,"ちさき(Japanese Hiragana)|治咲季, 小桜季, 茅早季, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-SAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 治 (chi) meaning ""cure, manage, govern, reign, administer, rule"", 小 (chi) meaning ""small, little"", 茅 (chi) meaning ""cogon grass (Imperata cylindrica), thatch"" combined with 咲 (saki) meaning ""blossom"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chisako,f,"ちさこ(Japanese Hiragana)|千紗子, 智佐子, 知佐子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-SA-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 紗 (sa) meaning ""gauze, gossamer"" and 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
