Chitragupta,m,चित्रगुप्त(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈt͡ɕit.ɾɐ.ɡup.tɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit चित्र (citra) meaning ""bright, clear, ornament, picture"" and गुप्त (gupta) meaning ""hidden, secret"". This is the name of a Hindu god who maintains a record of each person's actions on Earth (all kept in a book called the Agrasandhanī). He is the registrar of Yama, the god of death, who uses his records to decide the fates of the deceased."
