Chiwa,f,"千和, 智和, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese|Yao,CHEE-WA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 智 (chi) meaning ""wisdom, intellect"" or 散 (chi) meaning ""scatter"" combined with 和 (wa) meaning ""peace, harmony"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Chi-wai,,,Chinese (Cantonese),,,,,,,,Cantonese romanisation of Zhiwei or Cihui.
Chiwako,f,"ちわ子(Kanji/Hiragana)|千羽子, 千和子, 知和子, 智和子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-WA-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 羽 (wa) meaning ""plume, feather"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Chiwetel,m,,Igbo,CHOO-I-TEL,,,,,,,"Means ""God brings"" in Igbo."
Chi-won,m,"치원(Korean Hangul)|致遠, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕʰi.wʌn/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 致 (chi) meaning ""send, deliver, present"" combined with 遠 (won) meaning ""distant, remote, far"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Chixwaxwa,,,Mbunda,,,,,,,,"Means ""light, empty shell"" in Mbunda."
Chiya,f,"千夜, 千也, 千伸, 千彩, 茅夜, 千弥, 知也, 智八, 智弥, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ちや(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,CHEE-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 夜 (ya) meaning ""night"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyaki,f,"千夜姫, 知也希, 智弥稀, 千也希, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 夜 (ya) meaning ""night"" combined with 姫 (ki) meaning ""princess"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyako,f,"チヤコ(Japanese Katakana)|ちやこ(Japanese Hiragana)|茅夜子, 智哉子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YA-KO,,,,,,,"From 茅 (chi) meaning ""miscanthus reed"" and 夜 (ya) meaning ""night"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyami,f,"千夜美, 千夜実, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ちやみ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,CHEE-YAH-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 夜 (ya) meaning ""night"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyeko,f,,Japanese,/t͡ɕi.e̞.ko̞/,,,,,,,Archaic transcription of Chieko.
Chiyengele,,,Mbunda,,,,,,,,"Means ""red cloth belt"" in Mbunda. A notable bearer is the Senior Mbunda Chief in Bulozi, declared by King Mulena Mulambwa of the Aluyi people."
Chiyengo,,,Mbunda,,,,,,,,"Means ""big barrel"" in Mbunda."
Chiyo,f,,Shona,CHEE-YO,,,,,,,"Meaning ""grain""."
Chiyoe,f,"千代恵, 千代枝, 千代江, 千代栄(Japanese Kanji)|ちよえ(Japanese Hiragana)|チヨエ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-E,,,,,,,"This name combines 千 (sen, chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 代 (tai, dai, ka.eru, ka.waru, kawa.ru, -gawa.ri, -ga.wari, shiro, yo) meaning ""age, change, charge, convert, fee, generation, period, rate, replace, substitute"" with 恵 (e, kei, megu.mi, megu.mu) meaning ""blessing, favour, grace, kindness"", 枝 (shi, eda, e) meaning ""bough, branch, twig, limb"", 江 (kou, e) meaning ""bay, creek, inlet"" or 栄 (ei, you, e, saka.eru, ha.e, ha.eru, -ba.e) meaning ""flourish, glory, honour, prosperity, splendour.""This name was most commonly used from the Meiji Period (1868-1912) to the first half of the 20th century but nowadays, it's rarely given to girls, if given at all."
Chiyoeko,f,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Blended with (千代恵) chiyoe and ko
Chiyoho,f,"千世穂, 千代保, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-HO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" or 世 (yo) meaning ""world"" combined with 穂 (ho) meaning ""grain"" or 保 (ho) meaning ""protect, maintain"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyoka,f,千代香(Japanese Kanji),Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" combined with 香 (ka) meaning ""fragrance"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyomaru,m,"千代丸, 智誉丸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ちよまる(Japanese Hiragana)|チヨマル(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[t͡ɕì.jó̞.mà.ɾɯ̟̀ᵝ],,,,,,,"From Chiyo combined with the suffix 丸 (maru) meaning ""circle, round,"" used before the Meiji Period (1868-1912) as a suffix denoting affection (along with -maro (麿/麻呂)) and was given to boys of upper class until they came of age, usually at ages 13 to 17.This name is rarely used."
Chiyome,f,千代女(Japanese Kanji)|ちよめ(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese,[t͡ɕi.jo̞.me̞],,,,,,,"Derived from the Japanese kanji 千 (chi) meaning ""a thousand"" combined with 代 (yo) meaning ""generation; society, era"" and 女 (me) meaning ""woman; wife"".Other characters combinations are also possible."
Chiyomi,f,"千世美, 千代美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-MEE,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 世 (yo) meaning ""world"" or 代 (yo) meaning ""generation, age, replace, change, substitute"" and 美 (mi) meaning ""beauty"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyone,f,"千代音, 千世音, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-NE,,,,,,,"This name is made of 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 世 (yo, se) meaning ""world"", or 代 (yo) meaning ""generation, age, replace, substitute, period"", with 音 (ne, non) meaning ""sound, noise"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyono,f,"千代乃, 千世乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|チヨノ(Japanese Katakana)|ちよの(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/t͡ɕi.jo̞.no̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" or 世 (yo) meaning ""world"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Chiyonosuke,m,"千代之介, 千代之助, 千代乃介, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|千代ノ介(Kanji/Katakana)|ちよのすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|チヨノスケ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[t͡ɕì.jó̞.nó̞.sɨ̥́ᵝ.ké̞],,,,,,,"From Chiyo combined with the genitive particle の (no), written as 之, 乃 or the katakana equivalent ノ, and suke, originally denoting a kokushi (provincial governor) with the 2nd-highest level of suke (介), also written with other kanji like 助.One bearer of this name was actor and buyō dancer Chiyonosuke Azuma (東 千代之介), born Takayuki Wakawada (若和田 孝之) (1926-2000).This name is very rarely used."
Chiyori,f,"ちより(Japanese Hiragana)|千依, 千尚, 千頼, 千和, 知順, 千世理, 千世里, 千陽里, 智由, 智代理, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-REE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 知 (chi) meaning ""know, wisdom"" or 智 (chi) meaning ""wisdom, intellect"" combined with 依 (yori) meaning ""reliant, depend on, consequently, therefore, due to"", 尚 (yori) meaning ""esteem, furthermore, still, yet"", 頼 (yori) meaning ""trust, request"", 和 (yori) meaning ""harmony, Japanese style, peace, soften, Japan"", or 順 (yori) meaning ""obey, order, turn, right, docility, occasion"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyosaburo,m,,Japanese,CHEE-YO-SA-BOO-RO,,,,,,,Not available.
Chiyosaburou,m,,Japanese,CHEE-YO-SA-BOO-RO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Chiyosaburo.
Chiyoshi,,"チヨシ(Japanese Katakana)|ちよし(Japanese Hiragana)|智良, 知義, 千喜, 千芳, 知代司, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 吉 (yoshi) meaning ""good luck"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyosuke,m,"千代介, 千代輔, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),CHEE-YO-SKE:,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi, sen) meaning ""thousand"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generation, era"", and 輔, 助, or 介 (suke) means ""help, assist"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Chiyou,m,蚩尤(Chinese),Chinese Mythology,/ʈʂʰɚ˥˥.joʊ˧˥/(Chinese),,,,,,,"From Chinese 蚩 (chī) meaning ""ignorant, worm"" and 尤 (yóu) meaning ""outstanding, particular"". This is the name of a mythological tribal chieftain who famously opposed the Yellow Emperor. Various sources describe him as a horned humanoid with four eyes, six arms, and hoofed feet, with 81 brothers-in-arms. He was defeated and killed at the Battle of Zhuolu, but is said to have given rise to several ethnic minorities in southern China. The Hmong people in particular venerate him as their ancestor."
Chiyoyuki,m,"千代幸, 千代之, 千代有希, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),CHEE-YO-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 代 (yo) meaning ""world, society"", 幸 (yuki) meaning ""happiness, good fortune, luck"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Chiyu,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Chiyuu.
Chi-yuan,,"祺缘, 启元, etc.(Chinese)|祺緣, 啟元, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Taiwanese,/t͡ɕʰi.ɥɛn/(Chinese),,,,,,,Wade-Giles romanization of Qiyuan used in Taiwan.
Chiyuki,f,"知幸, 千雪, 智雪, 千幸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 幸 (yuki) meaning ""happiness, fortune"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Chiyuko,f,"茅友子, 茅悠子, 茅結子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),CHEE-YOO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 茅 (chi) meaning ""miscanthus reed"", 悠 (yu) meaning ""permanence"", and 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyumi,f,"千友美, 知友美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 友 (yu) meaning ""friend"" and 美 (mi) meaning ""beauty, beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyuno,f,知優乃(Japanese Kanji)|ちゆの(Japanese Hiragana)|チユノ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),CHEE-YOO-NO,,,,,,,"From 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"", 由 (yu) meaning ""cause, reason, origin"", and 乃 (no) meaning ""from, therefore, accordingly."" Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyuri,f,"ちゆり(Japanese Hiragana)|千百合, 知友莉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YOO-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 百合 (yuri) meaning ""lily."" Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyuu,,"千友, 知勇, 知友, 智遊, 痴遊, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-YUU:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 友 (yuu) meaning ""friend"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chiyva,,,Hindi|Indian,Cha-eye-va,,,,,,,The meaning of the name Chiyva is linked with destruction.
Chizaram,,,Nigerian|Igbo,,,,,,,,Means 'God answered me' in Igbo.
Chizitara,,,Igbo,,,,,,,,"Means ""God sent"" in Igbo."
Chizu,f,"チヅ(Japanese Katakana)|ちづ(Japanese Hiragana)|千都, 千鶴, 智珠, 智津, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-ZOO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Chidzu.
Chizue,f,"千鶴子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-ZOO-EH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 鶴 (tsu) meaning ""crane (bird)"" and 恵 (e) meaning ""favour, benefit"". Other kanji combinations are usable."
Chizumi,f,千鶴美(Japanese Kanji),Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Japanese 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" and 鶴 (tsu) meaning ""crane (bird)"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful, beauty"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Chizuo,m,"智津夫, 千津雄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ちづお(Japanese Hiragana)|チヅオ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/t͡ɕi.zɨᵝ.o̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 智 (chi) meaning ""wisdom, intellect"" or 千 (chi) meaning ""thousand"" combined with 津 (zu) meaning ""harbour, port, ferry"" and 夫 (o) meaning ""man, husband"" or 雄 (o) meaning ""hero, male, manly"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well.This was the real name of Japanese religious leader Shoko Asahara (1955-2018), who was born as Chizuo Matsumoto."
Chizuruko,f,"千鶴子, 智奉子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,CHEE-ZOO-ROO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 智 (chi) meaning ""intellect, knowledge, wisdom"", 鶴 (tsuru) meaning ""crane (bird)"" or 奉 (zuru) meaning ""to offer, to present"" and 子 (ko) meaning ""child"", as well as other character combinations."
Chizuye,f,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant of Chizue.
Chjara,f,,Corsican,,,,,,,,Corsican form of Clara.
