Choerilus,m,Χοιρίλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Possibly a diminutive form of Χοῖρος (Choiros) meaning ""young pig"" as well as ""fish of the Nile"". Choerilus of Samos was an epic poet of Samos, who flourished at the end of the 5th century BC."
Choerine,f,Χοιρίνη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"From the Greek name Χοιρίνη (Choirine), a feminine derivative of Choiros, which was itself derived from χοῖρος (choiros) meaning ""young pig"". This name was borne by a wife of the 5th-century BC Greek tragedian Euripides.Choerine is an attested Athenian name, but it could have easily been used for obscene puns, as the word χοῖρος (choiros) was also used to mean ""vulva"" - comic poets frequently punned on this word and its compounds."
