Chundi,f,चुन्दी(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/ˈt͡ɕun̪.d̪iː/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly from Sanskrit चुन्दी (cundī) meaning ""procuress, bawd"" or चुण्टी (cuṇṭī) meaning ""small well, reservoir"". This is the name of a bodhisattva in Buddhist tradition, particularly revered in China. She is associated with protection, spiritual practice, the purification of negative karma and the attainment of Buddhahood."
