Çınla,f,,Medieval Turkic,[tʃɯn.ɫɑ],,,,,,,"The imperative form of the ancient Turkic verb Çınlayu-, meaning ""to resonate,"" ""to echo,"" or ""to sound clear like a bell."" Rooted in Çın (the absolute truth/reality), Çınla serves as an existential call to ""resonate with the truth."" It describes a person who lives authentically, whose words and actions ring with clarity and honesty, and who cannot be swayed by falsehood."
