Cisne,,,South American|Central American (Rare),/ˈsiz.ne/(Latin American Spanish),,,,,,,"From the Ecuadorian titles of the Virgin Mary, La Virgen de El Cisne and Nuestra Señora de El Cisne, meaning ""The Virgin of El Cisne"" and ""Our Lady of El Cisne"" respectively (coinciding with the word for ""swan"").She is venerated at the basilica in El Cisne in the southern province of Loja.This name is also used in Nicaragua, albeit very rarely on males."
