Cissonius,m,,Celtic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Cissonius was an ancient Gaulish/Celtic god. After Visucius, Cissonius was the most common name of the Gaulish/Celtic Mercury; around seventeen inscriptions dedicated to him extend from France and Southern Germany into Switzerland.Cissonius was represented either as a bearded, helmeted man riding a ram and carrying a wine cup, or else as a young man with winged helmet and herald's staffaccompanied by a rooster and goat.The name has been interpreted as meaning ""courageous"", ""remote"" or else ""carriage-driver"". He was probably a god of trade and protector of travellers, since Mercury exercised similar functions in the Roman pantheon."
