Cleocritus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Kleokritos. This name was borne by an eponymous archon of Athens, who lived in the 5th century BC."
Cleodalis,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"The seneschal of King Leodegan of Carmelide. He assisted Leodegan, and Arthur, in battles against the Saxons at Carhaix and Aneblayse, and he led a battalion in Arthur’s war against Rome."
Cleodie,f,,"English (British, Rare)|Scottish (Rare)","KLOW-dee(British English, Scottish)",,,,,,,Allegedly derived from the Scottish surname McLeod.
Cleodora,f,,"Greek Mythology (Latinized)|American (South, Archaic)",/kli.oʊ.ˈdɔːɹ.ə/(American (South)),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Kleodora. In Greek mythology, Cleodora was a nymph of Mount Parnassos in Phokis. She was one of the prophetic Thriai, nymphs who divined the future by throwing stones or pebbles. She was loved by the sea god Poseidon and had a son called Parnassos by him. This name was also borne by one of the Danaids (i.e., the 50 daughters of Danaus)."
