Cneajna,f,,Medieval Romanian,,,,,,,,"Derived from Romanian cneaz (ultimately from Proto-Slavic *kъnędzь via Ukrainian and Russian князь (knjazʹ)) ""prince; ruler of a state or principality in past times"". This name was borne by the daughter of Alexandru cel Bun (Alexander the Good in English) who eventually married Vlad II Dracul."
