Cobain,m,,English (Rare),/koʊ.ˈbeɪn/,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Cobain, likely given in honor of Lead singer and guitarist of Nirvana, Kurt Cobain (1967-1994)."
Cobalt,m,,English,KO-bahlt,,,,,,,"From the metal or the shade of blue. Derived from German kobold, a type of house spirit. This in turn, has a few possible etymologies. One is that it come from Greek koba'los, meaning ""rogue"". Another theory is that it comes from the Old High German root chubisi, ""house, building, hut"" and the suffix -old meaning ""to rule""."
