Cocalus,m,Κώκαλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek κόκκαλος (kokkalos) meaning ""pine kernel"", itself a diminutive of κόκκος (kokkos) ""seed, grain, kernel"". This was the name of a legendary Sician king, who sheltered Daedalus after his escape from the Labyrinth."
