Codrus,m,Κόδρος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),/ˈkɒd.rəs/(English)|/ˈkoʊd.rəs/(English)|/ˈko.ðros/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Κόδρος (Kodros), which is probably derived from Ancient Greek κυδρός (kydros) meaning ""glorious, renowned, illustrious"" (see kydos). In Greek mythology, this was the name of a legendary king of Athens."
