Cointus,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Kointos, which is the hellenized form of the Latin name Quintus. In other words, this name is basically a latinization of a name that is already latinate in origin.This name was borne by Cointus of Phrygia (who is better known as Quintus of Phrygia), a martyr and saint from the 3rd century AD."
