Colbie,,,"English (Modern, Rare)",[ˈkoʊl.bi],,,,,,,Feminine form of Colby. A known bearer is the American singer-songwriter Colbie Caillat (1985-).
Colden,m,,"English (American, Rare)",,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Colden. Its rise in recent years may be due to similar sounding names like Colten.
Coldin,m,,English,KOL-DIN,,,,,,,"Coldin is a boy's name meaning ""dark valley"" that comes from the Old English name Colden."
Colebee,m,,Indigenous Australian,KOHL-bee,,,,,,,"This was the name of two famous Australian Aborigines, recorded in the early history of Sydney. The meaning of the name is yet unknown. Also, this particular spelling may be an anglicized form of the original Aboriginal name, since it is close in appearance to English (sur)names like Coleby and Colby."
