Consider,,,English (Puritan),,,,,,,,"Late Middle English from Old French considerer, from Latin considerare ""examine"", perhaps based on sidus, sider- ""star"". Possibly referring to Hebrews 10:24, ""And let us consider one another to provoke unto love and to good works"" or Matthew 6:28, ""And why take ye thought for raiment? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin."""
