Contessina,f,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"Diminutive of Contessa. Contessina de' Medici (1478-1515) was a daughter of the Florentine ruler Lorenzo ""the Magnificent"", named in honour of his paternal grandmother - Contessina de' Bardi (c.1390-1473)."
Contina,f,,"English (American, Modern)",,,,,,,,"Possibly a contraction of Constantina, or a creation using the popular name suffix -tina. Its spike in popularity in the States during the 70s coincides with similar names including Katina and Corina."
