Coosaponakeesa,f,,Creek,koo-suh-poe-nuh-kee-suh,,,,,,,"Means ""lovely fawn"" in Creek. Mary Musgrove, born Coosaponakeesa, was a cultural liaison between colonial Georgia and her Native American community in the mid-eighteenth century."
