Cumhaill,m,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Cumhaill mac Trénmhoir was a powerful warrior and chieftain of the Fianna, an elite, roving band of hunter-warriors who protected Ireland. His name derives from the Old Irish Cumall, which translates roughly to ""slave"" or ""bond-servant,"" though in tales, he was far from it. He was renowned for his strength, and was deeply tied to the land and the magical legacy of the Fianna.Cumhaill was the father of Ireland’s most famous hero, Fionn mac Cumhaill (Finn McCool). Primarily known as a tragic catalyst for the Fenian Cycle, his legacy sets into motion the adventures of his illustrious son."
