Cuthswiþ,f,,Anglo-Saxon,/ˈkuːθ.swiθ/(Old English),,,,,,,"Means ""famously strong"", derived from Old English cuþ ""known, familiar"" and swiþ ""strong"".This name was borne by a 7th-century abbess of Inkberrow (near Worcester) in England."
