Cutter,m,,English (Modern)|Popular Culture,KUT-ər,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Cutter.In the American television cartoon 'G.I. Joe', Cutter is the nickname of Skip A. Stone, the G.I. Joe team's hovercraft pilot. He first appeared in the cartoon in 1984 and has since made numerous appearances in the cartoon series and comic books and has been released as an action figure in the G.I. Joe toy line."
Cutzi,f,,Purépecha|New World Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""moon"" in Purépecha. In pre-Hispanic Purépecha mythology, the moon goddess Nana Cutzi (often translated as ""the curved mother"" or ""mother encorvada"") forms a fundamental cosmic pair with Tata Jurhiata, the sun god, and their union is believed to have brought light to the cosmos."
