Czar,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",ZAHR(English)|TSAHR(English)|SAHR(English),,,,,,,"From the English word czar, an alternate spelling of tsar meaning ""Russian emperor, Slavic monarch"", itself derived from Russian царь (carʹ), ultimately derived from Latin cognomen Caesar, used to metaphorically mean ""emperor, ruler, dictator"". The American rapper Meek Mill and his wife Milan Harris gave this name to their son in 2020."
