Dáinn,m,,Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""died"" in Old Norse (the past participle of the verb deyja ""to die""). This is the name of three characters in Norse mythology: a dwarf, a representative of the elves, and one of the stags that graze on the branches of Yggdrasill."
