Dalga,f,,Turkish,/ˈdaɫ.ɡa/,,,,,,,"Dalga is a name embodying the relentless, rhythmic energy of the ocean. It evolves from the archaic talkaġ or talkan, meaning ""ripple"" or ""wave."" This traces back to the Middle Turkic verb talka- (""to ripple, to churn""), which finds its origin in the Old Turkic tal- (""to strike,"" ""to whip""). Like a wave that strikes the shore and returns to the sea, this name symbolizes constant movement, power, and the cyclical nature of life."
