Damia,f,Δαμία(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek δᾶ (da) meaning ""earth, land, ground"" and μαῖα (maia) meaning ""good mother, dame"", a form of address for a woman older than the speaker. This was the name of the goddess and Hora of the fertile earth, worshipped alongside Auxesia. She may have also been worshipped as Carpo. It was also an epithet of the goddess Demeter (while her daughter, Persephone, was occasionally afforded the title Auxesia)."
