Damkina,f,𒀭𒁮𒆠𒈾(Sumerian Cuneiform),Near Eastern Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""true wife"", deriving from the Akkadian element kīnu ""honest, trustworthy, faithful"". The Akkadian name for the goddess Damgalnuna. She was the consort of Enki and mother of the god Marduk. One of her titles was 'banat shimti' meaning 'creator of fate', influenced by the goddess Shimti."
