Dandara,f,,Brazilian|History|Afro-American (Slavery-era),,,,,,,,"The name of an Afro-Brazilian warrior of the colonial period of Brazil who was part of the Quilombo dos Palmares, a settlement of Afro-Brazilian people who freed themselves from enslavement, in the present-day state of Alagoas. After being arrested on February 6, 1694, Dandara committed suicide, refusing to return to a life of slavery. She is a mysterious figure today, because not much is known about her life. Most of the stories about her are varied and disconnected. She was the wife of Zumbi dos Palmares, the last king of the Quilombo dos Palmares."
