Daráine,f,,Irish (Rare),dar-AWN-yeh,,,,,,,"Allegedly means ""daughter of Áine"" (from the Old Irish prefix der ""daughter"" and the name of the Irish goddess Áine). This is borne by Irish television presenter Daráine Mulvihill (c. 1983-), whose father, Liam Mulvihill, served as director general of the Gaelic Athletic Association (GAA) from 1979 until 2008."
