Daromir,m,Даромир(Bulgarian),Bulgarian|Croatian|Polish,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Slavic dar ""gift, present"", which in turn is derived from Proto-Slavic darъ ""gift, present"". Compare modern Polish darować ""to donate, to gift"" and Czech darovat ""to donate, to give"", as well as Proto-Slavic dati ""to give"". The second element of this name is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". As such, this name roughly means ""to gift peace"" or ""peace is a gift""."
