Dekabrist,m,Декабрист(Russian),Soviet|Russian,/dʲɪ.kɐ.ˈbrʲist/(Russian),,,,,,,"Derived from Russian декабрист (dekabrist) meaning ""Decembrist"", which is a term used to refer to someone who participated in (or sympathized with) the Decembrist revolt of 1825. This name was used by Communist parents who were eager to reject traditional names. Also compare the related name Dekabrin."
