Đế Lai,m,,Chinese Mythology (Vietnamized)|Vietnamese Mythology,/ʔɗe˧˦ laːj˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/ʔɗej˨˩˦ laːj˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/ʔɗej˦˥ laːj˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 帝 (đế) meaning ""emperor"" and 來 (lai) meaning ""to come, to arrive"". This is the name of the sixth emperor in the line of Thần Nông. According to the Complete Annals of Đại Việt (Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư), he is the father of Âu Cơ."
