Demitris,m,Δημήτρης(Greek),Greek,thee-MEE-trees,,,,,,,"• Origin: Greek • Meaning: “Follower of Demeter,” with Demeter being the Greek goddess of agriculture and harvest. • Usage: Common in Greece, often shortened to Dimitri or Mitsos as nicknames.• From Greek Δημήτρης (Dēmḗtrēs), derived from the goddess Demeter (Greek goddess of agriculture)."
