Desire,,,English (Puritan),/dɪ.ˈzaɪɹ/|/di.ˈzaɪɹ/,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin desidero ""to long for; to wish for; to desire"" (via Old French desir). This name was first used in the 16th century by the Puritans, probably with the intended meaning of ""desire the Lord"". It is also a diminutive or variant of Desiderata or Desiderius, etc."
