Dexikleia,f,Δεξίκλεια(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Dexikles.
Dexikles,m,Δεξικλῆς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from the Greek noun δέξις (dexis) meaning ""reception"", which is ultimately derived from the Greek verb δέχομαι (dechomai) meaning ""to take, to receive, to accept, to welcome"". Also compare the Greek verb δεξιάζω (dexiazo) meaning ""to approve"".Neither are to be confused with the Greek noun δεξιά (dexia) meaning ""right hand"" or the Greek adjective δεξιός (dexios) meaning ""on the right hand, on the right side"".The second element of this name is derived from the Greek noun κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory"". As such, the meaning of this name is something along the lines of ""reception of glory"" or ""welcoming glory""."
Dexileos,m,Δεξίλεως(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from the Greek noun δέξις (dexis) meaning ""reception"", which is ultimately derived from the Greek verb δέχομαι (dechomai) meaning ""to take, to receive, to accept, to welcome"". Also compare the Greek verb δεξιάζω (dexiazo) meaning ""to approve"".Neither are to be confused with the Greek noun δεξιά (dexia) meaning ""right hand"" or the Greek adjective δεξιός (dexios) meaning ""on the right hand, on the right side"".The second element of this name is derived from the Attic Greek noun λεώς (leos) meaning ""the people"" (see Leos). As such, the meaning of this name is something along the lines of ""reception of the people"" or ""welcomed by the people""."
Dexing,f,德幸(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 德 (dé) meaning ""heart, mind, morals, virtue"" and 幸 (xìng) meaning ""luck, favour, fortunately""."
Dexios,m,Δέξιος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""the skilful, the right, the adroit"" in Ancient Greek, derived from δεξιός (dexios) meaning ""on the right (hand, side)"" as well as ""fortunate"", ""northerly, northward"", and metaphorically ""dexterous, ready, skilful, clever; courteous""."
Dexip,m,,Catalan,,,,,,,,Catalan form of Dexippos via its latinized form Dexippus.
Dexiphanes,m,Δεξιφάνης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,"/dek.si.pʰá.nɛːs/(Attic Greek)|/ðek.si.ˈɸa.nis/(Koine Greek, Byzantine Greek)|/ðek.si.ˈfa.nis/(Constantinopolitan Greek)",,,,,,,"Means ""a welcome appearance"" or ""to appear welcoming"", derived from Greek δέξις (dexis) meaning ""reception"", itself from δέχομαι (dekhomai) meaning ""to accept, receive"", and φάνης (phanes) meaning ""appearing""."
