Dharmakar,m,धर्माकर(Sanskrit),Sanskrit,,,,,,,,"Dharmakar or Dharmakara is a name of Asian origin coming from the Sanskrit धर्म (""Dharma"", virtue, moral law, that which sustains creation, order of the world) + कर (""kāra"", hand, part of the body held in the forearm by the wrist). The name Dharmakara carries with it the message of justice and righteousness. A just and disciplined man. This name is mentioned in the Puranas (पुराण, purāṇas) and is the birth name of Amitabha Buddha.According to Nepalese tradition, the first ruler of Nepal was Dharmakar. This mythical figure related to the Nepalese genesis was said to have been a Chinese king and accompanied a wise bodhisattva to the Kathmandu Valley, then a lake. The bodhisattva stopped the flow of water and made the region habitable. The bodhisattva established a city in the valley, Manjupattan, and, after making Dharmakara ruler of Manjupattan, returned to China.Thus, Dharmakar is a name associated with Buddhism and Sanskrit tradition, as well as referring to royalty and Nepalese history. It's a strong, noble, and ancient name."
