Dhiran,m,Դիրան(Armenian),Armenian,Dee-ran,,,,,,,"is derived from ""Der"" or ""Dir,"" which means ""God,"" essentially translating to ""belonging to God"" or ""gift from God."" Tiran (c. 300/305 – 358 AD) known also as Tigranes VII, Tigranes or Diran was an Armenian prince who served as a Roman client king of Arsacid Armenia from 339 until 350. He was a contemporary of and is associated with the life of Sarkis the Warrior and his son, Martiros."
