Dhrishti,,धृष्टि(Hindi),Indian,dh-rish-Tea|dh-rish-Tee,,,,,,,"MEANING - bold, daring, courage. It should not be confused with name Drishti दृष्टि Origin- Sanskrit, Indian, Tamil, sikh, Buddhist, Hindi, Mauritian, Fijian It was the name of a minister of king Dasharatha"
Dhritarashtra,m,धृतराष्ट्र(Sanskrit),Hinduism|Buddhism,/d̪ʱr̩.t̪ɐ.ˈɾɑːʂ.ʈɾɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""supporter of the nation"" from Sanskrit धृत (dhṛta) meaning ""held, borne, maintained, supported"" and राष्ट्र (rāṣṭra) meaning ""kingdom, empire, people, nation"". In the Hindu epic the Mahabharata Dhritarashtra is the blind ruler of the Kuru kingdom. In Buddhist mythology this is also the name of one of the Four Heavenly Kings who acts as a guardian deity of the east."
Dhriti,f,ध्रिति(Nepali)|धृति(Hindi)|ధృతి(Telugu)|த்ரிதி(Tamil)|धृति(Sanskrit)|धृति(Sanskrit),Nepali|Indian|Hinduism|Sanskrit|Indian,dhrɪtɪ|Dhr-uti|Dhre-te,,,,,,,"Meaning ""She Who Has Courage and Patience""."
