Dhu al-Kifl,m,ذو الكفل(Arabic),Quranic,/ðu‿l.ˈkifl/(Arabic),,,,,,,"Means ""possessor of the lot"" from Arabic ذو (dhū) meaning ""possessor, owner"" combined with كفل (kifl) meaning ""lot, portion, share"". In Islamic tradition this is the name of a prophet commonly identified with Ezekiel from the Bible."
Dhu al-Qarnayn,m,ذو القرنين(Arabic),Quranic,/ðu‿l.ˈqar.najn/(Arabic),,,,,,,"Means ""possessor of the two horns"" from Arabic ذو (dhū) meaning ""possessor, holder"" combined with قرنين (qarnayn) meaning ""(two) horns"". This is the name of a legendary ruler mentioned in the Quran who is sometimes identified as Alexander the Great."
