Dio,m,Δηώ(Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized)|Italian|Greek (Rare),DEE-o(Italian),,,,,,,"Latinized form of Dion. In modern-day Italy, this name is also a short form of Diodato, Dionisio and other names starting with Dio-.Known bearers of this name include the 1st-century Greek orator and philosopher Dio Chrysostom and the 3rd-century Roman historian Cassius Dio (also called Dio Cassius)."
