Diocorystes,m,"Διοκορυστὴς, Διοκορυστής(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek Διός (Dios) meaning ""of Zeus"" and κορυστής (korystes) meaning ""helmed warrior, armed warrior"", itself from κόρυς (korys) ""helmet"". This was the name of one of the fifty sons of king Aegyptus in Greek mythology, who was married to the Daenid Hippodamia and killed by her on their wedding night."
