Diotrephes,m,Διοτρέφης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Biblical,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek Διος (Dios) ""of Zeus"" combined with Greek τρέφω (trepho) ""to nourish, to feed"" (also see Trophimus). This was the name of a minor character from the bible, who was mentioned in 3 John, verses 9–11."
