Dipankar,m,দীপঙ্কর(Bengali)|দীপাংকৰ(Assamese),Bengali|Assamese,/ˈd̪i.pɔŋ.kɔɾ/(Bengali)|/ˈd̪i.pɔŋ.kɔɹ/(Bengali),,,,,,,Modern form of Dipankara.
Dipankara,m,दीपंकर(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/ˈd̪iː.pɐŋ.kɐ.ɾɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""light maker"" from Sanskrit दीप (dīpa) meaning ""lamp, light"" and कर (kara) meaning ""maker"". In Buddhist tradition this is the name of the fourth of the 27 buddhas preceding Siddhartha Gautama, known in Pali as Dīpaṃkara. According to legend he confirmed that Sumedha, a previous incarnation of Siddhartha, would become a buddha in a future life."
