Dipanwita,f,দীপান্বিতা(Bengali),Bengali,/ˈd̪i.panː.i.t̪a/,,,,,,,"From Sanskrit दीपान्विता (dīpānvitā) meaning ""possessing lamps"", derived from दीप (dīpa) meaning ""lamp, light"" and अन्वित (anvita) meaning ""endowed with, possessing, having""."
Dipendra,m,दीपेंद्र(Hindi)|दीपेन्द्र(Nepali),Hindi|Nepali,,,,,,,,"Means ""lord of light"" from Sanskrit दीप (dīpa) meaning ""lamp, light"" combined with the name of the Hindu god Indra, used here to mean ""lord""."
