Dolos,m,Δόλος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Roman Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek δόλος (dolos), which literally means ""bait"" and has a figurative meaning of ""deceit, guile, treachery, trickery"". In Classical mythology, this was the name of the personification of craftiness and trickery, an apprentice of the titan Prometheus."
