Dominie,,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Dominie, or directly from the Scottish English word ""dominie"" meaning ""schoolmaster"", itself deriving from the Latin domine, which is the vocative case of dominus meaning ""lord"", ""master"". Alternatively could perhaps be seen as a nickname or feminine form of Dominicor Dominique. A notable female bearer is English folk musician Dominie Hooper."
