Doriel,,דוריאל(Hebrew),Hebrew|Literature,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""God's generation"" in Hebrew, in which case it would be derived from Hebrew dor ""generation"" (see also Dor) combined with Hebrew el ""God"". This is the name of a character in Elie Wiesel's novel ""A Mad Desire to Dance""."
