Dren,m,Дрен(Serbian),Serbian|Croatian,DRREN,,,,,,,"From дрен/dren meaning European Cornel (Cornus mas) (type of dogwood). The tree is a symbol of strength and health in Serbian culture, having an idiom ""здрав к'о дрен/zdrav ko dren"" which equates to English ""fit as a fiddle"". Therefore, the name is meant to denote ""a strong and healthy individual"". The region of Drenica in Kosovo is named after it."
