Duibhín,f,,Irish (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from Gaelic dubh ""dark, black"" combined with a diminutive suffix."
Duibhne,,,Irish|Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""ill-tempered, surly"", derived from dub ""black""."
Duibhshíth,m,,Irish,/d̪ˠuvˠ.ʃiː/,,,,,,,"Means ""black peace"" from Irish dubh meaning ""black"" and síth meaning ""peace""."
Duibhuidhir,m,,Old Irish,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Irish dub ""black"" and odar ""dun-coloured, greyish brown, tan"". Alternately, the second element could be eidhir ""sense, wisdom""."
Duìch,m,,Lombard,,,,,,,,Cremish Lombard form of Ludovicus.
Duihong,,"对红, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Duilia,f,,Italian,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Duilio.
Duilin,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Duilin was the name of the lord of the House of the Swallow in Gondolin. He was said to be the greatest bowman of Gondolin, and the swiftest elf amongst them. He died in the year FA 510 during the Fall of Gondolin, when he was shot by a fiery bolt from a Balrog."
