Dynþór,m,,"Icelandic (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Old Norse dynr meaning ""din, noise"" combined with Þór. This was the name of Denethor in the Icelandic translation of The Lord of the Rings (1954) by J. R. R. Tolkien. It was first accepted as an Icelandic given name in 2013."
