Dyr,m,,History,,,,,,,,"Variant of Dir recorded in the Nikon Chronicle. The name is likely derived from Old Norse dýr ""deer, wild animal"" or dýrr ""dear, precious""."
Dyra,f,,Swedish (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Norse element dýr ""deer; wild animal"" (though it is also associated with dýrr ""dear; expensive""), perhaps via the Old Swedish (masculine) name Dyre or an Old Norse name such as Dýrhildr or Dýrfinna. It has been used in Sweden since 1875."
