Dysis,f,Δύσις(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,DIE-sis,,,,,,,"Means ""sunset"" in Ancient Greek, literally ""sinking, lowering (of the sun or stars)"", as well as ""quarter where the sun sets, west"" and ""hiding place"". In Greek mythology, this was the name of the eleventh of the twelve Horae, goddesses of the hours, who presided over the hour of sunset. She was the nursemaid of Selene, goddess of the moon."
