Ealhflæd,f,,Anglo-Saxon,/ˈæ͜ɑlx.flæd/(Old English)|/ˈæ͜ɑɫx.flæd/(Old English),,,,,,,"Derived from the Old English elements ealh ""temple"" and flæd, possibly meaning ""beauty""."
