Edukondalu,m,ఏడుకొండలు(Telugu),Telugu,,,,,,,,"Means ""seven hills"" from Telugu ఏడు (ēḍu) meaning ""seven"" and కొండలు (koṇḍalu) meaning ""hills"". This is the Telugu name for Sapthagiri, a range of seven sacred hills in the town of Tirumala in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. In Hindu tradition the hills are believed to represent the seven heads of the naga king Shesha."
