Eidyia,f,"Εἰδυῖα, Ἰδυῖα(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek εἰδώς (eidos), present active participle of οἶδα (oida) meaning ""to know, be skilled in"". In Greek mythology she was the mother of the sorceress Medea, and may have personified 'the magical power of the eye, which in Greek superstition was the source of the witch's supernatural power - strengthened by the beams of the ancestral sun.'"
