Eito,m,"栄十, 栄人, 栄登, 栄都, 永人, 瑛士, 瑛斗, 英斗, 英杜, 英登, 詠人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,E:-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 栄 (ei) meaning ""glory, honour"", 永 (ei) meaning ""eternity"", 瑛 (ei) meaning ""sparkle of jewelry, crystal"", 英 (ei) meaning ""excellent, fine"" or 詠 (ei) meaning ""recitation, poem, song, composing"" combined with 十 (to) meaning ""ten"", 人 (to) meaning ""person"", 登 (to) meaning ""ascend, climb up"", 都 (to) meaning ""metropolis, capital, all, everything"", 士 (to) meaning ""gentleman, scholar, samurai"", 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation or 杜 (to) meaning ""woods, grove"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
