Elasah,m,אלעשה(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Elasah, meaning ""made by God,"" was the name of two individuals mentioned in the Bible."
Elatha,m,,Irish,,,,,,,,"In Irish mythology, Elatha was a king of the Fomorians. Elatha is described as being the ""beautiful Miltonic prince of darkness with golden hair"". He was the son of Delbaeth and a king of the Fomor, and he was the father of Bres by Eriu, a woman of the Tuatha Dé Danann. He came to her over the sea in a vessel of silver, himself having the appearance of a young man with yellow hair, wearing clothes of gold and five gold torcs. He was one of the Fomor who took part in the Second Battle of Magh Tuireadh.During the Second Battle of Magh Tuireadh, Elatha watched over his son the Dagda's magic harp, Uaithne, sometimes called Dur-da-Bla, ""the Oak of Two Blossoms,"" and sometimes Coir-cethar-chuin, ""the Four-Angled Music."" He is said to have a sense of humor and a sense of nobility."
