Elete,f,Ηλετη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, possibly related to Ancient Greek ἀλετός (aletos) meaning ""grinding"" or λιτή (lite) meaning ""prayer, entreaty"". This was the name of one of the Horai in Greek mythology, goddesses associated with the hours of a day and the months of a year. She presided over the eighth hour of the day, devoted to prayer, and was also known as Telete."
