Eleuther,m,Ἐλευθήρ(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek ἐλεύθερος (eleutheros) meaning ""free"". In Greek mythology Eleuther was the son of the god Apollo and Aithusa or Aethusa. It might also be an anglicized form of Eleutherius."
Eleuthera,f,Ἐλευθέρα(Ancient Greek),English (Rare)|Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἐλεύθερος (eleutheros) meaning ""free"". This is the name of an island in the Bahamas which was originally named Eleutheria; ἐλευθερία (eleutheria) means ""freedom"" in Greek, while ἐλεύθερα (eleuthera) means ""free"". This is also the name of a granddaughter of Patricia Knatchbull, 2nd Countess Mountbatten: Eleuthera du Breuil (1986-; named after the island, on which she was conceived)."
Éleuthère,m,,History (Ecclesiastical)|French (Rare),,,,,,,,French form of Eleutherius. This name was borne by French-born American industrialist Éleuthère Irénée du Pont (1771-1834).
