Elevación,f,,South American (Rare),/e.le.βa.ˈsjon/(Latin American Spanish),,,,,,,"From the Ecuadorian titles of the Virgin Mary, La Virgen de la Elevación and Nuestra Señora de la Elevación, meaning ""The Virgin of the Elevation"" and ""Our Lady of the Elevation"" respectively.She is venerated at the cathedral basilica in Ambato in the central province of Tungurahua."
Eleven,,,"Popular Culture|English (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From the name of the number 11, from Old English endleofon, itself from Proto-Germanic *ainalif meaning ""one left (from ten)"". This is the name of the protagonist of the Netflix series Stranger Things."
