Eliad,,אליעד(Hebrew),"Hebrew (Modern, Rare)",e-lee-AHD,,,,,,,"Combination of the names Eli 2 and Ad means ""My God is eternal"" in Hebrew, it can be also variant of the name El'ad."
Eliada,m,אֶלְיָדָע(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""God knows"" in Hebrew, derived from the roots אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"" and ידע (yada') meaning ""to know"" (compare Jada). In the Old Testament this is the name of several characters, including a son of King David."
