Éloa,f,,French|Literature,,,,,,,,"French form of Eloah'Éloa, ou La sœur des anges' ('Éloa, or the Sister of the Angels'), published in 1824, is French poet, playwright, and novelist Alfred de Vigny's epic tripartite philosophic poem of Eloa, an innocent angel who falls in love with a stranger at odds with God. It is made clear that the stranger is Lucifer. He falls in love with the girl, but his own twisted notions of love prohibit him from returning the girl's affection in a proper way. In the end, the girl is unable to help Lucifer and he drags her to hell with him. Even as she is falling, she does not know who he is until he tells her his name."
