Enakai,,,Chinese (Expatriate)|Hawaiian (Modern)|Japanese (Rare)|Obscure,"EN-NAH-KIE(Chinese, Japanese)|en-nah-kie(Hawaiian, Obscure)",,,,,,,"This name is sometimes cited as having Japanese and Hawaiian origins. Either a modern invented Hawaiian name from the words ena ""raging"" and kai ""sea"", or a variant of Nākai, ē nā kai meaning ""o the seas, o calm seas"" in Hawaiian. It is also a variant of Chinese name Eng Kai 4 meaning ""brave triumph"" and Japanese surname Enkai, meaning ""banquet""."
