Enzou,m,"円僧, 円三, 円蔵, 円造, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EN-ZO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 円 (en) meaning ""circle, ring"" combined with 僧 (zou) meaning ""Buddhist priest, monk"", 三 (zou) meaning ""three"", 蔵 (zou) meaning ""warehouse, storehouse"" or 造 (zou) meaning ""create, make, physique, structure"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Enzu,m,,Sicilian,,,,,,,,Sicilian form of Enzo.
Enzukai,m,炎図界(Japanese Kanji)|えんずかい(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese,,,,,,,,"The name Enzukai means ""World of Flames"" with a combination of En (炎 ""Flame""), Zu (図 ""Figure"") and Kai (界 ""World"")."
Eoban,m,,Medieval Dutch|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Eoban (died 5 June 754 at Dokkum) was a companion of St. Boniface, and was martyred with him on his final mission. In Germany, he is revered as a bishop and martyr."
Eobard,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Eobard was likely coined from |eo-| ""eon(ic)"" + bard, loosely ""story-teller"" or ""vagabond""This is the given name name of a DC Comics' villain known as Professor Zoom, or the Reverse Flash."
