Ergochares,m,Ἐργοχάρης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἔργον (ergon) meaning ""work, task, deed"" combined with either the Greek noun χαρά (chara) meaning ""joy, delight, happiness"" or the Greek noun χάρις (charis) meaning ""grace, kindness"" (see Chares).This was the name of an eponymous archon of Athens, who lived in the 3rd century BC."
Ergocles,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Ergokles. This was the name of an Athenian strategos (military general) from the 4th century BC.
