Eri,f,"恵里, 恵理, 恵梨, 絵里, 絵理, 絵梨, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|えり(Japanese Hiragana)|エリ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese|Biblical|Greenlandic|Provençal,/e̞.ɾi/|Eh-ree(Biblical English),,,,,,,"From Japanese 恵 (e) meaning ""favour, benefit"" or 絵 (e) meaning ""picture, painting"" combined with 里 (ri) meaning ""village"", 理 (ri) meaning ""reason, logic"" or 梨 (ri) meaning ""pear"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Eria,f,"えりあ(Japanese Hiragana)|映璃愛, 永里亜, 絵理愛, 絵里亜, 江理亜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,E-ṘEE-AH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 映 (e) meaning ""reflect, reflection, projection"", 永 (e) meaning ""eternity, long, lengthy"", 絵 (e) meaning ""picture, drawing, painting, sketch"" or 江 (e) meaning ""creek, inlet, bay"", 璃 (ri) meaning ""glassy, lapis lazuli"", 里 (ri) meaning ""village"" or 理 (ri) meaning ""reason, logic"" combined with 愛 (a) meaning ""love, affection"" or 亜 (a) meaning ""second, Asia"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
