Erigeneia,f,Ἠριγένεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ɛː.ri.ɡé.neː.a/(Attic Greek)|/i.ri.ˈʝe.ni.a/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Epithet of the Greek goddess of dawn Eos meaning ""early-born"" or ""child of dawn"", derived from Ancient Greek ἦρι (eri) ""early in the morning, at early morn"" and γενής (genes) ""born""."
