Eriopis,f,,Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Meaning ""with the lovely hair"". Derived from the prefix ἐρι- (""greatly, very"") and θρίξ (""hair""). This was the name of several minor characters in Greek mythology"
Eriphyle,f,Ἐριφύλη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""(of a) great nation"" in Greek, from the intensive prefix ἐρι- (eri-) ""very, much"" combined with φυλή (phylê) ""race, tribe"". In Greek mythology this name was borne by the wife of Amphiaraos and daughter of Lysimache and Talaos, king of Argos."
