Erotokritos,m,Ερωτόκριτος(Greek),Greek|Literature,,,,,,,,"Means ""the one who is tortured by love"" or ""chosen by love"", from Greek ἔρως (erôs) ""love"" (genitive ἔρωτος (erôtos); see Eros) and κριτός (kritos) ""separated, picked out, chosen"". This is the name of the title character of a poem written by Vitsentzos Kornaros in early 17th-century Crete. 'Erotokritos' is a classic example of Greek Renaissance literature and is considered one of the most important works of Cretan literature."
Erototokos,f,Ερωτοτόκος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""bearer of love"" or ""producing love"", derived from Ancient Greek ἔρως (eros) meaning ""love, desire"" and τόκος (tokos) meaning ""childbirth, parturition, bringing forth"". This was an epithet of the goddess Hecate."
