Erwyd,m,,Welsh,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly taken from the town Erwood, called Erwyd in Welsh. The town's name may have been derived from cerwyd, ""stag""."
Erwyn,m,,Welsh,Er-wyn,,,,,,,"Welsh name, composed by ""gwerd"" and ""gwyn"", with the meaning of ""green and white""."
