Erysichthon,m,Ἐρυσίχθων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˌɛ.rɪ.ˈsɪk.θɒn/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""earth tearer"" in Ancient Greek, derived from ἐρύω (eryo) meaning ""to drag forcefully, to pull along violently"" and χθών (chthon) meaning ""earth, ground, soil"". In Greek mythology, Erysichthon was a king of Thessaly cursed with insatiable hunger for cutting down a sacred grove of Demeter, eventually dying in poverty after selling all of his belongings to buy food."
