Eşay,f,,Turkish,esh-AH-ee,,,,,,,"A compound Turkish feminine name built from the Old Turkic element eş meaning ""peer, equal, friend, companion"" and ay meaning ""moon"". It translates beautifully to ""equal to the moon"" or ""the moon's twin companion."" It carries symbols of serene nocturnal radiance, unmatched beauty, loyalty, and walking in harmony alongside the light."
