Ethlend,f,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"A variant transcription of Eithne. Ethlend is the daughter of Balor and mother of Lugh. In some traditions Ethlend is the daughter of Delbáeth, the mother of the Dagda and Ogma, and the wife of Nuada Airgetlám. In a variant version of the birth of Aengus, she is the wife of Elcmar who is seduced by the Dagda: as such she may be a double, and is explicitly named as such, of Boann, who plays that role in the best-known version of the tale."
Ethlenn,f,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"A variant transcription of Eithne. Ethlenn is the daughter of Balor and mother of Lugh. In some traditions Ethlenn is the daughter of Delbáeth, the mother of the Dagda and Ogma, and the wife of Nuada Airgetlám. In a variant version of the birth of Aengus, she is the wife of Elcmar who is seduced by the Dagda: as such she may be a double, and is explicitly named as such, of Boann, who plays that role in the best-known version of the tale."
