Ethodaia,f,Ἐθοδαΐα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἔθος (ethos) meaning ""character, disposition; custom, habit"" combined with either δάϊς (dais) ""war, battle"", δαίω (daio) ""to kindle, burn, blaze"", or δαίς (dais) ""feast"". This was the name of a Niobid also known as Neaira in Greek mythology."
