Euschemon,m,Εὐσχήμων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective εὐσχήμων (euschemon) meaning ""elegant in figure, graceful"" as well as ""decent, becoming"".This name was borne by a 9th-century saint, who is also known as Euschemos."
Euschemos,m,Εὔσχημος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective εὔσχημος (euschemos) meaning ""with decency"" as well as ""elegant"".This name was borne by a 9th-century saint, who is also known as Euschemon."
