Eutyches,m,Εὐτυχής(Greek),Greek,Yutikhis,,,,,,,"Ancient greek name given to a presbyter and archimandrite of a monastery near Constantinople, first mentioned in 431. Eutyches was famous for his teachings about Jesus Christ devine nature."
Eutychian,m,,Late Roman (Anglicized),,,,,,,,Anglicized form of Eutychianus. This was the name of a pope from the 3rd century AD.
