Excellence,,,"English (African, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From the English word excellence meaning ""The quality of being excellent; brilliance"" or ""An excellent or valuable quality; something at which any someone excels; a virtue"".The vocabulary word comes from Old French excellence, from Latin excellentia (which in turn, comes from excellēns (“elevated, exalted”) +‎ -ia, present participle of excellō (“elevate, exult”)).As a given name, it's most common in Nigeria and several African countries."
