Exuperantia,f,,Late Roman,,,,,,,,"Variant of Exsuperantia, which is derived from the Latin noun exsuperantia ""preeminence, superiority, superfluity"". The noun itself is ultimately derived from exsuperans ""surpassing (greatly), exceeding (greatly), surmounting (greatly)"", which belongs to the verb exsupero (see Exuperius for more). This was the name of a virgin saint from the 4th century AD."
