Eyiz,f,,Turkish,eh-YEEZ,,,,,,,"An archaic, rugged geographical name rooted in the Old Turkic elements ayıg or eyiz, which described ""a terrible, steep mountain pass, an untamed wilderness, or a sheer cliff side."" It represents raw majesty, untamed natural grandeur, and an indomitable character that commands respect and stands tall against the howling winds of adversity."
