Eyjalín,f,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Elaboration of Eyja using an uncertain element, possibly Old Norse lín meaning ""flax, linen; linen garment, linen gear"" or Hlín (both the Old Norse word for ""protection"" and a poetic term for ""woman""). This was used by the Icelandic author Kristmann Guðmundsson for a character in his novel Ströndin blá, originally published in Norwegian as Den blå kyst (1931; and spelled Eialin in Norwegian)."
