Falcone,m,,Medieval Italian|Italian (Rare),/fal.ˈko.ne/(Italian),,,,,,,"Derived from Italian falcone meaning ""falcon"".This name also occurs as the Italian form of the Roman cognomen Falco, which is etymologically related and has the same meaning.A notable bearer of this name was the Italian politician Falcone Lucifero (1898-1997)."
