Favian,m,,Ancient Roman,Fah-vee-in or Fah-vee-on(Latin),,,,,,,"This name is of Latin origin. The direct meaning is unclear but some potential meanings are: ""understanding"" , ""brave man"" as well as ""man of wisdom."" It is derived from the Roman clan name ""Fabius,"" which means, ""bean grower."" It is a name that has been given to several Roman emperors and saints."
