Favonius,m,,Ancient Roman|Roman Mythology,,,,,,,,"Roman family name of disputed origin. According to the Oxford English Dictionary, it is from Latin favere ""to favor""; Ernest Klein says, by dissimilation from *fovonius, literally ""the warming wind"", from fovere ""to warm"". In Roman mythology Favonius was the personification of the west wind, equivalent to the Greek god Zephyros. Marcus Favonius was a politician during the fall of the Roman Republic, and the basis for a character in Shakespeare's tragedy 'Julius Caesar' (1599), i.e., the unnamed Poet who appears in Act IV Scene III."
