Fimafengr,m,,Old Norse|Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,Meaning unknown. In Norse mythology Fimafengr is one of Ægir's servants. Loki kills him and is driven out as a result.
Fimbrethil,f,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Can be Translated to either ""slim-birch"" or ""slender-beech"".In the Saga of Lord of the Rings by J.R.R. Tolkien; it is the name of an Ent wife of Treebeard who had been missing since Sauron's forces destroyed the gardens of the Entwives during the Second Age. At the time of the War of the Ring, Treebeard had not seen his beloved Fimbrethil for over 3,000 years."
Fimmilena,f,,Germanic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Fimmilena was a goddes known from inscriptions in Northern England. Her functions are unclear; there have, however, been efforts to link her name to the Fimelthing, a kind of court held in early medieval times."
