Firmatus,m,,"History|Medieval English (Latinized, ?)|Late Roman (?)|Old Norman (?)",,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin firmatus meaning ""firmed, strengthened"", itself a derivative of firmus ""firm, strong, enduring, stable"" (making it a cognate of Firminus; also compare Firmus). This was borne by Firmatus the deacon, an obscure early Christian martyr. It was also borne by Saint William Firmatus (c. 1095-1103), a Norman hermit and pilgrim from Tours (known in Guillaume Firmat in French)."
