Floranne,f,,French (Rare)|Dutch (Rare),,,,,,,,This given name can be a variant form of Floriane or Florianne as well as a combination of any name starting with Flor- with Anne 1.A known bearer of this name is the Dutch soccer player Floranne van den Broek (b. 1989).
Floransz,f,,Hungarian,,,,,,,,"Hungarian adoption of Florance, reflecting the French pronunciation."
Florant,m,,Arthurian Cycle|Franco-Provençal,,,,,,,,"Variant of Florent. In Wolfram von Eschenbach's Chrétien-inspired Middle High German romance Parzival, Sangive, the daughter of Igraine and Uther Pendragon, is wed by Arthur to Florant of Itolac, also known as the Turkoite (Turkoyt; probably meaning a Turkish origin).This is also a Franco-Provençal variant of Fllorant used in the Arpitan Valleys of Piedmont."
