Forgall,m,,Irish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Perhaps related to Irish forgella ""testifies"". In Irish legend he was the father of Emer, nicknamed ""the cunning, dextrous, wily"". The Wily Lord of Lusca tried to prevent his daughter marrying Cúchulainn and, rather than face the champion's wrath, leapt to his death from the ramparts of his fortress."
