Forsythia,f,,English (Rare),fawr-SITH-ee-ə|for-SIDH-ee-ə,,,,,,,"From the name of forsythia, any of a genus of shrubs that produce yellow flowers in spring. They were named in honour of the British botanist William Forsyth (1737-1804), whose surname was derived from Gaelic Fearsithe, a personal name meaning literally ""man of peace"" (cf. Fearsithe, Forsythe)."
