Fortebraccio,m,,Medieval Italian,,,,,,,,"Means ""strong arm"" in Italian, as it is derived from Italian forte meaning ""strong"" combined with Italian braccio meaning ""arm"" (the plural form is bracci).This is a nickname that was also used as a given name in medieval Italy. Nowadays it solely exists as both a descriptive and a patronymic surname."
