Furseus,m,,Old Irish (Latinized)|History,,,,,,,,Latinized form of Fursey.
Fursey,m,,Old Irish|History,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Latin virtus ""virtue"" via Old Irish firt. Saint Fursey was an early medieval Irish monk and visionary whose ""celebrated visions had considerable influence on dream literature of the later Middle Ages"", including Dante's 'Divine Comedy'."
Fursy,m,,"French (Belgian, Rare)|Picard|History (Ecclesiastical)",,,,,,,,French and Picard form of Fursey via Latinized Furseus.
