Fushou,m,福寿(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From 福 (fú) meaning ""blessing, happiness, prosperity"" and 寿 (shòu) meaning ""long life""."
Fuso,f,ふそ(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Japanese 父祖 (fuso), meaning ""ancestor""."
Fusu,,"扶苏, etc.(Chinese)|扶蘇, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese|Chinese Mythology,/fu.su/(Chinese),,,,,,,"From Chinese 扶苏 (fúsū), from the title of a poem from the Classic of Poetry, meaning ""a kind of tree"", ""shield on chariots"", or ""to assist"". Other hanzi combinations are possible. A notable bearer is Fusu (died 210 BC), the eldest son of Qin Shi Huang, who is sometimes worshipped in China today as a Door God."
Füsunkar,f,,Azerbaijani,,,,,,,,"Etymology uncertain, possibly derived from the Turkish Füsun."
Fu̍t,m,佛(Chinese),Buddhism,/fut̚/(Hakka),,,,,,,Hakka form of Buddha.
Futaba,f,"双葉, 二葉(Japanese Kanji)|ふたば(Japanese Hiragana)|フタバ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ɸɯ̟̥ᵝ.tä.bä/,,,,,,,"This name is used as 双葉 or 二葉, referring to a bud or a sprout, made up of 双 (sou, tagui, narabu, futa(tsu)) meaning ""pair"" or 二 (ji, ni, futa(.tsu), futata.bi) meaning ""two"" with 葉 (you, ha) meaning ""blade, leaf, needle."""
Futabako,f,"ふたばこ(Japanese Hiragana)|ふたば子(Kanji/Hiragana)|双葉子, 二葉子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),FTA-BA-KO,,,,,,,"From 双 (futa) meaning ""pair"" or 二 (futa) meaning ""two"" with 葉 (ha) meaning ""blade, leaf, needle"", and 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other character combinations are possible."
Futao,m,"双夫, 双雄, 二生, 二男, 二暢, 二夫, 二雄, 二郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU-TAH-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 双 (futa) meaning ""pair, set, comparison"" or 二 (futa) meaning ""two"" combined with 夫 (o) meaning ""man, husband"", 雄 (o) meaning ""hero, manly"", 生 (o) meaning ""life, genuine, birth"", 男 (o) meaning ""male"", 暢 (o) meaning ""stretch"" or 郎 (o) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Futing,f,芙霆(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 芙 (fú) meaning ""hibiscus"" and 霆 (tíng) meaning ""sudden peal of thunder""."
Futoru,m,太(Japanese Kanji)|ふとる(Japanese Hiragana)|フトル(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),[ɸɯ̟̥ᵝ.to̞.ɾɯ̟ᵝ],,,,,,,"From verb 太る (futoru) meaning ""to grow plump.""This name is rarely used."
Futoshi,m,"太, 大, 太志, 太士, 太四, 大志, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ふとし(Japanese Hiragana)|フトシ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,[ɸɯ̟̥ᵝ.to̞.ɕi],,,,,,,"From classical adjective 太し (futoshi) meaning ""fat, thick; daring, shameless.""Alternatively, it can be used as 大 (dai, tai, oo.kii, futo) meaning ""big, large,"" related to the adjective. They can also be combined with a shi kanji, like 志 meaning ""will, aim, goal,"" 士 meaning ""samurai"" or 四 meaning ""four."""
