Futura,f,,Italian,foo-TOO-ra,,,,,,,"Derived from the Italian word futuro meaning ""future""."
Future,,,English (Rare)|Western African|Southern African,FYOO-chər(English),,,,,,,"This name is from the English word derived from Old French futur meaning ""future, to come,"" which is then derived from Latin futurus meaning ""going to be, yet to be, the future (as a noun)."" The Latin word is an irregular suppletive future participle of esse meaning ""to be,"" which comes from the Proto-Indo-European root *bheue- meaning ""to be, exist, grow, come into being.""This name is also used in most countries of Western and Southern Africa where English is one of the official languages."
Fuu,,"ふう(Japanese Hiragana)|フウ(Japanese Katakana)|楓, 芙, 風, 踏羽, 殖優, 歩生, 斧有, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"". Other kanji or kanji combinations are also possible."
Fuue,f,"楓恵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 恵 (e) meaning ""favour"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuga,,"楓河, 風河, 楓我, 風我, 楓雅, 風雅, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-GAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" or 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" combined with 河 (ga) meaning ""river"", 我 (ga) meaning ""I, me"" or 雅 (ga) meaning ""elegant"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuho,f,"楓歩, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-HO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 歩 (ho) meaning ""walk"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuki,,"楓姫, 楓樹, 風葵, 風希, 楓葵, 扶希, 富輝, 富紀, 風季, 風貴, 風鬼, 豊貴, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ふうき(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,FUU:-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 姫 (ki) meaning ""princess"" (usually feminine) or 樹 (ki) meaning ""tree; plant"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuko,f,"ふうこ(Japanese Hiragana)|フウコ(Japanese Katakana)|楓子, 風子, 不子, 婦子, 二子, 富子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FOO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" or 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Fuuma,m,"ふうま(Japanese Hiragana)|楓馬, 楓磨, 楓麻, 風馬, 風舞, 風麻, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-MAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" or 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind, air, style, manner"" combined with 馬 (ma) meaning ""horse"", 磨 (ma) meaning ""grind, polish, scour, improve, brush (teeth)"", 麻 (ma) meaning ""hemp, flax, numb"" or 舞 (ma) meaning ""dance"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Fuuma Uehara, a Japanese actor and entertainer."
Fuume,f,"楓梅, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 梅 (me) meaning ""plum"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuna,f,"ふうな(Japanese Hiragana)|楓菜, 楓奈, 楓那, 風夏, 風菜, 風渚, 風奈, 風南, 風和, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" or 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"", 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"", 那 (na) meaning ""what"", 夏 (na) meaning ""summer"", 渚 (na) meaning ""beach, shore"", 南 (na) meaning ""south"" or 和 (na) meaning ""peace, harmony"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuno,f,"楓乃, 風桜乃, 風野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Fuupu,f,"楓譜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-PUU,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 譜 (pu) meaning ""musical note"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuurin,f,"楓鈴, 風林, 風鈴, 風凛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-ṘEEN,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 鈴 (rin) meaning ""bell, chime"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuusuke,m,"楓介, 風助, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,fuu:-ske  ,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" or 風 (fuu) meaning ""style, wind"" combined with 介 (suke) meaning ""shell, shellfish"" or 助 (suke) meaning ""assistance"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Fuuta,m,"楓汰, 風詩, 風太, 風汰, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-TAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" or 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" combined with 汰 (ta) meaning ""scour, wash out"", 詩 (ta) meaning ""poetry, poem"" or 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuto,m,"楓人, 楓斗, 風音, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"", 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind, style"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"", 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation or 音 (to) meaning ""sound"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuya,m,"楓也, 楓弥, 風哉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 楓 (fuu) meaning ""maple"" or 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" combined with 也 (ya) meaning ""also"", 弥 (ya) meaning ""universally"" or 哉 (ya), an exclamation. Other combinations of kanji are possible."
Fuuyou,,"風菜, 風葉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-YO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" combined with 菜 (you) meaning ""vegetables, greens"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuuyu,f,"風優, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,FUU:-YU,,,,,,,"From Japanese 風 (fuu) meaning ""wind"" combined with 優 (yu) meaning ""gentleness, lithe, superior"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuwa,f,"芙羽, 芙和, 歩羽, 歩和, 風羽, 風和, 楓羽, 楓和, 譜羽, 譜和, 浮羽, 浮和, 冨羽, 冨和, 吹羽, 吹和(Japanese Kanji)|ふわ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/ɸɯ̟ᵝ.β̞ä/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 芙 (fu) meaning ""nelumbo nucifera"", 歩 (fu) meaning ""walk, pawn"", 風 (fu) meaning ""wind, influence"", 楓 (fu) meaning ""liquidambar formosana"", 譜 (fu) meaning ""musical score"", 浮 (fu) meaning ""to float"", 冨 (fu) meaning ""wealth"", or 吹 (fu), the root form of 吹く (fuku) meaning ""to blow"" combined with 羽 (wa) meaning ""feather, wing"" and 和 (wa) meaning ""peaceful, Japanese""."
Fuwari,f,"フワリ(Japanese Katakana)|ふわり(Japanese Hiragana)|優風, 布分笑, 浮倭栞, 芙発舞, 巫輪浬, 譜琶陸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)",FOO-WA-REE,,,,,,,"This name is derived from the onomatopoeic adverb ふわり (fuwari) meaning “softly, gently, lightly.”It can be spelled with 優風, meaning ""gentle wind"", but it also could be spelled more conventionally with 蕗 (fu) meaning ""butterbur"" combined with 磐 (wa) meaning ""rock"", and 稟 (ri) meaning ""report"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Fuxia,f,福霞(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 福 (fú) meaning ""happiness, good fortune, blessing"" and 霞 (xiá) meaning ""rosy clouds""."
Fuxian,f,芙娴(Chinese),Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 芙 (fú) meaning ""hibiscus"" and 娴 (xián) meaning ""elegant, refined""."
Fuxiang,m,"福祥, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,Not available.
