Gabard,m,,"French (Caribbean, Rare)|Haitian Creole",,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from the French surname of Gabard, the origin of which is not quite certain. It could be a patronymic surname that is derived from the Germanic given name Gebhard, but it could also be a descriptive surname derived from Occitan gabar meaning ""to joke, to jest, to mock"".A known bearer of this name is the Haitian soccer player Gabard Fénélon (b. 1981)."
