Galdur,m,,"Icelandic (Modern, Rare)",/ˈkal.tʏr/,,,,,,,"Means ""magic"" in Icelandic, from Old Norse galdr ""magic chant; magic, spell""."
Gale,m,,West Frisian (Rare),,,,,,,,"This name is the Frisian form of the Germanic given name Gaito, which was ultimately derived from Proto-Germanic *gails meaning ""cheerful, jovial"". But in addition to that, it is also often a short form of Germanic given names that contain (or are related to) the aforementioned element of *gails, such as Geilhard.In other words, you could say that this name is basically the Frisian cognate of Gale 2."
