Galicano,m,,Spanish (Philippines),/ɡa.li.ˈka.no/(Filipino Spanish),,,,,,,"Means ""gallican"" in Spanish. A bearer of this name was Galicano Apacible, a Filipino physician and politician."
Galicia,f,,Galician|Spanish (Latin American),/ga.ˈli.θja/(Galician)|/ga.ˈli.sja/(Latin American Spanish),,,,,,,"From the land of Galicia in analogy to other toponymic names like América or África. It is associated to Galician emigration, so this name can be found now in Latin American countries."
