Galila,f,גלילה(Hebrew),Hebrew (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from the place name Galil גליל, this name was mostly used from the 19th until the early 20th century and occasionally used after the establishment of Israel. A notable bearer is the Israeli writer Galila Ron-Feder Amit (born in 1949), who has written over 400 books."
