Gallyon,,,Dutch (Rare),,,,,,,,"This given name is predominantly feminine in the Netherlands. It is not a typical Dutch first name and therefore its meaning is uncertain; it may possibly have been derived from the British surname Gallyon, which is Norman-French in origin (and is found in the spelling Gallion in modern France).A well-known bearer of this name is the Dutch television presenter Gallyon van Vessem (b. 1968)."
Galnai,f,Галнай(Buryat Cyrillic),Buryat,,,,,,,,"From the Buryat гал (gal) meaning ""fire""."
Galoes,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"Perceval’s paternal uncle, whose name Wolfram probably borrowed from Hartmann’s Galoes.The son of King Gandin and Queen Schoette, brother of the ladies Flurdamurs and Limmire, and the knight Sir Gahmuret.Galoes inherited the kingdom of Anjou. Galoes’s brother, Gahmuret, set out in search of adventure despite Galoes’s pleas for him to remain at court. Galoes loved the lady Annore, Queen of Averre, and he died in her service at Muntori. His slayer was Duke Orilus of Lalander."
