Gandhari,f,गान्धारी(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ɡɑːn̪.ˈd̪ʱɑː.ɾiː/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"From the name of the ancient kingdom of Gandhara that spanned parts of present-day Pakistan and Afghanistan. In the Hindu epic the Mahabharata Gandhari is a princess of Gandhara who marries Dhritarashtra, the blind king of Kuru."
Gandivadhara,m,गाण्डिवधर(Sanskrit),Hinduism,,,,,,,,"Means ""holder of Gandiva"" from Sanskrit गाण्डीव (Gāṇḍīva) referring to a divine bow described the Hindu epic the Mahabharata combined with धर (dhara) meaning ""bearer, holder, possessor"". This is an epithet of the hero Arjuna, who was gifted Gandiva by the god Varuna."
