Gangadhara,m,गङ्गाधर(Sanskrit)|ಗಂಗಾಧರ(Kannada)|గంగాధర(Telugu),Hinduism|Kannada|Telugu,/ɡɐŋ.ˈɡɑː.d̪ʱɐ.ɾɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""holder of the Ganges"" from the name of the Ganges River and Sanskrit धर (dhara) meaning ""bearing, possessing"". This is an epithet of the Hindu god Shiva."
