Garrincha,m,,Portuguese (Brazilian),ga-REEN-shu(European Portuguese)|ga-HEEN-shu(Brazilian Portuguese),,,,,,,"An invented name, derived from Portuguese carriça meaning ""wren"", referring to the small brown songbird. It was borne by the Brazilian soccer player Manuel Francisco dos Santos (1933-1983), who was better known as Mané Garrincha or simply Garrincha; he was given this nickname by his sister because of his small appearance."
