Garrison,m,Гаррисон(Russian),English|Soviet,GER-i-sən(English)|GAR-i-sən(English),,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Garrison. A famous bearer of the surname was American abolitionist William Lloyd Garrison (1805-1879). It is also borne by American humorist and radio personality Gary ""Garrison"" Keillor (1942-) and former football player Garrison Hearst (1971-). In USSR, this is used in honour of William Lloyd Garrison."
