Gefn,f,,Norse Mythology|Icelandic,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Norse gefa ""to give"", possibly meaning ""the giver"" or ""the gifted one"". In Norse mythology this is one of the names of the goddess Freyja. It is possible that Gefn was originally a goddess in her own right."
Gega,m,გეგა(Georgian),Georgian,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. The earliest known attestation of this name occurs in a Georgian source from the 16th century AD. It might possibly be related to Georgian გეგმა (gegma) meaning ""plan, project"" and Georgian გეგმი (gegmi) meaning ""plan"" as well as ""law, custom"".In modern times, this name is regularly used as a diminutive of Germane and Giorgi."
