Gehazi,m,גֵּיחֲזִי‎‎(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Means ""valley of visions"" in Hebrew, derived from גיא (gay) ""valley, ravine"" and חָזָה (khazá) ""to see, to look"". In the Old Testament, this was the name of a servant of the prophet Elisha who used his position of power to cheat Naaman the Syrian, resulting in Naaman's leprosy being transferred to him and his descendants."
