Gentle,,,English,,,,,,,,"Possibly from the word ""Gentle"", used in the beginning of the nouns gentleman meaning ""well-born man, man of good family or birth"" or from gentlewoman meaning ""woman of good family or breeding"". It could also come from the English word gentle meaning ""(of a person) mild in temperament or behavior; kind or tender"", ""moderate in action, effect, or degree; not harsh or severe""."
