Gerana,f,Γεράνα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek γέρανος (geranos) ""crane (bird)"". Gerana, otherwise known as Oenoe, was a queen of the Pygmy folk in Greek mythology. She boasted she was more beautiful than the goddess Hera and was transformed by the angry goddess into a crane. The bird descendants of Gerana waged an eternal war on the Pygmies during their winter migration to the shores of the river Oceanus."
