Gilberga,f,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Gilberga is an ancient variant of the names Gilberta and Gilberte. It has Germanic roots and comes from the Old High German elements gisil (meaning ""pledge"" or ""hostage"") and berht (meaning ""bright"" or ""famous""). This combines to give the name a meaning like ""bright pledge"" or ""famous pledge.""Historically, the name appeared among European nobility during the Middle Ages, with notable figures including Gilberga Ivrea (a 10th-century Italian aristocrat) and Gilberga of Aragon (a 11th-century Queen of Aragon)"
