Girdvainas,m,,Lithuanian,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from the Lithuanian noun girdas meaning ""rumour"", which is ultimately derived from the Lithuanian verb girdėti meaning ""to hear"". Also compare the related Lithuanian noun gandas meaning ""rumour, hearsay"". The second element is derived from the old Lithuanian noun vaina meaning ""cause, reason"" as well as ""fault""."
