Giseltrud,f,,Lombardic,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Germanic element gisal meaning ""hostage, pledge"" combined with drud ""strength"" or *trut ""maiden"". This name was borne by the wife of the Lombard king Aistulf. She was also a sister of Saint Anselm, Duke of Friuli."
