Gisken,f,,Norwegian,,,,,,,,"Diminutive of Giske, a Norwegian variant of the Low German name Geseke, itself a diminutive of Gesa. This was common in Norway in the 17th, 18th and 19th centuries. It was borne by Norwegian writer Gisken Wildenvey (1895-1985; born Jonette Pauline Andreassen)."
