Gloriette,f,,English,/ˈɡlɔɹ.i.ɛt/,,,,,,,"From the word for a pavilion or similar architectural structure in a garden which perhaps meant ""little glory"" from French (see Gloria). The largest and most well-known example is probably the Schönbrunner Gloriette, in the Schönbrunn Palace Garden at Vienna, built in 1775 for Holy Roman Empress Maria Theresa."
