Gói,f,,Norse Mythology|Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Name of a lunar month in the Old Norse calendar, lasting from the middle of February to the middle of March. It ultimately derives from a Proto-Indo-European word meaning ""winter; snow, frost"". In Norse mythology Gói is the daughter of Þorri. She is captured by King Hrólfr of the Hill, who makes her his wife, and the month was supposedly named after her."
