Goka,m,გოკა(Georgian),Georgian (Rare),,,,,,,,Diminutive of masculine names that start with Go- (such as Goderdzi and Goneri) or that otherwise contain -go- (such as Gigola).This name is not to be confused with the similar-looking name Gocha.
Gökay,,,Turkish,[goh-kye],,,,,,,"Gökay is a majestic Turkish name composed of Gök (""the Sky, the Heavens, the infinite blue, the celestial realm, the source of all life, the majestic vault above"") and Ay (""the Moon, the symbol of illumination in darkness, the measure of time, the beauty of the night, the silver glow""). Together, they create a name that signifies ""the celestial harmony,"" ""the union of the vast heaven and the reflective moon,"" and ""the spirit that encompasses both the depth of the sky and the clarity of moonlight."" It symbolizes ""a high-reaching ambition,"" ""enlightened intelligence,"" and ""a nature that brings light to the darkest corners of the world."""
Gökcan,,,Turkish (Modern),,,,,,,,"It is a combination of the words ""sky"" and ""soul"". It means ""bloomed, fresh soul, soul full of longing""."
