Göknur,m,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Derived from Turkish gök meaning ""sky"" and nur meaning ""light""."
Gökra,f,,Turkish (Modern),/ɡœk.ɾɑ/,,,,,,,"Gökra is a modern and evocative Turkish name. It is composed of Gök (""Sky"") and the suffix -ra (an archaic or poetic directional/locative marker derived from Old Turkic, signifying ""towards,"" ""in the direction of,"" or ""located at""). Literally translating to ""Towards the Sky"" or ""One belonging to the Heavens,"" this name symbolizes high aspirations, spiritual elevation, and a connection to the celestial realm. It evokes the image of someone who looks toward the highest point and remains untethered by the mundane."
Gökşan,,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Means ""celestial glory"" in Turkish."
