Gölge,f,,Turkish (Modern),/ˈɡœl.ɟɛ/,,,,,,,"The name Gölge acts as a mirror to the soul, often bestowed to signify one who walks as a silent, protective presence; a ""dark silhouette"" cast by the light of existence. Etymologically, it is connected to the Turkic root köl (""lake""). In Old Turkic, köl encompassed not only the concept of a stagnant body of water but also implied ""depth,"" ""a central depression,"" or ""an enclosed, protected area."" Just as a lake serves as a natural reservoir reflecting the sky, the name represents the ""reflection"" or ""imprint"" an individual leaves upon the world. It is a symbol of calm depth and the inseparable connection between an object and its shadow."
