Gon,m,"ゴン(Japanese Katakana)|ごん(Japanese Hiragana)|健, 権, 源, 魂, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|건(Korean Hangul)|建, 健, 虔, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Literature|Popular Culture|Japanese (Rare)|Spanish|Korean|Piedmontese,GON(Japanese)|/kʌn/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 銀 (gon) meaning ""silver"", 言 (gon) meaning ""speech, to say"", or 勤 (gon) meaning ""diligence"". Other kanji or kanji combinations can form this name.One notable bearer from literature is the titular character of the 'Gongitsune' children's book.Another fictional bearer is the protagonist of the 'Hunter x Hunter' manga series, Gon Freecss."
