Gonzaga,m,,"Eastern African|Portuguese (Brazilian, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Derived from the surname Gonzaga. It is given after Italian saint Aloysius Gonzaga and was also borne by Gonza, one of the Uganda Martyrs. This name is mostly used in Uganda and Brazil."
Gonzague,m,,French|French (Belgian),,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Gonzague. The name is usually used in honour of Louis de Gonzague (1568-1591, known in English as Aloysius Gonzaga), an Italian aristocrat who became a member of the Society of Jesus. While still a student at the Roman College, he died as a result of caring for the victims of a serious epidemic. He was beatified in 1605 and canonized in 1726; he is considered the patron of students, Christian youth and plague victims."
