Goor,m,,Dutch (Rare)|Limburgish (Rare),/ˈχoːr/(Dutch)|/ˈɣoːr/(Limburgish),,,,,,,"Short form of Gregoor and Gregorius (see Gregory).This name is not to be confused with the Dutch adjective goor meaning ""dirty, filthy, disgusting"".The well-known Dutch singer Gordon Heuckeroth (b. 1968) is often referred to as Goor, even though the name is not traditionally a short form of Gordon. The use of this nickname only began in his time with the Dutch supergroup De Toppers, of which he was a member from 2005 until 2011. He has since teamed up occasionally with his former band mate Gerard ""Geer"" Joling (b. 1960), performing as a musical duo under the name Geer & Goor. They have also made a few television programmes under that name."
