Gorgophone,f,Γοργοφόνη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""Gorgon-slayer"", the feminine form of Gorgophonus. In Greek mythology, Gorgophone is the name of a daughter of Perseus and Andromeda, as well as of one of the Daenids, who killed her husband Proteus on their wedding night. It was also an epithet of Athena."
Gorgophonus,m,Γοργοφόνος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Means ""Gorgon-killing"", derived from Ancient Greek Γοργώ (Gorgo) meaning ""gorgon (snake-haired monster)"", itself derived from γοργός (gorgos) meaning ""grim, fierce, terrible; vigorous, spirited"", and φόνος (phonos) meaning ""murder, slaughter"". This was the name of a grandson of Perseus in Greek mythology, as well as an epithet of Perseus himself as the killer of the gorgon Medusa."
Gorgos,m,Γόργος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from either the Greek adjective γοργός (gorgos) meaning ""grim, fierce, terrible"" or the Greek verb γοργεύω (gorgeuo) meaning ""to move rapidly, to hasten"". Also compare the Greek verb γοργόομαι (gorgoomai) meaning ""to be spirited""."
