Gorlois,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"In Arthurian legend, Gorlois of Tintagel was the Duke of Cornwall. He was the first husband of King Arthur's mother Igraine and the father of her daughters. The name Gorlois first appears in Geoffrey of Monmouth's Historia Regum Britanniae (c. 1136) as a rendering of Welsh Gwrlais."
