Gradimir,m,"Градимир(Bulgarian, Macedonian, Russian, Serbian)",Bulgarian|Macedonian|Russian|Serbian|Croatian,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name can be derived from Serbo-Croatian grȃd, which can mean ""city, town"" as well as ""fortress, castle"" (which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gordъ ""settlement, enclosed space""). It can also be derived from Serbo-Croatian grȁd ""hail"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gradъ ""hail"". The second element of this name is derived from Slavic mir ""peace""."
