Guanzhong,m,"冠中, 贯中, etc.(Chinese)|貫中, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/ku̯än.ʈ͡ʂʊŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 冠 (guān) meaning ""cap, crown, headgear"" or 贯 (guàn) meaning ""to follow in a continuous line, to pass through"" combined with 中 (zhōng) meaning ""middle"". Notable bearers include Ming dynasty novelist Luo Ben (c. 1330–1400 or c.1280–1360) (known by his courtesy name Guanzhong), the author of Romance of the Three Kingdoms, and contemporary Chinese painter Wu Guanzhong (1919–2010)."
