Guinizo,m,,History,,,,,,,,"A diminutive/pet form of older Germanic names—such as Winitio or names starting with wini (meaning ""friend"")—which evolved and adapted into Italian and Spanish dialects over centuries. The most notable historical figure with this name is Saint Guinizo (c. 1050). Born in Spain, he became a monk at the famed Abbey of Montecassino in Italy and lived as a hermit on the mountain."
