Gulvardi,f,გულვარდი(Georgian),Georgian,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is either derived from the Middle Persian noun gul meaning ""flower, rose"" or from the Georgian noun გული (guli) meaning ""heart"". Sources mention both as a possibility and therefore neither can be discounted.The second element is derived from the Georgian noun ვარდი (vardi) meaning ""rose"", which is ultimately of Iranian origin."
Gulvardisa,f,გულვარდისა(Georgian),Georgian (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Means ""heart of the rose"" in Georgian. It is derived from the Georgian noun გული (guli) meaning ""heart"" combined with Georgian ვარდის (vardis), which is the genitive of the noun ვარდი (vardi) meaning ""rose""."
Gülverdi,m,,Azerbaijani (Rare),,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is ultimately derived from the Middle Persian noun gul meaning ""flower, rose"", whilst the second element is possibly derived from the Arabic noun وردة (warda) meaning ""rose"".Also compare the Georgian name Gulvardi, which is strictly feminine."
