Günce,f,,Turkish,gyoon-JEH,,,,,,,"Formed from the Turkic element gün (or ancient kün) meaning ""sun, day"", paired with the diminutive or equative suffix -ce. The meaning of this name can be translated as “like the sun” or “resembling sunlight”; this symbolizes the person bearing the name with warmth, life renewed each day, and bright light. It is crucial to note that despite phonetic similarities, it is entirely native and unrelated to the Persian word Gonca (which means ""flower bud"")."
