Güz,f,,Turkish,/ɡyːz/,,,,,,,"The name Güz is an evocative Turkish moniker derived from the Old Turkic root güz, signifying ""Autumn."" Beyond the season of harvest, the name carries a deeper, poetic resonance: it represents the ""golden threshold of transition,"" a time of reflection, maturation, and the quiet wisdom found in the cooling of the year. It captures the essence of ""nature’s elegant descent"" into rest, symbolizing a soul that is contemplative, grounded, and harmoniously aligned with the cycles of life."
