Güzde,f,,Turkish,/ɡyːz.dɛ/,,,,,,,"Güzde is a melodic Turkish name derived from Güz (Autumn) and the locative suffix -de, collectively translating as ""in the autumn"" or ""residing in the heart of the harvest."" It symbolizes the ""tranquility of the season,"" representing someone who finds beauty in transition and possesses a ""settled, peaceful nature."" It is the name for one who carries the ""golden warmth of the falling leaves"" within their very being."
