Güzin,f,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Means ""exquisite, excellent"", ultimately derived from Persian."
Güzle,f,,Turkish,/ɡyːz.lɛ/,,,,,,,"Güzle is a poetic Turkish name combining Güz (Autumn) and the archaic/dialectal suffix -le. It evokes the image of ""being autumn-like"" or ""walking within the autumn landscape."" It signifies a person of ""reflective elegance,"" someone who radiates the calm, cool, and collected beauty of the season. The name carries the weight of history, historically referring to individuals deeply connected to the land and the changing tides of nature, often associated with the most ancient keepers of seasonal wisdom."
Guzma,m,グズマ(Japanese Katakana),Popular Culture,,,,,,,,"From the name of the flower Guzmania, also known as the tufted airplant, which was named in honor of Spanish naturalist Anastasio Guzman.This name was first used for a character in the video games Pokemon Sun and Moon. Guzma is the leader of Team Skull and the games' secondary antagonist."
Guzmán,m,,Spanish,gooth-MAN(European Spanish)|goos-MAN(Spanish)|gooz-MAHN(English),,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Guzmán, derived from the name of a Spanish town. The name itself possibly come from the Ancient Germanic elements gut meaning ""good"" and mann meaning ""man""."
Güzün,f,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Means ""autumn"" in Turkish."
Gvanca,f,"გვანცა(Svan, Georgian)",Svan|Georgian,/ɡvɑn.tsɑ/(Georgian),,,,,,,Variant transcription of Gvantsa.
Gvantsa,f,"გვანცა(Svan, Georgian)",Svan|Georgian,/ɡvɑn.tsɑ/(Georgian),,,,,,,"Derived from the Svan word გუანც (guanc), which literally means ""wren"" but means ""mischievous, restless, wild"" in a figurative sense.This name was most notably borne by Gvantsa Kakhaberidze, the third wife of king Davit VII of Georgia (1215-1270)."
Gvaram,m,გვარამ(Georgian),Medieval Georgian|Georgian (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Ultimately derived from Avestan Verethragna (see Bahram). Also compare the related names Guram and Varam.A notable bearer of this name was the Georgian Bagratid prince Gvaram Mampali (died in 882 AD), who is also known as Guaram."
