Gwangchorong,f,"광초롱(Korean Hangul)|光籠, 洸籠, 廣籠, 珖籠, 侊籠(Korean Hanja)",Korean (Rare),GWANG-CHORONG,,,,,,,"A really rare name actually. Combination of a gwang hanja, like 光 meaning ""light,"" 洸 meaning ""angry; brave, gallant,"" 廣 meaning ""large, extensive, spacious,"" 珖 meaning ""jade"" or 侊 meaning ""big; magnificent,"" and from either the adverb 초롱초롱 (chorong chorong) ""brightly, sparklingly"" or 초籠 (chorong), referring to a silk-covered lantern."
Gwang-deok,m,"광덕(Korean Hangul)|光德, 珖德, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwa̠ːŋ.tʌ̹k̚/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" or 珖 (gwang) meaning ""jade flute"", combined with 德 (deok) meaning ""benevolence, virtue"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gwang-hee,,"광희(Korean Hangul)|光熙, 光姬, 侊熙, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwaŋ.ʝi/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangul 광희 (see Gwang-hui).
Gwang-ho,m,"광호(Korean Hangul)|光浩, 光昊, 光鎬, 廣浩, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwaŋ.ɦo/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" or 廣 (gwang) meaning ""broad, wide, extensive"" combined with 浩 (ho) meaning ""great, numerous, vast"", 昊 (ho) meaning ""summer, sky, heaven"" or 鎬 (ho) meaning ""stove, bright"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gwang-hui,,"광희(Korean Hangul)|光熙, 光姬, 侊熙, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwaŋ.ʝi/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" or 侊 (gwang) meaning ""big"" combined with 熙 (hui) meaning ""bright, splendid, glorious"" or 姬 (hui) meaning ""beauty"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gwang-hye,f,"광혜(Korean Hangul)|光惠, 光慧, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,KWANG-HIE,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light, brilliant, shine; only"" combined with 惠 (hye) meaning ""favour, benefit"" or 慧 (hye) meaning ""bright, intelligent"". Other combinations of hanja characters can form this name as well."
Gwang-hyeon,m,"광현(Korean Hangul)|光鉉, 光炫, 光顯, 光玄, 洸鉉, 廣鉉, 珖賢, 侊炫, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwäŋ.ʝjʌn/,,,,,,,"Combination of a gwang hanja, like 光 meaning ""light,"" 洸 meaning ""angry; brave, gallant,"" 廣 meaning ""large, extensive, spacious,"" 珖 meaning ""jade"" or 侊 meaning ""big; magnificent,"" and a hyeon hanja, such as 鉉 meaning ""bowstring,"" 炫 meaning ""bright, brilliant; light, clear,"" 顯 meaning ""appearance; exposure; distinction,"" 玄 meaning ""dark; profound, mysterious"" or 賢 meaning ""benevolent; wise, sensible."""
Gwang-jae,m,"광재(Korean Hangul)|光才, 光再, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwa̠ːŋ.t͡ɕɛ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" combined with 才 (jae) meaning ""talent"" or 再 (jae) meaning ""again"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gwang-jin,m,광진(Korean Hangul),Korean,GWAHNG-JEEN,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 ""light, brilliant, shine; only"" and 眞 ""real, actual, true, genuine""."
Gwang-jo,m,"광조(Korean Hangul)|光照, 光祖, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwaŋ.t͡ɕo̞/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" combined with 照 (jo) meaning ""shine, illuminate, reflect"" or 祖 (jo) meaning ""ancestor, forefather"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
