Gwang-soo,m,"광수(Korean Hangul)|光壽, 廣壽, 光秀, 廣秀, 光洙, 廣洙, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwa̠ŋ.su/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangeul 광수 (see Gwang-su).
Gwang-su,m,"광수(Korean Hangul)|光壽, 廣壽, 光秀, 廣秀, 光洙, 廣洙, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kwa̠ŋ.su/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 光 (gwang) meaning ""light"" or 廣 (gwang) meaning ""broad, wide, extensive"" combined with 壽 (su) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" or 秀 (su) meaning ""luxuriant, beautiful, elegant, outstanding"" or 洙 (su), referring to a river in the Shadong region of China. Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
