Gyas,m,Γύης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Roman Mythology|Literature|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek γύης (gyes), which can mean either ""curved piece of wood in a plough"" or ""measure of land; field, earth"". Gyas, also called Gyges and Gyes, was one of the Hecatoncheires in Greek mythology, giants with fifty heads and a hundred hands. Gyas was also the name of a boat captain in Virgil’s Aeneid."
