Gyeong-min,,"경민(Korean Hangul)|京民, 景民, 敬民, 京珉, 耿敏, 坰旻, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kjʌŋ.min/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 京 (gyeong) meaning ""capital city"", 景 (gyeong) meaning ""scenery, view"", 敬 (gyeong) meaning ""respect, honour"", 耿 (gyeong) meaning ""bright, shining"" or 坰 (gyeong) meaning ""field, borderland, vicinity"" combined with 民 (min) meaning ""people, citizens"", 珉 (min) meaning ""jade, stone resembling jade"", 敏 (min) meaning ""quick, clever, sharp"" or 旻 (min) meaning ""heaven"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gyeong-mo,m,"경모(Korean Hangul)|京摸, 京模, 敬模, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kjʌŋ.mo/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 京 (gyeong) meaning ""capital city"" or 敬 (gyeong) meaning ""respect, honour"" combined with 摸 (mo) meaning ""touch, caress"" or 模 (mo) meaning ""model, standard, pattern"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
