Gyeong-taek,m,"경택(Korean Hangul)|京擇, 炅澤, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kjʌŋ.tʰɛk̚/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 京 (gyeong) meaning ""capital city"" or 炅 (gyeong) meaning ""brilliance"" combined with 擇 (taek) meaning ""select, choose, pick"" or 澤 (taek) meaning ""moist, marsh, grace, brilliance"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Gyeong-won,,"경원(Korean Hangul)|京元, 景元, 敬元, 京媛, 景媛, 敬媛, 京原, 景原, 敬原, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/kjʌŋ.wʌn/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 京 (gyeong) meaning ""capital city"" or 景 (gyeong) meaning ""scenery, view"" or 敬 (gyeong) meaning ""respect, honour"" combined with 元 (won) meaning ""first, origin"" or 媛 (won) meaning ""beautiful woman"" or 原 (won) meaning ""source, origin, beginning"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
