Gylippos,m,Γύλιππος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/dʒɪ.ˈlɪp.əs/(English)|/ɡý.lip.pos/(Attic Greek)|/ˈʝy.lip.pos/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"The first element of this name is a bit uncertain. It might possibly be derived from Greek γύλιος (gylios), the name for a long-shaped pouch or knapsack that Greek soldiers used for carrying their food supplies (see Gylon). The second element is derived from the Greek noun ἵππος (hippos) meaning ""horse""."
