Gyu-min,m,"규민(Korean Hangul)|圭民, 圭旼, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/ɡju.min/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 圭 (gyu) meaning “sharpened jade” combined with 民 (min) meaning ""people, citizens"" or 旼 (min) meaning ""gentle, affable”. Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
