H,f,,Rade|Mnong|Jarai,/ˈhə/(Rade),,,,,,,"Shortened from Hơ-Bia. In Rade, this is a mandatory feminine marker and is usually written before the given name with an apostrophe (H'), or sometimes a hyphen (H-). Following Vietnamese writing conventions it is also separated from the given name with a space. In Mnong, this is a middle name replacing surnames."
