Habrote,f,Ἀβρώτη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἁβρῶς (habros) meaning ""gracefully, delicately"", itself from ἁβρός (habros) ""graceful, delicate, refined, splendid"". In Greek mythology, Habrote or Abrota was the Boeotian wife of Nisos, king of Megara."
