Hadraniel,m,הדרניאל(Ancient Hebrew),Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Means ""majesty of God"" from Hebrew הָדָר (hadar) meaning ""majesty, splendour, glory"" and אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"". This is the name of an angel in Jewish mythology, said to guard the second gate in Heaven. He was the angel encountered by Moses during his journey to Heaven to obtain the Torah from God."
