Hadzuki,,"葉月, 晴月, 羽月, 波月, 覇月, 波津希, 羽津紀, 葉津樹(Japanese Kanji)|はづき(Japanese Hiragana)|ハヅキ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,HAH-ZUU-KEE|HAH-DZUU-KEE,,,,,,,"As a unisex name, this name combines 葉 (you, ha) meaning ""blade, leaf, needle"" or 晴 (sei, ha.re, haru) meaning ""clear weather, fair, fine"" with 月 (gatsu, getsu, tsuki) meaning ""moon, month.""As a feminine name, this name combines 羽 (u, ha, hane, wa) meaning ""feather,"" 波 (ha, nami) meaning ""billow, wave, ripple"" or 覇 (ha, haku, hatagashira) meaning ""hegemony, supremacy"" with 月. Rarer examples with 3 kanji for females include 波津希, 羽津紀 and 葉津樹 with 津 (shin, tsu, zu) meaning ""harbour, port,"" 希 (ki, ke, mare) meaning ""few, hope, wish, rare,"" 紀 (ki) meaning ""account, chronicle, history, narrative"" and 樹 (ju, ki) meaning ""timber, wood, tree.""Hadzuki/Hazuki (葉月) is the traditional name for August, meaning ""month of leaves"", with the older form of it being 葉落ち月 (haochidzuki/haochizuki, はおちづき) which means ""month of falling leaves."""
