Hakunei,,,Shona,Ha-koo-ne-ee,,,,,,,"This is a name that implies and asks, meaning ""What is not there?"". This is a name given by or to someone who is assumed to be falling short or without, so they name the child ""What could be missing?"" in a sense of affirmation, so to say there is perfection even if you (all) do not see it or doubt it. A short form of the name is Haku or Kunei."
