Hakuren,m,"伯廉, 伯連, 白廉, 白蓮, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-KUU-ṘEN,,,,,,,"From Japanese 伯 (haku) meaning ""chief, count, earl, uncle"" or 白 (haku) meaning ""white"" combined with 廉 (ren) meaning ""bargain, reason, charge, suspicion, point, account, purity, honest, low price, cheap, rested, contented, peaceful"", 連 (ren) meaning ""take along, lead, join, connect, party, gang, clique"" or 蓮 (ren) meaning ""lotus"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
