Halirrhothius,m,"Ἁλιρρόθιος, Ἁλιρόθιος(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology,/ˌhæl.ɪ.ˈroʊ.θi.əs/,,,,,,,"Means ""sea-beaten, buffeted by the sea"" in Ancient Greek, ultimately derived from ἅλς (hals) meaning ""sea, brine, salt"" and ῥόθος (rhosis) meaning ""rushing noise, tumult, roar of waves"" or ""rushing motion"". This was the name of a son of Poseidon in Greek mythology. In some accounts he raped Alcippe and was murdered by her father Ares in vengeance; in another version of the myth, he was instead accidentally killed by his own axe while cutting down an olive tree, and a grief-stricken Poseidon then accused Ares of murder."
