Halosydne,f,Ἁλοσύδνη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Often interpreted as ""sea-born"", though it could literally translate as ""sea-fed, nourished by the sea,"" deriving from Ancient Greek ἅλς (hals) meaning ""salt, brine, sea"" and ὑδνέω (hydneo) meaning ""to nourish"". This was an epithet of the Greek goddesses Amphitrite and Thetis, as well as of the Nereids."
