Hana-i,f,하나이(Korean Hangul),"Korean (Modern, Rare)",/hä.nä.i/,,,,,,,"From Hana 4 likely combined with the suffix 이 (-i), referring to a person, effectively meaning ""one person"" (compare other words like 둘이 (dul-i) meaning ""two people; pair; couple"" and 여럿이 (yeoreot-i) meaning ""many people"")."
Hanai,f,,Hawaiian,hah-NAI,,,,,,,"Derived from Hawaiian word hānai meaning ""foster child, to adopt, to nurture."" Could also be a shortened version of the name Hanaiakamalama."
Hanaiakamalama,,,Hawaiian,hah-NAH-ee-ah-kah-mah-LAH-mah,,,,,,,"A compound name in Hawaiian meaning ""work of the moon"" or ""guardian of the moon,"" derived from:hānai (hānai): ""to feed,"" ""to foster,"" or ""to care for."" ka: ""the."" mālama (mālama): ""moon"" or ""to care for."""
Hanaka,f,"瑛華, 英果, 英香, 華々, 花香, 花華, 華夏, 華花, 華華, 華香, 七香, 葉菜花, 話花, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 華 (hana) or 花 (hana) both meaning ""flower"" combined with 華 (ka) or 花 (ka) both meaning ""flower"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hanalei,,,Hawaiian,,,,,,,,"Means ""crescent bay"" from Hawaiian hana ""bay"" and lei. It is sometimes used as the Hawaiian form of Henry."
Hanaliza,f,,Sorbian,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hanəm,f,,Abkhaz,,,,,,,,"Derived from Turkic hanım meaning ""lady, mistress""."
Hanamarja,f,,Sorbian,,,,,,,,Combination of Hana and Marja as well as a Lower Sorbian variant of Anemarija.
Hanamaru,m,"花園, 花丸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-MAH-ṘUU,,,,,,,"From Japanese 花園 (hanamaru) meaning ""flower garden""."
Haname,f,"花愛, 花芽, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 花 (hana) meaning ""flower"" combined with 愛 (me) meaning ""love, affection"" or 芽 (me) meaning ""bud, sprout, shoot"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hanameel,m,חנמאל(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,,,,,,,,"Hanameel, meaning ""rest from God,"" a cousin of Jeremiah from whom the latter bought property. Jeremiah 32:7ff."
Hanami,f,花見(Japanese Kanji)|はなみ(Japanese Hiragana)|ハナミ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese,HA-NAH-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 花見 (hanami) meaning ""flower view"" or ""blossom view"" combining 花 (hana) meaning ""flower"" and 見 (mi) which actually means ""view, see, viewing""This might be a reference to a beautiful view of some cherry blossoms trees, Sakura, in Japan."
Hanana,f,"花々, 花夏, 花菜, 花那, 花名, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 花 (hana) meaning ""flower"" combined with 々, a phonetic character indicting a duplication of the beginning kanji, 夏 (na) meaning ""summer"", 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"", 那 (na) meaning ""what"" or 名 (na) meaning ""name"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hanane,f,"花音, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-NE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 花 (hana) meaning ""flower"" combined with 音 (ne) meaning ""sound"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Hananeel,m,חֲנִנאֵל(Hebrew),Biblical|Hebrew,,,,,,,,"Means ""God is gracious"" in Hebrew, from חָנַן (ḥanan) ""to be gracious"" and אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"". The name Elhanan is derived from the same roots in reverse order. This was the name of a tower in the northeastern corner of Jerusalem, as mentioned in Nehemiah 3:1 and 12:39."
Hananeh,f,,Persian,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Hanan 2, meaning ""mercy, compassion"". Various forms of this name are common in the Middle East."
Hananel,m,,Hebrew|Biblical,,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Hebrew חֲנִנאֵל (see Hananeel).
Hanani,m,,Hebrew (Rare)|Biblical,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hanania,f,,Biblical (Rare),,,,,,,,Feminine form of Hananiah.
