Hanaura,f,,Polynesian,Ha-na-ura,,,,,,,"From hamani synonym of hana meaning ""create"", or hana meaning ""sad, affected"" and ""ura"" meaning ""red, bright""."
Hanaya,f,"英耶, 英弥, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-NAH-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 英 (hana) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 耶 (ya), a phonetic character. Other kanji combinations are possible."
