Hanra,,"한라, 한나(Korean Hangul)",Korean,HAHN-RAH|HAHL-RAH|HAHN-NAH,,,,,,,"Meaning ""High Land"". From Ancient Native Korean 'Han(한) / Khan, Kan(칸)' Meaning ""Giant, Great, Big, High"" and Ancient Native Korean 'Na, Ra(나, 라)' Meaning ""Land"". Before Hangul was Created, This name was Recorded Korean Hanja ""漢拏"". This name is also used as a place name for the Korean mountain, 'Hallasan'."
