Harfang,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"From a name of the snowy owl, originally Swedish harfång, which means ""hare-catcher"" from har(e) ""hare"" and fånga ""to catch"". It occurs briefly in the 'Harry Potter' series belonging to a pure-blood wizard (Harfang Longbottom) and in 'The Chronicles of Narnia' series (in the sixth book, 'The Silver Chair') as the name of a city of giants (""the great city of the far northern giants (the civilized ones)"")."
