Hariasa,f,,Germanic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Hariasa is a Germanic goddess attested on a (now lost) stone bearing a Latin dedication to her. Her name is likely derived from Proto-Germanic *harja ""army; battle"". Linguist Siegfried Gutenbrunner reconstructed the form *Hari-ansus ""army goddess; war goddess"", while Rudolf Simek compares her name to that of the valkyrie Herja."
