Harimella,f,,Germanic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Harimella is a Germanic goddess known from an inscription in Dumfriesshire, Scotland. The first element of her name is derived from Germanic *xarjaz (harjaz) ""army"", the second element -mella is of debated origin and meaning. Theories include a derivation from Old Norse mjöll (and ultimately Proto-Germanic *mella) ""snow, new snow"", Old Irish mall ""slow"" and Germanic *maþlan ""gathering; gathering place""."
