Haruji,m,"春次, 春司, 治二, 春治, 春二, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-ṘOO-JEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 春 (haru) meaning ""spring"" combined with 次 (ji) meaning ""next, secondary"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Harukako,f,"春香子, 遥子, 遥夏子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),HAH-ṘOO-KAH-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 春 (haru) meaning ""spring"", 香 (ka) meaning ""fragrance"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Harukana,f,"遥奈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-ṘUU-KAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 遥 (haruka) meaning ""distant, remote"" combined with 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"". This name can also be formed of other kanji combinations."
