Harukaze,,"春風, 晴風, 陽風, 暖風, 悠風, 遙風, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|はるかぜ(Japanese Hiragana)|ハルカゼ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[hä.ɾɯ̟ᵝ.kä.ze̞],,,,,,,"From 春風 (harukaze) meaning ""spring breeze.""The first element can also be written as 晴 meaning ""clear, fine,"" 陽 meaning ""sun,"" 暖 meaning ""warmth,"" 悠 meaning ""quiet, calm"" or 遙 meaning ""far off, distant,"" among others.This name is rarely used."
