Harukuni,m,"悠薰, 浩郁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-ROO-KOO-NEE,,,,,,,"From 温 (haru) meaning ""warm"", 浩 (haru) meaning ""prosperous"" or 悠 (haru) meaning ""permanence"" and 邦 (kuni) meaning ""home country"", 郁 (kuni) meaning ""culture, cultural progress, fragrance, perfume"", or 薰 (kuni) meaning ""scent, fragrance, perfume, smolder"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
