Harumu,,"はるむ(Japanese Hiragana)|ハルム(Japanese Katakana)|令六, 温向, 会歩, 花舞, 桜無, 開澄, 遼生, 青好, 合身, 華頼, 美矛, 波瑠和, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HA-ROO-MOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 墾 (haru) meaning ""ground-breaking, open up farmland"", 覇 (haru) meaning ""hegemony, supremacy, leadership, champion"", or 明 (haru) meaning ""bright, light"" combined with 向 (mu) meaning ""yonder, beyond"", 務 (mu) meaning ""task, duties"" or 睦 (mu) meaning ""intimate, friendly, harmonious"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
