Hati,,,Norse Mythology|Swedish (Rare)|Finnish|Old Norse,,,,,,,,"Means ""despiser, hater"". In Norse mythology Hati is a wolf who pursues the moon. He is the son of Hróðvitnir (another name for Fenrir), the father of Hrímgarðr, and the brother of Skǫll, who pursues the sun."
