Hattusa-ziti,m,,Hittite,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""man from Hattusa"", deriving from the Luwian element ziti (""man""). The city of Hattusa was a major political center for the Hittite Empire. Name borne by an envoy of Suppiluliuma I, who was sent to the court of the Egyptian queen Ankhesenamun."
