Haude,f,,Old Celtic (Gallicized)|History (Ecclesiastical)|French,,,,,,,,"Gallicized form of the Celtic name Eodez or Heodez.A notable bearer of this name is the 6th-century saint Haude of Trémazan, who was born in the Gaulish region of Armorica (now Brittany in France) and lived there until her death in 545."
Haug,m,,East Frisian (Rare)|North Frisian (Rare)|West Frisian (Archaic)|Upper German,,,,,,,,"Frisian and Upper German form of Hugo as well as a short form of other Germanic given names that have hugu meaning ""heart, mind, spirit"" for a first element.Also compare Hauk."
