Haugspori,m,,Norse Mythology|Old Norse,,,,,,,,"Means ""hill treader"". This is the name of a dwarf in Norse mythology."
Hauk,,,East Frisian (Rare)|North Frisian (Rare)|West Frisian (Rare)|Norwegian,/ˈhæʉk/,,,,,,,"Frisian short form of Germanic given names that have hugu meaning ""heart, mind, spirit"" for a first element, such as Hugubert. Also compare Haug, which this name could be considered to be a variant form of."
Haukim,m,,Near Eastern Mythology,,,,,,,,"Haukim is a pre-Islamic deity who was originally worshipped in Qataban, in what is now South Arabia. He was concerned with arbitration and the law."
Hauksteinn,m,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Norse haukr ""hawk"" and steinn ""stone"". Also compare Haukur."
