Hauna,f,,Polynesian,Hau-na,,,,,,,"Variant of Haunua, or from Hawaiian hauna meaning ""odor, tainted"" or ""offering""."
Haunaele,,,Hawaiian,how-na-eh-leh,,,,,,,"Means ""riot, tumult"" in Hawaiian from the word haunaele."
Haunoa,,,Tahitian (Rare),Hau-nòa,,,,,,,"Meaning ""peace and liberty"" or ""free nation"" in Tahitian, from hau meaning ""wind, peace, nation"" and noa meaning ""freedom""."
Haunoarai,,,Polynesian|Tahitian,Hau-noa-rài,,,,,,,"Polynesian name, composed by ""hau"", meaning ""wind"" or ""peace"", by ""noa"", meaning ""freedom"" and ""rai"", meaning ""sky"", ""heaven"". Hence the meaning can be interpreted as ""peace and freedom from sky"" or ""heavenly wind of freedom""."
Haunoarii,m,,Polynesian|Tahitian,Hau-noa-rii,,,,,,,"From hau meaning ""peace, wind"", and no meaning ""from, of"" or noa meaning ""freedom"" and arii meaning ""chief, king"" in Tahitian. Hence the meaning can be interpreted as ""king of peace; king of wind"" or ""peaceful freedom king""."
ǃHãunu,m,,San Mythology,,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. In the San mythology, he existed along with his brother-in-law ǂKá̦gára, which they both fought with lightning that causes massive storms.Note: The ""ǃ"" sign reflects Latin retroflex click, instead of an exclamation mark (compare Nǃxau)."
Haunua,f,,Polynesian,Hau-nua,,,,,,,"Composed of hau, meaning ""wind"" and nua, meaning ""above""; hence the meaning is ""high wind, wind above""."
Haunui,m,,Tahitian,,,,,,,,"Means ""great peace"" from Tahitian hau meaning ""peace, concord"" and nui meaning ""great, big""."
Hauʻoli,,,Hawaiian,,,,,,,,"Means ""happiness"" in Hawaiian. This name was used by American actress Mary Astor as a middle name for her daughter, Marylyn Hauoli Thorpe, who was born in 1932 in Honolulu, Hawaii. A known bearer is American football player Hauʻoli Kikaha (1992-)."
Hauora,,,Māori,how-oh-ra,,,,,,,"From hauora meaning ""health"" in Māori, or hau meaning ""wind, breeze; vitality; fame"" and ora meaning ""life"" in Māori."
