Havaska,f,,Hungarian,,,,,,,,"Of debated origin and meaning. Theories include a derivation from Hungarian havas ""snowy, snow-covered; mountain"" and a modern form of an alleged Old Hungarian given name Havadi which is said to have meant ""moon"" in Old Hungarian, whereas in modern Szekler-Hungarian havadi is a general term for white springflowers, most commonly the white narcissus or the snowdrop flower."
