Hawaii,,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)|Hawaiian",hah-WIE(American English)|hah-WIE-ee(Hawaiian),,,,,,,"From the name of Hawai'i, a US state. The name Hawai'i originates from Proto-Polynesian hawaiki and Proto-Nuclear Polynesian sawaiki meaning ""homeland"" and ""place of the gods"", or possibly named for Hawaiʻiloa, legendary discoverer of the Hawaiian islands. Hawai'i is a cognate of Hawaiki."
Hawaiʻiloa,,,Hawaiian|Polynesian Mythology,hah-WIE-ee-loh-ah,,,,,,,"Means ""great Hawai'i"" in Hawaiian. This was the name of the mythical figure who apparently discovered Hawai'i, and became the namesake for the island. Hawai'i originates from Proto-Polynesian hawaiki and Proto-Nuclear Polynesian sawaiki meaning ""ancestral homeland; spirit world""."
Hawaiki,f,,Tahitian|Māori,HA-WA-EE-KEE,,,,,,,"Derived from Proto-Polynesian Sawaiki meaning ""Ra'iātea"", referring to the island of which the Polynesian peoples originated from. Today, Ra'iātea is the second largest island in French Polynesia."
