Ha-won,,"하원(Korean Hangul)|夏媛, 夏原, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/ha̠ː.wʌn/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 夏 (ha) meaning ""summer, great, grand"" combined with 媛 (won) meaning ""beautiful woman"" or 原 (won) meaning ""source, origin, beginning"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Hawra,f,حَوْراء‎(Arabic),Arabic|Muslim,,,,,,,,"Means ""having eyes with a marked contrast of black and white; gazelle-eyed"" in Arabic.In the Islamic religion, a ḥawrā is an angelic, virgin woman (similar to the Greek nymphs) who will accompany faithful believers in Paradise."
