Hayano,f,"はやの(Japanese Hiragana)|迅乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-YAH-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 迅 (haya) meaning ""swift, fast"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Hayao,m,"隼雄, 隼男, 隼夫, 隼郎, 勇夫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HAH-YAH-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 隼 (haya) meaning ""falcon"" or 勇 (haya) meaning ""brave"" combined with 雄 (o) meaning ""hero, manly"", 男 (o) meaning ""male"", 夫 (o) meaning ""man, husband"" or 郎 (o) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible.Famous bearer of this name is Japanese film director, producer, screenwriter, animator, author, and manga artist Hayao Miyazaki."
