Heleni,f,הֶלֵּנִי(Hebrew),"Portuguese (Brazilian, Rare)|History (Hebraized)|Hebrew (Modern)",/e.le.ˈni/(Brazilian Portuguese),,,,,,,Brazilian variant of Helene and Hebrewized spelling of Helene. As a Hebrew name it was borne by Queen Helena of Adiabene who was a Queen of a Vassal state of the Parthian Empire and a convert to Judaism. As a legtimate Hebrew name its usage is relatively modern.
Helenice,f,,Portuguese (Brazilian),,,,,,,,Elaboration of Helen by borrowing the suffix ice (from names like Beatrice).
