Helenore,f,,English (Rare)|Literature,,,,,,,,"An elaboration of Helen or Elenore. Used by Scottish poet Alexander Ross (1699-1784) in Helenore, or the Fortunate Shepherdess, published in 1768."
Hélénos,m,,Greek Mythology (Gallicized),,,,,,,,French form of Helenus.
Heleri,f,,Estonian (Modern),,,,,,,,Combination of Helena and Maria or Katariina.
Heleriin,f,,"Estonian (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Combination of Hele and Riin.
Helerin,f,,"Estonian (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Heleriin.
Helerio,m,,Spanish,,,,,,,,Spanish form of Helier via Helerius.
Helernus,m,,Roman Mythology,/he.ˈler.nus/(Classical Latin),,,,,,,Meaning unknown. It was borne by a minor god of the underworld in Roman mythology.
Helery,f,,Estonian (Modern),,,,,,,,Variant of Heleri.
Helevysa,f,,Medieval French,,,,,,,,Variant of Helewis.
