Helina,f,,Medieval Polish|Swedish (Rare)|Estonian (Rare),,,,,,,,Medieval Polish variant of Alina.
Helinä,f,,Finnish,HE-li-na,,,,,,,"Derives from Finnish word helinä, which means ""jingle"" in Finnish. It may possibly have been used also as a variant of Helena.Helinä is also Tinker Bell's Finnish name."
Helinda,f,,English (Rare),HEL-in-da,,,,,,,Not available.
Héline,f,,"French (Modern, Rare)|French (Belgian, Modern, Rare)|Flemish (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Éline.
Heline,f,Հեղինե(Armenian),Armenian|Old Swedish|Swedish (Rare),,,,,,,,Armenian form of Helen and Swedish variant of Helina.
Heling,m,"鹤龄, 鶴齡(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,"From Chinese 鹤 (hè) meaning ""crane (bird)"" and 龄 (líng) meaning ""age, duration""."
Helinka,f,,"English (Australian, Rare)",,,,,,,,Not available.
Helinna,f,,English (Rare),hə-LEEN-a,,,,,,,Variant of Helena.
Heliocles,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Heliokles. This name was borne by a Greek king of Bactria (now northern Afghanistan) from the 2nd century BC.
