Help,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"From the English word help, which is both a noun meaning ""succour, assistance"" and a verb meaning ""to support, to do good to""; in Middle English help also meant ""assistant, helper"". This is the name of a man in the First Part of The Pilgrim's Progress (1678) by John Bunyan."
