Henutmehyt,f,,Ancient Egyptian,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Egyptian ḥnwt meaning ""mistress, lady"" and mḥyt meaning ""north wind"", as well as referring to the goddess Mehyt. This was the name of a priestess who lived in Thebes during the 19th dynasty (c. 1250 BCE). Her gilded coffins are now on display at the British Museum in London."
