Heren,f,"碧恋, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HE-ṘEN,,,,,,,"From Japanese 碧 (he) meaning ""green, blue"" combined with 恋 (ren) meaning ""love"". This name can also be formed of other kanji combinations.Usage of this name is, most likely, influenced by the name Helen, Helene and Hellen."
Herena,f,,History (Ecclesiastical)|Polish (Archaic)|Catalan|Māori,,,,,,,,The name of an early Christian Saint from North Africa martyred in the 3rd century. Nothing about her is known except from her name.
