Hermolaus,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized)|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Hermolaos. This name was borne by Hermolaus of Macedon (4th century BC), a page of Alexander the Great who was executed for planning regicide. Saint Hermolaus is a saint of the Orthodox Church."
Hermolochos,m,Ἑρμόλοχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the name of the Greek messenger god Hermes combined with the Greek noun λόχος (lochos) meaning ""ambush"", a word that later came to signify a tactical sub unit of the ancient Greek army. The word is ultimately derived from the Greek verb λοχάω (lochao) meaning ""to lie in wait for, to waylay"" as well as ""to snare""."
