Herophilos,m,Ἡρόφιλος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/hɪ.ˈrɒ.fɪ.ləs/(English)|/hɛː.ró.pʰi.los/(Attic Greek)|/i.ˈro.ɸi.los/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from the name of the Greek goddess Hera combined with Ancient Greek φίλος (philos) meaning ""friend, lover"".This name was borne by a Greek physician from the 3rd century BC, considered to be one of the earliest recorded anatomists."
