Heyang,,,Chinese,HUH-YAHNG,,,,,,,"Derives from Mandarin (合阳 or 河阳), and is commonly used as a place name or surname, meaning ""sun"" or ""bright"" in a geographic context, such as the ""sunny side of a river"" or ""sunny side of a mountain"". It often reflects meanings of prosperity, warmth, and light."
