Heyman,m,,Medieval Dutch|Dutch (Rare)|German (Silesian)|Medieval German,HEY-mahn(Dutch),,,,,,,"Medieval Dutch form of Hagiman. In that era, Heyman was sometimes also used as a pet form of Hendrick.This name is still in use today, but it is rare and slightly less common than its modern form Heiman.A known bearer of this name was Heyman Dullaert (1636-1684), a Dutch painter and poet who was a student of the famous Dutch painter Rembrandt van Rijn (1606-1669)."
Heymann,m,היימאַן(Yiddish),"Yiddish (Rare, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Medieval Yiddish and Archaic diminutive form of Chayyim (see Chayim) by using the Middle German diminutive suffix Mann. This name could also be the German form of Hagiman in some cases; for this, compare the medieval Dutch name Heyman.A notable bearer of this name was the German Jewish philologist and philosopher Heymann Steinthal (1823-1899)."
