Hialeah,f,,Indigenous American,/ˌhaɪə.ˈliːə/,,,,,,,"Derived from the Muskogee haiyakpo meaning ""prairie"" and hili meaning ""pretty"". Alternatively, the name is of Seminole origin meaning ""upland prairie"". It also is the name of the 6th largest city in Florida.Possibly a spelling alternative to Hailey or Haley."
