Hibari,f,"ひばり(Japanese Hiragana)|雲雀, 灯巴里, 日羽理, 妃羽理, 陽羽理, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-BAH-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 雲 meaning ""cloud"" and 雀 meaning ""sparrow"". As a word. 雲雀 (hibari) means ""lark, skylark"". Other spellings are possible.A famous bearer is Hibari Misora (1937–1989). She was an award-winning Japanese enka singer and actress, born Kazue Kato."
