Hibernia,f,,English (Rare),hie-BUR-nee-ə,,,,,,,"From the Classical Latin name for Ireland, now used poetically. The name is a Latinized form of Ancient Greek Ἰουερνία (Iouernia) ""Ireland"", which is thought to be ultimately derived from Proto-Celtic *ɸīweriyū ""earth, soil"" (whence Éire), influenced by Latin hibernus ""wintry, of winter""."
