Hibika,f,"日日日, 妃美華, 響花, 響歌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-BEE-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"", 妃 (hi) meaning ""a ruler's wife, queen, empress"", 日 (bi) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"", 美 (bi) meaning ""beautiful"" or 響 (hibi) meaning ""sound, echo"" combined with 日 (ka) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"", 花 (ka) or 華 (ka) which both mean ""flower"" or 歌 (ka) meaning ""song, poetry"". Additionally, other kanji combinations can form this name."
Hibikana,f,"響佳奈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-BEE-KAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 響 (hibi) meaning ""sound, echo"", 佳 (ka) meaning ""good, beautiful"" combined with 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hibiku,f,"響, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-BEE-KOO,,,,,,,"From the word 響く (hibiku) meaning ""echo, noise, reverberation, sound"". Other spellings are possible."
Hibil,m,ࡄࡉࡁࡉࡋ(Mandaic),Mandaean|Gnosticism,/ˈhi.bɪl/(Mandaic),,,,,,,"Mandaic form of Hevel (see Abel). This is the name of an uthra (a celestial being) and one of the three sons of Adam in Mandaean tradition, considered an equivalent of the biblical Abel. However in some Mandaean texts he appears in the form of Hibil Ziwa (meaning ""Splendid Hibil""), in which he is referred to as a son of Manda d-Hayyi and instead associated with the angel Gabriel."
Hibina,f,"響菜, 響奈, 日々菜, 陽々奈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-BEE-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 響 (hibi) meaning ""sound, echo"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hibio,m,"日々雄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-BEE-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 々, a phonetic character indicting a duplication of the beginning kanji combined with 雄 (o) meaning ""hero, manly"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hibito,m,"響人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-BEE-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 響 (hibi) meaning ""sound"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hibiya,m,,"Japanese (Modern, Rare)|Popular Culture",HEE-BEE-YAH(Japanese),,,,,,,"This name is used as 響也 with 響 (kyou, hibi.ku) meaning ""echo, resound, ring, sound, vibrate"" and 也 (e, ya, ka, nari, mata) meaning ""to be (classical form).""One fictional bearer of this name is Hibiya Amamiya (雨宮 響也), known only as Hibiya (ヒビヤ) in the mixed-media project Kagerou Project.Baby boys with 響也 written on their name are most likely to be named Kyōya instead of Hibiya and Hibiya is more often seen as a surname and place name."
Hicabod,m,,Biblical Latin,,,,,,,,Form of Ichabod used in the Latin Old Testament.
Hiccup,m,,Popular Culture,,,,,,,,"The name of the protagonist of the ""How to train your dragon"" franchise."
