Hiddeke,f,,East Frisian (Archaic),,,,,,,,Not available.
Hide,,"秀, 英, 日出, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひで(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,[çí.dè̞],,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide), shifted from hiide, the stem of verb 秀でる (hiideru) (Old Japanese hiidzu) meaning ""to excel, surpass,"" in turn a combination of 穂 (ho>hi) meaning ""ear/head (of plant); point, tip"" and verb 出づ (idzu) (modern deru) meaning ""to come out."" Other kanji can be used in relation to the verb, e.g. 英 meaning ""wisdom, brilliance."" The combination 日出 is also used, stemming from a shortening of 日の出 (hinode) meaning ""sunrise.""In use as a(n uncommon) feminine name before the Meiji Period (1868-1912) with increase in usage for both genders in that period, Hide is, nowadays, mainly used as a (largely male) nickname for names like Hidenobu or Hideyoshi."
Hidechika,m,"秀誓, 秀和, 秀史, 英親, 英愛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-DE-CHEE-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 誓 (chika) meaning ""swear, pledge"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hidefumi,m,"英文, 秀文, 秀史, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-FOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 文 (fumi) meaning ""writing"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
Hideharu,m,"英治, 秀治, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-HAH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" and 治 (haru) meaning ""to govern, to rule, to administrate"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hidehiko,m,"秀彦, 英彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-KHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy, prince"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hidehiro,m,"英大, 秀浩, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-KHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 大 (hiro) meaning ""big, great"". Other kanji combinations can spell this name."
Hidehisa,m,"秀久, 英久(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-KHEE-SA,,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"", and 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago""."
Hideitsu,m,"英逸, 英五, 秀一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-DEH-EE-TSOO,,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 伍 (itsu) meaning ""five"" or 一 (itsu) meaning ""one"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hideji,m,"秀二, 英司...(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 二 (ji) meaning ""two"".This name can also be formed using other kanji combinations."
Hidekata,m,,"Japanese (Rare, Archaic, ?)",,,,,,,,Not available.
Hidekatsu,m,"ひでかつ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデカツ(Japanese Katakana)|秀勝, 英克, 轄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-KA-TSOO,,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 克 (katsu) meaning ""to overcome"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hidekazu,m,"豪一, 秀一, 英数, 英一, 秀量, 日出一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-KA-ZOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 豪 (hide) meaning ""bold, magnificent, Australia"" combined with 量 (kazu) meaning ""progress"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Hidekichi,m,"ヒデキチ(Japanese Katakana)|秀吉, 秀亀智, 日出吉, 秀喜知, 英吉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-KEE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""fine"" combined with 吉 (kichi) meaning ""good luck, fortune"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hidekuni,m,"ひでくに(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデクニ(Japanese Katakana)|秀国, 英邦, 郁國, 任薫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-KOO-NEE,,,,,,,"From 任 (hide) meaning ""duty, responsibility, term, to entrust, to appoint"" combined with 薫 (kuni) meaning ""scent, fragrant"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hidema,m,"秀馬, 秀磨, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-DE-MAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""to bear fruit"" combined with 馬 (ma) meaning ""horse"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Hidemaro,m,"秀麿, 英麿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひでまろ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデマロ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/çi.de̞.mä.ɾo̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" combined with 麿 (maro) meaning ""I, me"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Hidemasa,m,"英昌⁠, 秀匡, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-MAH-SAH,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" and 昌⁠ (masa) meaning ""good, prosper"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hidemitsu,m,"秀満, 英光, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-MEE-TSOO,,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide) meaning ""preeminence"" and 満 (mitsu) meaning ""to fulfill, to satisfy"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hideno,f,"英乃, 秀乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ヒデノ(Japanese Katakana)|ひでの(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,HEE-DE-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 英 (hide) meaning ""English"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Hidenobu,m,"英信, 英延, 秀信, 秀延, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-NO-BOO,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide, ei) meaning ""wisdom, brilliance"" or 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 信 (nobu) meaning ""trust, faith, believe"" or 延 (nobu) meaning ""prolong, stretch"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hidenori,m,"ヒデノリ(Japanese Katakana)|栄憲, 栄敬, 偉仁, 一孝, 豪律, 一周, 豪矩, 英典, 一徳, 英範, 豪文, 日出慎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-NO-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 豪 (hide) meaning ""bold, magnificent, Australia"", 偉 (hide) meaning ""admirable"" or 一 (hide) meaning ""one"" combined with 仁 (nori) meaning ""benevolence"", 雅 (nori) meaning ""gracious, graceful, refined, elegant"" or 智 (nori) meaning ""intellect, knowledge, wisdom"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hideomi,m,"秀臣, 英臣, 栄臣, 秀民, 日出臣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-DE-O-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 臣 (omi) meaning ""minister; statesman; official"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name.A famous bearer is Hideomi Yamamoto, a Japanese footballer who plays for Ventforet Kofu in the J. League Division 1."
Hidero,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Hiderou.
Hiderou,m,"栄郎, 英朗, 英郎, 秀廊, 秀朗, 秀郎, 日出郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-DE-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"", 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" or 栄 (hide) meaning ""glory, honour"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"", 朗 (rou) meaning ""bright, clear"" or 廊 (rou) meaning ""corridor"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hiderus,m,,Arthurian Cycle (Latinized),,,,,,,,Form of Edern used in Geoffrey of Monmouth's Historia Regum Brittaniae.
Hideshi,m,"ひでし(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデシ(Japanese Katakana)|秀, 秀磁, 継示, 継視, 豪資, 豪次, 英詞, 英嗣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 士 (shi) meaning ""samurai, warrior"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Hideshi Matsuda (1954-)​, a Japanese car racer and TV reporter."
Hidetada,m,"秀忠, 秀匡, 英忠, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-DEH-TAH-DAH,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" and 忠 (tada) meaning ""loyalty"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hidetaka,m,"英敬, 秀敬, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-TAH-KAH,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" or 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 敬 (taka) meaning ""respect, honor, reverence""."
Hideto,m,"秀人, 栄斗, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひでと(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒデト(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/çi.de̞.to̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" or 栄 (hide) meaning ""glory, honour, flourish, prosper"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""man, person, mankind, people"" or 斗 (to) meaning ""dipper"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Hidetomo,m,"秀朝, 英智, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-TO-MO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" or 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 智 (tomo) meaning ""knowledge, wisdom"". Other kanji combinations can be used, too."
Hidetoshi,m,"英俊, 秀俊, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DE-TO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" or 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 俊 (toshi) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 利 (toshi) meaning ""benefit, advantage"". Other kanji combinations can be used instead."
Hidetsugu,m,"秀次, 秀嗣, 英嗣, 英次, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-TSOO-GOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent"" combined with 次 (tsugu) meaning ""next, second"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Hideyasu,m,"秀廉, 英廉, 秀康, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-YAH-SOO,,,,,,,"From 秀 (hide) meaning ""preeminence"" and 廉 (yasu) meaning ""clean, honest, inexpensive"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hideyo,m,"秀世, 英世, 秀依, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-YO,,,,,,,"From the Japanese 秀 (hide) ""preeminence, to surpass, to excel"" and 世 (yo) ""world"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hideyori,m,"秀頼, 英依, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-DEH-YO-REE,,,,,,,"From 英 (hide) meaning ""wisdom, brilliance"" and 頼 (yori) meaning ""rely"". Other kanji combinations can be added."
Hideyuki,m,"英行, 英之, 英至, 秀行, 秀幸, 秀至, 偉至, 偉之, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-DEH-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 偉 (hide) meaning ""admirable"" or 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"" and 幸 (yuki) meaning ""happiness, good fortune, luck"" or 至 (yuki) meaning ""of, this"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hideyuu,m,"秀勇, 英佑, 秀祐, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-DE-YUU:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"" combined with 勇 (yuu) meaning ""brave"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
Hidhin,m,,Old Swedish,,,,,,,,Old Swedish form of Heðinn.
Hidilyn,f,,Filipino (Rare),[haɪ.dɪ.ˈlin],,,,,,,"Variant of Heidilyn. A bearer of this name is Hidilyn Diaz, a Filipino weightlifter and airwoman."
Hıdır,m,,Turkish,/hɯ.ˈdɯr/,,,,,,,Turkish form of Khidr.
Hidoyatullo,m,"Ҳидоятулло(Tajik, Uzbek Cyrillic)",Tajik|Uzbek (Rare),,,,,,,,Tajik and Uzbek form of Hidayatullah.
Hidser,m,,West Frisian (Rare),HID-sər,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. It might possibly be the West Frisian form of a masculine Germanic name that contains the Germanic element hild meaning ""battle"", such as Hildegar. Also compare Hedser."
Hidsert,m,,West Frisian (Archaic),HID-sərt,,,,,,,Variant of Hidser. It is possible that this name could also be the West Frisian form of Hildard or Hildeward. Also compare Hedsert and Idsert.
Hidzir,m,,Malay,,,,,,,,Malay variant of Khidr.
Hie,f,"姫愛, 陽依, 陽愛, 緋愛, 日笑, 陽恵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hi) meaning ""princess"" combined with 愛 (e) meaning ""love, affection"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hiê,f,慧(Chinese),Chinese (Min Dong),,,,,,,,Min Dong form of Hui.
Hiedra,f,,"Spanish (European, Rare)",/ˈɟ͡ʝe.ð̞ɾa/(Spanish),,,,,,,"Means ""ivy"" in Spanish. This is an obscure title of the Virgin Mary, Nuestra Señora de la Hiedra, meaning ""Our Lady of Ivy"", venerated at a hermitage in Constantina, Spain."
Hiei,m,飛影(Japanese Kanji),Japanese|Popular Culture,He-a(Japanese)|HEE-E-EE(Japanese),,,,,,,"Means ""flying shadow"" in Japanese, from 飛 (hi) ""jump, fly"" and 影 (ei) ""shadow"".A fictional bearer of this name is Hiei (飛影) from 'YuYu Hakusho'."
Hieke,f,,Dutch (Rare),HEE-KU,,,,,,,"Frisian name, an abbreviations from names with the element Hild. Related to Hidde and Hibbe."
Hieko,f,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hiel,m,"אֲחִיאֵל, חִיאֵל(Ancient Hebrew)",Biblical,,,,,,,,"Hiel the Bethelite, means ""the Divine brother, or kinsman, is God,"" rebuilt Jericho during the reign of King Ahab. (I Kings 16:34)"
Hielm,m,,Old Danish,,,,,,,,Old Danish form of Hialmr.
Hiểm,,,"Vietnamese (Rare, Archaic)",/hiəm˧˩/|/hiəm˧˨/|/him˨˩˦/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 獫 (hiểm) meaning ""a kind of dog with a long snout"". It may also come from Sino-Vietnamese 險 (hiểm) meaning ""dangerous, impassable""."
Hiên,,,Vietnamese,/hiən˧˧/|/hiəŋ˧˧/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 軒 (hiên) meaning ""veranda"" or 萱 (hiên) meaning ""orange daylily""."
Hiến,,,Vietnamese,/hiən˧˦/|/hiəŋ˦˧˥/|/hiəŋ˦˥/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 憲 (hiến) meaning ""law, statute"" or 獻 (hiến) meaning ""offer, present, donate""."
Hiện,,,Vietnamese,/hiən˧˨ʔ/|/hiəŋ˨˩ʔ/|/hiəŋ˨˩˨/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 現 (hiện) meaning ""to rise, to appear, to come into sight""."
Hienadź,m,Генадзь(Belarusian),Belarusian,/ˈɣʲe.nad͡zʲ/,,,,,,,Łacinka transcription of Henadz.
Hienadzij,m,Генадзій(Belarusian),Belarusian (Rare),,,,,,,,Belarusian form of Gennadios (see Gennadius).
Hienrych,m,Генрых(Belarusian),Belarusian,,,,,,,,Belarusian form of Henryk.
Hieora,f,"히어라, 희어라(Korean Hangul)",Korean (Rare),/hi.ʌ.ra/,,,,,,,"From 희어라 meaning ""be white and clear""."
Hieorhij,m,Георгій(Belarusian),Belarusian,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Heorhij.
Hiệp,,,Vietnamese,/hiəp̚˧˨ʔ/|/hiəp̚˨˩ʔ/|/hip̚˨˩˨/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 俠 (hiệp) meaning ""chivalrous, knight, hero"" or 協 (hiệp) meaning ""to unite, to be in accord""."
Hiéra,f,,Greek Mythology (Gallicized),,,,,,,,French form of Hiera.
Hiera,f,Ἱέρα(Ancient Greek)|혜라(Korean Hangul),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology|Korean,/he.ra/,,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""holy, sacred, divine"". In Greek mythology, Hiera was the wife of Telephus, the mythic founder of the city of Pergamum, and when Greeks attacked their city during the Trojan War she rallied a cavalry of Mysian women to defend it. She was killed during the battle, and her husband called a cease-fire to hold a funeral for her before resuming the fight and driving out the invaders."
Hieranim,m,Геранім(Belarusian),Belarusian,,,,,,,,Belarusian form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).
Hierão,m,,Portuguese,,,,,,,,Portuguese form of Hieron (see Hiero).
Hierasim,m,Герасім(Belarusian),Belarusian (Rare),/ɣʲe.ˈra.sʲim/,,,,,,,"Variant of Harasim, which is the main Belarusian form of Gerasimos."
Hierax,m,Ἱέραξ(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἱέραξ (hierax) meaning ""hawk, falcon"". This was the name of a Spartan admiral from the 4th century BC."
Hierdzień,m,Гердзень(Belarusian),Belarusian (Archaic),,,,,,,,Belarusian name for Gerdenis.
Hieria,m,"Ἱεριά, ῾Ιεριὰ(Ancient Greek)",Biblical Greek,,,,,,,,"Greek form of Jeriah, as it first appeared in the Septuagint."
Hierna,f,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"A form of Igraine, the mother of King Arthur"
Hiero,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Hieron. This name was borne by two tyrants of Syracuse, the earliest of which lived in the 5th century BC."
Hieroboam,m,Ἱεροβοάμ(Ancient Greek),Biblical Greek,,,,,,,,"Greek form of Jeroboam, as it first appeared in the Septuagint."
Hierocles,m,,Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,Latinized form of Hierokles. This name was borne by a Stoic philosopher from the 2nd century AD.
Hierodora,f,Ἱεροδώρα(Ancient Greek),Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred, divine"" combined with δῶρον (doron) meaning ""gift""."
Hierodoros,m,Ἱερώδωρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred, divine"" combined with δῶρον (doron) meaning ""gift"". Masculine form of Hierodora."
Hierodotos,m,Ἱερόδοτος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with the Greek adjective δοτός (dotos) meaning ""given, granted"".This name is not to be confused with the related name Herodotos (see Herodotus), which is very similar in appearance but has a different meaning."
Hieroklees,m,"Ἱεροκλέης, Ἱερόκλεες(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Epic Greek variant of Hierokles.
Hierokleia,f,Ἱερόκλεια(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Hierokles.
Hierokles,m,Ἱεροκλῆς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,"/hi.e.ro.klɛ̂ːs/(Attic Greek)|/i.e.ro.ˈklis/(Koine Greek, Byzantine Greek)|/ˈhaɪ.ə.ɹə.kliːz/(English)",,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred, divine"" and κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory""."
Hieromneme,f,Ἱερομνήμη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˌhaɪ.ər.ɒm.ˈniː.miː/(English),,,,,,,"Feminine form of Hieromnemon, meaning ""memory of the holy rites"" or ""mindful of sacred things"". This was the name of a naiad daughter of the river Simoeis in Greek mythology, who married into the Trojan royal family."
Hieromnemon,m,Ἱερομνήμων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun ἱερομνήμων (hieromnemon), which literally means ""mindful of the sacred"" but later came to refer to a representative of one of the twelve members of the Amphictyonic League, which was a religious association of ancient Greek tribes. The word itself consists of the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with the Greek adjective μνήμων (mnemon) meaning ""mindful"" (see Mnemon).This name was borne by an eponymous archon of Athens, who lived in the early 4th century BC."
Hiéron,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,French form of Hieron (see Hiero).
Hierón,m,,Spanish,,,,,,,,Spanish form of Hieron (see Hiero).
Hieron,m,Ἱέρων(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"". This name was borne by two tyrants of Syracuse, the earliest of which lived in the 5th century BC. Both are better known under the latinized form of their name, which is Hiero."
Hierona,f,,Dutch (Rare),,,,,,,,Contracted form of Hieronyma.
Hieronides,m,Ἱερωνίδης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Hieron"" in Greek, derived from the name Hieron combined with the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).A known bearer of this name was saint Hieronides of Alexandria (3rd century AD)."
Hieronike,f,Ἱερονίκη(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Hieronikos. Also compare the related Greek noun ἱερονίκης (hieronikes) meaning ""conqueror in the games""."
Hieronikos,m,Ἱερόνικος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with the Greek noun νίκη (nike) meaning ""victory""."
Hieronima,f,,Polish|Hungarian,hye-raw-NEE-ma(Polish),,,,,,,Polish and Hungarian feminine form of Jerome.
Hiêrônimô,m,,Vietnamese (Christian),/hi˧˧.ʔe˧˧.ɹo˧˧.ni˧˧.mo˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/hɪj˧˧.ʔej˧˧.ɹow˧˧.nɪj˧˧.mow˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,Vietnamese form of Hieronymus (see Jerome).
Hieronims,m,,Latvian (Archaic),,,,,,,,Archaic Latvian form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).
Hieronimu,m,,Sardinian (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Sardinian form of Hieronymus. Hieronimu Araolla, (Sassari, 1542 - Rome, 1615) was a Sardinian poet and priest."
Hieronimus,m,,Dutch (Rare)|German (Bessarabian),,,,,,,,Variant of Hieronymus.
Hieronomos,m,Ἱερόνομος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""sacred custom"", derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with the Greek noun νόμος (nomos) meaning ""usage, custom, law, ordinance"" (see Eunomia). In ancient Greece, ἱερονόμος (hieronomos) was also a term used to signify a temple-warden or a magistrate tasked with upholding the people's observance of religious laws.This name is frequently confused with the related name Hieronymos (see Jerome), which is very similar in appearance but has a different meaning."
Hieronyma,f,,Dutch (Rare),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Hieronymus. This name is quite old-fashioned in the Netherlands these days (it was more common in late medieval times), but it's still in use, although it's quite rare now. In 2010, there was a total of 38 bearers (of all ages) in the entire country."
Hiéronyme,,,French (Archaic),,,,,,,,French masculine and feminine form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).
Hiëronymus,m,,Dutch (Rare),/ɦi.jeː.ˈroː.ni.mʏs/|/ɦi.jə.ˈroː.ni.mʏs/,,,,,,,Dutch spelling of Hieronymus.
Hierophanes,m,Ἱεροφάνης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with Greek φανής (phanes) meaning ""appearing"" (see Theophanes). Also compare the related Greek word ἱεροφάντης (hierophantes) meaning ""hierophant"" (as in, an ancient Greek priest who interprets sacred mysteries and teaches rites of sacrifice and worship)."
Hierophon,m,Ἱεροφῶν(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/hiː.e.ro.pʰɔ̂ːn/(Attic Greek)|/i.e.ro.ˈɸon/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἱερόφωνος (hierophonos) meaning ""with sacred voice"", which consists of ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred, divine, holy"" combined with φωνή (phone) meaning ""voice"" as well as ""sound, tone""."
Hiérosme,m,,Medieval French,,,,,,,,Medieval French variant of Jérôme.
Hieroteu,m,,Catalan (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Catalan form of Hierotheus, which is the latinized form of Hierotheos."
Hierothea,f,Ἱεροθέα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,Feminine form of Hierotheos.
Hiérothée,m,,"History (Ecclesiastical)|French (African, Rare)",,,,,,,,"French form of Hierotheus, which is the latinized form of Hierotheos."
Hierotheos,m,Ἱερόθεος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Late Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Means ""sanctified by God"", derived from Ancient Greek ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred, divine"" combined with θεός (theos) meaning ""deity, god; divine"".A notable bearer of this name was saint Hierotheos the Thesmothete (1st century AD)."
Hierotheus,m,,Late Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Hierotheos. This name was borne by two patriarches of Alexandria and one patriarch of Jerusalem, all of whom lived in the 19th century."
