Hierotimos,m,Ἱερότιμος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with the Greek verb τιμάω (timao) meaning ""to honour, to esteem, to revere""."
Hieroxenos,m,"Ἱεροξένος, Ἱερόξενος(Ancient Greek)",Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek adjective ἱερός (hieros) meaning ""sacred"" combined with Greek ξένος (xenos) meaning ""foreign, strange"" as well as ""foreigner, guest"".This name is not to be confused with the related name Heroxenos, which is very similar in appearance but has a different meaning."
Hièrru,f,,Jèrriais,,,,,,,,"Jèrriais feminine given name of unknown etymology.It might be a much-mangled form of Medieval French Hodierna, although this is less than certain. It also coincides with the Jèrriais word for ivy."
