Hiếu Kỳ,m,,Vietnamese (Rare),/hiəw˧˦ ki˨˩/|/hiw˨˩˦ kɪj˦˩/|/hiw˦˥ kɪj˨˩/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 好奇 (hiếu kỳ) meaning ""curious"", composed of 好 (hiếu) meaning ""to be fond of"" and 奇 (kỳ) meaning ""strange, wonderful""."
Hiếu Thảo,,,Vietnamese,/hiəw˧˦ tʰaːw˧˩/|/hiw˨˩˦ tʰaːw˧˨/|/hiw˦˥ tʰaːw˨˩˦/,,,,,,,"Means ""having filial piety"", from Sino-Vietnamese 孝 (hiếu) meaning ""filial"" and Vietnamese thảo meaning ""pious"", possibly from a non-Sino-Vietnamese reading of Chinese 操 (thao)."
