Hijiri,,"ひじり(Japanese Hiragana)|聖, 日次稜, 日二凛, 日二璃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-ZHEE-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 聖 (hijiri) meaning ""holy, sacred"", or 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun"" combined with 次 (ji) meaning ""next"" that is then combined with 凛 (ri) meaning ""dignified, severe, cold"", 璃 (ri) meaning ""glassy, lapis lazuli"" or 稜 (ri) meaning ""majesty, power, angle, edge, corner"". Other spellings are possible."
