Himalia,f,Ἱμαλία(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/hɪ.ˈmeɪ.li.ə/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""abundance; heap of meal or flour"" as well as ""mill song, rhythmic tune for turning the mill"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, Himalia was a Rhodian nymph impregnated by Zeus when he turned into a shower of rain, giving birth to Spartaios, Kytos, and Kronios. A moon of Jupiter was named after her. Himalia was also an epithet of the goddess Demeter, and the name of an obscure protective deity of the millstone and agriculture who may have been identical to the Rhodian nymph."
Himangi,f,,Indian,hi-maan-gee,,,,,,,a girl with silver body
Himani,f,"হিমানী(Bengali, Assamese)|ହେମାନୀ(Odia)|हिमानी(Hindi, Nepali)|ਹਿਮਾਨੀ(Gurmukhi)",Bengali|Assamese|Hindi|Punjabi|Nepali,/ˈhi.ma.ni/(Bengali)|/ˈɦɪ.mɑː.niː/(Hindi),,,,,,,"Means ""mass of snow, snowdrift"" in Sanskrit."
Himanshi,f,,Indian,,,,,,,,Not available.
Himanshu,m,"हिमांशु(Hindi, Marathi)|ਹਿਮਾਂਸ਼ੂ(Gurmukhi)|হিমাংশু(Bengali, Assamese)|ହିମାଂଶୁ(Odia)",Hindi|Punjabi|Marathi|Bengali|Odia|Assamese,/ˈhi.maŋ.ʃu/(Bengali),,,,,,,"From Sanskrit हिमांशु (himāṃśu) meaning ""moon""."
Himar,,,Guanche|Spanish (Canarian),[i.ˈmaɾ](Canarian Spanish),,,,,,,Name of a Guanche person as reported by Canarian historian Gregorio Chil. It probably comes from the toponym of a valley named Himar (modernly called Jinámar) in the Canary Islands.
Himari,f,,Sinhalese,,,,,,,,Form of Himali
Himaru,,ひまる(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese,,,,,,,,"Himaru's the half sister of Meiyo, Ginaharu, and Misao from Ginaharu's Soccer."
Himas,m,,English,,,,,,,,This name is a shortened derivation of the biblical name Ahimaaz.
Himasini,f,ஹிமாசினி(Tamil),Tamil,Him-A-sin-I,,,,,,,"It is a name meaning ""snow girl"" or ""woman of snow,"" symbolizing purity, grace, and serenity."
Himavari,f,,Pakistani,,,,,,,,"From old Indus civilization. The meaning of the name is snow stream or frozen plants. Later it has been mentioned in Riga Veda as another name of Goddess of Saraswati who is Goddess of speech. Lexicographers like Hemchandra and Halayudh have also used Vari in their writings in which Vari is another name of Chaaya (छाय), wife of God Sun."
Himavarsh,m,,Indian,,,,,,,,Not available.
Himavat,m,हिमवत्(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈɦi.mɐ.ʋɐt̪/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""snowy, icy"" in Sanskrit, derived from हिम (hima) meaning ""cold, frost"". In Hindu tradition this is the personification of the Himalaya Mountains. He is the son of Brahma and Saraswati as well as the father of Ganga and Parvati."
Himawari,,"向日葵, 向日花, 日向咲, 向夏花, 陽葵, 陽周, 葵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひまわり(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒマワリ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Modern),[çì.má.ɰᵝà.ɾʲì],,,,,,,"From 向日葵 (himawari) which refers to the sunflower, originally deriving from 日 (hi) meaning ""sun"" combined with 回り (mawari) meaning ""rotation, circulation,"" from the misconception that the sunflowers follow the direction of the sun, the behaviour only occuring in immature flower buds and not in fully grown sunflowers (which faces east).Other ways to write this name include 向日花, 日向咲, 向夏花, 陽葵, 陽周 and 葵 with 花 meaning ""flower,"" 咲 meaning ""blossom,"" 夏 meaning ""summer"" and 周, related to 回."
Himaya,f,,Filipino|Cebuano,/hi-má-yâ/,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname, which means ""glory,"" ""bliss,"" or ""rapture"" in Cebuano."
Himchan,m,힘찬(Korean Hangul),Korean (Modern),/çim.t͡ɕʰän/,,,,,,,"From the present determiner form of adjective 힘차다 (himchada) meaning ""powerful, vigorous, energetic,"" effectively a combination of Him and verb 차다 (chada) meaning ""to fill."""
Hime,f,"姫, 妃, 陽芽, 陽女, 陽愛, 陽姫, 妃芽, 妃萌, 広愛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひめ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒメ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[çí.mè̞],,,,,,,"From 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" (also used for this name as 妃), derived from a combination of 日 (hi) meaning ""sun"" (used as a prefix or appellation in reference to the imperial family) and 女 (me) meaning ""woman.""It can also be written with two kanji, a (partial) hi kanji like 陽 (same as 日) or 広 meaning ""spacious, vast, wide"" combined with a me kanji such as 女, 芽/萌 meaning ""bud, sprout"" or 愛 meaning ""love, admiration."""
Himea,f,"姫亜, 姫愛, 媛阿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-AH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 亜 (a) meaning ""second, Asia"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himeka,f,"ヒメカ(Japanese Katakana)|ひめか(Japanese Hiragana)|姫郁, 姫嘉, 姫果, 姫歌, 姫雅, 姫樺, 日芽香, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-MEH-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 郁 (ka) meaning ""cultural progress, culture, fragrance, perfume"", 嘉 (ka) meaning ""praise, auspicious"", 雅 (ka) meaning ""grace, elegance, gracious, refined"", or 樺 (ka) meaning ""birch"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himeko,f,"ヒメコ(Japanese Katakana)|姫子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-MEH-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" and 子 (ko) meaning ""child, first sign of the Chinese zodiac, sign of the rat"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Himemi,f,"ひめみ(Japanese Hiragana)|妃美, 姫海, 姫見, 姫女魅, 姫深, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 妃 (hime) ""princess"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
Himena,f,"陽萌菜, 日芽菜, 妃奈, 姫菜, 姫雫, 姫名, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-ME-NA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 芽 (me) meaning ""bud, sprout, shoot"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himene,f,,Māori,,,,,,,,"Means ""melody"" in Maori."
Himeneo,m,,Biblical Spanish,,,,,,,,Spanish form of Hymenaeus.
Himeneu,m,,Biblical Portuguese,,,,,,,,Portuguese form of Hymenaeus.
Himeno,f,"姫希, 妃乃, 妃野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ヒメノ(Japanese Katakana)|ひめの(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,KHEE-MEH-NOH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 or 妃 (both hime) both meaning ""princess"" combined with 希 (no) meaning ""rare, hope, beg for"" or 乃 (no) meaning ""from, therefore, accordingly"" or 野 (no) meaning ""field, plain, wilderness"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himeo,f,"姫緒, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 緒 (o) meaning ""thread"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himerius,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Himerius of Immertal (d. ca. 620 AD) was a monk, hermit, and missionary in the Swiss Jura. His name may derive from the Greek Himeros."
Himerope,f,Ἱμερόπη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek ἵμερος (himeros) meaning ""longing, yearning after"" (as well as ""desire, love"" - compare Himeros) and οψ (ops) meaning ""face, eye"". According to an ancient vase painting and later sources, this was the name of one of the two Sirens in Greek mythology."
Himeros,m,Ἵμερος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""yearning, longing, desire, love"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, Himeros was one of the seven Erotes (love deities that acted as part of Aphrodite’s procession) and the personification of desire and lust."
Himesaki,f,"姫咲, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-SAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 咲 (saki) meaning ""blossom"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himesh,m,हिमेश(Marathi)|હિમેશ(Gujarati),Indian|Marathi|Gujarati,,,,,,,,"Means ""lord of snow"", derived from Sanskrit हिम (himá) meaning ""cold, snow, winter"" combined with ईश (īśá) meaning ""lord, master, ruler""."
Himeya,f,"姫矢, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 矢 (ya) meaning ""arrow"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himeyo,f,"日女代, 日米代, 姫代, 姫夜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-ME-YO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"", 女 (me) meaning ""female, woman, wife"", 米 (me) meaning ""rice"" or 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 代 (yo) meaning ""world, society"" or 夜 (yo) meaning ""night"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Himeyuri,f,姫百合(Japanese Kanji)|ひめゆり(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒメユリ(Japanese Katakana),"Japanese (Modern, Rare)",[çi.me̞.jɯ̟.ɾʲi],,,,,,,"From 姫百合 (himeyuri), referring to the type of lily known as Lilium concolor (or the morning star lily). It is derived from 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"" combined with 百合 (yuri) (see Yuri 2).This name is extremely rare."
Him-hye,,,Korean,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hīmi,m,,Māori,,,,,,,,Maori form of James or Jim.
Himier,m,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,French variant of Imier.
Himig,,,Tagalog,/ˈhi.miɡ/,,,,,,,"Means ""tune, melody"" in Tagalog."
Himika,f,"ひみか(Japanese Hiragana)|ひみ佳(Kanji/Hiragana)|日美香, 日実加, 仁心香, 一花, 妃実嘉, 妃未夏, 比実香, 緋水佳, 緋美香, 氷海風, 陽実佳, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Bengali (Rare)|Indian (Rare)|Japanese,HEE-MEE-KAH,,,,,,,Not available.
Himiko,f,"卑弥呼, 卑彌呼(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese Mythology,KHEE-MEE-KO,,,,,,,"This is from Old Japanese hime (姫) meaning 'young noblewoman, princess', or from hi (日) 'sun' and me (女) 'woman' or miko (覡 or 巫女) 'shamaness, shrine maiden, priestess'. Some sources posit that Himiko (Pimiko) is from an archaic Japanese title, himeko, which means 'princess', from hime with the female name suffix -ko (子) 'child'.A famous bearer of the name is the Empress Himiko (Pimiko), a shaman queen also known as Yamtohime No Mikoto, the Sun Queen or Sun Goddess of Japanese legend. She is alleged to be the first known ruler of Wa (Japan), and of the legendary land of Yamatai, believed by some to be the same as Wa. She is the supposed originator of the Grand Shrine of Ise, which is considered one of the most important Shintō sanctuaries in Japan to this day."
Himildrud,f,,Old High German,,,,,,,,"Combination of himil ""heaven"" and þrūþi ""strength""."
Himilrad,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old High German himil ""sky, heaven"" combined with Old High German rât ""counsel."""
Himiltrud,f,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old High German himil ""sky, heaven"" combined with þruþ ""strength."""
Himiltrude,f,,Germanic|History,,,,,,,,Variant of Himiltrud. Himiltrude was the name of the first wife of Charlemagne.
Himiltrudis,f,,Old High German,,,,,,,,Latinised form of Himildrud.
Himina,f,,Māori,hee-mee-na,,,,,,,"Variant of Himene, or Māori form of Jamesina."
Himinbjörg,f,,"Icelandic (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Means ""heaven mountain"" in Old Norse, derived from himinn ""sky, heavens"" and bjarg ""cliff, boulder, mountain"" (see berg). This is the name of a mythical place, the home of the Norse god Heimdall. The given name could derive from a 17th century oral saga titled Himinbjargar saga."
Himinglæva,f,,Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means 'the heaven-shining one, the transparent one"", referring to the transparency of water. In Norse mythology, Himinglæva was one of nine daughters of Ægir and Rán."
Himiona,m,,Māori,,,,,,,,Maori form of Simeon.
Himmat,m,"ϩⲓⲙⲙⲁⲧ(Nubian Coptic)|ਹਿੰਮਤ(Gurmukhi)|हिंमत, हिम्मत(Hindi, Marathi, Rajasthani)|હિંમત(Gujarati)",Nubian|Punjabi|Hindi|Marathi|Rajasthani|Gujarati,,,,,,,,Nubianized version of Mohammad
Himmer,m,,American (Hispanic),,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Himmer.
Himni,m,,Mormon,,,,,,,,Son of Mosiah in the Book of Mormon.
Himoyat,f,,Uzbek,,,,,,,,"Means ""defense, support"" in Uzbek."
Himu,,হিমু(Bengali),Bengali,,,,,,,,Not available.
Himuka,m,"日向, 陽向(Japanese Kanji)|ひむか(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒムカ(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)",[çí.mɯ̟̀ᵝ.kà],,,,,,,"Earlier form of Hyūga.Compared to its most recent form, this name is very rarely used."
Hîn,,興(Chinese),Chinese (Hakka),,,,,,,,Hakka Chinese form of Xing.
Hinae,f,"日菜絵, 雛恵, 雛衣, 比奈恵, 陽菜笑, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひなえ, ひなえ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,HEE-NAH-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"" combined with 絵 (e) meaning ""picture, painting, drawing, sketch"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinaga,f,"陽永, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 陽 (hina) meaning ""the sun"" combined with 永 (ga) meaning ""eternity"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinagi,f,"ヒナギ(Japanese Katakana)|ひなぎ(Japanese Hiragana)|日梛, 陽凪, 灯和, 雛銀, 桧成岐, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NA-GEE,,,,,,,"From the Japanese kanji 檜 (hi) meaning ""Japanese cypress"" or 緋 (hi) meaning ""scarlet"" combined with 渚 (nagi) meaning ""strand, beach, shore"", 凪 (nagi) meaning ""calm"", 和 (nagi) meaning ""harmony, Japanese style, peace, soften, Japan"". Other Kanji combinations are also possible."
Hinagiku,f,"珠野, 雛菊(Japanese Kanji)|ヒナギク(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese|Popular Culture,KHEE-NAH-GEE-KOO(Japanese)|HEE-NAH-GEE-KOO(Popular Culture),,,,,,,"This is the name of a main character in the Wedding Peach manga and TV series, one of the most popular animes released in the mid-90s. In her case it is spelled 珠野, which combines 珠 meaning ""pearl, gem, jewel"" with 野 meaning ""plains, field, life"". It is also a Japanese word, spelled 雛菊, meaning ""daisy"". In the manga the character named Hinagiku was a love angel, also referred to as Angel Daisy. Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinahina,f,,Hawaiian|Māori|Tahitian,hee-na-hee-na,,,,,,,"Means ""grey-ish"" in Hawaiian, Maori, and Tahitian. Hinahina refers to several types of small native coastal ground-shrubs. Hinahina is a village in New Zealand's South Island."
Hinaichigo,f,雛苺(Japanese Kanji)|ひないちご(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒナイチゴ(Japanese Katakana),Popular Culture,[çì.ná.ì.t͡ɕì.gò̞],,,,,,,"Combination of 雛 (hina) meaning ""doll; chick, young bird"" and 苺 (ichigo) meaning ""strawberry,"" used on a character in the manga and anime television series 'Rozen Maiden'.It is not used as a given name in Japan."
Hinaka,f,"日向花, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日向 (hina) meaning ""sunny place"" combined with 花 (ka) meaning ""flower, blossom"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinaki,f,"雛葵, 日向葵, 妃菜喜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 雛 (hina) meaning ""chick, young bird, doll"" or 日向 (hina) meaning ""sunny place"" combined with 葵 (ki) meaning ""hollyhock"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinako,f,"ひなこ(Japanese Hiragana)|一七子, 光南子, 秀菜子, 雛子, 燈名虹, 瞳菜子, 日夏子, 日向子, 日菜子, 日暖幸, 日奈子, 日捺子, 日南子, 日名子, 日陽子, 日和子, 妃七子, 妃凪子, 妃南子, 披名子, 比菜子, 比直子, 比南子, 緋奈子, 緋名子, 飛菜子, 柊南子, 姫菜子, 百南子, 品子, 陽夏子, 陽向子, 陽菜子, 陽笑子, 陽南子, 陽名菊, 陽和子, 鄙子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-NAH-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (hi) meaning ""one"", 光 (hi) meaning ""light"", 秀 (hi) meaning ""excel, excellence, beauty, surpass"", 雛 (hina) meaning ""chick, squab, duckling, doll"", 燈 (hi) meaning ""lamp, light"", 瞳 (hi) meaning ""pupil (of eye)"", 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 日向 (hina) meaning ""sunny place"", 妃 (hi) meaning ""queen, princess"", 披 (hi) meaning ""expose, open"", 比 (hi) meaning ""compare, race, ratio, Philippines"", 緋 (hi) meaning ""scarlet, cardinal"", 飛 (hi) meaning ""fly, skip (pages), scatter"", 柊 (hi) meaning ""holly"", 姫 (hi) meaning ""princess"", 百 (hi) meaning ""hundred"", 品 (hina) meaning ""goods, refinement, dignity, article"", 陽 (hi) meaning ""light, sun, male"", 陽向 (hina) meaning ""toward the sun"" or 鄙 (hina) meaning ""lowly, the country, the countryside, be countrified"", 七 (na) meaning ""seven"", 南 (na) meaning ""south"", 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"", 名 (na) meaning ""name"", 夏 (na) meaning ""summer"", 暖 (na) meaning ""warmth"", 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"", 捺 (na) meaning ""press, print, affix a seal, stamp"", 陽 (na) meaning ""light, sun, male"", 和 (na) meaning ""harmony, Japanese style, peace, soften, Japan"", 凪 (na) meaning ""lull, calm"", 直 (na) meaning ""straight"" or 笑 (na) meaning ""laugh"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"", 虹 (ko) meaning ""rainbow"", 幸 (ko) meaning ""happiness"" or 菊 (ko) meaning ""chrysanthemum"". Other kanji combinations are possible.Famous bearers are Hinako Sakurai, a Japanese model, actress, and tarento and Hinako Saeki, a Japanese actress who was born on February 16, 1977 in Nara, Japan."
Hinalana,f,,English (American),hinəlɑnæ(American English),,,,,,,Meaning Unknown.
Hinalei,,,Hawaiian,,,,,,,,"Combination of Hina 2, from the Hawaiian moon Goddess and lei ""flowers, lei, child""."
Hinaleimoana,,,Hawaiian,,,,,,,,Combination of Hinalei and Moana. Hinaleimoana Kwai Kong Wong-Kalu (1972- ) is a Native Hawaiian community leader in the field of Kanaka Maoli language and cultural preservation.
Hiname,f,"日南女, 雛愛, 陽南女, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-NAH-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 南 (na) meaning ""south"" combined with 女 (me) meaning ""female, woman, wife"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinami,f,"ひなみ(Japanese Hiragana)|斐己深, 妃南海, 斐己未, 比奈美, 飛南, 姫南海, 陽菜水, 陽菜未, 陽七海, 陽南実, 陽南美, 雛心, 日南, 妃南, 妃波, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NAH-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun"" or 陽 (hi) meaning ""sunshine, daytime"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""greens"" and 美 (mi) meaning ""beauty, beautiful"", 実 (mi) meaning ""reality, truth, fruit"" or 海 (mi) meaning ""sea, ocean"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hina-moe-aitu,f,,Polynesian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Feminine name meaning ""Hina sleeping with a god"". In this case, Hina is a variant form of Sina."
Hinana,f,"日向菜, 雛菜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日向 (hina) meaning ""sunny place"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinane,f,"ひなね(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒナネ(Japanese Katakana)|雛眠, 桧直値, 妃捺根, 氷菜寝, 妃凪寢, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-NA-NEH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 雛 (hina) meaning ""a chick, a young bird"" combined with 音 (ne) meaning ""sound"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Hinano,f,"ひなの(Japanese Hiragana)|日菜乃, 雛乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NA-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"" and 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Hinari,f,"ひなり(Japanese Hiragana)|雛利, 雛梨, 雛里, 日向梨, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-NAH-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 雛 (hina) meaning ""doll"" combined with 梨 (ri) meaning ""pear"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinasa,f,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hinat,f,,"Nabataean Arabic (Anglicized, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Hinat is the name found at the Tomb of Hinat, daughter of Wahbu, carved into Jabal al-Ahmar Necropolis of Hegra (Saudi-Arabia) 60 C.E. or 61 C.E., originating from the time of the Nabataeans. Hegra was the southernmost capital of the Nabatean people, a once-nomadic Arabian tribe. The Nabatean city peaked between about 50 BCE and 106 CE.The descendants of the Nabateans are modern Arabs, especially Jordanian Arabs."
Hinatea,f,,Tahitian,,,,,,,,"Means ""great white granddaughter admired by goddesses"" in Tahitian."
Hinato,m,"日南人, 陽斗, 雛斗, 雛人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-NAH-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"", 南 (na) meaning ""south"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"" or 陽 (hina) meaning ""light, sun, male"" combined with 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation. Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Hinatsu,f,"日夏, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"" combined with 夏 (natsu) meaning ""summer"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinauri,f,,Māori,,,,,,,,"Means ""dark grey"" in Maori."
Hinayu,f,"氷夏夜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 氷 (hi) meaning ""ice"", 夏 (na) meaning ""summer"" combined with 夜 (yu) meaning ""night; the evening"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Hinc,m,,Sorbian,,,,,,,,Sorbian form of Heinrich.
Hıncal,m,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Means ""get revenge"" in Turkish. A notable namesake is Hıncal Uluç, Turkish journalist and commentator."
Hinckley,,,English (Rare),/ˈhɪŋk.li/,,,,,,,"Transferred use of the surname Hinckley. Possibly sometimes given in honor of the 15th president of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, Gordon B. Hinckley (1910-2008)."
Hinczka,m,,Medieval Polish,,,,,,,,Polish form of Hinz.
Hind,m,הינד(Yiddish),Yiddish,,,,,,,,Not available.
Hinda,f,הינדא(Yiddish),Yiddish,HIN-dah,,,,,,,"Means ""deer"" in Yiddish, related to the English word ""hind""."
Hinder,m,,Swedish (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Variant of Henrik (compare Hindrik, Hinnerk)."
