Hinenuitepō,f,,Māori|Polynesian Mythology,hin-neh-noo-ee-teh-poh,,,,,,,"The Māori goddess of night and death. Her name Hine-nui-te-pō means ""Great woman of the night"" in Māori."
Hinepare,f,,Māori,hin-neh-pah-reh,,,,,,,"Means ""crowned girl, protected girl"" in Māori from hine meaning ""girl"" and pare meaning ""protect, crown, garland"" and ""lintel"" in Māori."
