Hineura,f,,Polynesian|Tahitian,Hinè-ura,,,,,,,"Polynesian origin name, composed by ""hine"", meaning ""young girl"" and ""ura"", meaning ""red"" or ""bright"", hence the meaning is ""radiant girl""."
Hinewai,f,,Māori (Rare),/ˈhiːnɛwaɪ/,,,,,,,"Combining ""Hine"" meaning ""girl"" or ""maiden"", and ""wai"" meaning water. Thus, Hinewai translates to ""maiden of the water"" or ""water maiden""."
Hinewehi,f,,Māori,hee-nuh-way-hee,,,,,,,"Means ""revered maiden"" in Māori from hine meaning ""girl, maiden"" and wehi meaning ""to revere, awesome, fear""."
