Hino,f,"日乃, 日暖, 燈乃, 妃乃, 斐乃, 比乃, 緋乃, 姫乃, 陽乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひの(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,KHEE-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Hinode,,"日之出, 日乃出, 旦, 旺, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|日の出(Kanji/Hiragana)|日ノ出(Kanji/Katakana)|ひので(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒノデ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[çì.nó̞.dé̞],,,,,,,"From 日の出 (hinode) meaning ""sunrise,"" also written with kanji relating to the image of a sunrise, such as 旦 meaning ""daybreak, dawn"" or 旺 meaning ""vigorous, prosperous.""This name is very rarely used."
Hinoko,f,"ヒノコ(Japanese Katakana)|ひのこ(Japanese Hiragana)|日乃子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KHEE-NO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"" or 火 (hi) ""fire"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle and 子 (ko) ""child"". Other kanji or combinations of kanji can also form this name."
Hinon,m,,New World Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""thunder"" in Iroquois. He was is the god of thunder in Iroquois and Wyandot mythology, where he is depicted as a thunderbird (the thunderbird is a symbol common to many Native American tribes, Hinon is only represented by the symbol by these specific peoples, not all)."
Hinook-Mahiwi-Kalinaka,f,,Indigenous American|Ho-Chunk,,,,,,,,"Means ""fleecy cloud floating in place"" in the Ho-Chunk language. This was the Ho-Chunk name of painter and teacher Angel De Cora Dietz."
Hinori,f,"ひのり(Japanese Hiragana)|日法, 葵乃里, 緋紀, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-NO-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 日 (hi) meaning ""sun, day"" combined with 法 (nori) meaning ""law, rule"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hinote,m,"陽の手, 陽の貞, 陽の哲, 陽の照, 陽の天, 日の手, 日の貞, 日の哲, 日の照, 日の天, 緋の手, 緋の貞, 緋の哲, 緋の照, 緋の天, 一の手, 一の貞, 一の哲, 一の照, 一の天, 火の手, 火の貞, 火の哲, 火の照, 火の天(Kanji/Hiragana)|陽野手, 陽野貞, 陽野哲, 陽野照, 陽野天, 陽乃手, 陽乃貞, 陽乃哲, 陽乃照, 陽乃天, 陽之手, 陽之貞, 陽之哲, 陽之照, 陽之天, 日野手, 日野貞, 日野哲, 日野照, 日野天, 日乃手, 日乃貞, 日乃哲, 日乃照, 日乃天, 日之手, 日之貞, 日之哲, 日之照, 日之天, 緋野手, 緋野貞, 緋野哲, 緋野照, 緋野天, 緋乃手, 緋乃貞, 緋乃哲, 緋乃照, 緋乃天, 緋之手, 緋之貞, 緋之哲, 緋之照, 緋之天, 一野手, 一野貞, 一野哲, 一野照, 一野天, 一乃手, 一乃貞, 一乃哲, 一乃照, 一乃天, 一之手, 一之貞, 一之哲, 一之照, 一之天, 火野手, 火野貞, 火野哲, 火野照, 火野天, 火乃手, 火乃貞, 火乃哲, 火乃照, 火乃天, 火之手, 火之貞, 火之哲, 火之照, 火之天(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-NO-TEH,,,,,,,"From 陽 (hi) meaning “light, sun, male”, 日 (hi) meaning “sun, day”, 緋 (hi) meaning “scarlet, dark red”, 一 (hi) meaning “one”, or 火 (hi) meaning “fire”, combined with の (no) (a possesive marker), 野 (no) meaning “field, wilderness, wild”, 乃 (no) meaning “to be, then, really, indeed”, or 之 (no) meaning “it, him, her” combined with 手 (te) meaning “hand, skill”, 貞 (te) meaning “virtue, chastity”, 哲 (te) meaning “wisdom, philosophy”, 照 (te) meaning “illuminate, shine” or 天 (te) meaning “heaven, sky”."
