Hirotoshi,m,"寛俊, 寛年, 寛寿, 啓俊, 啓敏, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-ṘO-TO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 寛 (hiro) meaning ""tolerant"" combined with 俊 (toshi) meaning ""genius, excellence"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Hirotoshi Ishii (1977-), a Japanese baseball player. He currently plays as a relief pitcher for the Tokyo Yakult Swallows."
Hirotsugu,m,"洋承, 広次, 弘次, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-RO-TSOO-GO,,,,,,,"From 裕 (hiro) meaning ""abundant"" and 次 (tsugu) meaning ""second, next"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hirou,m,"火郎, 日郎(Japanese Kanji)|ひろう(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 火(hi) meaning ""fire"" or 日(hi) meaning ""day"" and 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Hiroumi,m,"寛海, 裕海, 大海, 博海, 弘海, 洋海, 宏海, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひろうみ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒロウミ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/çi.ɾo̞.ɯᵝ.mi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 寛 (hiro) meaning ""tolerant, generous"", 裕 (hiro) meaning ""abundant, rich, plentiful"", 大 (hiro) meaning ""big, great, vast, high"", 博 (hiro) meaning ""command, esteem"", 弘 (hiro) meaning ""enlarge, expand, great"" or 洋 (hiro) meaning ""ocean"", 宏 (hiro) meaning ""wide, spacious, great, vast"" combined with 海 (umi) meaning ""sea, ocean"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Hiroya,m,"博也, 弘也, 浩哉, 寛也, 大也, 碩哉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-ṘO-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 大 (hiro) meaning ""big, large, great"", 碩 (hiro) meaning ""large, eminent, great"" or 博 (hiro) meaning ""command, esteem"" and 也 (ya) meaning ""to be, also, too"" or 哉 (ya), an exclamation. Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous bearer is Hiroya Shimamoto (1993-), a Japanese Nippon Professional Baseball pitcher for the Hanshin Tigers in Japan's Central League."
Hiroyasu,m,"裕坦, 浩安, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-RO-YA-SOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 裕 (hiro) meaning ""abundant"" or 浩 (hiro) meaning ""prosperous"" combined with 安 (yasu) meaning ""peace, quiet"", 康 (yasu) meaning ""peaceful"" or 坦 (yasu) meaning ""flat, smooth, level"", as well as other kanji which are pronounced the same way."
Hiroyo,f,"ひろよ(Japanese Hiragana)|大与, 紘代, 宥世, 皓央, 宙誉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-RO-YO,,,,,,,"From 宙 (hiro) meaning ""mid-air"" and 宥 (yo) meaning ""calm, soothe, pacify"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hiroyoshi,m,"啓義, 広喜, 浩義, 洋芳, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-RO-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 啓 (hiro) meaning ""to say, open or disclose"" or 広 (hiro) meaning ""vast, wide"" combined with 佳 (yoshi) meaning ""good, excellent"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
