Hisa,f,"久, 寿(Japanese Kanji)|ひさ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,HEE-SAH,,,,,,,"This name can be used as 久 (kyuu, ku, hisa.shii) meaning ""long time, old story"" or 寿 (shuu, ju, su, kotobuki, kotobu.ku, kotoho.gu, hisa) meaning ""congratulations, longevity, one's natural life.""Hisa was moderately popular in the Edo period (1603-1868) and in the Meiji period (1868-1912). By the Taishō period (1912-1926), however, it became uncommon."
Hisaaki,m,"久明, 寿明, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" and 明 (ake, aki) meaning ""bright, light, clear, daybreak"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisae,f,"ヒサエ(Japanese Katakana)|ひさえ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサ絵(Kanji/Katakana)|冴彩, 陽冴, 久江, 寿恵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,/çi.sa̠.e̞/,,,,,,,"From 陽 (hi) meaning ""sun, Yang"" and 冴 (sae) meaning ""skillfulness, clarity, cold, serene"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hisaé,f,"久江, 久恵, 寿恵(Japanese Kanji)|ヒサエ(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Gallicized, Modern)|French (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Gallicized version of Hisae, can also be inspired from Ysé"
Hisaharu,m,"久治, 寿治, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-HA-ROO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" and 治 (haru) meaning ""govern, rule"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisahide,m,"久英, 尚英, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KHEE-DE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" and 英 (hide) meaning ""excellent, fine"", as well as other combinations of kanji."
Hisahiko,m,"久彦, 悠彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" and 悠 (hisa) meaning ""permanence"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""prince"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hisahiro,m,"久浩, 尚浩, 寿寛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-KHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"", 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, incidentally"" or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" combined with 裕 (hiro) meaning ""abundant"", 寛 (hiro) meaning ""tolerant, generous"", or 浩 (hiro) meaning ""prosperous"""". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisahito,m,"悠人, 悠仁, 寿人, 尚仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KHEE-TO,,,,,,,"From 悠 (hisa) meaning ""permanence"" and 仁 (hito) meaning ""benevolence"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisaichi,m,"久一, 尚一, 久市, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-EE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, incidentally"", or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" combined with 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu, kazu) meaning ""one"" or 市 (shi, ichi) meaning ""market"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisaji,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
