Hisaka,f,"ひさか(Japanese Hiragana)|氷坂, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"", 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"", or 陽 (hi) meaning ""sunshine, light, male"", or 日 (hi) meaning ""sun"" combined with 紗 (sa) meaning ""gauze, thread, silk"" or 沙 (sa) meaning ""sand"", and then combined with 佳 (ka) meaning ""good, beautiful"" or 花 (ka) meaning ""flower"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
Hisakata,m,久方(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,HEE-SAH-KAH-TAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久方 (hisakata) meaning ""moon in the sky""."
Hisakazu,m,"久和, 久一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-KAH-ZOO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" combined with 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" . Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisaki,,"ひさき(Japanese Hiragana)|寿輝, 久貴, 久亀, 尚紀, 火崎, 日咲, 緋咲, 百咲, 姫咲, 陽咲, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-SAH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 寿 (hisa) meaning ""longevity, long life"", 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time"", 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, as always"", 火 (hi) meaning ""fire"" (for males), 日 (hi) meaning ""day, sun, Japan"", 緋 (hi) meaning ""scarlet"", 百 (hi) meaning ""hundred"", 姫 (hi) meaning ""princess"" or 陽 (hi) meaning ""light, sun, male"" (for females) combined with 輝 (ki) meaning ""brightness"", 貴 (ki) meaning ""expensive, worthful, precious"", 亀 (ki) meaning ""tortoise, turtle"", 紀 (ki) meaning ""chronicle"", 崎 (saki) meaning ""small peninsula, cape"" (for males) or 咲 (saki) meaning ""blossom"" (for females). Other kanji combinations are possible.Famous male bearers of this name are Japanese professor, poet, and novelist Hisaki Matsuura and French-Japanese mixed martial artist Hisaki Kato."
Hisam,m,,Arabic,Hi-sum,,,,,,,Hisam is of Arabic origin and means “sword.”
Hisamaru,m,"久円, 寿丸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-MAH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long-lasting, remaining unchanged, ancient"", and 丸 (maru) meaning ""round"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisami,f,"ひさみ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサミ(Japanese Katakana)|恒魅, 尚果, 永弥, 寿見, 彌未, 悠海, 壽彌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 寿 (hisa) meaning ""longevity, long life"" combined with 魅 (mi) meaning ""to bewitch, to charm, fascination"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisamitsu,m,"久光, 永光, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-MEE-TSOO,,,,,,,"From 永 (hisa, ei) meaning ""eternal"" or 久 (hisa, ku) meaning ""long lasting, long time ago, old story"" combined with 光 (mitsu, hika.ri) meaning ""light, radiance"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ḫišamītum,f,,Near Eastern Mythology|Semitic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""Lady of Ḫišamta"" (a city in the kingdom of Mari), utilising the Akkadian feminine suffix tum. Name borne by the tutelary goddess of Ḫišamta, who is thought to have been a localised adaptation of Ishtar."
Hisana,f,緋真(Japanese Kanji),Japanese (Rare),HEE-SAH-NAH,,,,,,,"""scarlet""; ""truth"" or ""reality"""
Hisano,f,"久乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-NO,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" and 乃 (no) a possessive particle. Other kanji combinations can be used to spell this name."
Hisanobu,m,"久信, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" and 信 (nobu) meaning ""trust, faith, believe"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisanori,m,"ひさのり(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサノリ(Japanese Katakana)|尚孝, 悠則, 寿徳, 永典, 尚紀, 久儀, 恒範, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-NO-REE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 永 (hisa) meaning ""lengthy, eternity, long"" combined with 成 (nori) meaning ""to become"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisao,m,"久雄, 久男, 久夫, 寿雄, 寿男, 寿夫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひさお(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサオ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/çi.sä.o̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" combined with 雄 (o) meaning ""hero, male, manly"", 男 (o) meaning ""male, man, son"" or 夫 (o) meaning ""man, husband"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Hisaomi,m,"ひさおみ(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサオミ(Japanese Katakana)|弥臣, 恒臣, 寿臣, 尚臣, 永臣, 悠臣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-O-MEE,,,,,,,"From 引 (hisa) meaning ""admit, tug, pull"" or 栄 (hisa) meaning ""glory, splendor, honor"" combined with 臣 (omi) meaning ""subject, vassal"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
