Hisashi,m,"久, 永, 尚, 久志, 久司, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ひさし(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサシ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/çi.sä.ɕi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisashi) meaning ""long time, long time ago"", 永 (hisashi) meaning ""perpetual, eternal"" or 尚 (hisashi) meaning ""still, yet"", as well as other kanji pronounced the same way. It can also be formed from 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" combined with 志 (shi) meaning ""will, purpose, ambition"" or 司 (shi) meaning ""director, boss"", as well as other combinations of kanji."
Hisataka,m,"尚貴, 久貴, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-TAH-KAH,,,,,,,"From 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, yet, further, more"" and 貴 (taka) meaning ""valuable"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
