Hisato,m,"寿人, 壽人, 久人, 尚人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,HEE-SAH-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 寿, 壽 (hisa) meaning ""longevity, long life"", 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time"" or 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, as always"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations can also make up this name.Famous bearer of this name is Hisato Satō, he is a Japanese football player who currently plays for Nagoya Grampus in the J2 League. He is a left-footed forward."
Hisatomo,m,"尚友, 久友, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-TO-MO,,,,,,,"From 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, yet, further, more"" and 友 (tomo) meaning ""friend"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hisaya,m,"ひさや(Japanese Hiragana)|壽哉, 悠八, 尚弥, 寿哉, 常也, 永彌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-YA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 壽 (hisa) meaning ""congratulations, long life"" or 悠 (hisa) meaning ""permanence"" combined with 哉 (ya) an exclamation. Other kanji combinations are possible."
Hisayo,f,"ひさ代(Kanji/Hiragana)|久代, 寿代, 久世, 寿世, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-YO,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine name derived from 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"" and 代 (yo) meaning ""era, generation"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Hisayoshi,m,"ひさよし(Japanese Hiragana)|ヒサヨシ(Japanese Katakana)|久義, 久吉, 久慶, 久嘉, 久佳, 久美, 久良, 久由, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SA-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time"" combined with 慶 (yoshi) meaning ""celebrate"", 嘉 (yoshi) meaning ""praise"", 佳 (yoshi) meaning ""beautiful, good"", 良 (yoshi) meaning ""good, virtuous, respectable"" or 由 (yoshi) meaning ""cause, reason"". Other kanji combinations are possible as well.Famous bearer of this name is Hisayoshi Chōno (1984-). He is a Nippon Professional Baseball player for the Yomiuri Giants in Japan's Central League."
Hisayuki,m,"久幸, 寿幸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KHEE-SAH-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"" or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"" combined with 幸 (yuki) meaning ""happiness"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
