Hokuto,,"北斗, 北都, 北翔(Japanese Kanji)|ほくと(Japanese Hiragana)|ホクト(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,HOK-TO|HO-KUU-TO,,,,,,,"As a unisex name, this name combines 北 (hoku, kita) meaning ""north"" with 斗 (to, tou) meaning ""Big Dipper, sake dipper"" or 都 (tsu, to, miyako) meaning ""capital, metropolis.""As a masculine name, it is used as 北翔 with 翔 (shou, kage.ru, to.bu) meaning ""fly, soar.""Fictional bearers of this name include Hokuto Sumeragi (皇 北都 - female) from manga/anime Tōkyō Babylon and Hokuto Dan (弾 北斗 - male) from tokusatsu TV program Kagaku Sentai Dynaman (科学戦隊ダイナマン).As a word, Hokuto (北斗) refers to the constellation, The Big Dipper, or The Plough.Even though this name is used on girls, Hokuto, for 99.9% of the time, it is exclusively used for boys."
