Hotham,m,חוֹתָם(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,HO-thəm(Biblical English)|ho-THAHM(Biblical English),,,,,,,"A biblical name meaning ""seal"", ""signet"", or ""lock"".In the Bible, there are two people named Hotham. The first, in 1 Chronicles 7:32, is the son of Heber, grandson of Beriah, and great-grandson of Asher. He is also the brother of Japhlet, Shomer, and Shua.The second, in 1 Chronicles 11:44, is the father of Shama and Jeiel, two of David's warriors."
