Huaxu,f,华胥(Chinese),Chinese|Chinese Mythology,/xʷaː.ɕʷyː/(Chinese Mythology),,,,,,,"From the characters 华 (huá, meaning ""flower; luxuriance"") and 胥 (xū, meaning ""all, each and every""). In Chinese mythology this name is borne by the mother of Fuxi and Nüwa. According to one popular story, she found a giant footprint in the Leize (Storm Marsh) and put her own foot in it, whereupon she became pregnant with Fuxi.This is also the name of a small town in Shaanxi Province, China."
