Hubal,m,هبل(Arabic),Near Eastern Mythology,,,,,,,,"May mean ""master god"". From the Aramaic hu meaning 'spirit, god', and Ba'al 'master, lord'.He was a god of divination, rain, and war worshipped in pre-Islamic Arabia, notably at the Kaaba in Mecca. He possibly originated somewhere in Moab, Mesopotamia, or Petra. Much about his character as a god is unclear."
