Huginn,m,,Norse Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Norse hugr ""mind, thought"" (see also Hugubert). In Norse mythology, Huginn is the name of one of Odin's two ravens. Huginn signifies Thought and each day, he and Muninn (the other raven) fly over all the nine worlds known in Norse mythology in order to gather news and information for Odin."
