Hunna,f,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Huno. Saint Hunna (died ca. 679) is a French saint who devoted herself to serving the poor women of Strasbourg, France. Because she undertook to do the washing for her needy neighbors, she was nicknamed by her contemporaries ""The Holy Washerwoman""."
