Hvalimir,m,Хвалимир(Serbian),Serbian,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from the Serbo-Croatian noun hvala ""thanks"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". A known bearer of this name was Hvalimir Belojević, a 9th-century Serbian duke."
Hvannar,m,,Icelandic (Rare),,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Norse hvǫnn, the name of a type of flower (species Angelica archangelica; also compare Hvönn) combined with Old Norse herr ""army, warrior""."
