Hvatmóðr,m,,Old Norse,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Germanic name elements hvatr ""active, brisk, vigorous, manly"" and móðr ""mind, spirit, courage""."
Hvězdomír,m,,Czech,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Czech hvězda ""star"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gvězda ""star"". Also compare Slovak hviezda and Russian zvezda, both of which mean ""star"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace""."
