Hvězdoslav,m,,Czech,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Czech hvězda ""star"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gvězda ""star"". Also compare Slovak hviezda and Russian zvezda, both of which mean ""star"". The second element is derived from Slavic slav ""glory""."
Hvid,,,Danish (Rare),,,,,,,,Means “white” in Danish.
Hviezdomir,m,,Slovak,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Slovak hviezda ""star"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gvězda ""star"". Also compare Czech hvězda and Russian zvezda, both of which mean ""star"". The second element is derived from Slavic mir ""peace"". In other words, this name is the Slovak cognate of Hvězdomír."
Hviezdoslav,m,,Slovak,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Slovak hviezda ""star"", which is ultimately derived from Proto-Slavic gvězda ""star"". Also compare Czech hvězda and Russian zvezda, both of which mean ""star"". The second element is derived from Slavic slav ""glory"". In other words, this name is the Slovak cognate of Hvězdoslav."
