Hwa-ryeon,f,"화련(Korean Hangul)|和蓮, 花蓮, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean (Rare),/ɸwa̠.ɾjʌ̹n/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 和 (hwa) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 花 (hwa) meaning ""flower"", combined with 蓮 (ryeon) meaning ""lotus"". This name can be formed using other hanja combinations as well."
Hwa-ryun,f,"화련(Korean Hangul)|和蓮, 花蓮, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean (Rare),/ɸwa̠.ɾjʌ̹n/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangul 화련 (see Hwa-ryeon).
Hwasa,f,화사(Korean Hangul),Korean,,,,,,,,"Origin Unknown.A famous barer of this is Anh Hye-jin,(born July 23, 1995),is known professionally by her stage name Hwasa. She is a South Korean singer, songwriter, and television personality. She rose to prominence as a member of the girl group Mamamoo in 2014."
