Hylaeus,m,Ὑλαῖος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized)|Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Greek Ὑλαῖος (Hylaios), meaning ""of the forest, from the woods; savage"", ultimately derived from Ancient Greek ὕλη (hyle) meaning ""forest, woodland, trees"". In Greek mythology, Hylaeus was the name of a centaur killed by Atalanta when he attempted to assault her."
