Iambe,f,Ἰάμβη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,ie-AM-bee,,,,,,,The name of a Thracian woman who managed to make the goddess Demeter laugh while in the midst of mourning her kidnapped daughter.
Iamblichus,m,Ἰάμβλιχος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Latinized form of Iamblikhos. This was the name of several Ancient Syrian people, including a 2nd-century Neoplatonic philosopher."
