I-an,,"이안(Korean Hangul)|李安, 利安, 李岸, 利岸, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/i.a̠n/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 李 (i) meaning ""plum, plum tree"" or 利 (i) meaning ""benefit, advantage"" combined with 安 (an) meaning ""peace, quiet"" or 岸 (an) meaning ""bank, shore, coast"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as wwll."
