Iasis,,Ἴασις(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek ἴασις (iasis) meaning ""cure, remedy, healing"", from ἰάομαι (iaomai) ""to heal"" (the source also of Jason). In Greek mythology, she was one of a group of spring nymphs whose waters were believed to cure aches and pains."
