Ib,f,イヴ(Japanese Katakana),"Popular Culture (Americanized, Rare)|English",,,,,,,,"This is the name of the protagonist to the game of the same name, Ib. Her name is a unique and uncommon spelling and pronunciation of Eve where instead of using the established katakana ブ which makes the B-OO sound, they use the rare ヴ which makes the V-OO sound.It is a misconception that her name is pronounce like I-B or I-V."
Ibaad,m,,Arabic,ee-BAHD,,,,,,,"Derives from the root ""ʿ-b-d"" which signifies worship, servitude, and devotion. It means ""worshippers,"" ""servants (of Allah),"" or ""devout worshippers,"" reflecting a strong, pious, and religious connotation in Islamic culture. It is often associated with humility and faith."
