Ibadullah,m,عِبَادُ الله(Arabic)|عباد اللہ(Urdu),Arabic|Urdu,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Arabic عباد ('ibad), which is the plural of the noun عبد ('abd) meaning ""servant, slave"". The second element is derived from the Arabic noun الله (Allah) meaning ""God"" (see Allah). As such, this name is closely related to the names Abd Allah and Abdullah.A known bearer of this name is the Pakistani politician Ibadullah Khan (b. 1974)."
