Ichiba,m,"一馬, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-BAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 馬 (ba) meaning ""horse"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichiei,m,"いちえい(Japanese Hiragana)|イチエイ(Japanese Katakana)|一英, 市栄, 一榮, 市衛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 榮 (ei) meaning ""reflection, projection"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible.Famous bearers of this name are Japanese novelist Ichiei Ishibumi (1981-), and former Japanese football player Ichiei Muroi (1974-)."
Ichigo,,"一吾, 一悟, 一護, 一期, 一五, 苺(Japanese Kanji)|いちご(Japanese Hiragana)|イチゴ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Modern)|Popular Culture,[ì.t͡ɕí.ɡó̞](Japanese),,,,,,,"As a masculine name, this name combines 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu) meaning ""one"" with 吾 (go, a-, waga-, ware) meaning ""I, my, one's own,"" 悟 (go, sato.ru) meaning ""perceive, realise, understand,"" 護 (go, mamo.ru) meaning ""safeguard, protect,"" 期 (ki, go) meaning ""date, period, term, time"" or 五 (go, itsu, itsu.tsu) meaning ""five.""As a rare feminine name, it's used as 苺 (bai, mai, ichigo) meaning ""strawberry.""Regarding the word for ""strawberry,"" it may come from either iwochiko (いをちこ), stemming from 魚 (iwo, Heian-period alternation of modern uo) meaning ""fish,"" 血 (chi) meaning ""blood"" and 子 (ko) meaning ""child,"" from the way the wild strawberry looks like a child with the blood of the fish, or ichibiko (いちびこ), likely stemming from a combination of prefix い (i), 血 (chi), used to denote the similarity between the colours of the wild strawberry and blood, and 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy,"" in this case, an honorary title for male chiefs and aristocrats in the old days, similar to the addition of 'Prince.'Fictional bearers (all of them in manga & anime) of this name include Ichigo Kurosaki (黒崎 一護 - male) from Bleach, Ichigo Momomiya (桃宮 いちご - female) from Tokyo Mew Mew, Ichigo Morino (森野 苺 - female) from Please Teacher! and Ichigo Hoshimiya (星宮 いちご - female) from Aikatsu!"
Ichiha,f,"一葉, 一巴, 一羽, 初葉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-HAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 葉 (ha) meaning ""leaf"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichihana,f,"一華, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-HAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 花 (hana) or 華 (hana) which both mean ""flower"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichihei,m,"一平, 市坪, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-HEH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 平 (hei) meaning ""calm, peaceful"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Ichihime,f,"一姫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-HEE-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Ichiju,m,"一寿, 一樹, 市寿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-JUU,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" or 市 (ichi) meaning ""market"" combined with 寿 (ju) meaning ""longevity, long life"" or 樹 (ju) meaning ""tree"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Ichik Hunba,m,,Manipuri,,,,,,,,"Means ""night-time deep silence"" in Meitei."
Ichiki,,"一樹, 一姫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,ee-chee-kee  ,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 樹 (ki) meaning ""tree"" or 姫 (ki) meaning ""princess"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Ichiko,f,"イチコ(Japanese Katakana)|市子, 一子, 壱子, 苺子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 市 (ichi) meaning ""market"" and 子 (ko) meaning ""child, sign of the rat, first sign of the Chinese zodiac"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Ichimaru,m,"一丸, 壱丸(Japanese Kanji)|いちまる(Japanese Hiragana)|イチマル(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[ì.t͡ɕí.mà.ɾɯ̟̀ᵝ],,,,,,,"Combination of 一/壱 (ichi) meaning ""one"" and the suffix 丸 (maru) meaning ""circle, round,"" used before the Meiji Period (1868-1912) as a suffix denoting affection (along with -maro (麿/麻呂)) and was given to boys of upper class until they came of age, usually at ages 13 to 17.This name is rarely used."
Ichimi,f,"いちみ(Japanese Hiragana)|一海, 一三, 一実, 一美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 海 (mi) meaning ""sea, ocean"", 三 (mi) meaning ""three"", 実 (mi) meaning ""fruit, good result, truth"" or 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Ichin,f,Ичин(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Etymology uncertain, possibly a Mongolian form of a Tibetan name."
Ichine,f,"一音, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-NE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 音 (ne) meaning ""sound"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichiniko,f,"一二子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-NEE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"", 二 (ni) meaning ""two"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichinkelem,f,Ичинкелем(Lezgin),Lezgin,,,,,,,,"Means ""apple sapling"" in Lezgin."
Ichinkhorloo,f,Ичинхорлоо(Mongolian Cyrillic),Mongolian,,,,,,,,"Combination of the names Ichin and Khorloo, both likely of Tibetan origin."
Ichinosuke,m,"いちのすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|イチノスケ(Japanese Katakana)|一の介, etc.(Kanji/Hiragana)",Japanese,/i.t͡ɕi.no̞.sɨᵝ.ke̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" and の (no), a possesive marker, and 介 (suke) meaning ""help, assist"" Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Ichio,m,"一雄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 雄 (o) meaning ""male"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichirin,,"一輪, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),EE-CHEE-REEN,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" and 輪 (rin) meaning ""ring, link."""
Ichirōbei,m,"一郎平, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-ṘO:-BE:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"", 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"" combined with 平 (bei) meaning ""peace, flat"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichirōta,m,"一郎太, 市郎太, 一朗太, 市朗太(Japanese Kanji)|いちろうた(Japanese Hiragana)|イチロウタ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),EE-CHEE-ṘO:-TAH,,,,,,,"This name combines 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu) meaning ""one"" or 市 (shi, ichi) meaning ""market"" & 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son"" or 朗 (rou, aki.raka, hoga.raka) meaning ""bright, cheerful, clear, merry"" with 太 (ta, tai, futo.i, futo.ru) meaning ""big, plump, thick.""One bearer of this name is actor Ichirōta Miyakawa (宮川 一朗太) (1966-).This name is very rarely given to boys, if given at all."
Ichisuke,m,"一助, 市助, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-SKE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" or 市 (ichi) meaning ""market"" combined with 助 (suke) meaning ""assistance"". Other kanji combinations can also make up this name.Famous bearer of this name is Japanese engineer and businessman Ichisuke Fujioka. He was described as ""the Edison of Japan""."
Ichita,m,"一太, 市太, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-TAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" or 市 (ichi) meaning ""market"" combined with 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big"". This name can also be formed of other kanji combinations."
Ichitarou,m,"いちたろう(Japanese Hiragana)|イチタロウ(Japanese Katakana)|一太郎, 市太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-TAH-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"", 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichito,m,"一斗, 一翔, 壱斗, 市人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation. Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Ichiya,m,"一也, 一夜, 一八, 市野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 也 (ya) meaning ""also"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer was Ichiya Kumagae, Japanese tennis player and the first Japanese Olympic medalist."
Ichiyuu,m,"一勇, 一幽, 一祐, 一遊, 一雄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-YOO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 勇 (yuu) meaning ""brave"", 幽 (yuu) meaning ""dark"", 祐 (yuu) meaning ""divine intervention, protection"", 遊 (yuu) meaning ""to play"" or 雄 (yuu) meaning ""hero, manly"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Ichizo,m,,Japanese,EE-CHEE-ZO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Ichizou.
Ichizou,m,"一三, 一象, 壱三, 壱造, 市蔵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-CHEE-ZO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 三 (zou) meaning ""three"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer was Ichizō Kobayashi, occasionally referred to by his pseudonym Itsuō (逸翁), was a Japanese industrialist. He is best known as the founder of Hankyu Railway, Takarazuka Revue, and Toho. He was named Ichizō, meaning ""one-three"", because of his birthday, January 3."
Ichkhan,m,Իշխան(Armenian),Armenian,[iʃ.ˈχɑn],,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Ishkhan.
Ichkit,m,იჩქით(Georgian),Georgian (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Derived from the archaic Georgian adjective იჩქითად (ichkitad) meaning ""suddenly, unexpectedly"". Also compare the modern Georgian adjective იჩქითი (ichkiti) meaning ""sparse, small""."
Ichlas,m,,Indonesian,,,,,,,,Indonesian variant of Ikhlas.
Ichpochton,f,,Nahuatl,,,,,,,,"Derived from Nahuatl ichpochtli ""maiden, young woman; daughter"" and the diminutive suffix -ton."
Ichrak,,,Arabic (Maghrebi),,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Ishraq
Ichsan,m,,Indonesian,,,,,,,,Indonesian form of Ihsan.
Ichwan,m,,Indonesian,/ˈix.wan/,,,,,,,Variant of Ikhwan.
Ici,,,Sioux|English (Rare),ee-chee|IE-see|EE-see,,,,,,,"A nickname and prefix in names, meaning ""with, together"" and ""to each other"" in Sioux."
Iciani,f,,Spanish (Latin American),ee see ah nee(Latin American Spanish),,,,,,,Not available.
Icidro,m,,American (Hispanic),,,,,,,,Variant of Isidro.
