Idmon,m,Ἴδμων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˈið.mon/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""having knowledge, skilled, knowing"" in Ancient Greek, ultimately derived from οἶδα (oida) meaning ""to know, be skilled in"". This is the name of several figures from Greek mythology, including the father of Arachne, a seer who joined the Argonauts, and one of the fifty sons of Aegyptus, who was killed by his wife, Pylarge, on their wedding night."
