Idomeneus,m,Ἰδομενεύς(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Late Greek|Ancient Greek,/aɪ.ˈdɒ.mɪn.i.əs/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""of Idomene, from Idomene"", derived from the name of the ancient city Idomene, itself meaning ""strength of Ida"", composed of the name of Mount Ida combined with Ancient Greek μένος (menos) ""mind, force, strength, courage"". In Greek mythology, Idomeneus was a Cretan king and commander who led the Cretan armies to the Trojan War, in eighty black ships. He was also one of the suitors of Helen, as well as a comrade of the Telamonian Ajax. Meriones was his charioteer and brother-in-arms."
