Idosław,m,,Polish (Rare),,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Polish idę ""I am going"" (though it literally means ""I go""), which is derived from Polish iść ""to go, to walk"" (which in turn is derived from Proto-Slavic it'i ""to go""). Also compare Croatian ići ""to go"". The second element of this name is derived from Slavic slav ""glory"". As such, this name roughly means ""I am going gloriously"" or ""I am going with glory""."
