Iehuiah,m,יְהֻוּיָה(Ancient Hebrew),Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""Yahweh is he, he is Yahweh"", derived from Hebrew יְהוֹ (yeho) referring to the Hebrew God, הוּא (hu) meaning ""he"" and יָהּ (yah) also referring to the Hebrew God. This is the name of an angel belonging to the order of the Powers. He is one of the 72 angels bearing the explicit name of God (the Shem HaMephorash), as interpreted by some Christian Kabbalists."
Ieialel,m,יֵיעַלֵּל(Ancient Hebrew),Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""might of God"", derived from Hebrew אֱיָל (eyal) meaning ""might, strength, power"" combined with אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"". This is the name of an angel belonging to the order of the Archangels. He is one of the 72 angels bearing the explicit name of God (the Shem HaMephorash), as interpreted by some Christian Kabbalists."
Ieiazel,m,יֵעִיַּזְּאֵל(Ancient Hebrew),Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""God will sprinkle"", derived from Hebrew יִזֶּה (yizze) meaning ""he will sprinkle, he will splatter"" combined with אֵל (ʾel) meaning ""God"". This is the name of an angel belonging to the order of the Powers. He is one of the 72 angels bearing the explicit name of God (the Shem HaMephorash), as interpreted by some Christian Kabbalists."
