Ikki,m,"一輝, 一貴, 一稀, 一希, 一樹, 一気, 一喜, 一期(Japanese Kanji)|いっき(Japanese Hiragana)|イッキ(Japanese Katakana)|Икки(Russian)",Japanese|Soviet,eek̚-kee,,,,,,,"This name combines 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu, i') meaning ""one"" with 輝 (ki, kagaya.ku) meaning ""radiance, shine, sparkle, brilliance,"" 貴 (ki, tatto.i, touto.i) meaning ""precious, prize, value,"" 稀 (ki, ke, mabora, mare) meaning ""rare,"" 希 (ki, ke, mare) meaning ""few, hope, wish, rare,"" 樹 (ju, ki) meaning ""timber, wood, tree,"" 気 (ki, ke, iki) meaning ""air, atmosphere, mind, mood, spirit,"" 喜 (ki, yoroko.bu) meaning ""rejoice, pleasure"" or 期 (ki, go) meaning ""date, period, term, time.""Ikki (一気, 一樹 & 一期) can also be used as words. The first one is used repeatedly as a party cheer, something along the lines of ""chug!"" and ""drink!"" The second one refers to a tree or one tree and the third one refers to one term/period or the first term/period.Note that the k̚ is an unreleased stop."
