Ikuma,m,"生真, 生馬, 郁真, 郁万, 行真, 育蒔, 伊玖磨, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|いくま(Japanese Hiragana)|イクマ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/i.kɯᵝ.mä/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 生 (iku) meaning ""virile, lively"", 郁 (iku) meaning ""cultured, refined"", 行 (iku) meaning ""go, carry out"" or 育 (iku) meaning ""raise, bring up"" combined with 真 (ma) meaning ""real, genuine, true"", 馬 (ma) meaning ""horse"", 万 (ma) meaning ""myriad, various, many, all"" or 蒔 (ma) meaning ""sowing seeds"". It can also be formed from 伊 (i) meaning ""this, that"" combined with 玖 (ku) meaning ""black jewel"" and 磨 (ma) meaning ""polish, grind"", as well as other combinations of kanji."
