Ileus,m,"Ἴλιος, Ἰλεύς(Ancient Greek)",Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"A son of Apollo by the Trojan nymph Ourea in Greek mythology. His name was apparently a play on the Ancient Greek word ἵλεος (ileos) meaning ""gracious, propitious, kindly"", since Apollo found Ourea to be favourable, as well as Ἴλιος (see Ilium), the name of the city he was conceived in. It may have also been an altered form of Oileus."
