Imamiah,m,עִמַּמִיָּה(Ancient Hebrew),Judeo-Christian-Islamic Legend,,,,,,,,"Possibly means ""Yahweh darkens"", derived from Hebrew עָמַם (ʿamam) meaning ""to darken, to dim, to hide"" combined with יָהּ (yah) referring to the Hebrew God. This is the name of an angel belonging to the order of the Principalities. He is one of the 72 angels bearing the explicit name of God (the Shem HaMephorash), as interpreted by some Christian Kabbalists."
