Imbrus,m,Ἴμβρος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˈɪm.brəs/,,,,,,,"Possibly from the name of the island Ἴμβρος (Imbros), of uncertain etymology. In Greek mythology, Imbrus was one of the fifty sons of King Aegyptus, and was killed by his wife Euippe on their wedding night. In some accounts, this was also the original name of Centaurus, father of the half-human, half-horse centaurs."
