İmge,f,,Turkish,/ˈimɡe/,,,,,,,"İmge is a purely Turkish concept derived from the Old Turkic root im (""sign,"" ""mark,"" or ""omen"") combined with the nominalizing suffix -ge. It signifies a ""vision,"" ""mental construct,"" or ""symbolic representation."" Unlike the French/Latin image (which traces back to imago (imitation/copy)) the Turkish İmge is rooted in the act of signifying or marking reality with meaning. It is not an imitation of the physical world but an original ""mental imprint."" To carry this name is to be a visionary; it represents an intellect that does not merely see the world but interprets, crafts, and defines it."
