Imna,m,יִמְנָע(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical|Biblical Hebrew,/jim.ˈnɔʕ/(Biblical Hebrew),,,,,,,"Might mean ""right hand, fortunate, prosperity"". It may also link to the Hebrew root מָנַע‎ (manaʿ) ""to withhold, restrain"". Imna was one of the sons of Asher, a son of Jacob, mentioned in the Book of Genesis (46:17) and 1 Chronicles."
Imnah,m,יִמְנָה(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,IM-nuh(Biblical English),,,,,,,"Translates ""right hand"" or ""prosperity."" Rooted in the ancient Hebrew language, the right hand is historically symbolic of strength, favour, and good fortune. It can be either the eldest son of Asher and a grandson to Jacob and Zilpah, or a Levite tasked with assisting in the distribution of freewill offerings to the Lord."
