İmre,f,,Turkish,EEM-reh,,,,,,,"İmre is a Turkish feminine name. It developed as a feminine variant of the popular masculine name Emre. Both names share the same Old Turkic root, originating from the verb imrenmek, which evolved from the ancient Turkic root amraq meaning ""loving"", ""dear"", or ""beloved"".Unlike some of its cognates in sister Turkic languages, the modern Turkish verb imrenmek does not carry a negative connotation of ""envy"" or ""jealousy"". Instead, it means ""to desire"", ""to yearn for"", ""to covet"", or ""to emulate with high admiration"". Therefore, the name carries the connotation of someone who is deeply admired, longed for, or desired.Just as the masculine Emre is often historically and etymologically confused with Emrah, the feminine İmre faces a similar confusion with the name İmra. However, they are completely unrelated.Emre/İmre is of purely Turkic origin, rooted in the morphophonological evolution of the Proto-Turkic root am- / amra-.Conversely, Emrah/İmra is derived from the Arabic name Imrah (or from the Arabic root i-m-r-a-h / imra'ah meaning ""woman""). Because these two name groups belong to entirely different language families (Turkic vs. Afroasiatic) and possess distinct phonetic evolutions, any shared identity between İmre and İmra is a folk-etymological myth."
