Ina-egasil-ramat,f,,Babylonian,,,,,,,,"Means ""She dwells in Esagil"". Name borne by the mother of Nupta, who was the wife of Itti-marduk-balatu. Ina-esagil-ramat is known primarily from documents detailing her dowry."
Ina-eturkalamma-alsišu,f,,Babylonian,,,,,,,,"Means ""In Eturkalamma, I called out to him"", deriving from the Akkadian element šasû (""to shout, to call for""). Eturkalamma was a temple to Ishtar in Babylon, where she was worshipped as Bēlet-bābili."
