In-seo,,"인서(Korean Hangul)|仁序, 寅序, 仁舒, 寅舒, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.sʌ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 仁 (in) meaning ""compassionate"" or 寅 (in), meaning “revere, respect”, also referring the to third Earthly Branches (3AM to 5AM), itself associated with the tiger of the Chinese zodiac combined with 序 (seo) meaning ""series, sequence"" or 舒 (seo) meaning ""open up, unfold, comfortable, easy"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
In-seok,m,인석(Korean Hangul),Korean,,,,,,,,Not available.
Inseon,f,"인선(Korean Hangul)|仁善, 仁仙(Korean Hanja)",Korean,,,,,,,,"Deriving from the Sino-Korean elements 仁 (in), meaning ""benevolence, kindness, humaneness"", and 善 (seon) meaning ""good, virtuous, charitable, kind"" or 仙 (seon) meaning ""immortal, transcendent, Taoist super-being"". Other hanja combinations are also possible."
In-seong,m,"인성(Korean Hangul)|人成, 寅成, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.sʌŋ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 人 (in) meaning “man, person, mankind” or 寅 (in), meaning “revere, respect”, also referring the to third Earthly Branches (3AM to 5AM), itself associated with the tiger of the Chinese zodiac combined with 成 (seong) meaning ""completed, finished succeeded"".Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
In-shik,m,"인식(Korean Hangul)|仁植, 寅植, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.ɕʰik̚/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangul 인식 (see In-Sik).
Inshushinak,m,,Near Eastern Mythology|Elamite Mythology,,,,,,,,"Inshushinak was the name of one of the major gods of the Elamite pantheon. He started out as a mere local god, in which capacity he was the patron deity of the city of Susa. This is also reflected in his name, as it is derived from Sumerian nin-shushinak meaning ""lord of Susa"". The fact that his name is Sumerian rather than Elamite, seems to indicate that Sumer has had some influence on Elamite religion (or merely on religious life in Susa) at some point in time. Either way, as the city of Susa rose in importance in Elam over time, so did the cult of Inshushinak: once Susa was firmly established as the capital city of Elam, Inshushinak became a national god and was ranked after Humban's wife Kiririsha in the Elamite pantheon. As a national god, he was responsible for oaths, but he also had a function in the underworld, where he was a judge of the dead. At least sixteen Elamite kings were named in his honour (which is consistent with the fact that nearly all rulers of Elam bore theophoric names)."
In-sik,m,"인식(Korean Hangul)|仁植, 寅植, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.ɕʰik̚/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 仁 (in) meaning ""compassionate"" or 寅 (in) referring to the third of the twelve Earthly Branches (itself associated with the tiger of the Chinese zodiac) combined with 植 (sik) meaning ""plant, tree, to plant, to grow"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
İnşirah,f,انشراح(Ottoman Turkish),Ottoman Turkish|Turkish (Rare),,,,,,,,"Ultimately from Arabic انشراح (inshirāh) meaning ""relief, cheerfulness""."
Insiya,f,انسیا(Urdu),Arabic (Rare)|Urdu|Indian (Muslim),,,,,,,,"Possibly the Arabic form of Ensieh. This name was used for the main character, Insia or Insiya Malik, in the 2017 Indian movie Secret Superstar."
Inske,,,East Frisian (Archaic),,,,,,,,For boys it's a short version of Ine 5 for girls it's a short version of names containing ine or a feminine version of the male name Ine 5.
In-song,,"인송(Korean Hangul)|仁松, 仁訟, 人松, 人訟, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.sʰo̞ŋ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 仁 (in) meaning ""compassionate"", or 人 (in) meaning ""man, person, mankind, people"", combined with 松 (song) meaning ""pine (tree)"". Other Hanja combinations are possible."
In-soo,m,仁秀(Korean Hanja)|인수(Korean Hangul),Korean,EEN-SOO,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 仁 (in) meaning ""humanity, virtue, benevolence, charity, man, kernel"" combined with 秀 (soo) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"". Other hanja combinations are possible.Famous bearers are Chun In-soo, a South Korean archer and Olympic champion, Insoo Hyun, an Associate Professor of Bioethics and Philosophy at Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland, Ohio and Kang In-Soo, a South Korean singer."
Inspektor,m,,English,,,,,,,,"Swedish for inspector, meaning ""overseer, superintendent,"" from Latin inspector ""one who views or observes,"" agent noun from past participle stem of inspicere ""look at, observe, view; look into, inspect, examine,"""
Instancia,f,,Medieval English,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Latin īnstantia meaning ""perseverance""."
İnsu,f,,Turkish (Rare),/in.su/,,,,,,,"İnsu is a compound name formed from in (referring to a ""hidden cave,"" ""den,"" ""shelter,"" or ""niche"") and su (""water""). It symbolizes a ""protected sanctuary of life,"" representing the ""serenity of water nestled within a hidden, secure space."" It acts as a poetic image of peace and natural concealment."
In-suk,f,인숙(Korean Hangul),Korean,EEN-SOOK,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 仁 ""humaneness, benevolence, kindness"" and 淑 ""good, pure, virtuous, charming""."
