Invención,f,,Spanish (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Spanish invención meaning ""invention, finding"". This name is given after Roodmass, the celebration of the finding of Jesus Christ's cross by Saint Helena, commemorated by the Catholic Church on 3rd May."
Inver,m,ინვერ(Georgian),Georgian (Rare),,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. It might possibly be the Mingrelian form of Enver, as En- tends to become In- in Mingrelian. A good example of this is the name of the river Enguri in western Georgia, which is known as ინგირი (Ingiri) in Mingrelian."
