In-yeong,f,"인영(Korean Hangul)|人英, 仁英, 人榮, 仁榮, 人永, 仁永, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/in.jʌŋ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 人 (in) meaning ""person, mankind, people"" or 仁 (in) meaning ""compassionate"" combined with 英 (yeong) meaning ""flower, petal, brave, hero"" or 榮 (yeong) meaning ""glory, honour, flourish, prosper"" or 永 (yeong), meaning ""perpetual, eternal"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
