Iorio,m,,Medieval Italian|Italian (Tuscan),"YAW-ryo(Medieval Italian, Tuscan Italian)",,,,,,,Medieval Italian form of Giorgio originally used in Southern Italy. After Gabriele D'Annunzio used this name in his tragedy La figlia di Iorio (1904) the name has been used mostly in Toscana (Tuscany) and Emilia-Romagna (both in central Italy).
