Iruma,m,"いるま(Japanese Hiragana)|イルマ(Japanese Katakana)|入間, 冶真, 入真, 射磨, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare)|Popular Culture,[i.ɾɯ̟.mä](Japanese),,,,,,,"From Japanese 冶 (iru) meaning ""smelting,"" 入 (iru) meaning ""entering,"" or 射 (iru) meaning ""shoot, archery, morphism"" combined with 真 (ma) meaning ""truth, reality"" or 磨 (ma) meaning ""polishing, grind."" Other Kanji combinations are possible."
