Isako,f,"イサ(Japanese Katakana)|いさこ(Japanese Hiragana)|勇子, 鯨子, 威子, 以佐子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,EE-SA-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 以 (i) meaning ""in view of, compared to"", 佐 (sa) meaning ""aid, help"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Isaku,m,"イサク(Japanese Katakana)|いさく(Japanese Hiragana)|伊作, 意咲, 一索, 尉策, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese|Albanian,EE-SA-KOO,,,,,,,"From 夷 (i) meaning ""flat, level, low, ancient tribes in China"" combined with 削 (saku) meaning ""whittle, plane"", or 威 (isa) meaning ""might, power, strength, authority"" combined with 丘 (ku) meaning ""hillock, mound, hill"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
