Ísalind,f,,"Icelandic (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Derived from Old Norse íss ""ice"" and lind ""lime tree, linden tree"" (also see Lind), or an Icelandic form of Old High German Iselinde. Alternatively, it could be a blend of names such as Ísabella and Rósalind."
