Ishat,f,𐎌𐎚𐎚(Ugaritic),Ugaritic Mythology,/ˈʔi.ʃat/,,,,,,,"In Ancient Syro-Canaanite religions Ishat was a goddess of fire, wife of Moloch. She was slain by Anat.Ishat was described as a fire goddess and the consort of Moloch (also known as Milcom), a deity associated with fire. According to certain mythological accounts, she was slain by the war goddess Anat. Anat boasts of having defeated various formidable beings, including Ishat, whom she refers to as ""the bitch of the gods,"" highlighting her formidable nature and the intensity of their conflict."
