Ishvari,f,ईश्वरी(Sanskrit),Hinduism,,,,,,,,"Means ""queen, mistress, goddess"" in Sanskrit, the feminine form of ईश्वर (īśvará) which is both an adjective meaning ""able to do, capable of"" and a noun meaning ""lord, king, God"". In Hinduism this is an epithet referring to the Goddess, the divine female counterpart of Ishvara. It is also a term that refers to the shakti, or the feminine energy of the Trimurti, which refer to Saraswati, Lakshmi and Parvati (i.e. the Tridevi)."
