Ismakiah,m,יִשְׂמַכְיָהוּ(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,is-mə-KIE-ə(Biblical English)|iz-mə-KIE-ə(Biblical English),,,,,,,"From the Hebrew name יִשְׂמַכְיָהוּ (Yismakhyahu) meaning ""Yahweh will sustain"", from the roots סמך (samak) meaning ""to support, to uphold"" and יָהּ (yah) referring to the Hebrew God. In the Old Testament Ismakiah or Ismachiah was a Levite who was assigned by King Hezekiah to be an overseer of the church."
