Isonoe,f,Ισονόη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/aɪ.ˈsɒ.noʊ.iː/(English),,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek ἰσονοέω (isonoeo) meaning ""to consider oneself equal, worthy"" or ""to think equally"", composed of ἴσος (isos) ""equal"" and νόος (noos) ""mind, thought"". Isonoe, also called Hesione and Isione, was one of the Daenids in Greek mythology, and the mother of Orchomenos by Zeus. A moon of Jupiter is named after her."
