Ittoku,m,"一徳, 一得(Japanese Kanji)|いっとく(Japanese Hiragana)|イットク(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,eet̚-tok|eet̚-to-kuu,,,,,,,"This name combines 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu, i') meaning ""one"" with 徳 (toku) meaning ""benevolence, goodness, virtue"" or 得 (toku, u.ru, e.ru) meaning ""profit, advantage, benefit, gain.""As a word, Ittoku means ""virtue"" (一徳) and ""one advantage, merit"" (一得) respectively.One bearer of this name is actor Ittoku Kishibe (岸部 一徳) (1947-), born Shūzō Kishibe (岸部 修三).Note that the t̚ is an unreleased stop."
