Itylus,m,Ἴτυλος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology (Latinized),/ˈi.ty.los/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology. In Greek mythology, Itylus was the son of Aedon and King Zethus of Thebes. Envious of Niobe, the wife of her husband's brother Amphion, who had six sons and six daughters, Aedon attempted to kill the eldest of Niobe's sons, but by mistake slew her own son Itylus. In later myths, he is instead called Itys, and intentionally killed as vengeance against his father."
