Iuli,m,,Old Norse|Old Danish,,,,,,,,"Short form of names containing Old Norse ígull meaning ""sea urchin"", ultimately derived from Proto-Germanic *igilaz ""hedgehog"" (compare Modern Swedish igelkott and Faroese igelkøttur, both meaning ""hedgehog""). Examples of such names are Ígulgæirr and Ígulfríðr."
