Ivalú,f,,"Spanish (Latin American, Rare)",,,,,,,,"Combination of Ivanna (which is used as a feminine form of Iván) or another name beginning with the same sound (such as Ivelisse) with Lourdes (compare Lulú), Luisa or Lucía."
Ivaly,f,,English (American)|American (Hispanic),,,,,,,,"Of uncertain origin and meaning.It might be a feminized form of Ival, however, given how rare the masculine name Ival is, this is unlikely. It might also be a transferred use of the extremely rare surname Ivaly, which is also a rather unlikely source. It might simply be an elaborated form of Iva. It might even be a rare variant of Ivelis, itself a rare variant of Yvelisse (via the variants Ivelisse and Ivalisse). The variant Ivalia suggests that it might have been influenced, if not been based on, Evalia and thus Evelia."
