Ixquic,f,,Mayan Mythology|New World Mythology|Spanish (Latin American),sh-KEEK|EE-skee(Latin American Spanish),,,,,,,"Means ""blood lady"" in Quiché (Mayan), from the feminine prefix ix- combined with qiq ""blood"". In Mayan mythology she was the mother of the twin gods Hunahpu and Ixbalanqué."
