Izayoi,f,イザヨイ(Japanese Katakana)|いざよい(Japanese Hiragana)|十六夜(Japanese Kanji),Japanese (Rare),EE-AH-YO-EE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 十 (i) meaning ""six"", 六 (za) meaning ""ten"", and 夜 (yoi) meaning ""night"", denoting the sixteenth night in the lunar calendar. Traditionally, this is the name for the day after Tsukimi, the Harvest Moon festival."
