Izbylut,m,,Polish (Rare),eez-BI-loot,,,,,,,"From the Slavic elements, izby meaning ""to get rid of"", ""to dispose of"", ""to rid"", ""to do away with"", ""to clear out"", ""to dispense with"", ""to divest"", ""to choke off"", ""to bundle off"", ""to bundle out"", ""to deliver oneself of"" and lut meaning ""dour"", ""sharp"", ""acute"", ""pungent"", ""nipping"", ""strident"", ""with an edge"", ""clarion"". Thus it may mean ""the one who got rid of sternness""."
