İzge,f,,Turkish,/iz-ɡe/,,,,,,,"Derived from the root iz (mark, trace, spectrum). In the context of 1940s scientific neologisms in Turkish, it was coined to represent ""a spectrum or a diverse manifestation of light/energy."" It symbolizes the ""trace of the infinite,"" representing a person who leaves a unique, multifaceted footprint upon the world."
