Iztaccihuatl,f,,New World Mythology|Aztec and Toltec Mythology,/iʃ.tak.ˈsi.wat͡ɬ/(New World Mythology),,,,,,,"Means ""White woman"" in Nahuatl. In Tlaxcaltecan mythology, she was a princess who fell in love with Popocatepetl, one of her fathers warriors. The emperor sent Popocatepetl to war, promising him to become the husband of Iztaccíhuatl when he returned. Iztaccíhuatl was falsely told that Popocatépetl had died during the war and died in greif. A volcano in Mexico is named after her."
