Jamphel,,འཇམ་དཔལ(Tibetan),Buddhism|Tibetan|Bhutanese,,,,,,,,"Means ""gentle splendour"" from Tibetan འཇམ ('jam) meaning ""soft, gentle"" and དཔལ (dpal) meaning ""splendour, glory, magnificence"". This is the Tibetan name for the bodhisattva Manjushri, used as a calque of Sanskrit मञ्जुश्री (mañjuśrī)."
