Jerimoth,m,ירִימוֹת(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,jeri-mahth(Biblical English),,,,,,,"Jerimoth (sometimes spelled Jeremoth) is a Hebrew name that translates to ""heights,"" ""elevations,"" ""exaltations,"" or ""He's mostly elevated."" In the Hebrew Bible, it's a common given name belonging to at least eight different men, primarily found in the books of Chronicles."
