Jérômée,f,,French (Archaic),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Jérôme, perhaps via its other feminine form Jérômie.A known bearer of this name was the German writer Jenny von Gustedt (1811-1890), who was born as Jérômée Catharina Rabe von Pappenheim. She was the illegitimate daughter of Jérôme Bonaparte (1784-1860), the youngest brother of the French statesman Napoléon Bonaparte (1769-1821)."
Jéromette,f,,French (Archaic)|Literature,,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Jérôme, which is the modern French form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).In literature, this is the name of the titular character of the short story Miss Jéromette and the Clergyman (1875) written by the English author Wilkie Collins (1824-1889)."
