Jérômie,f,,"French (Rare)|French (Swiss, Rare)|French (Belgian, Archaic)|French (Quebec, Archaic)","/ʒe.ʁɔ.mi/(French, Swiss French, Belgian French, Quebec French)",,,,,,,"Feminine form of Jérôme, which is the modern French form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).A known bearer of this name is the Swiss figure skater Jérômie Repond (b. 1999), who won the Swiss junior championship four times and also participated in the first season of Switzerland's Next Top Model."
Jeromin,m,,German (Rare),ye-ro-min,,,,,,,Masculine form (backformation) of Jeromine.The name is borne by the political economist Jeromin Zettlmeyer.
Jeromina,f,,German (Rare),YE-ro-mee-na,,,,,,,Feminine form of Jérôme.
Jéromine,f,,"French (Rare)|French (Quebec)|French (Belgian, Rare)|French (Swiss, Rare)","/ʒe.ʁɔ.min/(French, Quebec French, Belgian French, Swiss French)",,,,,,,"Feminine form of Jérôme, which is the modern French form of Hieronymos (see Jerome).Known bearers of this name include the French explorer Jéromine Pasteur (b. 1954) and the French alpine skier Jéromine Géroudet (b. 1990)."
Jerommeke,m,,Dutch (Rare)|Flemish (Rare)|Literature,yə-RAWM-mə-kə(Dutch)|zhə-RAWM-mə-kə(Flemish),,,,,,,"Diminutive of Jerom and sometimes also of Jeroom. Also compare Jeroomke, which is the usual diminutive of Jeroom.In Belgium (specifically Flanders) and the Netherlands, this name is best known for being the pet name of Jerom, the strongman in the well-known Belgian comic strip Suske en Wiske, which is known as Spike and Suzy in Great Britain and as Willy and Wanda in the United States."
