Jiaxiang,m,"佳翔, 珈翔, 佳祥, 珈祥, 佳响, 珈响, 佳湘, 珈湘, etc.(Chinese)|佳翔, 珈翔, 佳祥, 珈祥, 佳響, 珈響, 佳湘, 珈湘, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕi̯ä.ɕi̯ɑŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese (jiā) meaning ""good, auspicious"" or 珈 (jiā) referring to a type of ornament worn on a woman's hairpin combined with 翔 (xiáng) meaning ""soar, glide"" or 祥 (xiáng) meaning ""good luck, good omen"" or 响 (xiǎng) meaning ""sound, echo"" or 湘 (xiāng) which refers to the Xiang River in southern China. Other character combinations can form this name as well."
