Jilmay,f,Жилмай(Uzbek),Uzbek,[dʒil.ˈmɑj],,,,,,,"Formed from the Uzbek verb root Jilmay (""to smile""), this name is a beautiful example of a state-of-being name. It translates to ""The Eternal Smile"" or ""The One Who Radiates Joy."" Symbolically, it represents a person whose very nature is soft, approachable, and inherently optimistic. It paints a picture of a gentle presence that breaks tension and brings warmth to any environment, suggesting a soul that handles life's challenges with a grace that is both persistent and disarming."
