Jireh,,,"Filipino|English (African, Rare)|French (African, Rare)|Spanish (Latin American, Rare)|American (Modern)",/ˈd͡ʒaɪ.ɹə/(English),,,,,,,"From the second part of Jehovah-jireh, the name of the mountain on which God ordered Abraham to sacrifice his son Isaac in the Old Testament. The place name, יְהוָה יִרְאֶה‎ (YHWH yir'e) in the original Hebrew, means ""Yahweh sees"" or ""Yahweh will see"" from an active form (a third person singular) of the verb רָאָה (raʾa) ""to see"", though it is popularly interpreted as meaning ""Yahweh will see to it, Yahweh will provide"". According to the Book of Genesis, it was so named by Abraham after God provided a ram to sacrifice in place of Isaac.The Christian song Jireh (2021) by Maverick City Music and Elevation Worship may have helped popularize the name, which entered the United States top 1000 list for boys in 2023."
