Jirōta,m,"二郎太, 次郎太, 治郎太, 司郎太, 道郎太, 二朗太, 次朗太, 治朗太, 司朗太, 道朗太(Japanese Kanji)|じろうた(Japanese Hiragana)|ジロウタ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),JEE-ṘO:-TAH,,,,,,,"This name combines 二 (ji, ni, futa, futata.bi, futa.tsu) meaning ""two,"" 次 (shi, ji, tsugi, tsu.gu) meaning ""next, second,"" 治 (ji, chi, osa.maru, osa.meru, nao.su, nao.ru) meaning ""cure, govern, heal, reign, rule,"" 司 (shi, tsukasado.ru, tsukasa) meaning ""administer, direct, government office, official, rule"" or 道 (tou, dou, michi, ji) meaning ""course, journey, road, street, moral principle"" & 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son"" or 朗 (rou, aki.raka, hoga.raka) meaning ""bright, cheerful, clear, merry"" with 太 (ta, tai, futo.i, futo.ru) meaning ""big, plump, thick.""This name is very rarely given to boys, if given at all."
