Jondo,m,ჯონდო(Georgian),Georgian,,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain. Most Georgian sources neglect to provide a meaning for this name; there is only one Georgian source that attempts to do so, and it connects the name to Joni 2 (ultimately of Hebrew origin). If Jondo is indeed etymologically related to that name, then perhaps it would be a better comparison to say that Jondo is the Georgian equivalent of Johnno or Jonno.Meanwhile, a Russian source states that Jondo is a Georgian derivative of the Persian name Jandar. This is possible, as it wouldn't be the first time that Persian -a- became -o- in Georgian. For another example of that, see Bondo."
