Jongho,m,종호(Korean Hangul),Korean,/tɕoŋ.ɦo/,,,,,,,"The Korean name Jongho (종호) generally means ""wide influence"" or ""fullness"" and is composed of the Hanja characters 鍾 (jong), meaning ""bell,"" and 浩 (ho), meaning ""wide/large, or fullness"". It implies a person who can make a resounding impact and set a broad example."
