Joshaphat,m,יְהוֹשָׁפָט(Ancient Hebrew),Biblical,JAHSH-ə-fat(Biblical English),,,,,,,"Contracted form of Jehoshaphat.In the Bible, there are two people named Joshaphat. The first, in 1 Chronicles 11:43, is one of David's warriors. The second, in 1 Chronicles 15:24, is one of the priests who played their trumpets for the ark of God."
