Jubilee,,,English|Popular Culture,/ˌd͡ʒu.bə.ˈli/(English)|/ˈd͡ʒu.bə.ˌli/(English),,,,,,,"From the name of the Jewish special year of emancipation or from the major anniversary of an event. The word ultimately comes from Hebrew יוֹבֵל (yovél) ""shofar, ram's horn trumpet"", as the instrument was used to proclaim such event (see Leviticus 25:9). This may also refer to an African-American a cappella ensemble known as the Fisk Jubilee Singers and the religious musical groups that were influenced by them, the Jubilee quartets.Nowadays, it is mostly used femininely, but it is seldom used as a masculine name. A famous bearer of the name is the fictional American superhero Jubilee from the X-men comics, who is actually the short form of her given name, Jubilation Lee."
