Judaline,f,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,"This name is a combination of Judith with the popular name suffix -line. Alternatively, it can also be considered a variant form of Judalyn. Last but not least, it should also be noted that there are sources that claim that the name is a Jewish diminutive of Judith.This name is probably best known from the song ""Judaline"" from the 1948 musical ""A Date with Judy"".A known bearer of this name was Judith ""Judaline"" Sherwood (1938-1985), the niece of American actress Judy Garland (1922-1969)."
