Judson,m,,English|American (South),JUD-sən,,,,,,,"From an English surname that meant ""son of Jud"", Jud being a medieval diminutive of Jordan.In the 19th century USA Judson became a given name that was frequent among Baptists because of Adoniram Judson (1788-1850), a Baptist missionary in Burma (Myanmar) who was one of the first famous American missionaries. In addition to naming sons Judson after him, Baptists often named churches Judson Baptist Church or Judson Memorial Baptist church after Adoniram Judson."
