Ju-min,,주민(Korean Hangul),Korean|Popular Culture,/tɕu.min/(Korean),,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 柱 (ju) meaning ""pillar, column; branch"" or 周 (ju) meaning ""circumference"" and 民 (min) meaning ""people,"" 玟 (min) meaning ""streaks in jade; gem"" or 旻 (min) meaning ""(autumn) sky,"" among other hanja combinations.One fictional bearer of this name is Han Ju-min, one of the main characters in the visual novel 'Mystic Messenger'."
