Jung,m,"戎, etc.(Chinese)",Limburgish (Rare)|Chinese,/ˈjøŋ/,,,,,,,"Derived from Limburgish jung meaning ""boy"" or its diminutive jungske meaning ""little boy"".In Limburg, this name is strictly used informally, i.e. not as an official name on birth certificates. Often though, the nickname is given early in childhood and in most cases it gets stuck on the bearer, to the point where his Christian name is barely used again in daily life. See also Sonny for the English equivalent of this name."
