Junhua,,"军华, 军花, 俊华, 君骅, etc.(Chinese)|軍華, 軍华, 俊華, 君驊, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.xwa/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 军 (jūn) meaning ""army"", 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 君 (jūn) meaning ""king, ruler"" combined with 华 (huá) meaning ""splendid, illustrious, flowery, Chinese"", 花 (huā) meaning ""flower, blossom"" or 骅 (huá) meaning ""fine horse"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
