Jun-hyeok,m,"준혁(Korean Hangul)|俊赫, 浚赫, 埈赫, 準赫, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕun.ʝjʌk̚/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 俊 (jun) meaning ""talented, handsome"", 浚 (jun) meaning ""dredge, unearth, extract"", 埈 (jun) meaning ""high, steep, towering"" or 準 (jun) meaning ""rule, guideline, standard"" combined with 赫 (hyeok) meaning ""bright, radiant"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
