Junro,m,"淳朗, 潤朗, 純朗, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,JOON-RO,,,,,,,"From 淳 (jun) meaning ""pure"", 潤 (jun) meaning ""moisture"", or 純 (jun) meaning ""pure, clean, simple"" combined with 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son"" or 朗 (rou, aki.raka, hoga.raka) meaning ""bright, cheerful, clear, merry"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Junrong,,"俊荣, 俊融, 俊榕, etc.(Chinese)|俊榮, 俊融, 俊榕, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɻʊŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" combined with 荣 (róng) meaning ""glory, honour, flourish, prosper"", 融 (róng) meaning ""fuse, harmonize"" or 榕 (róng) meaning ""banyan tree"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junru,,"君如, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese|Chinese (Cantonese),/tɕʷin.ʐʷuː/(Chinese)|/tɕyn.ɹu/(Chinese)|/kʷɐn.jy/(Cantonese),,,,,,,"From Chinese 君 (jūn) meaning ""monarch, sovereign"" or ""gentleman"" combined with 如 (rú) meaning ""like, as, if"". Other hanzi combinations are possible."
Jun-sang,m,"준상(Korean Hangul)|準相, 畯相, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/d͡ʑun.saŋ/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 準 (jun) meaning ""rule, guideline, standard"", 畯 (jun) meaning ""rustic, crude"" combined with 相 (sang) meaning “mutual, together, jointly”. Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Junsei,m,"順正, 純政, 潤世, 準生, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,JOON-SE,,,,,,,"From the Japanese word 純正 (junsei) meaning ""genuine"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Junsheng,m,"俊生, 俊陞, 俊圣, 均生, 均晟, 浚生, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ʂɤŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"", 均 (jūn) meaning ""equal, even, balanced"" or 浚 (jùn) meaning ""profound, deep, enlighten, dredge, dig"" combined with 生 (shēng) meaning ""living, fresh"", 陞 (shēng) meaning ""rise, lift, ascend, promote"", 圣 (shèng) meaning ""holy, sacred"" or 晟 (shèng) meaning ""splendour, brightness, light"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Jun-soo,m,"준수(Korean Hangul)|俊秀, 遵守 準數, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕun.su/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangul 준수 (see Jun-su).
Jun-su,m,"준수(Korean Hangul)|俊秀, 遵守 準數, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕun.su/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 俊 (jun) meaning ""talented, handsome"", 遵 (jun) meaning ""obey, follow, honour"" or 準 (jun) meaning ""rule, guideline, standard"" combined with 秀 (su) meaning ""luxuriant, beautiful, elegant, outstanding"", 守 (su) meaning ""defend, protect, guard"" or 數 (su) meaning ""number, figure, fate, destiny"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Junsuke,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Junta,m,"惇太, 純太, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|じゅんた(Japanese Hiragana)|ジュンタ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/d͡ʑɯᵝn.tä/,,,,,,,"Derived from the Japanese kanji 惇 (jun) meaning ""kind, sincere"" or 純 (jun) meaning ""pure, clean, simple"" combined with 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big, great"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Juntarou,m,"隼太郎, 淳太郎, 準太郎, 醇太郎, 潤太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,JOON-TAH-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 隼 (jun) meaning ""falcon"", 淳 (jun) meaning ""pure"", 準 (jun) meaning ""rule, guideline, standard"", 醇 (jun) meaning ""rich, good as wine"" or 潤 (jun) meaning ""soft, moist"", 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Junte,m,,Sami,JOON-te,,,,,,,Sami form of Jonte.
Jünter,m,,Popular Culture,YUUN-tər,,,,,,,Jünter is the Ripuarian and Berlin dialect form of Günter.It is the name of the mascot of the German football club Borussia Mönchengladbach (honoring Günter Netzer).
Junto,m,"准斗, 洵斗, 淳人, 潤人, 純人, 純斗, 純渡, 純登, 純都, 遵人, 順人, 順斗, 順渡, 順登, 順都, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,JUUN-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 准 (jun) meaning ""quasi-, semi-, associate"", 洵 (jun) meaning ""alike, truth"", 淳 (jun) meaning ""pure"", 潤 (jun) meaning ""wet, be watered, profit by, receive benefits, favor, charm, steep"", 純 (jun) meaning ""genuine, purity, innocence, net (profit)"", 遵 (jun) meaning ""abide by, follow, obey, learn"" or 順 (jun) meaning ""obey, order, turn, right, docility, occasion"" combined with 斗 (to), which refers to a Chinese constellation, 人 (to) meaning ""person"", 渡 (to) meaning ""transit, ford, ferry, cross, import, deliver, diameter, migrate"", 登 (to) meaning ""ascend, climb up"" or 都 (to) meaning ""metropolis, capital, all, everything"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Junue,f,,"Spanish (Mexican, Rare)",,,,,,,,Not available.
