Junuunay,,,New World Mythology,,,,,,,,Not available.
Junwei,,"俊维, 俊威, 俊伟, 军伟, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.weɪ̯/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 军 (jūn) meaning ""army"" combined with 维 (wéi) meaning ""tie, fasten, preserve, maintain"", 威 (wēi) meaning ""power, pomp"" or 伟 (wěi) meaning ""great, robust, extraordinary"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junwen,,"俊文, 骏文, etc.(Chinese)|俊文, 駿文, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.wən/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 骏 (jùn) meaning ""good horse, fast"" combined with 文 (wén) meaning ""literature, culture, writing"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Jun-won,m,"준원(Korean Hangul)|俊元, 俊源, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕun.wʌn/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Korean 俊 (jun) meaning ""talented, handsome"" combined with 元 (won) meaning ""first, origin"" or 源 (won) meaning ""spring, source"". Other hanja combinations can form this name as well."
Jun-woo,m,"준우(Korean Hangul)|俊優, etc.(Korean Hanja)",Korean,/t͡ɕun.u/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Korean Hangul 준우 (see Jun-u).
Junxi,,"俊茜, 俊熙, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɕi/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" combined with 熙 (xī) meaning ""bright, splendid, glorious"". Other hanzi combinations are possible."
Junxia,f,"军霞, 俊霞, etc.(Chinese)|軍霞, 俊霞, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɕja/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 军 (jūn) meaning ""army"" or 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" combined with 霞 (xiá) meaning ""rosy clouds, mist"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junxian,f,"俊娴, 珺娴(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,"From the Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, capable, handsome, pretty"" or 珺 (jùn) meaning ""beautiful jade"" and 娴 (xián) meaning ""elegant, refined""."
Junxiang,,"军翔, 骏祥, etc.(Chinese)|軍翔, 駿祥, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɕjaŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 军 (jūn) meaning ""army"" or 骏 (jùn) meaning ""good horse, fast"" combined with 翔 (xiáng) meaning ""soar, glide"" or 祥 (xiáng) meaning ""good luck, good omen"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junxiong,m,"俊雄, 君雄, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɕi̯ʊŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 君 (jūn) meaning ""king, ruler"" combined with 雄 (xióng) meaning ""hero, male, manly"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junxuan,m,"浚瑄, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.ɕy̯ɛn/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 浚 (jùn) meaning ""to dredge, to extract"" combined with 瑄 (xuān) meaning ""6-cun-large jade annulus"". Other hanzi combinations are possible."
