Junyi,m,"峻毅, 竣毅, 峻 一, 竣一(Chinese)",Chinese,,,,,,,,"From 峻 (jùn) meaning ""high, steep, towering"" or 竣 (jùn) meaning ""to complete, to finish"" and 一 (yī) meaning ""one"" or 毅 (yì) meaning ""resolute, decisive, firm""."
Junying,,"君瑛, 钧瑛, 俊英, 隽英, etc.(Chinese)|君瑛, 鈞瑛, 俊英, 雋英, etc.(Traditional Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.iŋ/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 君 (jūn) meaning ""king, ruler"", 钧 (jūn) referring to an ancient unit of measurement (equivalent to about 15 kilograms), 俊 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" or 隽 (jùn) meaning ""talented, handsome"" combined with 瑛 (yīng) meaning ""jade"" or 英 (yīng) meaning ""flower, petal, brave, hero"". Other character combinations can form this name as well."
Junyu,,"君宇, 俊宇, 俊愉, 俊煜, 钧宇, 峻宇, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese,/t͡ɕyn.y/,,,,,,,"From Chinese 君 (jūn) meaning ""king, ruler"" combined with 宇 (yǔ) meaning ""house, eaves, universe"", as well as other hanzi combinations that can form this name."
