Juria,f,"樹利亜, 樹里亜, 樹里愛, 樹莉亜, 樹理愛, 樹梨亜, 樹梨愛, 寿莉亜, 寿理愛, 寿里亜(Japanese Kanji)|じゅりあ(Japanese Hiragana)|ジュリア(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Modern)|American (South, Archaic)|Romani (Archaic)",JUU-ṘEE-AH,,,,,,,"This name can be used as 樹利亜, 樹里亜, 樹里愛, 樹莉亜, 樹理愛, 樹梨亜, 樹梨愛, 寿莉亜, 寿理愛 or 寿里亜 with 樹 (ju, ki) meaning ""timber, wood, tree"", 寿 (shuu, ju, su, kotobuki, kotobu.ku, kotoho.gu) meaning ""congratulations, longevity,"" 利 (ri, ki.ku) meaning ""advantage, benefit, profit, gain"" 里 (ri, sato) meaning ""parent's home, ri (unit of distance - equal to 3.927 km), village,"" 莉 (rai, ri, rei), part of 茉莉 (matsuri) meaning ""jasmine,"" 理 (ri, kotowari) meaning ""justice, logic, reason, truth,"" 梨 (ri, nashi) meaning ""pear tree,"" 亜 (a, tsu.gu) meaning ""Asia, come after, rank next"" and 愛 (ai, ito.shii, o.shimu, kana.shii, mana, me.deru, a) meaning ""affection, love.""One bearer of this name is fashion icon Juria Nakagawa (中川 ジュリア) (1995-).Usage of this name may, most likely, be influenced by the name Julia."
Juriaan,m,,Dutch|Dutch (Surinamese)|Flemish (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Jurriaan.
Juriah,f,,"American (South, Archaic)",,,,,,,,"Variant of Jeriah. Although the Biblical character Jeriah is male, this name was also given to girls, starting around the mid-1700's."
Jurian,,"寿理安, 寿莉杏, 樹里杏, 樹莉杏(Japanese Kanji)|じゅりあん(Japanese Hiragana)|ジュリアン(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Modern, Rare)",/dʑɨᵝ.ɾʲi.ãɴ/,,,,,,,"Translated form of Julian and Julianne.This name is also used among the Japanese, though rarely, and can be written into kanji as 寿理安, 寿莉杏, 樹里杏 or 樹莉杏 with 樹 (ju, ki) meaning ""tree,"" 寿 (shuu, ju, su, kotobuki, kotobu.ku, kotoho.gu) meaning ""congratulations, longevity,"" 理 (ri, kotowari) meaning ""logic, reason,"" 莉 (rai, ri, rei), part of 茉莉 (matsuri), which refers to the Arabian jasmine, 里 (ri, sato), referring to a unit of distance called ri, or otherwise meaning ""village,"" 安 (an, yasu, yasu.i/maru, yasu.raka) meaning ""peaceful"" and 杏 (an, kyou, kou, anzu) meaning ""apricot."""
