Juthwara,f,,History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Anglo-Saxon corruption of Brythonic Aud Wyry, meaning ""Aud the Virgin"" (see Aude; though, according to Baring-Gould, Aud is 'from the Welsh Aidd, ""zeal, warmth, ardour"", cognate to the Irish aed, ead (see Áed) and the Gaelic eud'). This was the name of a 6th-century virgin and martyr from Dorset, known as Aud Wyry in Brittany."
