Kaeota,f,แก้วตา(Thai),Thai,/kɛːw˥˩.ˈtaː˧/,,,,,,,"Means ""beloved, dear"". From Thai แก้ว (kaeo) meaning ""glass, crystal"" and ตา (ta) meaning ""eye"" (literally ""lense of an eye"")."
Kaera,f,"歌恵羅, 歌恵良, 華依羅, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-E-ṘAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 歌 (ka) meaning ""song, sing"" or 華 (ka) meaning ""flower"", 恵 (e) meaning ""favor, blessing, grace, kindness"" or 依 (e) meaning ""reliant, depend on, consequently, therefore, due to"" combined with 羅 (ra) meaning ""gauze, thin silk"" or 良 (ra) meaning ""good, pleasing, skilled"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Kaera Uehara, a Japanese actress."
