Kageko,f,"カゲ子(Kanji/Katakana)|かげ子(Kanji/Hiragana)|影子, 景子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KAH-GEH-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 景 (kage) or 影 (kage) both meaning ""shadow, figure"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child, sign of the rat, first sign of the Chinese zodiac"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kagemi,f,"景実, 景美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-GE-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 景 (kage) meaning ""vista, view, scene"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kagemori,m,"かげもり(Japanese Hiragana)|カゲモリ(Japanese Katakana)|景盛, 影森, 景守, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KA-GE-MO-REE,,,,,,,"From 景 (kage) meaning ""scenery, view, vista"" and 盛 (mori) meaning ""to prosper"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kagemoto,m,"景元, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-GE-MO-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 景 (kage) meaning ""scenery, view"" combined with 元 (moto) meaning ""beginning, former time, origin"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.Kagemoto is most commonly used as a surname."
Kagen,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",KAY-gən(American English),,,,,,,Variant of Keegan.
Kagerō,,"景郎, 陽炎, 蜉蝣(Japanese Kanji)|かげろう(Japanese Hiragana)|カゲロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare)|Popular Culture,KAH-GE-ṘO:(Japanese),,,,,,,"This name can be used as 景郎, 陽炎 or 蜉蝣 with 景 (kei, kage) meaning ""scenery, view,"" 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son,"" 陽 (you, hi) meaning ""daytime, heaven, male, positive, sunshine, yang principle,"" 炎 (en, honoo) meaning ""blaze, flame, inflammation,"" 蜉 (fu), an outdated kanji meaning ""kind of ant, may fly"" and 蝣 (yuu), another outdated kanji meaning ""may fly.""This name coincides with the words 陽炎 meaning ""heat haze, shimmer of hot air"" and 蜉蝣 meaning ""mayfly, ephemeropteran, dragonfly, damselfly.""Fictional bearers of this name include Kagerō (陽炎 - female) from Basilisk, another Kagerō (陽炎 - female) from Ninja Scroll and Kagerō Shōkiin (青鬼院 蜻蛉 - male) from Inu x Boku SS.This name is extremely rare. According to data compiled from phonebooks, only 9 people (all most likely male) were given 景郎, 2 were given 陽炎 and 1 was given 蜉蝣."
Kageya,m,"影也, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-GE-YAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 影 (kage) meaning ""light"" combined with 也 (ya) meaning ""also"". This name can be formed with other kanji combinations as well."
ǀKágge̥n,m,,San Mythology,/ǀ͡kag.gen/|/ǀa.ɡən/,,,,,,,"Meaning unknown. In San mythology, he was described as a mantis and a folk hero of the ǀXam people.Note: The ""ǀ"" sign reflects Latin dental click, instead of the lowercase L."
Kaggwa,m,,Ganda,,,,,,,,second child (boy) after twins
Kaghan,m,,Turkish (Rare),,,,,,,,Rare variant transcription of Kağan.
Kaginga,m,,African Mythology,,,,,,,,Kaginga is both the spiritual incarnation of evil and the villainous deity of bad luck in Lega mythology. His name does not have a well known meaning.
Kagisoyame,m,,Tswana,,,,,,,,"Means ""my peace"" in Setswana."
