Kainaz,f,,Indian (Parsi),,,,,,,,"From the royal title Kai, a derivative of Avestan 𐬐𐬀𐬎𐬎𐬌 (kavi/kauui) meaning ""king"" and also ""poet-sacrificer"" or ""poet-priest"" (which was borne by the Kayanian kings, such as Kay Khosrow, who are the heroes of the Avesta (the sacred texts of Zoroastrianism) and of the 10th-century Persian epic the Shahnameh), combined with Persian ناز (nāz) meaning ""delight, comfort, coquetry""."
