Kalamos,m,Κάλαμος(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek,/ˈka.la.mos/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Means ""reed"" in Ancient Greek. In Greek mythology, Kalamos was a son of the river god Meander. When his companion Karpos drowned in a swimming contest, Kalamos allowed himself to drown as well out of grief, and was transformed into a reed."
