Kallianax,m,"Καλλιάναξ, Καλλίαναξ(Ancient Greek)",Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Greek κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty, nobility"" and ἄναξ (anax) meaning ""master, lord, king""."
Kallianeira,f,Καλλιάνειρα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek elements κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and ἀνήρ (aner) meaning ""man"". This was the name of a Nereid in Greek mythology."
Kallichore,f,Καλλιχόρη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/kə.ˈlɪ.kɒ.riː/(English),,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek καλλίχορος (kallichoros) meaning ""beautiful in the dance"", composed of κάλλος (kallos) ""beauty"" and χορός (choros) ""dance"". This is the name of one of the nymphs who nursed the infant Dionysus in Greek mythology. She is sometimes listed as one of the Muses. A moon of Jupiter is named after her."
Kallidoros,m,Καλλιδώρος(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""beautiful gift"" from Greek κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and δῶρον (doron) meaning ""gift"". Compare Calidore"
Kalligeneia,f,Καλλιγένεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""bearer of a fair offspring, producer of beautiful things"", derived from the Greek elements κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and γενής (genes) meaning ""born"". This was an epithet of the goddess Demeter."
Kalligenes,m,Καλλιγένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""bearer of a fair offspring, producer of beautiful things"", derived from the Greek elements κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and γενής (genes) meaning ""born"". Masculine form of Kalligenia."
Kallik,,,Inuit|Literature,Kal -ick(Inuktitut),,,,,,,"Used by Erin Hunter in the Seekers series of novels. It means, ""Lightning""."
Kallikles,m,Καλλικλῆς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/kal.li.klɛ̂ːs/(Attic Greek),,,,,,,"From Ancient Greek κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory""."
Kallikratidas,m,Καλλικρατίδας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Aeolic and Doric Greek form of Kallikratides, because it contains ίδας (idas), which is the Aeolic and Doric Greek form of the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).This name was borne by a Spartan naval commander from the 5th century BC. He is better known under the latinized form of his name, which is Callicratidas."
Kallikratides,m,Καλλικρατίδης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Means ""son of Kallikrates"" in Greek, derived from the name Kallikrates combined with the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides)."
