Kallisthene,f,Καλλισθένη(Ancient Greek),Late Greek|History (Ecclesiastical),,,,,,,,"Feminine form of Kallisthenes.A notable bearer of this name is saint Callisthene of Ephesus (4th century AD), whose native name was Kallisthene."
Kallisthenes,m,Καλλισθένης(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,/kal.lis.ˈθe.nis/(Koine Greek)|/kə.ˈlɪs.θə.ˌniːz/(English),,,,,,,"Means ""beautiful strength"", derived from Greek κάλλος (kallos) meaning ""beauty"" and σθένος (sthenos) meaning ""vigour, strength""."
