Kalma,f,,Finnish Mythology,,,,,,,,"Finnish Goddess of death and decay, residing in the underworld. The name means ""corpse stench"", and can be used as a poetic word for death.Her father is Tuoni and her mother Tuonetar. Kalma may also have several sisters, Kipu-Tyttö, Kivutar, Loviatar, and Vammatar, all of whom live in the Finnish underworld realm of Tuonela."
