Kalybe,f,Καλύβη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Late Greek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek καλύβη (kalybe) meaning ""hut, cabin"", specifically a type of rustic rural hut. This was the name of a nymph in Greek mythology, the mother of Boukolion by king Laomedon of Troy. It was also the name of a follower of Dionysos in the Indian War."
