Kamaladevi,f,"कमलादेवी, कमलदेवी(Hindi)|கமலாதேவி(Tamil)",Indian|Hindi|Tamil,,,,,,,,Combination of Kamala and Devi.
Kamalag,,Altai: Камалак(Kamalak) / Камалаг (Kamalag) Tuvan: Камалак (Kamalak) Khakas: Камалаг (Kamalag),Altai,kah-mah-LAHG,,,,,,,"The term Kamalag is rooted in the Siberian Turkic linguistic tradition (Altai, Tuva, and Khakas). It refers to the majestic Siberian cedar (Pinus sibirica) or noble pine species native to the taiga.The name derives from the ancient root *kam- or *kamal-, meaning ""to surround,"" ""to protect,"" or ""to stand firm."" Linguistically, it serves as a powerful symbol of:1. Unyielding longevity: The tree's ability to thrive in extreme conditions.2. Protective shelter: Representing a guardian presence.3. Silent resistance: Endurance against sub-zero climates.In many of these cultures, such names were traditionally given as protective names for children, intended to bestow the strength and endurance of the evergreen upon the bearer."
