Kamiko,f,"かみこ(Japanese Hiragana)|かみ子(Kanji/Hiragana)|カミ子(Kanji/Katakana)|紙子, 郁海子, 郁実子, 郁美子, 佳見子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-MEE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 紙 (kami) meaning ""paper"" or 郁 (ka) meaning ""fragrance, perfume"" and 海 (mi) meaning ""sea, ocean"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible.As a word, 紙衣 or 紙子 (kamiko) refers to Japanese paper clothes, which are a part of a crafting tradition that is rarely practiced in Japan today."
