Kamitsuhiko,m,カミツヒコ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese,KAH-MEE-TSOO-HEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 加密列 KAMITSURE (カミツレ), meaning CHAMOMILLE in japanese, an annual herbal plant very commonly used in both aesthetics and medicine from the botanical genus MATRICARIA, of the family of plants ASTERACEAE, of the botanical order ASTERALES. Also from 雷 KAMINARI, which means THUNDER, and the combination of the kanji 雷 KAMITSU, 光 HI and 子 KO, which they mean, respectively, THUNDER, LIGHT and CHILD. Literally means CHILD OF THE LIGHTNING THUNDER in japanese."
