Kamphon,m,"กัมพล, กำพล(Thai)",Thai,/kam˧.ˈpʰon˧/,,,,,,,"Spelled as กัมพล, it means ""wool, woolen"" in Thai, ultimately from Sanskrit कम्बल (kambala). It is taken from the name of the throne of Indra, called पाण्डुकम्बल (pāṇḍukambala), which is described as feeling as soft as wool.Spelled as กำพล, it is derived from Thai กำ (kam) meaning ""to grasp, to hold"" and พล (phon) meaning ""strength, power""."
