Kamrušipa,f,,Luwian|Luwian Mythology,/ˈkam.ru.ʃe.pa/(Luwian),,,,,,,"Means ""spirit of the clouds"" or ""spirit of smoke"" in Luwian. In Luwian Mythology, Kamrušipa was the wife of the sun god Tiwaz/Tiwad and the mother of the guardian god Runtiya, she is revered as a goddess of magic, medicine, and healing."
