Kanae,f,"かなえ, かなゑ(Japanese Hiragana)|カナエ(Japanese Katakana)|叶, 鼎, 奏愛, 愛惠, 叶詠, 嘉苗, 茄那慧, 伽那枝, 家名江, 郁南栄, 海南衣, 果菜笑, 架名映, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-NA-E,,,,,,,"Derived from the verb 叶える (kanaeru) meaning ""to come true"". It can be spelled with 愛 (kanae) meaning ""love, affection"" or the combination of 茄 (ka) meaning ""eggplant"", 那 (na) meaning ""what"", and 惠 (e) meaning ""blessed"". Other Kanji combinations are possible."
Kanafinwë,m,,Literature,,,,,,,,"Means ""strong-voiced Finwë"". In Tolkien's Legendarium this is the father-name of Maglor, Fëanor's second son and the foster father of Elrond and Elros. Unlike the rest of his brothers he is never reported to have died, but is said to wander the shores of Middle-earth in pain and regret for the crimes he committed in pursuit of the Silmarils."
