Karamatullah,m,كرامات الله(Arabic)|کرامت الله(Pashto)|کرامت‌الله(Persian),Arabic|Afghan|Pakistani,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from Arabic كرامات (karamat), which is the plural form of كرامة (karama) meaning ""dignity, generosity"" (compare Karam). Karamat is also a term in Sunni Islam, which refers to the miracles that were performed by Muslim saints. The second element of this name is derived from the Arabic noun الله (Allah) meaning ""God"" (see Allah)."
