Katsuaki,m,"嘉津彬, 活秋, 活彰, 捷明, 活璃, 捷彰, 克顕, 克秋, 克昌, 克明, 克亮, 雄晃, 勝章, 勝明, 勝朗, 捷昭, 雄章, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-AH-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 活 (katsu) meaning ""lively, alive"", 捷 (katsu) meaning ""quick, rapid, fast"", or 雄 (katsu) meaning ""hero, manly"" combined with 彰 (aki) meaning ""obvious, clear"", 璃 (aki) meaning ""glassy, lapis lazuli"", 顕 (aki) meaning ""visible, appear"", 亮 (aki) meaning ""clear, help"", 朗 (aki) meaning ""bright, clear"" or 彬 (aki) meaning ""refined, gentle"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsue,f,"かつえ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツエ(Japanese Katakana)|佳鶴栄, 佳津恵, 佳都枝, 佳律江, 加都江, 嘉津江, 活恵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 佳 (ka) meaning ""beautiful, good"", 鶴 (tsu) meaning ""crane"" combined with 栄 (e) meaning ""glory, honour"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuei,m,"勝栄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつえい(Japanese Hiragana)|カツエイ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.e̞ː/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, success"" and 栄 (ei) meaning ""glory, honour, flourish, prosper"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsufumi,m,"かつ ふみ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツ フミ(Japanese Katakana)|筈史⁠, 勝文, 勝史, 筈⁠文, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-FOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From 筈⁠ (katsu) meaning “notch, nock of a bow and arrow” combined with 文 (fumi) meaning ""writing"" or 史 (fumi) meaning ""history"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsufusa,m,"カツフサ(Japanese Katakana)|かつふさ(Japanese Hiragana)|筈総, 克房, 活成, 捷記, 雄総, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-FOO-SA,,,,,,,"From 筈 (katsu) meaning ""should be, ought, nock of a bow and arrow"" and 総 (fusa) meaning ""overall, general, total"". Other kanji combinations are permissible."
Katsugorō,m,勝五郎(Japanese Kanji)|かつごろう(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"", 五 (go) meaning ""five"", and 郎 (rō) as a masculine suffix meaning ""son"" or ""young man""."
Katsuhei,m,"勝平, 克平, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつへい(Japanese Hiragana)|カツヘイ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.he̞ː/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, success"" or 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome, win"" and 平 (hei) meaning ""level, even peaceful"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsuhide,m,"かつひで(Japanese Hiragana)|カツヒデ(Japanese Katakana)|克秀, 筈英, 勝偉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-KHEE-DE,,,,,,,"From 筈⁠ (katsu) meaning “notch of an arrow, nock” combined 英 (hide) meaning ""wisdom, brilliance"" or 秀 (hide) meaning ""excellent, outstanding"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsuhiko,m,"勝彦, 克彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-KHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 勝 (katsu) meaning ""excel, prevail, victory, win"" and combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy, prince"". Other kanji combinations can be used instead."
Katsuhira,m,,Japanese (Rare)|Popular Culture (Rare),Kah-tsu-heer-a(Japanese),,,,,,,"Katsu means ""Victory"" and Hira means ""Peace"". Katsuhira Agata is a fictional character from the Kiznaiver series. Katsuhira Tokushi, was a historical artist born in Akita Prefecture."
Katsuhiro,m,"勝浩, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-KHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" combined with 浩 (hiro) meaning ""prosperous"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuhisa,m,"かつひさ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツヒサ(Japanese Katakana)|勝久, 克久, 勝尚, 克尚, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-KHEE-SA,,,,,,,"From 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" and 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsuichi,m,"勝一, 克一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-EE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" or 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome"" combined with 一 (ichi, kazu) meaning ""one"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuichiro,m,,Japanese,KAH-TSOO-EE-CHEE-RO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Katsuichirou.
Katsuichirou,m,"勝一郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-EE-CHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"", 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsuie,m,"勝家, 克家, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KA-TSOO-EE-E,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""to overcome"" and 家 (ie) meaning ""family, house(hold)"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsuji,m,"勝治, 勝司, 勝次, 勝二, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつぢ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツヂ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.d͡ʑi/|/kät͡s.d͡ʑi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, success"" combined with 治 (ji) meaning ""govern, administer"", 司 (ji) meaning ""manage, control, officer"", 次 (ji) meaning ""order, sequence, next"" or 二 (ji) meaning ""two"". Other combinations of kanji can form this name as well."
Katsujiro,m,"家二郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-ZHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From 家 (katsu, ie, ya) meaning ""house, home, building, dwelling"" combined with 二 (ji) meaning ""two"" and 郎 (rō) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsujirou,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Katsujiro.
Katsukazu,m,"家紀, 雄紀, 捷紀, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-KAH-ZOO,,,,,,,"From 捷 (katsu) meaning ""quick, fast, rapid, victory, conquest, success"" or 家 (katsu) meaning ""house, home, building, dwelling"" combined with 紀 (kazu) meaning ""narrative, chronical, account"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsuki,m,"克樹, 勝樹, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつき(Japanese Hiragana)|カツキ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.kʲi/|/kät͡s.kʲi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome, win"" or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, success"" combined with 樹 (ki) meaning ""tree, plant"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Katsukiyo,m,勝人(Japanese Kanji),Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" combined with 人 (kiyo) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsumaru,m,"カツマル(Japanese Katakana)|かつまる(Japanese Hiragana)|優丸, 勝丸, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KAH-TSOO-MAH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 優 (katsu) meaning ""gentle, excellent, superior, surpass, kind"" combined with 円 (maru) meaning ""round, circle, tranquil"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsumasa,m,"克正, 克雅, 勝正, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-MAH-SAH,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome, kindly, skillfully"" or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, win, prevail, excel"" combined with 正 (masa) meaning ""right, proper"" or 雅 (masa) meaning ""elegant, graceful"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsumoto,m,且元(Japanese Kanji),Japanese|Popular Culture,,,,,,,,"From Japanese kanji 且 (katsu) meaning ""moreover; furthermore"" combined with 元 (moto) meaning ""cause; origin; foundation"".Katsumoto Katagiri (1556-1615) was a Japanese warlord daimyō in the Edo period.Lord Katsumoto Moritsugu is the fictional main character in the 2003 film 'The Last Samurai'."
Katsunaru,m,"勝徳, 優成, 克匠, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-NAH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 勝 (shou, ka.tsu, katsu, -ga.chi, sugu.reru, masa.ru) meaning ""excel, prevail, victory, win"" and combined with 徳 (naru, toku) meaning ""virtue"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsundo,m,"勝人, 克人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつんど(Japanese Hiragana)|カツンド(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[kà.t͡sɨ̃́ᵝǹ.dò̞],,,,,,,Shift from Katsuhito.This name is very rarely used.
Katsuni,m,"勝仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSUU-NEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""wins, victories"" combined with 仁 (ni) meaning ""benevolence"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsunobu,m,"勝信, 勝延, 克信, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-NO-BOO,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome"", 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, triumph"", 和 (katsu, wa, kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 雄 (katsu, o) meaning ""hero, manly"", combined with 信 (nobu) meaning ""trust"", 延 or 伸 (nobu) meaning ""prolong, stretch, extend"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsunori,m,"克法, 活法, 勝法, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-NO-REE,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome"", 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, triumph"", 和 (katsu, wa, kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 雄 (katsu, o) meaning ""hero, manly"", combined 儀 (nori) meaning ""ceremony, rites"", 憲 (nori) meaning ""law"", 紀 (nori) meaning ""chronicle"", 典 (nori) meaning ""rule, ceremony"", or 法 (nori) meaning ""law, act, method""."
Katsunosuke,m,"勝之祐, 勝之介, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつのすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツノスケ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.no̞.sɨᵝ.ke̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" combined with 之 (no) a possesive marker, and 祐 (suke) meaning ""divine intervention, protection"" or 介 (suke) meaning ""help, assist"". Other Kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsuomi,m,"かつおみ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツオミ(Japanese Katakana)|一臣, 恰臣, 雄臣, 桂臣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-O-MEE,,,,,,,"From 割 (katsu) meaning ""proportion, cut, divide"" combined with 臣 (omi) meaning ""subject, vassal"". Other kanji combinations can be used to spell this name."
Katsura,,"桂, 葛(Japanese Kanji)|かつら(Japanese Hiragana)|カツラ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),KAH-TSUU-ṘAH,,,,,,,"This name is used as 桂 (kei, katsura) meaning ""Japanese Judas-tree"" (unisex) or 葛 (kachi, katsu, kuzu, tsudzura, katsura) meaning ""arrowroot, kudzu"" (feminine).桂 originally came about from a compound of 香 (ka) meaning ""(good) smell, fragrance, scent,"" 出 (zu), a contraction of now obsolete 出ず (izu) meaning ""to go out"" (出る/deru in modern Japanese), and ら, which is a nominalising and pluralising suffix, reflecting the good smell of the wood.Katsura is also used as a surname.This name is rarely given to children, if given at all."
Katsurako,f,"カツラコ(Japanese Katakana)|桂子, 葛子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KAH-TSUU-ṘAH-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 桂 (katsura) meaning ""the katsura, the Japanese Judas tree"" or 葛 (katsura) meaning ""arrowroot, kudzu"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsurao,m,"桂男, 桂夫, 桂雄, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSUU-ṘAH-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 桂 (katsura) meaning ""the katsura, the Japanese Judas tree"" combined with 男 (o) meaning ""male"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsushi,m,"かつし(Japanese Hiragana)|カツシ(Japanese Katakana)|活志, 且史, 豪至, 健氏, 葛次, 括嗣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 褐 (katsu) meaning ""brown, coarse wool fabric"" or 渇 (katsu) meaning ""to parch, to resect, to dry up"" combined with 氏 (shi) meaning ""family, clan"" or 嗣 (shi) meaning ""to inherit, to take over position, to succeed"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsushiro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Katsushirou,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Katsuichiro.
Katsusuke,m,"克輔, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-SKE:,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome, kindly, skillfully"" or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, win, prevail, excel"" combined with 輔 (suke) meaning ""help"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsutada,m,"かつただ(Japanese Hiragana)|カツタダ(Japanese Katakana)|割但, 克曽, 且惟, 捷紀, 括伊, 一正, 雄真, 褐唯, 桂直, 越匡, 勝曾, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-TA-DA,,,,,,,"From 活 (katsu) meaning ""life"" and 祇 (tada) meaning ""peaceful, great, local or national god"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsutaka,m,"克孝, 雄天, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-TAH-KAH,,,,,,,"From 雄 (katsu) meaning ""male, someone or something excellent"" combined with 天 (taka) meaning ""heavens, sky"". Other combinations of kanji can be used."
Katsutaro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Katsutarou,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Katsutaro.
Katsuteru,m,"家照, 勝照, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-TEH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 家 (katsu) meaning ""house, one's own home"" and 照 (teru) meaning ""to shine"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Katsuto,m,"家任, 勝任, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-TO,,,,,,,"From 家 (katsu, ie, ya) meaning ""house, home, building, dwelling"" combined with 任 (to) meaning ""responsibility, duty, to entrust"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsutoshi,m,"勝敏, 勝利, 勝俊, 克俊, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-TO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 克 (katsu) meaning ""to overcome"" combined with 利 (toshi) meaning ""advantage, benefit"". Other combinations of kanji are possible."
Katsutsugu,m,"克嗣, 活嗣, 勝次, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-TSOO-GOO,,,,,,,"From 活 (katsu) meaning ""life"", 克 (katsu) meaning ""to overcome, to subdue"", or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" combined with 嗣 (tsugu, tsuguru) meaning ""descendants, heirs"" or 次 (tsugu, tsuguru) meaning ""next, secondary"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuyo,f,"かつよ(Japanese Hiragana)|勝代, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-YO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome"" or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" combined with 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" or 世 (yo) meaning ""world"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuyori,m,"筈誉利⁠, 筈頼⁠, 勝頼, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-YO-REE,,,,,,,"From 筈⁠ (kachi, katsu, yahazu, hazu) meaning “notch of an arrow, nock” combined with 誉 (yo) meaning ""reputation, honor, glory"" and 利 (ri) meaning ""profit, advantage, benefit"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Katsuyoshi,m,"健仁, 勝祥, 健良, 勝義, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-TSOO-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 健 (katsu) meaning ""healthy, strength, strong, robust"" combined with 吉 (yoshi) meaning ""fortune, good luck"", 仁 (yoshi) meaning ""benevolence"", or 祥 (yoshi) meaning ""good sign, auspicious omen, happiness"". This name can be formed from other kanji combinations as well."
Katsuyuki,m,"克幸, 克行, 勝幸, 勝之, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かつゆき(Japanese Hiragana)|カツユキ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.t͡sɨᵝ.jɨᵝ.kʲi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome, win"" or 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory, success"" combined with 幸 (yuki) meaning ""happiness, good luck"", 行 (yuki) meaning ""row, line"" or 之 (yuki), a possessive marker. Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Katsuzo,m,"かつぞう(Japanese Hiragana)|カツゾウ(Japanese Katakana)|雄蔵, 克三, 勝造, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-ZO,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Katsuzou.
Katsuzou,m,"かつぞう(Japanese Hiragana)|カツゾウ(Japanese Katakana)|勝三, 克蔵, 雄造, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-TSOO-ZO,,,,,,,"From 勝 (katsu) meaning ""victory"" or 克 (katsu) meaning ""overcome skillfully, kindly"", with 蔵 (zou) meaning ""own, possess, storehouse,"" or 三 (zou) meaning ""three"" or 造 (zou) meaning ""create, build."" Other kanji are possible."
Katsy,f,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,"Diminutive of Katherine, Kathleen, Katrina and other names beginning with Kat- or Kath-."
Katt,f,,English,KAT,,,,,,,Variant of Cat.
Kattaḫḫa,f,,Hittite Mythology|Hattian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Likely deriving from the Hattic word kattaḫ (""queen""), this theonym was applied to several goddesses, the most prominent of whom was the tutelary goddess of the city of Ankuwa. She is listed alongside other 'queen goddesses' in treaties, such as Ḫuwaššanna."
