Kättilger,m,,Old Swedish,,,,,,,,"Old Swedish combination of ketill ""cauldron hat"", ""helmet"" and geirr ""spear""."
Kättilö,f,,Old Swedish,,,,,,,,"Old Swedish form of Kætiløy, composed of Old Norse ketill ""kettle, cauldron"" and ey ""island""."
Kattin,f,,Basque,/ka.ˈcin/,,,,,,,Diminutive of Katalin and Kattalin.
Kattis,f,,Swedish,/ˈkat.ɪs/,,,,,,,Diminutive of Katarina and its variants.
Kattleya,f,,German,/ˈkæt.liə/,,,,,,,Derived from: Cattleya (/ˈkætliə/) is a genus of orchids from Costa Rica south to Argentina.
