Kattyria,f,,American (Hispanic),,,,,,,,Variant of Katiria.
Káťulka,f,,Czech,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Kateřina.
Katuma,m,,Luba,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Luba word kàtùmà meaning ""last-born of triplets"", ultimately from the word tùmà meaning ""to send"". Superstition suggests that third-born children with this name, because of their name, should not be sent on errands or deliveries."
Katumaros,m,,Gaulish,,,,,,,,"Derived from Proto-Celtic *katus ""battle"" and *māros ""great""."
Katumin,f,,Mormon,,,,,,,,"In LDS history, Joseph Smith received a bunch of old Egyptian scrolls. The Book of Abraham was translated from them, and fragments of a few other books were translated. One such fragment told of Princess Katumin, who was a daughter of Pharaoh Onitas."
Ka-tung,m,"家棟, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese (Cantonese),/kaː.tʊŋ/(Cantonese),,,,,,,Cantonese romanisation of Jiadong.
Katupyry,m,,Guarani,,,,,,,,"Means ""skillful"" in Guarani."
Katurah,f,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Variant of Keturah.
Katuri,m,,Aymara,,,,,,,,"Means ""hunter"" in Aymara."
Katuša,f,,Czech|Slovak,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Kateřina (Czech) and Katarína (Slovak). Also compare Katuška.
