Kazu,,"数, 和, 計, 知, 一, 二, 五, 佳寿, 嘉寿, 花寿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かず(Japanese Hiragana)|カズ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,[ká.zɨ̀ᵝ],,,,,,,"From 数 (kazu) meaning ""number, amount."" Other kanji used in relation include 和 meaning ""sum,"" 計 meaning ""measurement, weighing,"" 知 meaning ""wisdom"" or any kanji referring to numbers, such as 一 meaning ""one,"" 二 meaning ""two"" or 五 meaning ""five."" It can also be written as a combination of a ka kanji, like 佳 meaning ""beautiful, good,"" 嘉 meaning ""praise, esteem"" or 花 meaning ""flower,"" and a zu kanji, e.g. 寿 meaning ""congratulations; longevity.""It is also used as a short form of names that begin with Kazu-, such as Kazuya or Kazuko."
Kazuaki,m,"和明, 和昭, 一昭, 一晃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かずあき(Japanese Hiragana)|カズアキ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.zɨᵝ.ä.kʲi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 明 (aki) meaning ""bright, light, clear"", 昭 (aki) meaning ""bright, luminous"" or 晃 (aki) meaning ""bright, clear"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Kazuakira,m,"和明, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,kah-zuu-ah-kee-ṙah  ,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" combined with 明 (akira) meaning ""bright"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazuchika,m,"かずちか(Japanese Hiragana)|カズチカ(Japanese Katakana)|和睦, 一親, 数悠, 計愛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-CHEE-KA,,,,,,,"From 和 (kazu) meaning ""serenity, tranquility, Japan, peace, harmony"" combined with 哉 (chika) meaning ""exclamation"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazufumi,m,"数郁, 寿生充, 量甫巳, 法輔果, 三豊彌, 楓実憲, 十歩生, 重二質, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-FOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From 麗 (kazu) meaning ""lovely, graceful, beautiful, resplendent"", 春 (kazu) meaning ""spring"", 万 (kazu) meaning ""hundred"" or 嘉 (kazu) meaning ""auspicious, praise"" combined with 典 (fumi) meaning ""ceremony, rites"" or 章 (fumi) meaning ""section, chapter"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazuha,,"かずは(Japanese Hiragana)|カズハ(Japanese Katakana)|壱生, 寿春, 数芭, 万波, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-HA,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine name derived from 冬 (kazu) meaning ""winter"" and 葉 (ha) meaning ""blade, leaf"" or 杷 (ha) meaning ""loquat, rake"". Other kanji combinations can be used to spell this name."
Kazuharu,m,"計榛, 壱遥, 知青, 数暖, 千晴, 寿春, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-HA-ROO,,,,,,,"From 計 (kazoeru, kei, kai) meaning ""plan, total, -meter (measuring device)"", 壱 (kazu, ichi) meaning ""number one"", or 知 (kazu, chi, tomo) meaning ""wisdom"" combined with 春 (haru, shun) meaning ""spring"", 榛 (haru, hari, saibari) meaning ""Asian hazel"", 遥 (haru, haruka) meaning ""distant, remote, far away"". Other kanji combinations can be used instead."
Kazuhide,m,"量偉, 二任, 知栄, 数成, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-KHEE-DE,,,,,,,"From 五 (kazu) meaning ""five"" combined with 豪 (hide) meaning ""bold, magnificent, Australia"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuhira,m,"一平, 和平, 数平(Japanese Kanji)|かずひら(Japanese Hiragana)|カズヒラ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),KAH-ZUU-HEE-ṘAH|KAH-DZUU-HEE-ṘAH,,,,,,,"This name combines 一 (ichi, itsu, hito-, hito.tsu, kazu) meaning ""one,"" 和 (o, ka, wa, nago.mu, nago.yaka, yawa.ragu, yawa.rageru, kazu) meaning ""harmony, Japanese style, peace, soften"" or 数 (saku, shu, su, suu, soku, kazu, kazo.eru, shibashiba, se.meru, wazurawa.shii) meaning ""figure, number, count"" with 平 (hyou, byou, hei, tai.ra, -daira, hira, hira-) meaning ""plain, flat, even, level.""This name is rarely given to boys, if given at all."
Kazuhiro,m,"和弘, 和博, 和宏, 和浩, 一弘, 一博, 一宏, 一浩, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かずひろ(Japanese Hiragana)|カズヒロ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.zɨᵝ.çi.ɾo̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 弘 (hiro) meaning ""enlarge, expand, great"", 博 (hiro) meaning ""command, esteem"", 宏 (hiro) meaning ""wide, spacious, great, vast"" or 浩 (hiro) meaning ""prosperous"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Kazuhisa,m,"一久, 和久, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-KHEE-SAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" or 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" combined with 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time ago"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kazuhito,m,"和仁, 数仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-KHEE-TO,,,,,,,"From 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" and 仁 (hito) meaning ""benevolence"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuho,,"カズホ(Japanese Katakana)|かずほ(Japanese Hiragana)|一星, 寿穂, 壱保, 歌寿帆, 数歩, 多穂, 和布, 和穗, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-HO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 多 (kazu) meaning ""much, many"" combined with 穗 or 穂 (ho) meaning ""ear of grain"" or 星 (ho) meaning ""star, dot"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazuhoshi,m,"一星, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZUU-HO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 星 (hoshi) meaning ""star"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazuichi,m,"かずいち(Japanese Hiragana)|一壱, 計一, 寿一, 数市, 和以智, 和壱, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-EE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" combined with 市 (ichi) meaning ""market"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazuichirou,m,"かずいちろう(Japanese Hiragana)|カズイチロウ(Japanese Katakana)|量一朗, 主一良, 和市郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KA-ZOO-EE-CHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"", 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Kazuka,f,"かずか(Japanese Hiragana)|一嘉, 寿日, 数花, 春香, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 嘉 (ka) meaning ""excellent, good"". This name can be formed of other kanji characters as well."
Kazuke,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kazumasa,m,"数正, 和正, 和昌, 和政, 一眞, 一正, 一将, 一存, 一政, 員昌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-MAH-SAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" or 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" combined with 正 (masa) meaning ""just, right, correct, proper"" or 政 (masa) meaning ""government"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kazumichi,m,"和路, 一 倫, 和皆, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-MEE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace, even, level"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 路 (michi) meaning ""road"", 倫 (michi) meaning ""morals, ethics"", or 皆 (michi) meaning ""all, everything"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazumitsu,m,"和光, 一光, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-MEE-TSOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace, even, level"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 光 (mitsu) meaning ""light""."
Kazuna,f,"かずな(Japanese Hiragana)|一夏, 一菜, 一那, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" and 那 (na) meaning ""that, that one"" or 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens"", as well as other character combinations."
Kazunari,m,"一成, 一也, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZUU-NAH-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 成 (nari) meaning ""to become"" or 也 (nari) meaning ""also"". Other combinations of kanji characters are possible.Famous bearers of this name are Japanese football player of Korean descent Kazunari Okayama (Kang Il-Sung) and Japanese Nippon Professional Baseball player Kazunari Sanematsu."
Kazune,,"和音, 一音, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-NE,,,,,,,"From 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace, harmony"" and 音 (ne) meaning ""sound, echo"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazunobu,m,"和伸, 和延, 一信, 員信, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かずのぶ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/käh.zɨᵝ.no̞.bɯᵝ/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"", 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" or 員 (kazu) meaning ""member"" combined with 伸 (nobu) meaning ""extend, stretch, open"", 延 (nobu) meaning ""prolong, stretch"" or 信 (nobu) meaning ""trust"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazunori,m,"壱憲, 壱典, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-NO-REE,,,,,,,"From 計 (kazoeru, kei, kai) meaning ""plan, total, -meter (measuring device)"", 壱 (kazu, ichi) meaning ""number one"", or 知 (kazu, chi, tomo) meaning ""wisdom"" combined with 儀 (nori) meaning ""ceremony, rites"", 憲 (nori) meaning ""law"" or 典 (nori) meaning ""rule, ceremony"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuomi,m,"数臣, 和臣, 一 臣, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-OH-MEE,,,,,,,"From 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"", 数 (kazu) meaning ""number, amount"", or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 臣 (omi) meaning ""one who serves a lord; a vassal, subject"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazurakinotakanukahime,f,葛城高顙媛(Japanese Kanji),Japanese Mythology,,,,,,,,"In Japanese mythology, this is the name of the mother of Empress Jingū and the descendant of Amenohiboko. Her name is derived from 葛 (kazura) meaning ""creeping plant"", 城 (ki) meaning ""castle, fort"", 高 (taka) meaning ""high, higher, maximum"", 顙 (nuka) meaning ""forehead, to bow"" and 媛 (hime) meaning ""princess""."
Kazurō,m,"かずろ(Japanese Hiragana)|カズロ(Japanese Katakana)|和郎, 和朗, 一郎, 一朗, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace, harmony"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"" or 朗 (rou) meaning ""bright, clear"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name.A famous bearer of this name is Japanese astronomer, Kazuro Watanabe (1955-)."
Kazusa,,"一沙, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-SA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 沙 (sa) meaning ""sand"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazushi,m,"和司, 和志, 一志(Japanese Kanji)|かずし(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From the Japanese kanji 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace; harmony"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one; wholly"" combined with 司 (shi) meaning ""boss"" or 志 (shi) meaning ""purpose, will, ambition"".Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazushige,m,"和繁, 和成, 一重, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-SHEE-GEH,,,,,,,"From 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace, harmony, Japan"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 繁 (shige) meaning ""flourishing, luxuriant""."
Kazusuke,m,"一右, 一介, 一助, 一典, 一輔, 一祐, 和佐, 和輔, 和亮, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZUU-SKE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 右 (suke) meaning ""(direction) the right"", 介 (suke) meaning ""shell, shellfish"", 助 (kazu) meaning ""assistance"", 典 (suke) meaning ""ceremony, rule"", 輔 (suke) meaning ""help"" or 祐 (suke) meaning ""divine intervention, protection"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazutaka,m,"かずたか(Japanese Hiragana)|カズタカ(Japanese Katakana)|一峻, 数宇, 嘉孝, 和隆, 一剛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-TA-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 嘉 (kazu) meaning ""praise, auspicious"" combined with 剛 (taka) meaning ""sturdy"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazutami,m,,Japanese,KAH-ZOO-TAH-MEE,,,,,,,"Kazu can mean ""one"" or ""peace, harmony"" and tami means ""people, citizens, civil, nationals""."
Kazuteru,m,"和光, 法輝, 一瑛, 一耀, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-TEH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 法 (kazu) meaning ""method, law, regulation, model"" or 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace"" combined with 光 (teru) meaning ""light, radiance"" or 照 (teru) meaning ""to shine"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuto,m,"一人, 和人(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Japanese kanji 一 (read kazu instead of ichi or hito) meaning ""one"" or 和 (kazu) meaning ""peace"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person, individual"".Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kazutomo,m,"一朋, 和朋, 和知, 和智, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かずとも(Japanese Hiragana)|カズトモ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.zɨᵝ.to̞.mo̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" or 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" combined with 朋 (tomo) meaning ""friend"", 知 (tomo) meaning ""know, perceive, comprehend"" or 智 (tomo) meaning ""wisdom, intellect"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Kazutoshi,m,"寿俊, 和年, 和俊, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KAH-ZOO-TO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 和 (kazu) meaning ""Japan, peace, harmony"" or 寿 (kazu) meaning ""longevity, congratulations, long life"" combined with 年 (toshi) meaning ""years"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuyasu,m,"かずやす(Japanese Hiragana)|カズヤス(Japanese Katakana)|一泰, 数康, 一靖, 和恭, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-YA-SOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 安 (yasu) meaning ""calm, peaceful"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Kazuyasu Minobe (born 1987), a Japanese male épée fencer, a bronze medalist at the 2015 and 2016 Asian Championships."
Kazuyo,f,"和世, 和代, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KA-ZOO-YO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 世 (yo) meaning ""generation"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kazuyoshi,m,"和義, 和良, 和佳, 一義, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|かずよし(Japanese Hiragana)|カズヨシ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kä.zɨᵝ.jo̞.ɕi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 和 (kazu) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu) meaning ""one"" combined with 義 (yoshi) meaning ""justice, righteousness"", 良 (yoshi) meaning ""good, virtuous, respectable"" or 佳 (yoshi) meaning ""good, auspicious, beautiful"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
