Keaundra,f,,English,,,,,,,,"Keaundra is a feminine name of American creation that can have a variety of roots and meanings. It can serve as a variant of Kiana 1, which is the Hawaiian variant of Diana, meaning “divine,” and “goddess-like.” If you want to give baby a celestial name to match their angel-like spirit, Keaundra can make for a great choice. Keaundra may also come from the Old Irish name Cian‎, meaning “lasting” or “ancient”—a perfect choice to match your little one’s old soul. For an extra touch, Keaundra can also be a fun spin on the Welsh and Old English name Kendrick, with meanings ranging from “royal power” to “chief hero.” With the name Keaundra, your little majesty is sure to know that they’re destined for greatness."
