Kefira,f,,English (Rare)|Various (Rare),,,,,,,,"Meaning uncertain, possibly a variant of Chephirah, the name of a biblical town derived from Hebrew כפר (kapar) ""village"". Alternatively it might be intended to mean ""young lioness"" from the feminine form of Biblical Hebrew כְּפִיר (kephir) ""young lion""; compare the modern Hebrew masculine name Kfir.It does not appear to be used as a name by Hebrew speakers, perhaps because it also coincides with a word meaning ""denial (of God), heresy, atheism""."
