Keigo,m,"慶悟, 圭吾, 景瑚, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese|Japanese,KE-GO|KEY-A-GO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 慶 (kei) meaning ""celebrate"", 敬 (kei) meaning ""respect"", 啓 (kei) meaning ""open, begin"" or 恵 (kei) meaning ""favour, benefit"" combined with 悟 (go) meaning ""enlightenment, to apprehend, realize, become aware"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Keigo Higashi, a Japanese footballer (1990-)."
