Keiichi,m,"圭一, 敬一, 恵一, 啓一, 慶一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|けいいち(Japanese Hiragana)|ケイイチ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ke̞ː.i.t͡ɕi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 圭 (kei) meaning ""gemstone"", 敬 (kei) meaning ""respect, honour"", 恵 (kei) meaning ""favour, benefit"", 啓 (kei) meaning ""open, begin"" or 慶 (kei) meaning ""congratulate, celebrate, celebration"" combined with 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Keiichiro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Keiichirou.
Keiichirou,m,"けい いちろう(Japanese Hiragana)|ケイイチロウ(Japanese Katakana)|経壱朗, 形一鷺, 馨一郎, 圭壱朗, 契逸炉, 系一櫓, 慧溢郎, 敬市諒, 渓一郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KE-EE-CHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 佳 (kei) meaning ""good"", 一 (ichi) meaning ""one"" and 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer is Keiichiro Koyama (1984-), a Japanese musician and leader of the Johnny's Entertainment group NEWS."
