Kesao,m,"今朝雄, 今朝男, 今朝夫, 袈裟雄, 袈裟男, 袈裟夫(Japanese Kanji)|けさお(Japanese Hiragana)|ケサオ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,KE-SAH-O,,,,,,,"This name combines 今朝 or 袈裟 (kesa) (see Kesa) with 雄 (yuu, o-, osu, on) meaning ""male, masculine,"" 男 (dan, nan, o, otoko) meaning ""man, male"" or 夫 (fu, fuu, bu, otto, sore, o) meaning ""husband, man.""This name was occasionally used from the Meiji period (1868-1912) to the first half of the 20th century but nowadays, it is rarely given to boys, if given at all."
