Ketboga,m,,Medieval Turkic,Ketbogha,,,,,,,"Ketboga/Ketboğa is actually composed of two words Ket and Boğa. First one is Ket-/Kıt- verb which means ""conquering, defeating"" and Boga/Boğa is clearly Turco-Mongol word for ""bull"". There are two famous governor and general in history. One is famous Hulagu Khan's general -Noyan in Mongol- Ketboga Noyan other is Al Adil Kitbugha. Pronunciation varies from culture to culture but the etymology is same."
