Kethlenda,f,,Irish Mythology|Literature,,,,,,,,"""Kethlenda"" is an anglicized spelling of the Old Irish name Cethlenn (or Ceithlenn). In Irish mythology, she is a powerful prophetess, a Fomorian queen, and the wife of Balor of the Evil Eye.Kethlenda is the form of the name that appeared in Roderick O'Flaherty's Ogygia or Rerum Hibernicarum Chronologia, written in Latin, reused as ""Kethlenda of the Crooked Teeth"" by story-reteller P. W. Joyce, and more."
