Khaemwaset,m,𓈍𓅓𓌀𓏏𓊖(Hieroglyphs),Ancient Egyptian,KHAYM-wah-set,,,,,,,"From Egyptian ḫꜥ-m-wꜣst meaning ""he who appears in Thebes"", derived from ḫꜥ ""to rise, appear, shine forth"", m ""in"", and wꜣst ""Thebes (city)"". This was the name of several figures in Egyptian history, including a 19th dynasty prince, the fourth son of Ramses the Great. Khaemwaset later took on the name Setne."
