Kheildar,m,خیلدار(Persian),Persian,kheyldaar,,,,,,,"origin of the surname Kheildar (phonetically Xeyldaar) is of Persian origin and is specifically associated with the northern area near Kordan, north of Karag, and West of Tehran, capital of Iran. The name is a compound word: Kheil (خيل) means a group of people, clan, or tribe, and dar (دار) is a suffix meaning owner, keeper, or master. Therefore, Kheildar translates directly to ""Owner/Leader of a Clan or Group of People"" and primarily functions as a last name, likely originating as a status title for a leader in that region of Northern Iran."
