Kiều,,,Vietnamese|Literature,/kiəw˨˩/(Vietnamese)|/kiw˦˩/(Vietnamese)|/kiw˨˩/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 嬌 (kiều) meaning ""seductive, spoiled, loveable"", 喬 (kiều) meaning ""tall, lofty"", or 翹 (kiều) meaning ""bird tail, outstanding, extraordinary"". This is the name of the main character Vương Thúy Kiều (王翠翘) in the epic poem Đoạn Trường Tân Thanh, better known as Truyện Kiều (The Tale of Kiều), by Nguyễn Du."
