Kikka,f,"きっか(Japanese Hiragana)|菊花, 杏香, 喜花, 貴都嘩, 桔花, 桔椛, 橘花, 橘香, 姫華, 希花, 希華, 生翔, 祈花, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese|Finnish,keek̚-kah|KIK-kah,,,,,,,"This name can be used as 菊花 (kikka) meaning ""chrysanthemum flower"". It can also be used as 杏 (ki) meaning ""apricot"", 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 貴 (ki) meaning ""valuable"", 桔 (ki), used in plant names, 橘 (ki) meaning ""mandarin orange"", 姫 (ki) meaning ""princess"", 希 (ki) meaning ""hope, beg, request, rare"", 生 (ki) meaning ""life, genuine, birth"" or 祈 (ki) meaning ""pray, wish"", 都 (k) meaning ""metropolis, capital, all, everything"" combined with 香 (ka) meaning ""fragrance"", 花 (ka) or 華 (ka) both meaning ""flower"", 嘩 (ka) meaning ""noisy"", 椛 (ka) meaning ""autumn foliage, birch, maple, (kokuji)"" or 翔 (ka) meaning ""soar, fly"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
