Kikokiko,m,,Moriori|Polynesian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""malevolent; carnivore"" in Maori, and Moriori. This is the name of a Moriori god who is mentioned in one of the traditional Moriori migration stories."
Kikorangi,,,Māori,kee-ko-rang-ee,,,,,,,"Means ""light blue, sky blue"" in Māori. Similar to Kahurangi. Kikorangi refers to kiko ""body, flesh"" of Rangi, sky god whose body is the blue sky."
