Kikuji,m,"喜久治, 菊二, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きくじ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/kʲi.kɯᵝ.ʑi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""joy, delight, pleasure"", 久 (ku) meaning ""long time"" and 治 (ji) meaning ""govern, regulate, administer"". It can also be formed from 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" and 二 (ji) meaning ""two"", as well as other kanji combinations."
Kikuka,f,"キクカ(Japanese Katakana)|きくか(Japanese Hiragana)|喜久香, 掬花, 掬華, 菊香, 暉久佳, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 久 (ku) meaning ""long time"" combined with 香 (ka) meaning ""fragrance"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kikuko,f,"喜久子, 菊子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きくこ(Japanese Hiragana)|キクコ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kʲi.kɯᵝ.ko̞/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""joy, rejoice"" and 久 (ku) meaning ""long time ago"" or 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other combinations of kanji can form this name as well."
Kikumi,f,"喜久美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きく実, きく水(Kanji/Hiragana)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 久 (ku) meaning ""long time"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are possible as well."
Kikuna,f,"キクナ(Japanese Katakana)|きくな(Japanese Hiragana)|菊菜, 菊奈, 希紅名, 希久奈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-KOO-NA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" combined with 菜 (na) meaning ""vegetables, greens "" or 奈 (na) meaning ""Nara, what?, apple tree"". Other kanji combinations are possible. As a word, 菊菜 (kikuna) means ""edible chrysanthemum, Chrysanthemum coronarium, crown daisy, garland chrysanthemum, Glebionis coronaria""."
Kikunana,f,"菊七, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KUU-NAH-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" combined with 七 (nana) meaning ""seven"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kikune,f,"きくね(Japanese Hiragana)|キクネ(Japanese Katakana)|菊禰, 菊寧, 菊根, 菊音, 菊眠, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-KOO-NE,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine given name derived from 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" and 禰 (ne) meaning ""ancestral shrine"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kikuno,f,"きくの(Japanese Hiragana)|キクノ(Japanese Katakana)|菊乃, 鞠野, 掬野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 鞠 (kiku) meaning ""ball"" or 掬 (kiku) meaning ""to scoop water up with hands"" combined with 野 (no) meaning ""field, plain"" or 乃 (no) meaning ""of"". Other Kanji combinations are possible."
Kikunori,m,"菊典, 菊憲, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-NO-REE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" combined with 典 (nori) meaning ""rule, ceremony"" or 憲 (nori) meaning ""law"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kikunosuke,m,"菊之助, 菊之介, 菊之輔, 喜久之助, 喜久之介, 喜久之輔(Japanese Kanji)|きくのすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|キクノスケ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),k-kuu-no-ske|KEE-KUU-NO-SKE,,,,,,,"This name combines 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" or 喜 (ki, yoroko.basu, yoroko.bu) meaning ""rejoice, pleasure"" & 久 (kyuu, ku, hisa.shii) meaning ""long time"" and 之 (shi, oite, kono, kore, no, yuku) meaning ""of, this"" with 助 (jo, suke, su.keru, tasu.karu, tasu.keru) meaning ""assist, help, save, rescue,"" 介 (kai, suke) meaning ""concern oneself with, jammed in, mediate, help, care"" or 輔 (fu, ho, tasu.keru, suke) meaning ""help.""One bearer of this name is kabuki actor, Kikunosuke Onoe V (五代目 尾上 菊之助) (1977-), born Kazuyasu Terashima (寺嶋 和康).This name is very rarely used on boys, if given at all."
Kikuo,m,"きくお(Japanese Hiragana)|キクオ(Japanese Katakana)|技寿夫, 規矩雄, 規欧男, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-O,,,,,,,"From Japanese 技 (ki) meaning ""skill"", 駈 (ku) meaning ""run, gallop"" combined with 夫 (o) meaning ""man, husband."" Other kanji combinations are possible.A famous bearer of this name is Japanese professional golfer Kikuo Arai (1943-)."
Kikuša,f,,Slovak,,,,,,,,Slovak diminutive of Kristína. Also compare Kikuška.
