Kikuto,m,"きくと(Japanese Hiragana)|キクト(Japanese Katakana)|掬人, 菊人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-KOO-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kikuya,f,"きくや(Japanese Hiragana)|菊弥, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-KOO-YA,,,,,,,"Derived from the Japanese kanji 菊 (kiku) meaning ""chrysanthemum flower"" combined with 弥 (ya) meaning ""widely, increasingly, more and more, for a long time"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
