Kimiaki,m,"きみあき(Japanese Hiragana)|キミアキ(Japanese Katakana)|王朗, 王聡, 君晶, 君彰, 君秋, 君璃, 公顕, 公照, 公章, 公朗, 仁晃, 仁前, 仁成, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-A-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 王 (kimi) meaning ""king, rule, magnate"" or 君 (kimi) meaning ""mister, you, ruler, male name suffix"" combined with 彰 (aki) meaning ""clear, obvious"", 章 (aki) meaning ""badge, chapter, section"", 顕 (aki) meaning ""appear, visible"", 照 (aki) meaning ""illuminate, shine, compare, sunlight"", or 亮 (aki) meaning ""clear, bright, help"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
