Kimihiko,m,"君彦, 公彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-KHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""lord, noble"" or 公 (kimi) meaning ""prince"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""prince"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
