Kimihisa,m,"君尚, 君久, 君寿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-KHEE-SAH,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""mister, you, ruler, male name suffix"", 公 (kimi) meaning ""public, prince, official, governmental"" combined with 久 (hisa) meaning ""long time, long time ago"", 尚 (hisa) meaning ""still, yet, furthermore"", or 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kimihito,m,"公史, 公一, 君人, 公仁, 竜人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-KHEE-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 竜 (kimi) meaning ""dragon"" combined with 人 (hito) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kimika,f,"君香, 公佳, 后華, 喜美香, 季美花, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きみ佳, etc.(Kanji/Hiragana)|きみか(Japanese Hiragana)|キミカ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[kʲí.mʲì.kàh],,,,,,,"From Kimi combined with a ka kanji, like 香 meaning ""fragrance,"" 佳 meaning ""beautiful, good"" or 花/華 meaning ""flower."""
