Kimishige,m,"仁重, 君重, 公成, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-SHEE-GE,,,,,,,"From 仁 (kimi) meaning ""benevolence"" or 君 (kimi) meaning ""you, thou, nobleman, lord, ruler, master"" combined with 茂 (shige) meaning ""lush, luxuriant"" or 重 (shige) meaning ""layers, folds"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kimisuke,m,"きみすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|キミスケ(Japanese Katakana)|仁祐, 王右, 公介, 主助, 貴美輔, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-SKE,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""lord, noble"" combined with 亮 (suke) meaning ""help, clear"". Other kanji combinations are permissible."
Kimitada,m,"公忠, 公唯, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-TAH-DAH,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""lord, noble"" or 公 (kimi) meaning ""public, official, government"", combined with 唯 (tada) meaning ""just, only, simply"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kimito,m,"君人, 公人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 君 or 公 (kimi) meaning ""lord"" combined with 人 (to) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations can also make up this name."
Kimitsugu,m,"君次, 公禎, 君亜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-TSOO-GOO,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""lord, noble"" or 公 (kimi) meaning ""public, official, government"", combined with 禎 (tsugu) meaning ""divine grace, auspicious, straightforward"", meaning 亜 (a, tsugu) meaning “second, Asia, sub-”, or 次 (ji, tsugu) meaning ""next"". Other kanji conbinations are possible."
Kimitsuna,m,"きみつな(Japanese Hiragana)|キミツナ(Japanese Katakana)|皇繋, 王綱, 君維, 仁絆, 竜繋, 乾綱, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-MEE-TSOO-NA,,,,,,,"From 乾 (kimi) meaning ""emperor, paradise, northeast"" combined with 維 (tsuna) meaning ""to tie, to fasten up"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kimiya,f,"کیمیا(Persian)|キミヤ(Japanese Katakana)|公哉, 君也, 貴美弥, 樹見哉, 亀美也, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Persian|Kongo|Japanese,/kʰʲiː.mi.ˈjɒː/|KEE-MEE-YA,,,,,,,"Means ""alchemy, elixir of life"" in Persian, ultimately from Ancient Greek χυμεία (khumeía)."
Kimiyasu,m,"ヤスミ(Japanese Katakana)|きみお(Japanese Hiragana)|公泰, 公康, 規民保, 君康, 君八洲, 生美靖, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-YA-SOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 公 (kimi) meaning ""lord"" combined with 寧 (yasu) meaning ""peaceful, rather"". Other combinations of kanji characters are also possible."
Kimiyo,f,"きみよ(Japanese Hiragana)|キミヨ(Japanese Katakana)|キミ代(Kanji/Katakana)|君予, 公夜, 仁世, 主与, 希美淑, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-YO,,,,,,,"From 仁 (kimi) meaning ""benevolent, compassionate"" and 夜 (yo) meaning ""night"". Other kanji combinations can be used as well.Known bearers of this name include the Japanese former tennis player Kimiyo Hatanaka (1944-), Japanese table tennis player Kimiyo Matsuzaki (1938-), and Japanese artist Kimiyo Mishima (1932-)."
Kimiyoshi,m,"君吉, 君良, 公由, 公美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-MEE-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 君 (kimi) meaning ""noble, lord"" and 美 (yoshi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well. A known bearer is the Japanese film director, Kimiyoshi Yasuda (1911-1983)."
