Kim Quy,m,,Vietnamese Mythology,/kim˧˧ kwi˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/kim˧˧ kwɪj˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 金 (kim) meaning ""gold"" and 龜 (quy) meaning ""turtle"". In Vietnamese mythology, this is the name of a mythical golden turtle. He gifts An Dương Vương his golden claw to use as a crossbow trigger, and he appears from the Hoàn Kiếm lake in Hanoi to recall Thuận Thiên, the mythical sword lent to Lê Lợi to fight Ming invaders."
