Kinga,m,"金峨, 金鵞(Japanese Kanji)|きんが(Japanese Hiragana)|キンガ(Japanese Katakana)","Japanese (Rare, Archaic)",KEENG-GAH,,,,,,,"This name combines 金 (kin, kon, gon, kana-, kane, -gane) meaning ""gold"" with 峨 (ga, kewa.shii) meaning ""steep"" or 鵞 (ga) meaning ""goose.""Bearers of this name include Nihon-ga painter Kinga Furuichi (古市 金峨) (1805-1880) and author Kinga Baitei (梅亭 金鵞) (1821-1893).This name is very rarely given to boys, if given at all."
Kingdavid,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)|English (African)",/kɪŋ ˈdɛɪ.vɪd/(American English),,,,,,,"Combination of King and David, possibly used in reference to the Biblical character, King David of Israel."
Kingdom,m,,"English (American, Rare)|English (African)",,,,,,,,"Either a transferred use of the surname Kingdom or else directly from the English word, perhaps taken from the biblical phrase kingdom of God. A famous bearer was the English engineer Isambard Kingdom Brunel (1806-1859), whose middle name was his mother's maiden name."
