Kingly,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From the English word kingly, referring to something or someone who is like a king, or a variant of Kinglee."
Kingman,m,,"English (American, Rare)",KING-mən(American English),,,,,,,Transferred usage from the surname Kingman. A known bearer was the American diplomat Kingman Brewster Jr. (1919-1988).
