Kingo,m,金吾(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,KEEN-GOH,,,,,,,"The name Kingo means ""my gold."" The kanji character 金 (kane/kin) means ""gold"" and 吾 (ware/go) means ""my, one's own."""
Kingoro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kingorou,m,"金五郎, 欣五郎, 琴五郎, 錦五郎, 近五郎, 均五郎(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEEN-GO-RO,,,,,,,"From 金 (kin, kon, gon, kana-, kane) meaning ""gold,"" 欣 (kin, gon, kon, yoroko.bu) meaning ""delight, pleasure,"" 琴 (kin, koto), referring to the qin, a 7-stringed Chinese zither, 錦 (kin, nishiki) meaning ""brocade,"" 近 (kin, kon, chika.i) meaning ""near, close"" or 均 (kin, nara.su) meaning ""average, level"", combined with 五 (go) meaning ""five"", and 郎 (ro, ryo) meaning ""son""."
Kingou,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kingrun,m,,Arthurian Cycle,,,,,,,,"The seneschal of King Clamide.With Clamide, he invaded the land of Brobarz and besieged Belrepeire (Beaurepaire), castle of the lady Condwiramurs (Kondviramur). Clamide and Kingrun would have succeeded but for the arrival of Perceval, who defeated them both in combat.Kingrun had killed Schenteflurs, the son of Gornemant, and for this reason he refused when Perceval ordered him to report to Gornemant. Rather than kill Kingrun, Perceval sent him to King Arthur instead.Kingrun’s counterpart in Chrétien de Troyes is Anguiguerron."
Kingsbury,m,,English (Rare),,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Kingsbury.
Kingsette,f,,"English (American, Rare, Archaic)",KING-set(American English),,,,,,,Extremely rare feminization of King by way of adding the French diminutive ending -ette.
Kingsford,m,,Scottish|African,,,,,,,,Transferred use of the surname Kingsford.
King-shun,m,"景淳, 景信, etc.(Chinese)",Chinese (Cantonese),/kɪŋ.sɵn/(Cantonese),,,,,,,Cantonese romanisation of Jingchun or Jingxin.
Kingslee,,,"English (Modern, Rare)",/ˈkɪŋz.li/,,,,,,,Variant of Kingsley.
Kingsleigh,f,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",/ˈkɪŋz.li/(American English),,,,,,,Variant of Kingsley.
Kingsolomon,m,,"English (Modern, Rare)",/kɪŋ.ˈsɑl.ə.mən/,,,,,,,"Combination of King and Solomon, used in reference to the Biblical character, King Solomon of Israel."
