Kinh Đô,m,,Vietnamese (Rare),/kïŋ˧˧ ʔɗo˧˧/|/kɨn˧˧ ʔɗow˧˧/,,,,,,,"From Sino-Vietnamese 京都 (kinh đô) meaning ""capital city""."
Kinh Dương Vương,m,,Vietnamese Mythology,/kïŋ˧˧ zɨəŋ˧˧ vɨəŋ˧˧/(Vietnamese)|/kɨn˧˧ jɨəŋ˧˧ vɨəŋ˧˧/(Vietnamese),,,,,,,"Means ""King of Kinh Dương"", from Sino-Vietnamese 涇 (kinh) referring to the Jing River, 陽 (dương) meaning ""light, sun, male"", and 王 (vương) meaning ""king"". In Vietnamese mythology, he is the husband of Thần Long and the father of Lạc Long Quân. He is considered the first king of the Vietnamese people, the founder of the Hồng Bàng dynasty."
Kinheja,m,,Creek,,,,,,,,Variant of Kinache.
