Kinji,m,"キンジ(Japanese Katakana)|きんじ(Japanese Hiragana)|欣司, 欽治, 勤爾, 錦士, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEEN-ZHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 勤 (kin) meaning ""diligent"" combined with 次 (ji) meaning ""next, secondary"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Kinjirō,m,"金次郎, 金二郎, 金治郎, 欽次郎, 欣次郎, 錦治郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きんじろう(Japanese Hiragana)|キンジロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kʲĩɲ.ʑi.ɾo̞ː/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 金 (kin) meaning ""gold"", 欽 (kin) meaning ""respect, revere"", 欣 (kin) meaning ""take pleasure in, rejoice"" or 錦 (kin) meaning ""brocade"" combined with 次 (ji) meaning ""order, sequence, next"", 二 (ji) meaning ""two"" or 治 (ji) meaning ""govern, administer"" and 郎 (rō) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
