Kinu,f,絹(Japanese Kanji)|きぬ(Japanese Hiragana)|キヌ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese|Aymara,KEE-NUU|Keenoo,,,,,,,"This name is used as 絹 (ken, kinu) meaning ""silk.""It is not known how popular Kinu was in the early and middle part of the Edo period (1603-1868), but it was moderately popular in the latter part of that period and in the Meiji period (1868-1912). The name dropped down in popularity in the Taishō period/era (1912-1926)."
