Kirie,f,"キリエ(Japanese Katakana)|きりえ(Japanese Hiragana)|桐絵, 桐枝, 桐江, 霧江, 霧絵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)","Japanese|Popular Culture|English (American, Modern, Rare)",KEE-ṘEE-EH(Japanese)|/ˈki.ɹi.eɪ/(American English),,,,,,,"From Japanese 桐 (kiri) meaning ""paulownia, princess tree, empress tree, foxglove-tree"" combined with 絵 (e) meaning ""picture, painting"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.This name is borne by the character Kirie Goshima (五島桐絵 Goshima Kirie), the protagonist of the horror manga series Uzumaki by Junji Ito."
