Kirrilie,f,,English (Australian),KI-ri-lee(Australian English),,,,,,,"Used in Australia and New Zealand that can be an elaboration of the European name Kira 2 and Keira through the addition of a lee sound. It may have also originated from the Aboriginal word 'kira' which means ""leaf"" and the Maori 'Kiri' which means ""tree bark"". Also closely related to Kirralee, Kiralee and Kirrily"
Kirry,f,,Manx,,,,,,,,"Manx diminutive of Katherine and cognate of Kate and Katie. It also may be inspired by the Manx word kirree meaning ""sheep"", and is found as the subject of two Manx folk songs: 'Ny Kirree Fo 'Niaghtey' (English: 'The Sheep Under the Snow') and 'O Kirree T'ou Goll Dy Faagail Mee' ('Oh Kirree, Thou Wilt Leave Me')."
