Kirththish,m,කීර්ත්තිෂ්(Sinhala),Sinhalese,[ˈkiːr.t̪iʃ],,,,,,,"Means, “rules with glory”. A modern Sanskrit-Dravidian hybrid name, commonly used among Tamil and occasionally Sinhalese communities in Sri Lanka and southern India. Derived from the Sanskrit कीर्ति (kīrti) which means ""fame, glory, reputation, honor"" and the suffix ईश (īśa) which means ""lord, ruler, god""."
