Kishichirou,m,"喜七郎, 喜七朗, 貴七朗, 樹七朗, 木七朗, 木七郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-SHEE-CHEE-ṘO:,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 七 (shichi) meaning ""seven"" combined with 郎 (rou) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations can be possible.A famous bearer is Kishichiro Okura, he was a Japanese entrepreneur and hotelier."
Kishimojin,f,鬼子母神(Japanese Kanji),Japanese Mythology,,,,,,,,"The name of a Japanese protector goddess of children and child rearing who is sometimes also seen as a vicious demon of misery and unhappiness towards children and parents. Her name is derived from 鬼 (ki) meaning ""ghost, evil spirit, demon"", 子 (shi) meaning ""child"", 母 (mo) meaning ""mother"" and 神 (jin) meaning ""god, deity, spirit""."
