Kiyoe,f,聖恵(Japanese Kanji)|きよえ(Japanese Hiragana),Japanese,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Japanese kanji 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy; sacred"" combined with 恵 (e) meaning ""blessing; grace; favor"".Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous bearer is Kiyoe Yoshioka (b. 1984), a Japanese singer and vocalist best known for being the lead vocalist of the band Ikimonogakari."
Kiyofumi,m,"清史, 清文, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-FOO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" combined with 文 (fumi) meaning ""sentence"" or 史 (fumi) meaning ""history"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.Famous bearers of this name are Japanese racing cyclist Kiyofumi Nagai and Japanese singer-songwriter Kiyofumi Ohno."
Kiyoha,f,"きよ葉(Kanji/Hiragana)|清葉, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-YO-HAH,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" and 葉 (ha) meaning ""sheet, leaf"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoharu,m,"清春, 清陽, 精治, 精晴, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-HA-ROO,,,,,,,"It can be written with 精 (kiyo) meaning ""energy, vigor"" combined with 治 (haru) meaning ""govern, rule, treatment"", 陽 (haru) meaning ""sun, male, light"", or 晴 (haru) meaning ""clear or fine weather, sunniness"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyohiko,m,"虚彦, 貴彦, 虚彦, 紀世彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy, sacred"" or 虚 (kiyo) meaning ""emptiness, void"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy, prince"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyohime,f,清姫(Japanese Kanji),Japanese Mythology|Japanese,Kee-oh-HEE-may(Japanese)|KEE-YOH-HEE-MAY(Japanese),,,,,,,"The name translates to ‘pure lady’. It’s the name of a princess from Japanese mythology, who falls in love with a Buddhist monk named anchin, and after she was rejected, her passion for him turned her into a dragon and she consumed both herself and anchin in the bell of the dojoji temple."
Kiyohiro,m,"清洋, 清裕, 喜代裕, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KHEE-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" combined with 裕 (hiro) meaning ""abundant"". Different combinations of kanji can also form this name."
Kiyohisa,m,"聖寿, 虚寿, 清寿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KHEE-SAH,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""sacred, holy"" and 寿 (hisa) meaning ""long life, lifespan"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyohito,m,"聖仁, 虚人, 清人, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KHEE-TO,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy; sacred"" or 虚 (kiyo) meaning ""emptiness, void"" combined with 人 (hito, to) meaning ""person"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoi,f,"キヨイ(Japanese Katakana)|きよい(Japanese Hiragana)|清, 清衣, 槻代衣, 貴良, 稀儀, 綺儀, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-EE,,,,,,,"From the adjective 清い (kiyoi) meaning ""clean, pure, clear"" or 綺 (ki) meaning ""thin silk"" combined with 良 (yoi) meaning ""good"". Other kanji or kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoichi,m,清一(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,Kee-yoh-ee-chee,,,,,,,Derived from Kiyo combined with Ichi.Other characters combinations are also possible.
Kiyoichiro,m,清一郎(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,Kee-yoh-ee-chee-roh,,,,,,,Derived from Kiyo combined with Ichirō.Other characters combinations are also possible.
Kiyoichirou,m,清一郎(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,Kee-yoh-ee-chee-roh,,,,,,,Derived from Kiyo combined with Ichirō.Other characters combinations are also possible.
Kiyoji,m,"清司, 清二, 精司, 精二, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-ZHEE,,,,,,,"It can be written as 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, clean"" or 精 (kiyo) meaning ""energy, vigour"" and 二 (ji) meaning ""two"" or 司 (ji) meaning ""officer, boss"". This name can also be formed using other kanji combinations."
Kiyojiro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kiyojirou,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Kiyojiro.
Kiyoka,f,"キヨカ(Japanese Katakana)|きよか(Japanese Hiragana)|潔加, 浄華, 喜代歌, 希世加, 希陽加, 季世華, 季楊花, 規予香, 貴与香, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 葵 (ki) meaning ""althea, hollyhock"", 夜 (yo) meaning ""night"" combined with 華 (ka) meaning ""flower"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyokata,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,"A notable bearer is the artist Kiyokata Kaburaki (1878-1972), known in the West as Kaburagi. His legal first name was Kenichi."
Kiyokatsu,m,"きよかつ(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨカツ(Japanese Katakana)|貴恰, 精括, 清且, 聖活, 斉宗, 喜代葛, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KA-TSOO,,,,,,,"From 斉 (kiyo) meaning ""uniformity, evenness, equality"" or 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy, sacred"" combined with 且 (katsu) meaning ""moreover, furthermore, also"", 括 (katsu) meaning ""tie up, fasten"", or 恰 (katsu) meaning ""just like, just as, appropriate, exactly"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyokazu,m,"清和, 清一, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KAH-ZOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo, shi) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" combined with 和 (kazu, wa) meaning ""harmony, peace"" or 一 (kazu, ichi) meaning ""one"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoki,m,"青享, 清喜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-KEE,,,,,,,"From 青 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, clean"" and 享 (ki) meaning ""to enjoy, to receive, to undergo, to answer"" or 起 (ki) meaning ""to rise, to wake up"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyomaro,m,"清麿, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-YO-MAH-RO,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, purity"" and 麿 (maro, maru) meaning ""I (pronoun)"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyome,f,"清萌, 浄萌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きよめ(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,KEE-YO-ME,,,,,,,"As a vocabulary word it can be spelled as 清め or 浄め meaning ""purification"". As a name, it can be from 清 or 浄 (kiyo) meaning ""purify, clean, Manchu dynasty, exorcise, cleanse"" and 萌 (me) meaning ""sprout""."
Kiyomi,f,"清美, 紀代美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きよみ(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨミ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kʲi.jo̞.mi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" or 紀 (ki) meaning ""record, chronicle"" and 代 (yo) meaning ""generation, era"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other combinations of kanji can form this name as well."
Kiyomichi,m,"きよみち(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨミチ(Japanese Katakana)|清道, 虚道, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-MEE-CHEE,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy; sacred"" or 虚 (kiyo) meaning ""emptiness, void"" combined with 道 (michi) meaning ""path"". Other kanji combinations can also form this name."
Kiyomii,f,,"African American (Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Kiyomi.
Kiyomitsu,m,"清光, 清允, 喜代光, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-MEE-TSOO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" combined with 光 (mitsu) meaning ""light, radiance"". Different combinations of kanji can also form this name."
Kiyomizu,f,"清水, 清瑞, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-MEE-ZUU,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure"" combined with 水 (mizu) meaning ""water"" or 瑞 (mizu) meaning ""auspicious"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyomu,m,"きよむ(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨム(Japanese Katakana)|浄, 清, 雪, 澄, 淨霧, 斉芽, 心求, 圭楽, 貴牟, 斎萠, 淳祈, 人富, 白静, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-MOO,,,,,,,"From the Japanese word 清む or 浄む (kiyomu) meaning ""to purify"", 澄 (kiyomu) meaning ""clear, pure"" or 雪 (kiyomu) meaning ""snow, cleanse"". Other spellings are permissible."
Kiyona,f,"喜代奈, 希世菜, 希世奈, 汐菜, 潔那, 清奈, 清名, 綺波, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generations"" combined with 奈 (na) meaning ""apple tree"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyone,f,"きよね(Japanese Hiragana)|廉禰, 浄根, 聖音, 廉嶺, 浄寧, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-NE,,,,,,,"From 廉 (kiyo) meaning ""honest, inexpensive, clean"" and 音 (ne) meaning ""noise, sound"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyono,f,"きよの(Japanese Hiragana)|清乃, 希世乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-NO,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine given name derived from 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, clean"" and 乃 (no) meaning ""of"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyonobu,m,"きよのぶ(Japanese Hiragana)|精延, 精伸, 精信, 清延, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-NO-BOO,,,,,,,"This name can be made with 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clean, pure"" or 精 (kiyo) meaning ""vigour, energy, spirit"", with 伸/延 (nobu) meaning ""prolong, lengthen, stretch, grow, extend"", 信 (nobu) meaning ""believe, faith, trust"", or 進 (nobu) meaning ""move on, advance, make progress"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyora,f,"きよら(Japanese Hiragana)|希世楽, 汐羅, 清, 清來, 生世良, 聖愛, 聖良, 貞女, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-ṘAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 希 (ki) meaning ""hope"", 世 (yo) meaning ""world"" combined with 楽 (ra) meaning ""music"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyori,f,"きより(Japanese Hiragana)|清里, 清梨, 希依, 希和, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-REE,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, clean"" and 梨 (ri) meaning ""pear"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyoshige,m,"清茂, 清成, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-SHEE-GEH,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""pure, clean"" and 繁 (shige) meaning ""luxurious, flourishing"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoshiko,f,"白恋, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-SHEE-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 白 (kiyo) meaning ""white"" combined with 恋 (shiko) meaning ""to love"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoshizu,m,"清閑, 清静, ⁠虚静, 精鎮, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YOH-SHEE-ZOO,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" combined with 閑 (shizu) meaning ""calm, leisure, quiet, tranquil, free time"" or 静 (shizu) meaning ""calm, silent, quiet"". Other kanji combinations are possible. If spelled 清閑 (seikan) it means ""tranquility""."
Kiyotada,m,"喜代忠, 清正, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TAH-DAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" combined with 正 (tada, tadashi, masa) meaning ""correct, proper, justice"" or 忠 (tada, tadashi, chu) meaning ""loyalty"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyotaka,m,"喜代隆, 潔孝, 潔貴, 潔嵩, 潔隆, 浄隆, 清尭, 清孝, 清孝, 聖考, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TA-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" combined with 隆 (taka) meaning ""noble"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyotaro,m,,Japanese,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kiyoteru,m,"貴咏晶, 清輝, 聖明, 精昭(Japanese Kanji)|キヨテル(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TEH-ROO,,,,,,,"From 貴 (ki) meaning ""valuable"", 咏 (yo) meaning ""recitation, poem, composing, song"", and 昭 (teru) meaning ""bright, enlightened, glorious"", 晶 (teru) meaning ""crystal, diamond, clear"" or 明 (teru) meaning ""bright, enlighten, clarifying, understanding"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyoto,m,"喜代人, 潔人, 潔斗, 潔都, 浄人, 清音, 清仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""rejoice"", 代 (yo) meaning ""generation"" combined with 人 (to) ""person"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyotomi,m,"清富, 精富, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TO-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" or 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy"" combined with 富 (tomi) meaning ""wealth, abundance"". Other kanji combinations are usable."
Kiyotomo,m,"キヨトモ(Japanese Katakana)|きよとも(Japanese Hiragana)|清智, 心友, 喜代具, 己代具, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TO-MO,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy, sacred, divine"" or 心 (kiyo) meaning ""heart, mins, soul"" combined with 友 (tomo) meaning ""friend"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyotoshi,m,"貴利, 貴寿, 貴年, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From 貴 (kiyo) meaning ""valuable, expensive, worthful"" or 清 (kiyo) ""Qing dynasty, clear, pure, clean"" combined with 利 (toshi) meaning ""benefit, profit"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyotsugu,m,"きよつぐ(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨツグ(Japanese Katakana)|聖丞二 虚緒, 清嗣, 潔告, 雪次, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-TSOO-GOO,,,,,,,"From 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy; sacred"" or 虚 (kiyo) meaning ""emptiness, void"" combined with 丞 (tsugu) meaning ""to help, to rescue"", 継 (tsugu) meaning ""to succeed someone, inherit"", or 禎 (tsugu) meaning ""divine grace, auspicious, straightforward"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyoyasu,m,"清悌, 聖悌, 潔悌, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-YA-SOO,,,,,,,"From 廉 (kiyo) meaning ""clean, honest, inexpensive"" or 潔 (kiyo) meaning ""pure"" combined with 悌 (yasu) meaning ""respect for one's elders, filial piety"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kiyoyoshi,m,"きよよし(Japanese Hiragana)|キヨヨシ(Japanese Katakana)|廉喜, 圭儀, 潔好, 聖良, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-YO-SHEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 廉 (kiyo) meaning ""clean, honest, inexpensive"" or 圭 (kiyo) meaning ""corner, edge, square jewel, angle"" combined with 兆 (yoshi) meaning ""trillion"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kiyoyuki,m,"清侑, 聖侑, 清之, 精之, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YO-YOO-KEE,,,,,,,"From 清 (kiyo) meaning ""clear, pure, clean"" or 聖 (kiyo) meaning ""holy"" combined with 侑 (yuki) meaning ""help, recommend, reward, forgive"". Other kanji combinstions are possible."
Kiysha,f,,African American,,,,,,,,Variant of Keisha.
Kiyuko,f,,Japanese (Rare),KEE-YOO-KO,,,,,,,"Ki means ""hope"", yu can mean ""reason, truth, cause"", ""tie, bind"", and ko means ""child, sign of the rat""."
Kiyumi,f,"貴弓美, 貴由美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-YUU-MEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 貴 (ki) meaning ""expensive"", 弓 (yu) meaning ""archery bow"" or 由 (yu) meaning ""reason, cause"" combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kiyuri,f,"きゆり(Japanese Hiragana)|キユリ(Japanese Katakana)|希百合, 木百合, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KEE-YOO-ṘEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 希 (ki) meaning ""hope, ambition, rare"" and 百合 (yuri) meaning ""lily"". This name can also be formed from other combinations of kanji characters."
Kiza,f,,"Russian (Rare, Archaic)",,,,,,,,Russian form of Kitsa.
Kizashi,,"兆, 萌, 萌士, 萌司, 萌詩, 輝志, 稀士, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きざし(Japanese Hiragana)|キザシ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),[kʲí.zà.ɕì],,,,,,,"From 兆し/萌し (kizashi) meaning ""sign, omen.""These single kanji can be suffixed with a shi kanji, such as 士 meaning ""samurai,"" 司 meaning ""office,"" 志 meaning ""will, aim, goal"" or 詩 meaning ""poem."" These shi kanji, alongside , can follow a ki kanji, like 輝 meaning ""brightness, brilliance"" or 稀 meaning ""rare.""This name is rarely used."
Kizen,m,"喜善, 喜然, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きぜん(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/kʲi.d͡zẽ̞ɴ/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 喜 (ki) meaning ""joy"" combined with 善 (zen) meaning ""goodness, virtue"" or 然 (zen) meaning ""however, therefore, so"". Other Kanji combinations are possible."
