Kiziah,,,African American,,,,,,,,Variant of Keziah as well as a short form of Hezekiah.
Kizil,m,,Turkish,,,,,,,,"Means ""bright red"" in Turkish."
Kızılay,,,Turkish (Rare),,,,,,,,"From Turkish kızıl meaning ""bright red, scarlet"" and ay meaning ""moon""."
Kizil-ool,m,,Siberian|Khakas,,,,,,,,"Means ""red boy"" in Khakas."
Kizito,m,,Eastern African|Ganda|History (Ecclesiastical),kee-ZEE-to(Eastern African),,,,,,,St. Kizito is the youngest of the 22 Ugandan martyrs. He is the patron saint of children and primary schools.
Kizkitza,f,,Basque,/kis̻.ˈki.ts̻a/,,,,,,,"After Mount Kizkitza in the Basque town of Itsaso, which has an hermitage dedicated to Our Lady of Kizkitza. According to folk legend, the locals saw a light on Mount Kizkitza and they found the Virgin Mary there. They then decided to build a shrine in her honour in their village, but the Marian apparition kept happening at the top of the mountain at night. In the end, they had to build the shrine at the mountain."
Kizor,f,Кизор(Mordvin),Mordvin,,,,,,,,"Means ""summer"" in Moksha."
Kizuki,,"木月, 気月, 稀月, 希月, 妃月, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KEE-ZOO-KEE,,,,,,,"Kizuki has various spellings. It combines 木 (ki) meaning “tree”, 気 (ki) meaning “spirit”, 稀 (ki) meaning “rare”, 希 (ki) “hope, rare” and 妃 (ki) meaning “princess” with 月 (tsuki) meaning “moon, month”."
Kizumi,f,"築実, 築美(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"kizumi means either ""build reality"" or ""build beauty"". the kanji used for the first meaning are築 (kizu) which means 'build' and 実 (mi) meaning reality. the second meaning has 築 (kizu) and 美 (mi) meaning beauty."
Kizuna,,"絆, 希沙, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|きずな(Japanese Hiragana)|キズナ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/kʲi.zɨᵝ.nä/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 絆 (kizuna) meaning ""bond, connection, emotional tie"". It can also be formed from 希 (ki) meaning ""rare, hope, expect, strive"" combined with 沙 (suna) meaning ""sand, grit"", as well as other combinations of kanji."
Kizza,,,Ganda,,,,,,,,"""born after twins""Twins in the Ganda culture have their own special names. The parents and siblings earn a new name upon the birth of twins in the family."
Kizzey,f,,"English (American, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Kizzy.
