Kleandridas,m,Κλεανδρίδας(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"Aeolic and Doric Greek form of Kleandrides, because it contains ίδας (idas), which is the Aeolic and Doric Greek form of the patronymic suffix ἴδης (ides).This name was borne by a Spartan general from the 5th century BC. He is better known under the latinized form of his name, which is Cleandridas."
