Koalani,f,,Hawaiian,koh-ah-LAH-nee,,,,,,,"Koalani appears to be a modern Hawaiian-inspired compound name formed from the Hawaiian elements koa, meaning ""warrior,"" ""soldier,"" or ""brave one,"" and lani, meaning ""heaven,"" ""sky,"" ""royal,"" or ""heavenly."" Based on these established meanings, the name can be interpreted as ""heavenly warrior"" or ""royal warrior."" Although the individual elements are well documented in the Hawaiian language and occur in many traditional and contemporary Hawaiian names, Koalani itself does not appear to have a known historical record in early Hawaiian naming sources and is most likely a modern creation combining traditional Hawaiian name elements into a new form."
Koaliʻi,m,,Hawaiian (Rare),/ko.a.ˈli.ʔi/,,,,,,,"Means ""chiefly warrior"" or ""ruling warrior,"" from koa meaning ""soldier, warrior, fighter"" and liʻi, shortened from aliʻi meaning ""chief, officer, ruler, monarch, peer, headman, aristocrat, king, commander."""
Koamalu,m,,Hawaiian (Rare),/ko.a.ˈma.lu/,,,,,,,"Means ""brave strength,"" from koa meaning ""brave, bold, fearless, valiant"" and malu meaning ""shelter, protection, peace, control, strength."""
