Kohara,f,,Polynesian Mythology,,,,,,,,"Kohara is the goddess of tuna, and is considered the ""mother of all tuna fish"". The word also means ""to throw a flash of lightning, as a deity"". In Māori mythology, lightning begat tuna. In that sense, Kohara can be considered the ""ancestor of tuna""."
