Korkyra,f,Κόρκυρα(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/kɔːr.ˈkaɪ.ər.ə/(English)|/ˈkor.cy.ra/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology. In Greek mythology, Korkyra was a naiad-nymph and daughter of the river god Asopos and nymph Metope. The god Poseidon kidnapped and brought her to the island of Korkyra (now known as Kerkyra, or Corfu in English), which was named after her. She became its personification and tutelary goddess."
