Kōtarō,m,"康太郎, 光太郎, 幸太郎, 浩太郎, 孝太郎, 晃太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|こうたろう(Japanese Hiragana)|コウタロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ko̞ː.tä.ɾo̞ː/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 康 (kō) meaning ""peace"", 光 (kō) meaning ""light, brilliant, shine"", 幸 (kō) meaning ""happiness, good luck"", 浩 (kō) meaning ""prosperous"", 孝 (kō) meaning ""filial piety, obedience"" or 晃 (kō) meaning ""bright, clear"" combined with 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big, great"" and 郎 (rō) meaning ""son"". This name can be formed from other combinations of kanji as well."
Kotaro,m,"康太郎, 光太郎, 幸太郎, 浩太郎, 孝太郎, 晃太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|こうたろう(Japanese Hiragana)|コウタロウ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ko̞ː.tä.ɾo̞ː/,,,,,,,Alternate transcription of Japanese Kanji 康太郎 or 光太郎 or 幸太郎 or 浩太郎 or 孝太郎 or 晃太郎 (see Kōtarō).
