Kote,m,კოტე(Georgian),Georgian|Popular Culture,KO-TAY(Georgian),,,,,,,"Short form of Konstantine, which tends to be used as an independent name rather than as an unofficial nickname.In popular culture, this is the name of the eponymous character of the comic opera Keto and Kote (1919) composed by the Georgian composer Viktor Dolidze (1890-1933)."
