Kotetsu,m,"小鉄, 小徹, 小哲, 虎鉄, 虎徹, 虎哲(Japanese Kanji)|こてつ(Japanese Hiragana)|コテツ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ko̞.te̞.t͡sɨᵝ/,,,,,,,"This name combines 小 (shou, chii.sai, ko-, o-, sa-) meaning ""little, small"" or 虎 (ko, tora) meaning ""tiger"" with 鉄 (tetsu, kurogane) meaning ""iron,"" 徹 (tetsu) meaning ""penetrate, clear, pierce"" or 哲 (tetsu, satoi, aki.raka) meaning ""philosophy, sagacity."""
Kothar-wa-khasis,m,𐎋𐎘𐎗𐎆𐎃𐎒𐎒(Ugaritic),Semitic Mythology|Ugaritic Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""skillful and wise"". Name borne by an Ugaritic god of craftsmanship and magic. Some academics consider him to be equivalent to the Greek god Hephaestus."
