Kotoa,f,"琴愛, 琴亜, 今歩, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-AH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 愛 (a) meaning ""love, affection"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotoba,f,"詩, 言葉(Japanese Kanji)|ことば(Japanese Hiragana)|コトバ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,KO-TO-BA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 詩 (kotoba) meaning ""poem"" or 言葉 (kotoba) meaning ""words"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotobuki,,寿(Japanese Kanji)|ことぶき(Japanese Hiragana)|コトブキ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),[ko̞.to̞.bɯ̟ᵝ.kʲi],,,,,,,"From 寿 (kotobuki) meaning ""congratulations; longevity,"" derived, via a sound shift, from a combination of 言 (koto) meaning ""word"" and continuative/stem form of obsolete verb 祝く (hoku) meaning ""to pray for a good outcome"" (compare Kotohogi). It originally referred to saying something in prayer for a good outcome, then to saying something favourable in hope for a felicitous or auspicious occasion, shifting to its present meaning.One bearer of this name is manga artist and actor, Kotobuki Shiriagari (しりあがり 寿) (1958-), born Toshiki Mochidzuki (望月 寿城).This name is very rarely used and is more commonly used as a surname."
Kotoe,f,"コト恵(Kanji/Katakana)|琴絵, 琴恵, 琴枝, 紀恵, 琴, 琴詠, 琴得, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-E,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 絵 (e) meaning ""picture"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous bearer is Kotoe Taichi, a Japanese voice actress and actress."
Kotoha,f,"コトハ(Japanese Katakana)|ことは(Japanese Hiragana)|琴葉, 言羽, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-HA,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine given name derived from 琴 (koto) meaning ""koto, harp"" and 葉 (ha) meaning ""leaf"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
Kotohiko,m,"異彦, 琴彦, 言彦, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 異 (koto) meaning ""uncommon, special"", 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp or 言 (koto) meaning ""to say, speech"" combined with 彦 (hiko) meaning ""boy, prince"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kotohime,f,"琴姫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-HEE-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kotohito,m,"載仁, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 載 (koto) meaning ""force"" combined with 仁 (hito) meaning ""two"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Kotoho,f,"ことほ(Japanese Hiragana)|コトホ(Japanese Katakana)|壽, 寿, 琴帆, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KO-TO-HO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 帆 (ho) meaning ""sail"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotohogi,,寿(Japanese Kanji)|ことほぎ(Japanese Hiragana)|コトホギ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese (Rare),[ko̞.to̞.ho̞.ɡʲi],,,,,,,"From 寿 (kotohogi) meaning ""congratulations; longevity"" (see Kotobuki for further details).This name is extremely rare."
Kotoi,f,"琴妃, 言伊, 言意, 言衣, 琴意, 殊生, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ことい(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,KO-TO-EE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 妃 (i) meaning ""empress"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kotoji,m,"ことじ(Japanese Hiragana)|琴司, 琴糸, 琴次, 琴治, 琴柱, 琴二, 言糸, 言治, 古都路, 柱, 琴路, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-JEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, 言 (koto) meaning ""say, word"", 古 (ko) meaning ""old"" or 柱 (kotoji) meaning ""pillar, post, cylinder, support"", 都 (to) meaning ""metropolis, capital, all, everything"" combined with 司 (ji) meaning ""director, official, govt office, rule, administer"", 糸 (ji) meaning ""thread"", 次 (ji) meaning ""next, order, sequence"", 治 (ji) meaning ""reign, be at peace, calm down, subdue, quell, govt, cure, heal, rule, conserve"", 柱 (ji) meaning ""pillar, post, cylinder, support"", 二 (ji) meaning ""two"" or 路 (ji) meaning ""path, route, road, distance"". Other kanji or kanji combinations can form this name as well."
Kotoka,,"コトカ(Japanese Katakana)|ことか(Japanese Hiragana)|琴奏, 琴楓, 古都華, 琴郁, 恩樺, 寿冬花, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-KA,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp (mostly feminine) or 言 (koto) meaning ""to say"" (mostly masculine), combined with 奏 (ka) meaning ""to play (music)"" or 郁 (ka) meaning ""fragrance, perfume"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotokaze,m,琴風(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,"/'ko.to.,ka.ze/",,,,,,,This name literally means zither wind.
Kotoki,,"琴樹, 琴喜, 小時, 言喜, 琴輝, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-KEE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 樹 (ki) meaning ""tree"". Other kanji combinations are also possible.A famous female bearer is Kotoki Zayasu, a Japanese volleyball player who plays for RC Cannes. She played for the Japan national team during the 2016 Summer Olympics."
Kotoko,f,"ことこ(Japanese Hiragana)|琴子, 香藤子, 言子, 瑚桃子, 古都子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotome,f,"琴芽, 琴女, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 芽 (me) meaning ""bud, sprout, shoot"" or 女 (me) meaning ""female, woman, wife"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kotomi,f,"琴美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|ことみ(Japanese Hiragana)|コトミ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ko̞.to̞.mi/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 美 (mi) meaning ""beautiful"", as well as other combinations of kanji. This name is commonly written in hiragana as well."
