Kotona,f,"琴菜, 琴那, 言和, 胡都菜, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-NAH,,,,,,,"From Japanese 琴 (koto), which refers to a type of musical instrument similar to a harp, combined with 和 (na) meaning ""peace, harmony, Japan, serenity, tranquility"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kotono,f,"琴乃, 言乃, 古都野, 小冬埜, 瑚永埜, 光時野, 木外希, 杏乙祈, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KO-TO-NO,,,,,,,"Japanese feminine name derived from 琴 (koto) meaning ""harp-like instrument"" and 乃 (no) meaning ""of"". Other kanji combinations can be used."
