Kōya,m,"康也, 公也, 晃也, 航也, 紘也, 昂也, 功也, 宏矢, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|こうや(Japanese Hiragana)|コウヤ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese,/ko̞ː.jä/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 康 (kō) meaning ""peace"", 公 (kō) meaning ""prince"", 晃 (kō) meaning ""bright, clear"", 航 (kō) meaning ""sail, navigate"", 紘 (kō) meaning ""large, vast, expansive"", 昂 (kō) meaning ""high-spirited"", 功 (kō) meaning ""success, great achievement"" or 宏 (kō) meaning ""wide, spacious, great, vast"" combined with 也 (ya) meaning ""to be, also"" or 矢 (ya) meaning ""arrow"". Other combinations of kanji can form this name as well."
