Koyah,m,,Haida (Anglicized),,,,,,,,"Anglicized form of Haida xhuuyaa ""raven"". Koyah (fl. 1787–1795) was the chief of Ninstints or Skungwai, the main village of the Kunghit-Haida during the era of the Maritime Fur Trade in Haida Gwaii off the North Coast of British Columbia, Canada."
