Kreuzwendedich,m,,"German (Rare, Archaic)",kroits-VEN-də-dikh,,,,,,,"Derived from the German phrase Kreuz, wende Dich! ""Cross, turn around"". The name is often given to children whose older siblings have died in infancy.This rare name is traditional in a few German families (mostly from the nobility) since the 30 Years' War. A famous bearer of the name was Prussian Minister Georg von Rheinbaben, full name Georg Kreuzwendedich Freiherr von Rheinbaben (1855-1921)."
