Kshitigarbha,m,क्षितिगर्भ(Sanskrit),Buddhism,/ˈkʂi.t̪i.ɡɐɾ.bʱɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""earth-womb"" from Sanskrit क्षिति (kṣiti) meaning ""earth"" and गर्भ (garbha) meaning ""womb, interior, inside"". This is the name of a bodhisattva in Buddhist tradition, typically portrayed as a monk with a halo or crown."
Kshitindra,m,"क्षितीन्द्र(Sanskrit, Hindi, Marathi, Nepali)",Sanskrit|Indian|Nepali|Hinduism|Punjabi|Hindi|Gujarati,kshitindra(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Name- Kshitindra क्षितीन्द्रMEANING - ""king of earth, sovereign"". It is joining of क्षिति + इन्द्र .Here क्षिति means earth & इन्द्र means king/chiefOrigin - Sanskrit Usage - Sanskrit, Indian, Tamil, Telugu, Nepali, Sinhala, Hindi, Sikh, Buddhist"
Kshitip,m,"क्षितिप(Sanskrit, Hindi, Marathi, Nepali)",Indian|Sanskrit|Hindi|Hinduism|Fijian|Nepali|Marathi|Gujarati|Bengali|Punjabi,kshit-ip(Indian),,,,,,,"Name - Kshitip { Xitip } क्षितिपMEANING - ""protector of earth"", king. It is joining of क्षिति + प .Here क्षिति means earth + प means protectorOrigin : Sanskrit Usage : Sanskrit, Indian, Tamil, Telugu, Nepali, Sinhala, Hindi, Sikh, Buddhist, Mauritian, FijianSource - Monier Williams Sanskrit-English dictionary"
