Kuafu,m,夸父(Chinese),Chinese Mythology,/kʰʷaː.fʷuː/,,,,,,,"From a combination of the characters 夸 (kua, meaning “boast”) and 父 (fu, meaning “father”). Kuafu was a giant in Chinese mythology most well known for trying to chase or race with the sun. After dying from thirst, his wooden staff transformed into a forest of peach trees. Alternatively, he is killed by the dragon Yinglong during the Yellow Emperor’s battle with Chiyou.An account in the Shanhaijing (山海经) describes him as holding a yellow snake in each hand and wearing two more as earrings."
