Kuini,f,,Hawaiian|Māori|Cook Islands Māori|Samoan|Tongan|Tahitian,kwee-nee,,,,,,,"Hawaiian, Māori, Samoan, Tongan, and Tahitian translation of Queenie. In New Zealand the name Kuīni, and English language equivalent Queen, are on a watchlist maintained by the New Zealand Registrar-General of Births, Deaths and Marriages, alongside other ranks and titles, offensive and obscene words. Currently the name Kuini can only be used if prospective parents can prove that there is prior use of the name Kuini in their family ancestry."
