Kültem,f,,Turkish,kewl-TEHM,,,,,,,"Derived from the Old Turkish verb root kül- or küli- meaning ""to gather, to heap up, to bring things together"" into a unified whole. Paired with the archaic nominal suffix -tem, it means ""a bunch, a bundle, a bouquet of freshly harvested crops,"" representing unity, togetherness, prosperity, and the joy of harvest."
