Kumatarō,m,"熊太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)|くまたろう(Japanese Hiragana)",Japanese,/kɯᵝ.mä.tä.ɾo̞ː/,,,,,,,"From Japanese 熊 (kuma) meaning ""bear (animal)"" combined with 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big, great"" and 郎 (rō) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations can form this name as well."
