Kumbhakarna,m,कुम्भकर्ण(Sanskrit),Hinduism,/ˈkum.bʱɐ.kɐɾ.ɳɐ/(Sanskrit),,,,,,,"Means ""pot-eared, pitcher-eared"" from Sanskrit कुम्भ (kumbha) meaning ""pitcher, pot, jar"" combined with कर्ण (karṇa) meaning ""ear"". In the Hindu epic the Ramayana he is a younger brother of the demon king Ravana. He is described as a giant of great strength with a ravenous appetite, only awakening for one day every six months to devour as much as he pleases. He is ultimately slain by the hero Rama."
