Küntogdı,,,Medieval Turkic,/kyn.toɡ.dɯ/,,,,,,,"A classic Turkic name composed of kün (""Sun"") and toğ (""to be born/arise""), meaning ""The sun has risen"" or ""Birth of the day."" In the philosophical framework of the Kutadgu Bilig, he is the personification of the ""Sun-King,"" representing the divine mandate of ""Law and Justice"" (Kün-Togdı) that brings light to the social order, serving as the celestial counterpart to his vizier, Aydolu."
