Kurleigh,m,,English,KUR-lee,,,,,,,"Alternate spelling of Curley and Curly. A notable bearer of this name is Kurleigh Gittens Jr. (born 1997), a Canadian football player of Guyanese origin."
Kurlinda,f,,Romani (Archaic),,,,,,,,Variant of Corlinda.
Kurman,m,Құрман(Kazakh)|قۇرمان(Kazakh Arabic),Kazakh,,,,,,,,Kazakh form of Kurban.
Kurmanbek,m,Курманбек(Kyrgyz)|Құрманбек(Kazakh)|قۇرمانبەك(Kazakh Arabic),Kyrgyz|Kazakh,,,,,,,,"From the given name Kurman, derived from Arabic قُرْبَان (qurbān) meaning ""sacrifice"", combined with the Turkish military title beg meaning ""chieftain, master""."
Kurmangazy,m,Құрманғазы(Kazakh)|قۇرمانعازى(Kazakh Arabic),Kazakh,,,,,,,,"Derived from Arabic قُرْبَان (qurbān) meaning ""sacrifice, gift (to God)"" combined with غَازِي‎ (ḡāzī) ""hero, champion, warrior"". A famous bearer was Kurmangazy Sagyrbaev (1818-1889), a Kazakh folk instrumentalist and composer known for his work using the dombra (a two-stringed plucked instrument)."
Kurmanjan,f,Курманжан(Kyrgyz),Kyrgyz,,,,,,,,Meaning uncertain. Name borne by a prominent Kyrgyz politician (1811-1907) who served as Datka (governer) of Alai from 1862 until her death.
