Kurōdo,m,蔵人(Japanese Kanji)|くろうど(Japanese Hiragana)|クロウド(Japanese Katakana),Japanese,KUU-ṘO:-DO,,,,,,,"This name is used as 蔵人 with 蔵 (sou, zou, osa.meru, kaku.reru, kura, kurou) meaning ""own, possess, storehouse"" and 人 (jin, nin, -to, hito, -ri) meaning ""person.""Kurōdo is classified as a hyakkanna (百官名), a court rank-style name that samurai used to announce oneself and give himself authority, since it comes from the name of an office of the imperial Japanese government (蔵人所/kurōdo-dokoro).One bearer of this name is actor and hip-hop singer, Claude Maki (goes by A.K.T.I.O.N. when he's a hip-hop singer), born Kurōdo Maki (真木 蔵人) (1972-).This name can also be romanised as Kurando."
Kuroe,,,Japanese,KURO-eh,,,,,,,Variant transcription of Kuroi.
Kurogane,m,,Japanese,KU-RO-GAN-E,,,,,,,"Means ""black steel"". Most notable as the name of one of the main characters from the CLAMP manga Tsubasa Reservoir Chronicles."
Kurohime,f,"黒姫, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KUU-ṘO-HEE-ME,,,,,,,"From Japanese 黒 (kuro) meaning ""black"" combined with 姫 (hime) meaning ""princess"". Other kanji combinations are also possible."
Kurokeme,m,,Ijaw,Ku Raw Ke Me,,,,,,,Not available.
Kuroko,f,"くろご(Japanese Hiragana)|クロ(Japanese Katakana)|くろ子(Kanji/Hiragana)|黒子, 寿路子, 懐露子, 駈櫓子, 九漏子, 来炉子, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KOO-RO-KO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 黒 (kuro) meaning ""black"" combined with 子 (ko) meaning ""child"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kuromi,f,"クロミ(Japanese Katakana)|くろみ(Japanese Hiragana)|黒実, 黒見, 黒美, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Popular Culture,KOO-ROO-MEE(Japanese),,,,,,,"From Japanese 黒 (kuro) meaning ""black"" combined with 見 (mi) meaning ""to see"". Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Kurona,,くろな(Japanese Hiragana)|クロナ(Japanese Katakana),Japanese,KOO-RO-NA,,,,,,,Not available.
Kurono,f,"玄乃, 玄之, 黒乃, 玄野, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KUU-ṘO-NO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 玄 (kuro) meaning ""mysterious"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle. Other combinations of kanji characters can also form this name."
Kuronue,m,,Popular Culture,ker-own-oo-ae|ker-own-a-way,,,,,,,"""black crane""-------------------------------------means 'black bat'"
Kuroo,m,黒尾(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,Kur-OH|Kur-OOH,,,,,,,Not available.
