Kurōta,m,"九郎太, 九朗太(Japanese Kanji)|くろうた(Japanese Hiragana)|クロウタ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),KUU-ṘO:-TAH,,,,,,,"This name combines 九 (kyuu, ku, kokono, kokono.tsu) meaning ""nine"" & 郎 (ryou, rou, otoko) meaning ""son"" or 朗 (rou, aki.raka, hoga.raka) meaning ""bright, cheerful, clear, merry"" with 太 (ta, tai, futo.i, futo.ru) meaning ""big, plump, thick.""This name is very rarely given to boys, if given at all."
Kurotaro,m,"黒太郎, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese (Rare),KOO-RO-TAH-RO,,,,,,,"From Japanese 黒 (kuro) meaning ""black"" combined with 太 (ta) meaning ""thick, big, great"" and 郎 (rō, ryo) meaning ""son"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
Kuroyefa,,,Western African|Ijaw,,,,,,,,"Means ""nothing is difficult in life"" in Ijaw."
Kuroyuri,,黒百合(Japanese Kanji),Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 黒百合 (kuroyuri) meaning “Black Lily”. In Hanakotoba, the Japanese language of flowers, the kuroyuri means love/curse.The name comes from 黒 (kuro) and 百合 (lily)."
Kurraki,m,,Indigenous Australian,,,,,,,,"Means ""white cockatoo"" in Kaurna."
Kurre,m,,Swedish|Finnish,,,,,,,,Diminutive of Kurt.
Kurrency,m,,"English (American, Modern, Rare)",,,,,,,,Variant of Currency.
