Kürşat,m,,Turkish,/cyɾ.ˈʃat/,,,,,,,"From Old Turkic kür meaning ""valiant, brave"" combined with the title şad meaning ""governor, leader"". This is the name of a legendary hero in Turkish literature."
Kurshina,f,,??,,,,,,,,Not available.
Kursiya,f,,Uzbek,,,,,,,,"Derived from Uzbek kursiy meaning ""the throne of Allah""."
Kurstan,m,Курстан(Kyrgyz),Kyrgyz,,,,,,,,"Basically means ""country of the brave"", derived from the Old Turkic adjective kur meaning ""brave, unwavering, powerful"" combined with the Persian suffix ستان‎ (stan) meaning ""place of, country""."
Kurstanbek,m,Курстанбек(Kyrgyz),Kyrgyz,,,,,,,,"Combination of Kurstan with the Turkish military title beg meaning ""chieftain, master"". As such, the meaning of this name is basically ""leader of the land of the brave""."
