Kutadgu,,,Medieval Turkic,/ku.tad.ɡu/,,,,,,,"Kutadgu is a Turkic name derived from the root Kut (the divine mandate of heaven, prosperity, happiness) + -adgu (denoting the state of being/becoming). It is the name of the light that illuminates the architecture of life itself. In Yusuf Has Hacib's magnum opus, it signifies the ""Wisdom that leads to Happiness."" It is the central knot that binds all elements: the justice of Küntogdı, the radiance of Aydolu, the intellect of Ögdülmiş, and the eternal awakening of Odgurmış. When these four threads converge, the Kut (the sacred blessing of balance) is achieved, allowing society to flourish in divine order."
