Kymopoleia,f,Κυμοπόλεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Means ""wave-walker"" from Greek κῦμα (kuma) ""wave, billow"" and πολέω (poleo) ""to go about, to range over"". Kymopoleia, Greek goddess of heavy seas and storms, was a daughter of the sea god Poseidon and Amphitrite and she was the wife of Briareus, one of the three Hundred-Handlers. Her only known mention occurs in Hesiod's Theogony."
