Kyniska,f,Κυνίσκα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,,,,,,,,"From κυνίσκα (kyniska), the Aeolic and Doric Greek form of κυνίσκη (kyniske) meaning ""female puppy"", itself from κύων (kyon) ""dog"" (genitive κυνός (kynos)). This was the name of a 5th-century BC Spartan princess, the granddaughter of Zeuxidamus, whose nickname had been Κυνίσκος (Kyniskos) ""puppy"" (metaphorically ""a little cynic""). Kyniska or Cynisca is famous for being the first woman to win at the Olympic Games, competing in the sport of chariot racing."
