Kyono,f,"協乃, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,,,,,,,,"From Japanese 協 (kyou) meaning ""unite, cooperate"", 京 (kyou) meaning ""capital city"", 郷 (kyou) meaning ""village"", 杏 (kyou) meaning ""apricot"" combined with 乃 (no), a possessive particle."
Kyōnosuke,m,"京之介, 京之助, 郷之介, 郷之助, 杏之介, 杏之助, 恭之介, 恭之助, 協之介, 協之助(Japanese Kanji)|きょうのすけ(Japanese Hiragana)|キョウノスケ(Japanese Katakana)",Japanese (Rare),KYO:-NO-SKE,,,,,,,"This name combines 京 (kyou, kin, kei, miyako) meaning ""capital,"" 郷 (kyou, gou, sato) meaning ""district, home town, native place, village,"" 杏 (an, kyou, kou, anzu) meaning ""apricot,"" 恭 (kyou, uyauya.shii) meaning ""respect, reverent"" or 協 (kyou) meaning ""cooperation"" with 之 (shi, oite, kono, kore, no, yuku) meaning ""of, this"" & 介 (kai, suke) meaning ""concern oneself with, jammed in, mediate, shellfish"" or 助 (jo, suke, su.keru, tasu.karu, tasu.keru) meaning ""assist, help, rescue.""This name is rarely given to boys, if given at all."
