Kyouhei,m,"きょうへい(Japanese Hiragana)|慶丙, 喬兵, 叶平, 亨丙, 匡兵, 馨平, 叫丙, 恭兵, 教平, 京丙, 協兵, 杏平, 享丙, 強兵, etc.(Japanese Kanji)",Japanese,KYO-HE,,,,,,,"From Japanese 郷 (kyou) meaning ""hometown, township, village, countryside"", 鏡 (kyou) meaning ""mirror"", 響 (kyou) meaning ""echo, reverberate, sound, resonance"", or 暁 (kyou) meaning ""daybreak, dawn, in the event"" combined with 平 (hei) meaning ""even, flat, peace"", 兵 (hei) meaning ""soldier, private, troops, army, warfare, strategy, tactics"" or 丙 (hei) meaning ""third of the ten heavenly stems, third in rank"". Other kanji combinations are possible."
