Ladon,m,Λάδων(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology|Ancient Greek|Romani (Archaic)|English (American),"/ˈleɪ.dən/(English)|/lá.dɔːn/(Attic Greek)|/ˈla.ðon/(Koine Greek, Byzantine Greek)|/lə.ˈdɑn/(American English)",,,,,,,"Uncertain etymology, perhaps related to λαδρέω (ladreo) meaning ""to flow strongly"". In Greek mythology, Ladon was the dragon or serpent that guarded the golden apples of the Hesperides, and was killed by Herakles. It was also the name of a river god who was the father of Daphne and Metope."
