Lafcadio,m,,Obscure,/ləf.ˈkɑ.di.oʊ/(English),,,,,,,"After the Greek island of Lefkada (Λευκάδα) in the Ionian Sea. This was the name of Lafcadio Hearn, an international writer born in Lefkada and known for his writings about Japan (especially his collections of Japanese legends and ghost stories) and about the city of New Orleans."
