Lamorna,f,,"Cornish|English (British, Rare)",,,,,,,,"From a Cornish place name of uncertain meaning, perhaps from lann ""area around a church"" combined with a contracted form of morlanow ""high tide"". It appears in the title of the folk song 'Way Down to Lamorna', as well as W. H. Davies' poem 'Lamorna Cove' (1929)."
