Lamprokles,m,Λαμπροκλῆς(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek,"/lam.pro.klɛ̂ːs/(Attic Greek)|/lam.pro.ˈklis/(Koine Greek, Byzantine Greek)|/lam.bro.ˈklis/(Constantinopolitan Greek)",,,,,,,"Derived from Greek λαμπρός (lampros) meaning ""bright, brilliant"" (compare lampo) and κλέος (kleos) meaning ""glory"". This was the name of the eldest son of Socrates."
