Lanassa,f,Λάνασσα(Ancient Greek),Ancient Greek|Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Derived from the Greek noun λαός (laos) meaning ""(the) people"" combined with the Greek noun ἄνασσα (anassa) meaning ""queen, lady"".This name was borne by a princess of Syracuse in Sicily, who lived in the 3rd century BC.In Greek mythology, Lanassa was a great-granddaughter of Heracles."
