Landbert,m,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"Means ""bright land"", derived from the Germanic element land ""land"" combined with Old High German beraht ""bright."""
Landburg,f,,Germanic,,,,,,,,"The first element of this name is derived from the Germanic element land ""land."" The second element is derived from Gothic bairgan (bergan in Old High German) ""to keep, to save, to preserve"", or from Old High German burg ""fortress."""
