Laomedeia,f,Λαομέδεια(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/ˌleɪ.ə.mə.ˈdiː.ə/(English),,,,,,,Feminine form of Laomedon. This was the name of one of the fifty Nereids in Greek mythology. A moon of Neptune is named after her.
Laomenes,m,Λαομένης(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Possibly derived from Ancient Greek λαός (laos) meaning ""people"" combined with either μένω (meno) meaning ""to stay, wait, remain, last"" or μένος (menos) meaning ""mind, strength, courage"". This was the name of one of the fifty (or fifty-one) grandsons of Thespius fathered by Heracles in Greek mythology, his mother being Oreia."
