Laophonte,f,Λαοφόντη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,,,,,,,,"Etymology uncertain, derived from Ancient Greek λαός (laos) meaning ""the people"" and potentially φόνος (phonos) meaning ""murder, slaughter"" (compare Polyphonte). In Greek mythology Laophonte was an Aetolian princess, daughter of King Pleuron. In some accounts, she is instead called Eurythemiste."
