Laothoe,f,Λαοθόη(Ancient Greek),Greek Mythology,/laː.o.tʰó.ɛː/(Attic Greek)|/la.o.ˈθo.i/(Koine Greek),,,,,,,"Derived from Ancient Greek λαος (laos) meaning ""people, folk"" combined with θοός (thoos) meaning ""swift, nimble"". This was the name of several women in Greek mythology, including one of the fifty daughters of King Thespius, mother of Antiphus by Heracles."
