Larimar,f,,"Spanish (Caribbean, Rare)",/la.ɾi.ˈmaɾ/(Spanish),,,,,,,"From the name of a type of blue gemstone found only in the Dominican Republic, which is a combination of Larissa with the Spanish word mar meaning ""sea"" (from Latin mare). It was coined by Miguel Méndez, who rediscovered the gemstone in 1974 on a beach (it had been discovered in 1916 by the Spanish priest Miguel Fuertes Lorén), and named it for his daughter. A known bearer is Dominican beauty pageant winner Larimar Fiallo (1983-), full name Larissa del Mar Fiallo Scanlon."
