Laudatus,m,,Late Roman|Welsh (Latinized),,,,,,,,"Derived from Latin laudatus meaning ""praised, lauded, commended, esteemed"", which is ultimately derived from Latin laudo meaning ""to praise, to laud, to commend"".Also, in some cases, the name is a latinization of a non-latinate name. A good example of this is the obscure Welsh saint Lleudadd (6th century AD), whose name was often latinized to Laudatus."
